[.svgmap]
====
image::analysis_schemaexpg2.svg[]

* <<express:analysis_schema.model_action_domain>>; 1
* <<express:analysis_schema.model_action_domain>>; 2
* <<express:analysis_schema.temporal_decomposition_of_model_action>>; 3
====
*)

(*"analysis_schema.behavioural_decomposition_of_numerical_model"
A <<express:analysis_schema.behavioural_decomposition_of_numerical_model,behavioural_decomposition_of_numerical_model>> is a decomposition of a <<express:analysis_schema.numerical_model,numerical_model>> into differnet subbehaviours.
*)


(*"analysis_schema.behavioural_decomposition_of_numerical_model.parts"
the <<express:analysis_schema.numerical_model,numerical_model>> that is the union of the **parts**
*)


(*"analysis_schema.behavioural_decomposition_of_numerical_model.whole"
the <<express:analysis_schema.numerical_model,numerical_model>> that is the union of the **parts**. the set of instances of <<express:analysis_schema.numerical_model,numerical_model>> that are subbehaviours of the **whole** ;
*)


(*"analysis_schema.model_action_domain"
A <<express:analysis_schema.model_action_domain,model_action_domain>> is a type of <<express:analysis_schema.numerical_model,numerical_model>>. It is the response of a <<express:analysis_schema.numerical_model,numerical_model>> during a period of time.
*)

(*"analysis_schema.model_action_domain.__example"
Beam type XYZ regarded as a set of cross-sections of time instants during loading procedure L1 is a <<express:analysis_schema.model_action_domain,model_action_domain>>. This <<express:analysis_schema.model_action_domain,model_action_domain>> is the domain of distributions whihc vary in two dimensions - position along the beam and time. The distributions include rotation for each instant, and bending moment for each position for each instant.
*)

(*"analysis_schema.model_action_domain.final"
the <<express:analysis_schema.model_state_domain,model_state_domain>> that is a boundary of the <<express:analysis_schema.model_action_domain,model_action_domain>> for the final time.
*)


(*"analysis_schema.model_action_domain.initial"
the <<express:analysis_schema.model_state_domain,model_state_domain>> that is a boundary of the <<express:analysis_schema.model_action_domain,model_action_domain>> for the initial time.
*)


(*"analysis_schema.model_product_domain"
A <<express:analysis_schema.model_product_domain,model_product_domain>> is a type of <<express:analysis_schema.numerical_model,numerical_model>> that is only a spatial decomposition and that has an indefinite time dimension.
*)

(*"analysis_schema.model_product_domain.__example"
Beam type XYZ regarded as a set of cross sections is a <<express:analysis_schema.model_product_domain,model_product_domain>>.
*)

(*"analysis_schema.model_product_domain.temporal_parts"
the instances of <<express:analysis_schema.model_action_domain,model_action_domain>> that are preformed by the <<express:analysis_schema.model_product_domain,model_product_domain>>.
*)


(*"analysis_schema.model_product_domain.temporal_parts.__note"
Each member of a <<express:analysis_schema.model_product_domain,model_product_domain>> corresponds to a *physical_product*. For each referenced <<express:analysis_schema.model_action_domain,model_action_domain>> there is a subset (itself a <<express:analysis_schema.model_action_domain,model_action_domain>>) that corresponds to the *physical_product*. This subset is a view of a *physical_action* performed by the *physical_product*.
*)

(*"analysis_schema.model_product_domain_with_mesh"
A <<express:analysis_schema.model_product_domain_with_mesh,model_product_domain_with_mesh>> is a type of <<express:analysis_schema.model_product_domain,model_product_domain>> that has a mesh.
*)


(*"analysis_schema.model_product_domain_with_mesh.model_mesh"
the <<express:mesh_topology_schema.mesh,mesh>> discretizing the <<express:analysis_schema.model_product_domain,model_product_domain>>.
*)


(*"analysis_schema.model_property_distribution"
A <<express:analysis_schema.model_property_distribution,model_property_distribution>> is a function that has a <<express:analysis_schema.numerical_model,numerical_model>> and a property space as its range. Each member of the <<express:analysis_schema.numerical_model,numerical_model>> has a value within the property space. There can be distributions with respect to space and time for a <<express:analysis_schema.model_action_domain,model_action_domain>>. There can be distributions with respect to space for a <<express:analysis_schema.model_product_domain,model_product_domain>>.
*)


(*"analysis_schema.model_property_distribution.creating_software"
the name of the software used to create the <<express:analysis_schema.model_property_distribution,model_property_distribution>>. The vendor, version, computer system, operating system and description shall be specified.
*)


(*"analysis_schema.model_property_distribution.domain"
the <<express:analysis_schema.numerical_model,numerical_model>> that is the domain of the <<express:analysis_schema.model_property_distribution,model_property_distribution>>.
*)


(*"analysis_schema.model_property_distribution.range"
the **general_property** that is the range of the <<express:analysis_schema.model_property_distribution,model_property_distribution>>.
*)


(*"analysis_schema.model_state_domain"
A <<express:analysis_schema.model_state_domain,model_state_domain>> is a type of <<express:analysis_schema.numerical_model,numerical_model>> that has no time dimension. A <<express:analysis_schema.model_state_domain,model_state_domain>> is either independent of time, or a time slice.

For a time slice:

* usually, each member of the domain has the same time; or
* exceptionally, for 'inclined time planes,' different members may have different times. In this case, the domain does not include members with the same spatial position and different times.
*)

(*"analysis_schema.model_state_domain.__example"
Beam type XYZ regarded as a set of cross-sections at the end of loading procedure L1 is a <<express:analysis_schema.model_state_domain,model_state_domain>>. This <<express:analysis_schema.model_state_domain,model_state_domain>> is the domain of distributions which vary in one dimension - position along the beam. The distributions include rotation for each position, and bending moment for each position.
*)

(*"analysis_schema.numerical_model"
A <<express:analysis_schema.numerical_model,numerical_model>> is an aspect of a physical object relevant to a particular type of behavoir. A <<express:analysis_schema.numerical_model,numerical_model>> takes a particular view of its domain in terms of dimensionality and continuity. A <<express:analysis_schema.numerical_model,numerical_model>> is a view of a **temporal_spatial_object** specificiation as a set or space. The members of the set or space may consist of:

* points in space-time;
* spatial or temporal aggregations that are finite in one or more dimensions.
*)

(*"analysis_schema.numerical_model.__example"
Examples include: 3D continuum (volume elements in FEA); 2D continuum (shell elements in FEA); 1D continuum (beam elements in FEA); lumped masses (in a many-body problem).
*)
(*"analysis_schema.numerical_model.__example"
Beam type XYZ during the loading procedure L1 regarded as a point set is a <<express:analysis_schema.numerical_model,numerical_model>>. This <<express:analysis_schema.numerical_model,numerical_model>> is the domain of distrubiton which vary in four dimensions - position and time. The distributions include displacement for each position for each instant and stress for each position for each instant.
*)
(*"analysis_schema.numerical_model.__example"
Beam type XYZ durng loading procedure L1 regarded as a set of cross-sections for time instants is a <<express:analysis_schema.numerical_model,numerical_model>> This <<express:analysis_schema.numerical_model,numerical_model>> is the domain of distributions which vary in two-dimensions - position along the beam and time. The distributions include rotation for each position and for each instant, and bending moment for each position for each instant.
*)
(*"analysis_schema.numerical_model.__example"
Beam type XYZ during heating procedure H1 regarded as a set of 10 segments for time instants is an numerical model. This numerical model is the domain of distributions which vary in two dimensions (one discrete and one continuous) - sub-beam and time. The distributions include average temperature for each segment for each instant, and thermal energy for each segment for each instant.
*)
(*"analysis_schema.numerical_model.__example"
Beam type XYZ during heating procedure H1 regarded as a set of 10 segments for 20 time steps is an numerical model. This numerical model is the domain of distributions which vary in two dimensions (both discrete) - sub-beam and time. The distributions include average temperature for each segment for each step, and total thermal energy gain for each segment for each step.
*)
(*"analysis_schema.numerical_model.__example"
Beam type XYZ during loading procedure L1 is a physical activity; a specifcation that has an individual bfam of type XYZ being loaded according to L1 as a member. Beam type XYZ during loading procedure L1, regarded as a set of cross-sections for time instants is a model action domain. The cross-section at end 2 of the beam at the end of the loading procedure is a physical state that is a member of this set or space. The cross-section at end 2 of an individual beam of type XYZ that has been loaded according to procedure L1 is a member of this physical state.
*)

(*"analysis_schema.numerical_model.__note"
Only an object that is a set or space can be the domain of a distribution function.
*)

(*"analysis_schema.numerical_model.__note"
A <<express:analysis_schema.numerical_model,numerical_model>> has a dimensionality that is chosen for the purposes of numerical analysis and is usually less than or equal to that of the corresponding <<express:product_analysis_schema.temporal_spatial_domain,temporal_spatial_domain>>. Hence a physical beam at an instance in time is a 3D <<express:product_analysis_schema.temporal_spatial_domain,temporal_spatial_domain>>. A corresponding numerical model which uses beam theory is 1D.
*)

(*"analysis_schema.numerical_model.analysis_type"
a description of what type of analysis is to be performed with this numerical analysis.
*)


(*"analysis_schema.numerical_model.creating_software"
the name of the software used to create <<express:analysis_schema.numerical_model,numerical_model>>. The version of the software shall be specifed.
*)


(*"analysis_schema.numerical_model.description"
text that provides further information about the <<express:analysis_schema.numerical_model,numerical_model>>.
*)


(*"analysis_schema.numerical_model.id"
identifier for the <<express:analysis_schema.numerical_model,numerical_model>>.
*)


(*"analysis_schema.numerical_model.name"
user-specified instance identifier.
*)


(*"analysis_schema.numerical_model.intended_analysis_code"
set of one or many names of the intended analysis code that a numerical model was created for. Each intended analysis code shall have the vendor, version, computer system, operating system and descriptions specifed.
*)


(*"analysis_schema.numerical_model.wr:wr1"
The <<express:analysis_schema.numerical_model,numerical_model>> shall be associated with a temporal spatial domain via a view relationship.
*)


(*"analysis_schema.simulation_run"
A <<express:analysis_schema.simulation_run,simulation_run>> is an individual activity that simulates a <<express:analysis_schema.numerical_model,numerical_model>>.
*)

(*"analysis_schema.simulation_run.__example"
A particular run carried out on a particular computer by a particular analysis code at a particular time is a simulation run.
*)

(*"analysis_schema.simulation_run.description"
the text that provides further information about the <<express:analysis_schema.simulation_run,simulation_run>>.
*)


(*"analysis_schema.simulation_run.id"
the identifier for the <<express:analysis_schema.simulation_run,simulation_run>>.
*)


(*"analysis_schema.simulation_run.name"
the words by which the <<express:analysis_schema.simulation_run,simulation_run>> is known.
*)


(*"analysis_schema.simulation_run.results"
the instances of model property distribution that result from the simulation.
*)


(*"analysis_schema.simulation_run.simulated"
the <<express:analysis_schema.numerical_model,numerical_model>> that is simulated.
*)


(*"analysis_schema.spatial_decomposition_of_numerical_model"
A **spatial_decomposition_of_numerical_model** is a decomposition of a <<express:analysis_schema.numerical_model,numerical_model>> into different subspaces.
*)


(*"analysis_schema.spatial_decomposition_of_numerical_model.parts"
the set of instances of <<express:analysis_schema.numerical_model,numerical_model>> that are subspaces of the whole.
*)


(*"analysis_schema.spatial_decomposition_of_numerical_model.whole"
the <<express:analysis_schema.numerical_model,numerical_model>> that is the union of the **parts**.
*)


(*"analysis_schema.temporal_decomposition_of_model_action"
A **temporal_decomposition_of_model_action** is a decomposition of a <<express:analysis_schema.model_action_domain,model_action_domain>> into different time instants.
*)


(*"analysis_schema.temporal_decomposition_of_model_action.parts"
the set of instances of <<express:analysis_schema.model_action_domain,model_action_domain>> at different times.
*)


(*"analysis_schema.temporal_decomposition_of_model_action.whole"
the <<express:analysis_schema.model_action_domain,model_action_domain>> that is the union of the **parts**.
*)


(*"analysis_schema.temporal_spatial_domain_for_model"
The <<express:analysis_schema.temporal_spatial_domain_for_model,temporal_spatial_domain_for_model>> function determines whether or not the given <<express:analysis_schema.numerical_model,numerical_model>> is associated with a <<express:product_analysis_schema.temporal_spatial_domain,temporal_spatial_domain>> by a <<express:analysis_product_relationships_schema.view_relationship,view_relationship>>.

The <<express:analysis_product_relationships_schema.view_relationship,view_relationship>> can be:

* with the given <<express:analysis_schema.numerical_model,numerical_model>>; or
* with another <<express:analysis_schema.numerical_model,numerical_model>> of which the given <<express:analysis_schema.numerical_model,numerical_model>> is a part, either directly or indirectly.

The function returns true if there is an association, otherwise it returns a value of false.
*)


(*"analysis_schema.temporal_spatial_domain_for_model.domain"
(input) the <<express:analysis_schema.numerical_model,numerical_model>> to be checked.
*)


(*"analysis_schema.sc1_numerical_model"
An <<express:analysis_schema.sc1_numerical_model,sc1_numerical_model>> constrains the subtypes for the <<express:analysis_schema.numerical_model,numerical_model>>.
*)


(*"analysis_schema.__schema_file"
data/resource_docs/numerical_analysis/resource.xml
*)


