* <<express:effectivity_schema.conditional_configuration>>; 25
* <<express:effectivity_schema.condition>>; 26
====
*)

(*"effectivity_schema.condition"
A **condition** is a type of <<express:action_schema.action_method,action_method>> that must be fulfilled before a statement or relationship becomes valid.
*)


(*"effectivity_schema.conditional_effectivity"
A **conditional_effectivity** is a type of <<express:effectivity_schema.condition,condition>> or <<express:effectivity_schema.effectivity,effectivity>> for which the domain of applicability is defined by an explicit condition.
*)


(*"effectivity_schema.conditional_configuration"
A **conditional_configuration** is a type of <<express:effectivity_schema.conditional_effectivity,conditional_effectivity>> and represents an association of a <<express:product_concept_schema.product_concept_feature_association,product_concept_feature_association>> object with a design or process in order to define a valid usage of it in the context of a certain class of product.
*)


(*"effectivity_schema.conditional_configuration.configuration_type"
the **configuration_type** defines the valid usage of a **conditional_configuration**.
*)


(*"effectivity_schema.conditional_configuration.inheritance_type"
the **inheritance_type** specifies the inheritance scheme for the configuration information as either **exception**, **inherited**, or **local**.

* An **exception** inheritance_type is when no inheritance scheme is applicable and all required configuration information must be attached locally at the business object.
* An **inherited** inheritance_type is when a scheme for inheritance of configuration information applies. The complete configuration information shall be collected from the different levels in the structure by evaluation of results.
* A **local** inheritance_type is when no inheritance scheme is applicable and all required configuration information must be attached locally at the business object. Nevertheless, any potentially inherited configuration information of a higher level shall be consistent, i.e., it shall be a subset of the locally defined configuration information.
*)


(*"effectivity_schema.dated_effectivity"
A **dated_effectivity** is a type of <<express:effectivity_schema.effectivity,effectivity>> for which the domain of applicability is defined as a possibly open-ended interval of time.
*)


(*"effectivity_schema.dated_effectivity.effectivity_end_date"
the <<express:date_time_schema.date_time_or_event_occurrence,date_time_or_event_occurrence>> that defines the upper bound of the interval of applicability. If a value for this attribute is not defined, the interval of applicability has no upper limit.
*)


(*"effectivity_schema.dated_effectivity.effectivity_start_date"
the <<express:date_time_schema.date_time_or_event_occurrence,date_time_or_event_occurrence>> that defines the lower bound of the interval of applicability. If a value for this attribute is not defined, the interval of applicability has no lower limit.
*)


(*"effectivity_schema.dated_effectivity.wr:WR1"
One or both of the **effectivity_start_date** or **effectivity_end_date** shall be specified.
*)


(*"effectivity_schema.effectivity"
An **effectivity** is the identification of a domain of applicability for product data. An **effectivity** may be either a <<express:effectivity_schema.serial_numbered_effectivity,serial_numbered_effectivity>> or a <<express:effectivity_schema.dated_effectivity,dated_effectivity>>, or a <<express:effectivity_schema.lot_effectivity,lot_effectivity>>, or a <<express:effectivity_schema.time_interval_based_effectivity,time_interval_based_effectivity>>.
*)

(*"effectivity_schema.effectivity.__example"
A process is effective from 1998 March 1 through 1998 December 31.
*)

(*"effectivity_schema.effectivity.id"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> that distinguishes the **effectivity**.
*)


(*"effectivity_schema.effectivity.id.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"effectivity_schema.effectivity.id.__note"
The context in which id is used as a discriminating characteristic can be identified in an annotated Express schema that uses or specializes this entity, or by default, in an agreement of common understanding between partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"effectivity_schema.effectivity.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **effectivity**.
*)


(*"effectivity_schema.effectivity.description.__note"
This attribute is an upwardly compatible addition to *effectivity* as specified in ISO 10303-41:1994.
*)

(*"effectivity_schema.effectivity.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **effectivity** is known.
*)


(*"effectivity_schema.effectivity.name.__note"
This attribute is an upwardly compatible addition to *effectivity* as specified in ISO 10303-41:1994.
*)

(*"effectivity_schema.effectivity.wr:WR1"
Each **effectivity** shall be the <<express:basic_attribute_schema.description_attribute.described_item,described_item>> in at most one <<express:basic_attribute_schema.description_attribute,description_attribute>>.
*)


(*"effectivity_schema.effectivity.wr:WR1.__note"
The <<express:basic_attribute_schema.description_attribute,description_attribute>> data type is defined in <<express:basic_attribute_schema,basic_attribute_schema>> of this document.
*)

(*"effectivity_schema.effectivity.wr:WR2"
Each **effectivity** shall be the <<express:basic_attribute_schema.name_attribute.named_item,named_item>> in at most one <<express:basic_attribute_schema.name_attribute,name_attribute>>.
*)


(*"effectivity_schema.effectivity.wr:WR2.__note"
The <<express:basic_attribute_schema.name_attribute,name_attribute>> data type is defined in <<express:basic_attribute_schema,basic_attribute_schema>> of this document.
*)

(*"effectivity_schema.effectivity.wr:WR2.__note"
A template for constraining the population of the entity data types defined in the <<express:basic_attribute_schema,basic_attribute_schema>> is described in annex E.
*)

(*"effectivity_schema.effectivity_relationship"
An **effectivity_relationship** is a relationship between two instances of the entity data type <<express:effectivity_schema.effectivity,effectivity>> with a description of their relationship.
*)


(*"effectivity_schema.effectivity_relationship.__note"
The role of *effectivity_relationship* can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or by default, in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"effectivity_schema.effectivity_relationship.__note"
Relationships represented using this entity may be parent child relationship. Annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity specify whether or not the relationship is directed.
*)

(*"effectivity_schema.effectivity_relationship.__note"
This entity, together with the <<express:effectivity_schema.effectivity,effectivity>> entity, is based on the relationship template that is described in annex E.3.
*)

(*"effectivity_schema.effectivity_relationship.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **effectivity_relationship** is known.
*)


(*"effectivity_schema.effectivity_relationship.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **effectivity_relationship**. The value of the attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"effectivity_schema.effectivity_relationship.related_effectivity"
the other instance of effectivity that is a part of the relationship. If one element of the relationship is dependent upon the other, this attribute shall be the dependent one.
*)


(*"effectivity_schema.effectivity_relationship.related_effectivity.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"effectivity_schema.effectivity_relationship.relating_effectivity"
one of the instances of <<express:effectivity_schema.effectivity,effectivity>> that is a part of the relationship.
*)


(*"effectivity_schema.effectivity_relationship.relating_effectivity.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"effectivity_schema.lot_effectivity"
A **lot_effectivity** is a type of <<express:effectivity_schema.effectivity,effectivity>> for which the domain of applicability is defined as a given batch of items.
*)


(*"effectivity_schema.lot_effectivity.effectivity_lot_id"
the identification of the batch of items.
*)


(*"effectivity_schema.lot_effectivity.effectivity_lot_size"
the size of the batch of items.
*)


(*"effectivity_schema.serial_numbered_effectivity"
A **serial_numbered_effectivity** is a type of <<express:effectivity_schema.effectivity,effectivity>> for which the domain of applicability is defined as a possibly open-ended interval of serial numbers.
*)


(*"effectivity_schema.serial_numbered_effectivity.__note"
A serial number is represented in this International Standard as an identifier. It is supposed here that, regardless of their format, identifiers used to represent serial numbers are ordered.
*)

(*"effectivity_schema.serial_numbered_effectivity.effectivity_start_id"
the first valid serial number.
*)


(*"effectivity_schema.serial_numbered_effectivity.effectivity_end_id"
the last valid serial number. If a value for this attribute is not defined, the interval of applicability has no upper bound.
*)


(*"effectivity_schema.time_interval_based_effectivity"
A **time_interval_based_effectivity** is a type of <<express:effectivity_schema.effectivity,effectivity>> for which the domain of applicability is defined as a <<express:date_time_schema.time_interval,time_interval>>.
*)


(*"effectivity_schema.time_interval_based_effectivity.__note"
This entity data type provides greater functionalities than the entity data type <<express:effectivity_schema.dated_effectivity,dated_effectivity>>. In particular, it allows the specification of an effectivity period in which the period of time is defined by a date and a duration.
*)

(*"effectivity_schema.time_interval_based_effectivity.effectivity_period"
the <<express:date_time_schema.time_interval,time_interval>> defining the period of time when the associated product data are effective.
*)


(*"effectivity_schema.acyclic_effectivity_relationship"
The **acyclic_effectivity_relationship** function determines whether the graph of instances of the entity data type <<express:effectivity_schema.effectivity,effectivity>> that contains relation as one of its links contains a cycle. This function may be used to evaluate either a <<express:effectivity_schema.effectivity_relationship,effectivity_relationship>> or any of its subtypes.

The function returns TRUE if no cycle has been detected. Otherwise it returns FALSE.
*)


(*"effectivity_schema.acyclic_effectivity_relationship.__note"
The algorithm of the function is explained in annex E.2.
*)

(*"effectivity_schema.acyclic_effectivity_relationship.__note"
This function is not used in this schema. It is defined here because other ISO 10303 integrated resources and application protocols that use the <<express:effectivity_schema.effectivity_relationship,effectivity_relationship>> entity include rules that use this function.
*)

(*"effectivity_schema.acyclic_effectivity_relationship.relation"
(input) the candidate <<express:effectivity_schema.effectivity_relationship,effectivity_relationship>> to be checked.
*)


(*"effectivity_schema.acyclic_effectivity_relationship.relatives"
(input) the set of instances of the entity data type <<express:effectivity_schema.effectivity,effectivity>> for which the function is searching in the <<express:effectivity_schema.effectivity_relationship.relating_effectivity,relating_effectivity>> parameter of the **relation** argument.
*)


(*"effectivity_schema.acyclic_effectivity_relationship.specific_relation"
(input) the fully qualified entity name of a type of <<express:effectivity_schema.effectivity_relationship,effectivity_relationship>> entity.
*)


