SCHEMA fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema '{iso standard 10303 part(104) version(3) object(1) fea-scalar-vector-tensor-schema(4)}';

  REFERENCE FROM measure_schema
      (context_dependent_measure);

  REFERENCE FROM representation_schema
      (representation_item);

(*
=== FEA scalar vector tensor schema type definitions: The FEA representation of scalars, vectors, and tensors

Finite element analysis requires scalars, 2D and 3D vectors, and 2D and 3D second and fourth order tensors to represent the input and output of finite element analyses. The 3D fourth order tensors are used for material response, and are documented in <<subsec-fea-representation-of-response-tensor>>.

NOTE: The types in this clause are organized in groups of similar subject matter.
*)

TYPE angular_value =
     context_dependent_measure;
END_TYPE;

TYPE scalar =
     context_dependent_measure;
END_TYPE;

TYPE tensor1 = SELECT
  (tensor1_2d,
   tensor1_3d);
END_TYPE;

TYPE tensor1_2d =
     ARRAY [1:2] OF context_dependent_measure;
END_TYPE;

TYPE tensor1_3d =
  ARRAY [1:3] OF context_dependent_measure;
END_TYPE;

TYPE symmetric_tensor2_2d = SELECT
  (anisotropic_symmetric_tensor2_2d);
END_TYPE;

TYPE anisotropic_symmetric_tensor2_2d =
  ARRAY [1:3] OF context_dependent_measure;
END_TYPE;

TYPE symmetric_tensor2_3d = SELECT
  (isotropic_symmetric_tensor2_3d,
   orthotropic_symmetric_tensor2_3d,
   anisotropic_symmetric_tensor2_3d);
END_TYPE;

TYPE isotropic_symmetric_tensor2_3d =
     context_dependent_measure;
END_TYPE;

TYPE orthotropic_symmetric_tensor2_3d =
     ARRAY [1:3] OF context_dependent_measure;
END_TYPE;

TYPE anisotropic_symmetric_tensor2_3d =
     ARRAY [1:6] OF context_dependent_measure;
END_TYPE;

TYPE symmetric_tensor4_2d = SELECT
  (anisotropic_symmetric_tensor4_2d);
END_TYPE;

TYPE anisotropic_symmetric_tensor4_2d =
     ARRAY [1:6] OF context_dependent_measure;
END_TYPE;

TYPE tensor_type = SELECT
  (scalar,
   angular_value,
   tensor1_2d,
   tensor1_3d,
   anisotropic_symmetric_tensor2_2d,
   isotropic_symmetric_tensor2_3d,
   orthotropic_symmetric_tensor2_3d,
   anisotropic_symmetric_tensor2_3d,
   anisotropic_symmetric_tensor4_2d,
   anisotropic_symmetric_tensor4_3d,
   fea_isotropic_symmetric_tensor4_3d,
   fea_iso_orthotropic_symmetric_tensor4_3d,
   fea_transverse_isotropic_symmetric_tensor4_3d,
   fea_column_normalised_orthotropic_symmetric_tensor4_3d,
   fea_column_normalised_monoclinic_symmetric_tensor4_3d);
END_TYPE;

TYPE symmetric_tensor4_3d = SELECT
 (anisotropic_symmetric_tensor4_3d,
  fea_isotropic_symmetric_tensor4_3d,
  fea_iso_orthotropic_symmetric_tensor4_3d,
  fea_transverse_isotropic_symmetric_tensor4_3d,
  fea_column_normalised_orthotropic_symmetric_tensor4_3d,
  fea_column_normalised_monoclinic_symmetric_tensor4_3d);
END_TYPE;

TYPE anisotropic_symmetric_tensor4_3d =
     ARRAY [1:21] OF context_dependent_measure;
END_TYPE;

TYPE fea_isotropic_symmetric_tensor4_3d =
     ARRAY [1:2] OF context_dependent_measure;
END_TYPE;

TYPE fea_iso_orthotropic_symmetric_tensor4_3d =
     ARRAY [1:3] OF context_dependent_measure;
END_TYPE;

TYPE fea_transverse_isotropic_symmetric_tensor4_3d =
     ARRAY [1:5] OF context_dependent_measure;
END_TYPE;

TYPE fea_column_normalised_orthotropic_symmetric_tensor4_3d =
     ARRAY [1:9] OF context_dependent_measure;
END_TYPE;

TYPE fea_column_normalised_monoclinic_symmetric_tensor4_3d =
     ARRAY [1:13] OF context_dependent_measure;
END_TYPE;

ENTITY tensor_representation_item
  SUBTYPE OF (representation_item);
  tensor_value              : tensor_type;
END_ENTITY;

END_SCHEMA; -- fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema



(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema"

The subject of the *fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema* is the definition of the scalars, vectors (first order tensors) and tensors that are necessary to represent the input and output of finite element analyses.

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.__fund_cons"

==== General

The fundamental concepts and assumptions include the concept that units are assigned in a context, and the value of the measure is assigned directly.

==== The FEA representation of scalars, vectors, and tensors

Finite element analysis requires scalars, 2D and 3D vectors,
and 2D and 3D second and fourth order tensors to represent
the input and output of finite element analyses. The 3D
fourth order tensors are used for material response,
and are documented in <<subsec-fea-representation-of-response-tensor>>.

* <<express:fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.angular_value,angular_value>>
* <<express:fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.scalar,scalar>>
* <<express:fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.tensor1,tensor1>>
* <<express:fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.tensor1_2d,tensor1_2d>>
* <<express:fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.tensor1_3d,tensor1_3d>>
* <<express:fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.symmetric_tensor2_2d,symmetric_tensor2_2d>>
* <<express:fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.anisotropic_symmetric_tensor2_2d,anisotropic_symmetric_tensor2_2d>>
* <<express:fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.symmetric_tensor2_3d,symmetric_tensor2_3d>>
* <<express:fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.isotropic_symmetric_tensor2_3d,isotropic_symmetric_tensor2_3d>>
* <<express:fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.orthotropic_symmetric_tensor2_3d,orthotropic_symmetric_tensor2_3d>>
* <<express:fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.anisotropic_symmetric_tensor2_3d,anisotropic_symmetric_tensor2_3d>>
* <<express:fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.symmetric_tensor4_2d,symmetric_tensor4_2d>>
* <<express:fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.anisotropic_symmetric_tensor4_2d,anisotropic_symmetric_tensor4_2d>>
* <<express:fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.tensor_type,tensor_type>>

[[subsec-fea-representation-of-response-tensor]]
==== The FEA representation of a fourth order material response tensor

The following TYPEs are used to specify material response in 3D space:

* <<express:fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.symmetric_tensor4_3d,symmetric_tensor4_3d>>
* <<express:fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.anisotropic_symmetric_tensor4_3d,anisotropic_symmetric_tensor4_3d>>
* <<express:fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.fea_isotropic_symmetric_tensor4_3d,fea_isotropic_symmetric_tensor4_3d>>
* <<express:fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.fea_iso_orthotropic_symmetric_tensor4_3d,fea_iso_orthotropic_symmetric_tensor4_3d>>
* <<express:fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.fea_transverse_isotropic_symmetric_tensor4_3d,fea_transverse_isotropic_symmetric_tensor4_3d>>
* <<express:fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.fea_column_normalised_orthotropic_symmetric_tensor4_3d,fea_column_normalised_orthotropic_symmetric_tensor4_3d>>
* <<express:fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.fea_column_normalised_monoclinic_symmetric_tensor4_3d,fea_column_normalised_monoclinic_symmetric_tensor4_3d>>


==== Tensor representation

The ENTITY data type associated with tensor representations is <<fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.tensor_representation_item,tensor_representation_item>>

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.angular_value"

An *angular_value* is a zero order tensor representing the magnitude of an angular value about an axis.

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.angular_value.wr:IP1"

the axis shall be the Z-axis of the founding placement of the referencing entity.

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.scalar"

A *scalar* is a zero order tensor.

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.tensor1"

A *tensor1* is a first order tensor, or vector.

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.tensor1_2d"

A *tensor1_2d* is a first order tensor, or vector in 2D space.

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.tensor1_2d.ARRAY[1]"

the 1 component of the tensor.

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.tensor1_2d.ARRAY[2]"

the 2 component of the tensor.

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.tensor1_3d"

A *tensor1_3d* is a first order tensor, or vector, in 3D space.

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.tensor1_3d.ARRAY[1]"

the 1 component of the tensor.

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.tensor1_3d.ARRAY[2]"

the 2 component of the tensor.

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.tensor1_3d.ARRAY[3]"

the 3 component of the tensor.

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.symmetric_tensor2_2d"

A *symmetric_tensor2_2d* is a symmetric second order tensor in 2D space.

A 2D second order tensor stem:[s_{ij}] is the relationship between two 2D vectors stem:[f_i] and stem:[n_i], as shown below:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
f_i =  \sum_{j=1}^2 s_{ij} n_j \; {\rm for} \; i = 1,2
++++

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.anisotropic_symmetric_tensor2_2d"

An *anisotropic_symmetric_tensor2_2d* is an anisotropic symmetric second order tensor in 2D space.

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.anisotropic_symmetric_tensor2_2d.ARRAY[1]"

the 11 component of the tensor.

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.anisotropic_symmetric_tensor2_2d.ARRAY[2]"

the 22 component of the tensor.

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.anisotropic_symmetric_tensor2_2d.ARRAY[3]"

the 12 component of the tensor.

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.symmetric_tensor2_3d"

A *symmetric_tensor2_3d* is a symmetric second order tensor in 3D space.

A 3D second order tensor stem:[s_{ij}] is the relationship between two 3D vectors stem:[f_i] and stem:[n_i], as shown below:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
f_i =  \sum_{j=1}^3 s_{ij} n_j \; {\rm for} \; i = 1,3
++++

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.isotropic_symmetric_tensor2_3d"

An *isotropic_symmetric_tensor2_3d* is an isotropic symmetric second order tensor in 3D space, which is characterized by one independent value.

The value stem:[s] is a term in the tensor as follows:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
   \left(
\begin{array}{ccc}
s  & 0  & 0      \\
0  & s  & 0      \\
0  & 0  & s
\end{array}
\right)
++++

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.orthotropic_symmetric_tensor2_3d"

An *orthotropic_symmetric_tensor2_3d* is an orthotropic symmetric second order tensor in 3D space, which is characterized by three independent values.

The values stem:[s_{11}], stem:[s_{22}], and stem:[s_{33}] are terms in the tensor as follows:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
   \left(
\begin{array}{ccc}
s_{11}  & 0  & 0      \\
0  & s_{22}  & 0      \\
0  & 0  & s_{33}
\end{array}
\right)
++++

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.orthotropic_symmetric_tensor2_3d.ARRAY[1]"

the tensor components stem:[s_{11}] defined above.

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.orthotropic_symmetric_tensor2_3d.ARRAY[2]"

the tensor components stem:[s_{22}] defined above.

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.orthotropic_symmetric_tensor2_3d.ARRAY[3]"

the tensor components stem:[s_{33}] defined above.

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.anisotropic_symmetric_tensor2_3d"

An *anisotropic_symmetric_tensor2_3d* is an anisotropic symmetric second order tensor in 3D space.

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.anisotropic_symmetric_tensor2_3d.ARRAY[1]"

the 11 component of the tensor.

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.anisotropic_symmetric_tensor2_3d.ARRAY[2]"

the 12 component of the tensor.

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.anisotropic_symmetric_tensor2_3d.ARRAY[3]"

the 13 component of the tensor.

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.anisotropic_symmetric_tensor2_3d.ARRAY[4]"

the 22 component of the tensor.

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.anisotropic_symmetric_tensor2_3d.ARRAY[5]"

the 23 component of the tensor.

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.anisotropic_symmetric_tensor2_3d.ARRAY[6]"

the 33 component of the tensor.

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.symmetric_tensor4_2d"

A *symmetric_tensor4_2d* is a symmetric fourth order tensor in 2D space.

A 2D fourth order tensor stem:[d_{ijkl}] is the relationship between two 2D second order tensors stem:[s_{ij}] and stem:[e_{ij}], as shown below:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++

s_{ij} =  \sum_{k=1}^2 \sum_{l=1}^2 d_{ijkl} e_{kl} \;
 {\rm for} \; i = 1,2 \; {\rm and} \; j = 1,2

++++

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.anisotropic_symmetric_tensor4_2d"

An *anisotropic_symmetric_tensor4_2d* is an anisotropic symmetric fourth order tensor in 2D space.

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.anisotropic_symmetric_tensor4_2d.ARRAY[1]"

the 1111 component of the tensor.

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.anisotropic_symmetric_tensor4_2d.ARRAY[2]"

the 1122 component of the tensor.

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.anisotropic_symmetric_tensor4_2d.ARRAY[3]"

the 1112 component of the tensor.

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.anisotropic_symmetric_tensor4_2d.ARRAY[4]"

the 2222 component of the tensor.

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.anisotropic_symmetric_tensor4_2d.ARRAY[5]"

the 2212 component of the tensor.

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.anisotropic_symmetric_tensor4_2d.ARRAY[6]"

the 1212 component of the tensor.

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.tensor_type"

A *tensor_type* is the value of a field variable.

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.symmetric_tensor4_3d"

A *symmetric_tensor4_3d* is a symmetric fourth order material response tensor in 3D space. A 3D fourth order tensor stem:[d_{ijkl}] represents the relationship between two 3D second order tensors stem:[s_{ij}] and stem:[e_{ij}], as shown below:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++

s_{ij} =  \sum_{k=1}^3 \sum_{l=1}^3 d_{ijkl} e_{kl} \;
 {\rm for} \; i = 1,3 \; {\rm and} \; j = 1,3

++++

In finite element analysis it is common to represent a symmetric 3D second order tensor stem:[s_{ij}] as a (6) array stem:[S_i], with terms:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
\left(
\begin{array}{c}
s_{11} \\
s_{22} \\
s_{33} \\
s_{12} \\
s_{23} \\
s_{31}
\end{array}
\right)
++++

Correspondingly, a symmetric 3D fourth order tensor stem:[d_{ijkl}] is represented as a symmetric stem:[(6 xx 6)] matrix stem:[D_{ij}] with terms:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
\left(
\begin{array}{cccccc}
d_{1111} & d_{1122} & d_{1133} & d_{1112} & d_{1123} & d_{1131} \\
         & d_{2222} & d_{2233} & d_{2212} & d_{2223} & d_{2231} \\
         &          & d_{3333} & d_{3312} & d_{3323} & d_{3331} \\
         &          &          & d_{1212} & d_{1223} & d_{1231} \\
         & \mbox{symmetric} & & & d_{2323} & d_{2331} \\
         &          &          &          &          & d_{3131}
\end{array}
\right)
++++

Note that if:

* stem:[sigma_ij] is stress, with (6) array representation stem:[S_i];
* stem:[varepsilon_ij] is strain;
* stem:[alpha_kl] is the coefficient of linear thermal expansion;
* stem:[T] is temperature;
* stem:[beta_kl] is the coefficient of linear moisture expansion;
* stem:[M] is moisture content;
* stem:[d_{ijkl}] is elasticity, with stem:[6 xx 6] matrix representation stem:[D_{ij}],

then:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
\Delta \sigma_{ij} =  \sum_{k=1}^3 \sum_{l=1}^3 d_{ijkl} (\Delta \varepsilon_{kl} -
 \alpha_{kl}\Delta T - \beta_{kl}\Delta M)  \;
 {\rm for} \; i = 1,3 \; {\rm and} \; j = 1,3
++++

and in contracted notation:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
S_i =  \sum_{j=1}^{6} D_{ij} (E_{j} - E_{j}^{T} - E_{j}^{M})  \;
 {\rm for} \; i = 1,6
++++

where stem:[E_j] is the engineering representation of the strain with components:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
  \left(
\begin{array}{c}
\varepsilon_{11} \\
\varepsilon_{22} \\
\varepsilon_{33} \\
2\varepsilon_{12} \\
2\varepsilon_{23} \\
2\varepsilon_{31}
\end{array}
\right)
++++

A second order tensor shall be represented by its true mathematical components, and not by the components of its engineering representation.

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.anisotropic_symmetric_tensor4_3d"

An *anisotropic_symmetric_tensor4_3d* is an anisotropic symmetric fourth order tensor in 3D space.

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.anisotropic_symmetric_tensor4_3d.ARRAY[1]"

the 1111 component of the tensor.

*)

(*"fea_scalar_vector_tensor_schema.anisotropic_symmetric_tensor4_3d.ARRAY[2]"

the 1122 component of the tensor.

*)

