A state definition has two roles:

* as a state definition with a value that contains numeric information, it can reference a *specified_state*, *calculated_state*, or *linearly_superimposed_state* entity, thereby defining the variables within the model for that state;

* as a state definition with a value that is unspecified, it can reference an *output_request_state* entity to define the information to be calculated by the finite element analysis application for one or more **control_analysis_step**s.

NOTE: An EXPRESS-G Partial Model illustrating the relationships of the state definitions is shown in <<fig-state-definition-express-g-partial-model>>.

[[fig-state-definition-express-g-partial-model]]
