====

==== Function definitions

These definitions are used to ensure the correctness of information in many of the finite element analysis control and result schema information model entities:

* *necessary_value_coordinate_system*
* *consistent_set_values*
* *consistent_list_values*
* *consistent_value*
* *variable_value_type*
* *appropriate_set_value_existence*
* *appropriate_list_value_existence*
* *appropriate_value_existence*


*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.model_or_control_element"

A *model_or_control_element* enables an attribute to reference either a control (constraint element) or a model element.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.cylindrical_harmonic_number"

A *cylindrical_harmonic_number* is a number identifying the harmonic for a *cylindrical_harmonic_control* and a <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.state,state>> in an axisymmetric analysis.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.cylindrical_harmonic_number.wr:WR1"

a harmonic number shall be positive or zero.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_3d_face"

A *volume_3d_face* is an element face of a volume 3D element.

<<fig-volume-3d-elements-hexahedron-faces-and-edges>>, <<fig-volume-3d-elements-wedge-faces-and-edges>>, <<fig-volume-3d-elements-tetrahedron-faces>>, and <<fig-volume-3d-elements-pyramid-faces-and-edges>> in <<sub-eltopo>> establish graphically the relationship between the element face number and the positions in the volume 3D element *required_node_list* for the vertex nodes. The element faces are in the same positions with respect to this list for each element order.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_3d_face.wr:WR1"

a volume 3D element face shall be in the range from 1 to 6.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_2d_face"

A *volume_2d_face* is an element face of a volume 2D element.

<<fig-volume-2d-elements-triangle-faces-and-edges>> and <<fig-volume-2d-elements-quadrilateral-faces-and-edges>> in <<sub-eltopo>> establish graphically the relationship between the element face number and the positions in the volume 2D element *required_node_list* for the vertex nodes. The element faces are in the same positions with respect to this list for each element order.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_2d_face.wr:WR1"

a 2D volume element face shall be in the range from 1 to 4.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_3d_edge"

A *volume_3d_edge* is an element edge of a volume 3D element.

<<fig-volume-3d-elements-hexahedron-faces-and-edges>>, <<fig-volume-3d-elements-wedge-faces-and-edges>>, <<fig-volume-3d-elements-tetrahedron-faces>>, and <<fig-volume-3d-elements-pyramid-faces-and-edges>> in <<sub-eltopo>> establish graphically the relationship between the element edge number and the element edge positions in the volume 3D element. The element edges are in the same positions with respect to this list for each element order.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_3d_edge.wr:WR1"

a volume 3D edge shall be in the range from 1 to 12.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_2d_edge"

A *volume_2d_edge* is an element edge of a volume 2D element.

<<fig-volume-2d-elements-triangle-faces-and-edges>> and <<fig-volume-2d-elements-quadrilateral-faces-and-edges>> in <<sub-eltopo>> establish graphically the relationship between the element edge number and the element edge positions in the volume 2D element. The element edges are in the same positions with respect to this list for each element order.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_2d_edge.wr:WR1"

a volume 2D edge shall be in the range from 1 to 4.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_3d_face"

A *surface_3d_face* is a top or bottom of a surface 3D element.

<<fig-surface-3d-elements-triangle-faces-and-edges>> and <<fig-surface-elements-quadrilateral-faces-and-edges>> in <<sub-eltopo>> establish graphically the relationship between the element face number, and the top and bottom of a surface 3D element. The element faces are in the same positions with respect to this list for each element order.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_3d_face.wr:WR1"

a surface 3D element face shall be in the range from 1 to 2.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_3d_face.wr:IP1"

an element face of 1 shall be the positive stem:[z] parametric axis side of the element, the 2 element face shall be the negative stem:[z] parametric axis side of the element.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_3d_edge"

A *surface_3d_edge* is an element edge of a surface 3D element.

<<fig-surface-3d-elements-triangle-faces-and-edges>> and <<fig-surface-elements-quadrilateral-faces-and-edges>> in <<sub-eltopo>> establish graphically the relationship between the element edge number and the element edge positions in the surface 3D element. The element edges are in the same positions with respect to this list for each element order.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_3d_edge.wr:WR1"

a surface 3D element edge shall be in the range from 1 to 4.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_2d_face"

A *surface_2d_face* is the top or bottom of a surface 2D element.

<<fig-surface-2d-elements-faces-and-edges>> in <<sub-eltopo>> establishes graphically the relationship between the face number, and the top and bottom of a surface 2D element. The faces are in the same positions with respect to this list for each element order.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_2d_face.wr:WR1"

a surface 2D face shall be in the range from 1 to 2.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_2d_face.wr:IP1"

an element face of 1 shall be the positive stem:[z] parametric axis side of the element, an element face of 2 shall be the negative stem:[z] parametric axis side of the element.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_2d_edge"

A *surface_2d_edge* is an element edge of a surface 2D element.

<<fig-surface-2d-elements-faces-and-edges>> in <<sub-eltopo>> establishes graphically the relationship between the element edge number and the edge positions in the surface 2D element. The element edges are in the same positions with respect to this list for each element order.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_2d_edge.wr:WR1"

a surface 2D element edge shall be in the range from 1 to 2.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.field_value"

A *field_value* is the value of a field variable.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.unspecified_value"

An *unspecified_value* is a type that specifies an undefined value.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.measure_or_unspecified_value"

A *measure_or_unspecified_value* is a measure value or is not specified.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.boundary_variable"

A *boundary_variable* is a field variable on a boundary of an element.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.boundary_aggregated_variable"

A *boundary_aggregated_variable* is an aggregated field variable on a boundary of an element.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_variable"

A *volume_variable* is a field variable within the volume of an element.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_aggregated_variable"

A *volume_aggregated_variable* is an aggregated field variable within an element.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_element_variable"

A *surface_element_variable* is a field variable at a point on the surface of an element.

NOTE: Many application defined variables are selected in the *volume_variable*.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.boundary_edge_variable"

A *boundary_edge_variable* is a field variable on an element edge of a surface.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_element_variable"

A *curve_element_variable* is a field variable at a point on a curve element.

NOTE: Many application defined variables are selected in the *volume_variable*.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_scalar_variable"

A *curve_scalar_variable* is a scalar field variable that is aggregated over the section of a curve element at a point along its length.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_scalar_variable.curve_axial_force"

the total direct force acting across a plane normal to the axis of a curve element. A positive value denotes tension.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_scalar_variable.curve_axial_strain"

the elastic strain along the axis of a curve element. This is given by:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
\varepsilon  =  \frac{\partial u}{\partial x}
++++

where:

stem:[u]:: is translation of the element axis in the stem:[x] direction of the curve element axis system;

stem:[x]:: is the axis of the curve element axis system tangential to the element.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_scalar_variable.torque"

the total moment of shear force about the axis of a curve element acting across a plane normal to the axis. A positive value results from a deformation such that the rotation of the section about a direction tangential to the axis increases with distance in that direction.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_scalar_variable.curve_warping"

the warping of the section of a curve element.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_scalar_variable.bi_moment"

the conjugate of warping of the section of a curve element.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_scalar_variable.twist"

the torsional (twisting) of a curve element which is given by:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
\phi  = \frac{\partial \theta}{\partial x}
++++

where:

stem:[theta]:: is rotation of the element section about the stem:[x] direction of the curve element axis system;

stem:[x]:: is the axis of the curve element axis system tangential to the element.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_scalar_variable"

A *surface_scalar_variable* is a scalar field variable that is aggregated through the section of a surface element at a point on its surface.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_scalar_variable.thickness"

the thickness at a point on the surface of a surface element.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_scalar_variable.surface_thermal_gradient"

a scalar quantity that is defined over a surface element. The surface thermal gradient is defined as follows:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
\frac{\partial \theta}{\partial z}
++++

where:

stem:[theta]:: is the temperature at a point within the thickness of the surface.
stem:[z]:: is distance through the thickness in the surface element stem:[z] axis direction.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_scalar_variable.reference_surface_thermal_gradient"

the reference temperature for the surface thermal gradient.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_scalar_variable"

A *volume_scalar_variable* is a scalar field variable that is evaluated at a point within the volume of an element.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_scalar_variable.temperature"

the temperature at a point.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_scalar_variable.moisture"

the moisture content at a point.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_scalar_variable.reference_temperature"

the reference temperature at a point.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_scalar_variable.strain_energy_per_unit_volume"

the strain energy density evaluated at a point.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.boundary_curve_scalar_variable"

A *boundary_curve_scalar_variable* is a scalar field variable that is evaluated at a point along the element edge of a surface 3D element.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.boundary_curve_scalar_variable.normal_force_per_unit_length"

a scalar that is defined over a boundary element edge. The normal force per unit length acts into the element.

Normal_force_per_unit_length is a special case of *applied_force_per_unit_length*.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.boundary_surface_scalar_variable"

A *boundary_surface_scalar_variable* is a scalar field variable that is evaluated at a point on the element face a surface or volume element.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.boundary_surface_scalar_variable.pressure"

a scalar that is defined over a boundary surface or element edge. The pressure is the force per unit area acting normal to the surface into the element.

Pressure is a special case of *applied_force_per_unit_area*.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.aggregated_scalar_variable"

An *aggregated_scalar_variable* is a scalar variable that is obtained by aggregation of a field within an element or over an element boundary. The variable may be evaluated for an element face, a single element, an element group or an entire model.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.aggregated_scalar_variable.total_strain_energy"

the total strain energy within a volume of the model.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.aggregated_scalar_variable.mass"

the mass of a single element, an element group, or an entire model.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.aggregated_scalar_variable.volume"

the volume of a single element, an element group, or an entire model.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_angular_variable"

A *volume_angular_variable* is a scalar variable that is applied to a volume about the origin of the founding placement of the using entity, and about the stem:[Z] axis of that placement.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_angular_variable.constant_angular_acceleration"

a constant angular acceleration applied to a volume.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_angular_variable.application_defined_angular_scalar_variable"

a scalar variable that is arbitrarily defined.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.aggregated_angular_variable"

An *aggregated_angular_variable* is an aggregated scalar variable that is applied to a volume about the origin of the founding placement of the using entity, and about the stem:[Z] axis of that placement.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.aggregated_angular_variable.total_applied_moment"

the total applied moment applied to a volume.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.aggregated_angular_variable.application_defined_aggregated_angular_scalar_variable"

A scalar variable that is arbitrarily defined.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.application_defined_scalar_variable"

A *application_defined_scalar_variable* is a scalar variable that is arbitrarily defined. The string shall be suitable for human interpretation.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_vector_2d_variable"

A *curve_vector_2d_variable* is a 2D vector field variable that is aggregated over the section of a curve element at a point along its length.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_vector_2d_variable.curve_shear_force"

the aggregate shear force at a point on a curve element. The sign convention is defined by the following equation:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
f =    {\bf F}^{t}  \:
          \left( \begin{array}{c} n_y \\ n_z \end{array} \right)
++++

where:

stem:[F]:: is the aggregate shear force vector at a point on the curve with respect to the specified curve coordinate system;

stem:[f]:: is the force applied by the curve on the side of the point with the higher stem:[x] coordinate of the specified system to the side with the lower stem:[x] coordinate, in the direction of unit vector stem:[n] normal to the curve;

stem:[n_y] and stem:[n_z]:: denote the components of unit vector stem:[n] in the directions of the axes stem:[y] and stem:[z] of the specified curve coordinate system.

The first component of stem:[F] is the force in the direction of the curve coordinate system stem:[y] axis, and the second component of stem:[F] is the force in the direction of the curve coordinate system stem:[z] axis.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_vector_2d_variable.curve_bending_moment"

the aggregate bending moment at a point on a curve element. The sign convention is defined by the following equation:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
m =    {\bf M}^{t}  \:
          \left( \begin{array}{c} n_y \\ n_z \end{array} \right)
++++

where:

stem:[M]:: is the aggregate bending moment at a point on the curve with respect to the specified curve coordinate system;

stem:[m]:: is the moment applied by the curve on the side of the point with the higher stem:[x] coordinate of the specified system to the side with the lower stem:[x] coordinate, evaluated about the unit vector stem:[n] normal to the curve;

stem:[n_y] *and* stem:[n_z]:: denote the components of unit vector stem:[n] in the directions of the axes stem:[y] and stem:[z] of the specified curve coordinate system.

The first component of stem:[M] is the moment about the curve coordinate system stem:[y] axis, and the second component of stem:[M] is the moment about the curve coordinate system stem:[z] axis.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_vector_2d_variable.curve_element_curvature"

this is the curvature vector for a curve which is defined as:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
{\bf c} =
      \left( \begin{array}{c}
     {\displaystyle  - \frac{\partial^2 v}{\partial x^2} }  \\
     {\displaystyle  - \frac{\partial^2 w}{\partial x^2} }
                                     \end{array} \right)
++++

where:

stem:[c]:: is the curvature vector;

stem:[v]:: is displacement in the direction of the stem:[y] axis of the specified curve coordinate system;

stem:[w]:: is displacement in the direction of the stem:[z] axis of the specified curve coordinate system.

This definition of curvature is only valid for small deformations to a curve with a small initial curvature.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_vector_2d_variable.curve_thermal_gradient"

a 2D vector that is defined over a curve element. The curve thermal gradient is defined as follows:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
\left( \begin{array}{c}
    {\displaystyle \frac{\partial \theta}{\partial y}}   \\
    {\displaystyle \frac{\partial \theta}{\partial z}}
       \end{array}  \right)
++++

where:

stem:[theta]:: is the temperature at a point within the section of the curve;
stem:[y]:: is distance through the section in the curve element stem:[y] axis direction;
stem:[z]:: is distance through the section in the curve element stem:[z] axis direction.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_vector_2d_variable.reference_curve_thermal_gradient"

the reference temperature for the curve thermal gradient.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_vector_2d_variable"

A *surface_vector_2d_variable* is a 2D vector field variable that is aggregated through the section of a surface element at a point on its surface.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_vector_2d_variable.surface_out_of_plane_shear_force"

the aggregate out-of-plane shear force at a point on a curve element. The sign convention is defined by the following equation:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
f =  {\bf F}^{t}  \:
          \left( \begin{array}{c} n_x \\ n_y \end{array} \right)
++++

where:

stem:[F]:: is the aggregate out-of-plane shear force at a point on the surface with respect to the specified surface coordinate system;

stem:[f]:: is the force in the direction of the stem:[z] axis of the specified coordinate system, applied across a unit width of surface normal to the unit vector stem:[n] in the plane of the surface. The force is applied by the surface on the side of the unit width in the direction of the normal stem:[n] to the side away from the normal;

stem:[n_x] *and* stem:[n_y]:: denote the components of unit vector stem:[n] in the directions of the axes stem:[x] and stem:[y] of the specified surface coordinate system.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_vector_2d_variable.surface_out_of_plane_shear_strain"

this is the out of plane shear strain vector for a surface, which is defined as:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
\varepsilon =
      \left( \begin{array}{c}
      {\displaystyle  \frac{\partial w}{\partial x} +
                      \frac{\partial u}{\partial z} }  \\
      {\displaystyle  \frac{\partial w}{\partial y} +
                      \frac{\partial v}{\partial z} }
                                     \end{array} \right)
++++

where:

stem:[x]:: is distance over the surface in the direction of the stem:[x] axis of the specified surface coordinate system;

stem:[y]:: is distance over the surface in the direction of the stem:[y] axis of the specified surface coordinate system;

stem:[u]:: is displacement in the direction of the stem:[x] axis of the specified surface coordinate system;

stem:[v]:: is displacement in the direction of the stem:[y] axis of the specified surface coordinate system;

stem:[w]:: is displacement in the direction of the stem:[z] axis of the specified surface coordinate system.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.application_defined_vector_2d_variable"

A *application_defined_vector_2d_variable* is a 2D vector variable that is arbitrarily defined. The string shall be suitable for human interpretation.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_vector_3d_variable"

A *curve_vector_3d_variable* is a 3D vector field variable that is aggregated over the section of a curve element at a point along its length.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_vector_3d_variable.applied_force_per_unit_length"

the force per unit length of an element applied to the model.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_vector_3d_variable.applied_moment_per_unit_length"

the moment per unit length of an element applied to the model.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_vector_3d_variable"

A *surface_vector_3d_variable* is a 3D vector field variable that is aggregated through the section of a surface element at a point on its surface.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_vector_3d_variable.applied_force_per_unit_area"

force per unit area of an element applied to the model.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_vector_3d_variable.applied_moment_per_unit_area"

moment per unit area of an element applied to the model.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_vector_3d_variable"

A *volume_vector_3d_variable* is a 3D vector field variable at a point within the volume an element.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_vector_3d_variable.position"

the position of a point within the volume of an element.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_vector_3d_variable.applied_force_per_unit_volume"

the force per unit volume of an element applied to the model.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_vector_3d_variable.applied_moment_per_unit_volume"

the moment per unit volume of an element applied to the model.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_vector_3d_variable.displacement"

the displacement of a point within an element.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_vector_3d_variable.infinitesimal_rotation"

the infinitesimal rotation of fibres embedded within the material of an element at a point. These rotations are assumed to be small for a linear analysis, so that they can be regarded as a vector quantity.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_vector_3d_variable.acceleration"

a 3D vector that is defined over a volume of an element.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.boundary_curve_vector_3d_variable"

A *boundary_curve_vector_3d_variable* is a 3D vector field variable that is evaluated at a point along the element edge of a 3D surface element.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.boundary_curve_vector_3d_variable.applied_force_per_unit_length"

the force per unit length of element edge applied to the model.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.boundary_curve_vector_3d_variable.applied_moment_per_unit_length"

the moment per unit length of element edge applied to the model.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.boundary_surface_vector_3d_variable"

A *boundary_surface_vector_3d_variable* is a 3D vector field variable that is evaluated at a point on the element face of a volume element.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.boundary_surface_vector_3d_variable.applied_force_per_unit_area"

the force per unit area of element face applied to the model.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.boundary_surface_vector_3d_variable.applied_moment_per_unit_length"

the moment per unit area of element face applied to the model.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.aggregated_vector_3d_variable"

An *aggregated_vector_3d_variable* is a 3D vector variable that is obtained by aggregation of a field within an element or over an element boundary. The variable may be evaluated for an element face, a single element, an element group or an entire model.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.aggregated_vector_3d_variable.total_applied_force"

the total applied force applied to a volume of the model.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.aggregated_vector_3d_variable.total_applied_force.centre_of_mass_offset"

a 3D vector that is obtained by integration over an element, element group or whole model. The offset is the distance of the centre of mass from the origin of the master coordinate system for the model.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.application_defined_vector_3d_variable"

A *application_defined_vector_3d_variable* is a 3D vector variable that is arbitrarily defined. The string shall be suitable for human interpretation.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_tensor2_2d_variable"

A *surface_tensor2_2d_variable* is a 2D second order tensor field variable, that is aggregated through the section of a surface element at a point on its surface.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_tensor2_2d_variable.surface_membrane_force"

the aggregate membrane force at a point on a surface element. The sign convention is defined by the following equation:

[stem%unnumbered]
++++
bb f = cc F ((n_x),(n_y))
++++

where:

stem:[cc F]:: is the aggregate membrane force tensor at a point on the surface with respect to the specified surface coordinate system;

stem:[f]:: is the force in the plane of the surface with respect to the stem:[x] and stem:[y] axes of the specified coordinate system, applied across a unit width of surface normal to the unit vector stem:[n] in the plane of the surface. The force is applied by the surface on the side of the unit width in the direction of the normal stem:[n] to the side away from the normal;

stem:[n_x] *and* stem:[n_y]:: denote the components of unit vector stem:[n] in the directions of the axes stem:[x] and stem:[y] of the specified surface coordinate system.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_tensor2_2d_variable.surface_membrane_strain"

the aggregate membrane strain for the surface, which is defined as:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
\varepsilon =
      \left( \begin{array}{cc}
     {\displaystyle   \frac{\partial u}{\partial x} }  &
                 {\displaystyle \frac{\partial u}{\partial y} } \\
     {\displaystyle   \frac{\partial v}{\partial x} }  &
                 {\displaystyle \frac{\partial v}{\partial y} }
                                     \end{array} \right)
++++

where:

stem:[u]:: is displacement in the direction of the stem:[x] axis of the specified surface coordinate system;

stem:[v]:: is displacement in the direction of the stem:[y] axis of the specified surface coordinate system.

This tensor is symmetrical and only three components are stored. The engineering convention, in which the off-diagonal components are summed, is not used.

This definition of strain is only valid for small deformations to a surface with a small initial strain.

*surface_bending_moment*:: the aggregate bending moment at a point on a surface element. The sign convention is defined by the following equation:

[stem%unnumbered]
++++
bb m = cc M ((n_x),(n_y))
++++

where:

stem:[cc M]:: is the aggregate membrane force tensor at a point on the surface with respect to the specified surface coordinate system;

stem:[m]:: is the moment about the stem:[x] and stem:[y] axes of the specified coordinate system, applied across a unit width of surface normal to the unit vector stem:[n] in the plane of the surface. The moment is applied by the surface on the side of the unit width in the direction of the normal stem:[n] to the side away from the normal;

stem:[n_x] *and* stem:[n_y]:: denote the components of unit vector stem:[n] in the directions of the axes stem:[x] and stem:[y] of the specified surface coordinate system.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_tensor2_2d_variable.surface_curvature"

the curvature tensor for a surface which is defined as:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
c =
   \left( \begin{array}{cc}
 {\displaystyle - \frac{\partial^2 w}{\partial x^2} } &
          {\displaystyle - \frac{\partial^2 w}{\partial x \partial y} } \\
 {\displaystyle - \frac{\partial^2 w}{\partial x \partial y} } &
          {\displaystyle - \frac{\partial^2 w}{\partial y^2} }

                                     \end{array} \right)
++++

where:

stem:[c]:: is curvature tensor;

stem:[x]:: is distance over the surface in the direction of the stem:[x] axis of the specified surface coordinate system;

stem:[y]:: is distance over the surface in the direction of the stem:[y] axis of the specified surface coordinate system;

stem:[w]:: is displacement in the direction of the stem:[z] axis of the specified surface coordinate system.

This tensor is symmetrical and only three components are stored. The engineering convention, in which the off-diagonal components are summed, is not used.

This definition of curvature is only valid for small deformations to a surface with a small initial curvature.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.application_defined_tensor2_2d_variable"

A *application_defined_tensor2_2d_variable* is 2D second order tensor variable that is arbitrarily defined. The string shall be suitable for human interpretation.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_tensor2_3d_variable"

A *volume_tensor2_3d_variable* is a 3D second order tensor field variable, that is evaluated at a point within the volume of an element.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_tensor2_3d_variable.total_strain"

the elastic strain tensor stem:[varepsilon] that is the sum of the elastic strain stem:[varepsilon^{E}] and the thermal strain stem:[varepsilon^{T}]. All strains are expressed using the mathematical convention.

For a linear elastic analysis the elastic strains are given by:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
\varepsilon_{ij}^{E} = 1/2
      \left( \frac{\partial v_i}{\partial x_j} +
             \frac{\partial v_j}{\partial x_i}  \right)
++++

where:

stem:[v]:: is the translation at a point within the element;

stem:[x]:: is the position at a point within the element.

For a linear elastic analysis the thermal strains are given by:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
\varepsilon_{ij}^{T} = \alpha_{ij}(T-T_0)
++++

where:

stem:[alpha]:: is the tensor of secant thermal expansion coefficients at a point within the element;

stem:[T]:: the temperature at a point within the element;

stem:[T_0]:: the reference temperature.

For a linear elastic analysis the total strains are given by:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
\varepsilon_{ij} = \varepsilon_{ij}^{E} + \varepsilon_{ij}^{T}
++++

This tensor is symmetrical and only six components are stored. The engineering convention, in which pairs of off-diagonal components are summed, is not used.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_tensor2_3d_variable.stress"

the stress tensor stem:[sigma] that is defined so that for a linear elastic analysis, the total strain energy per unit volume is given by:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
\Delta v = \sum_i \sum_j   \sigma_{ij} \Delta \varepsilon_{ij}
++++

where:

stem:[Delta v]:: is the change of the strain energy per unit volume at a point within the element;

stem:[Delta varepsilon]:: is the change of the strain tensor.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.aggregated_tensor2_3d_variable"

An *aggregated_tensor2_3d_variable* is an aggregated 3D second order tensor field variable that is evaluated at a point within the volume of an element.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.aggregated_tensor2_3d_variable.rotational_inertia"

a 3D second order tensor that is obtained by integration over an element, element group or whole model. The rotational inertia is evaluated about the centre of mass for the domain of integration.

This tensor is symmetrical and only six components are stored.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.application_defined_tensor2_3d_variable"

A *application_defined_tensor2_3d_variable* is a 3D second order tensor variable that is arbitrarily defined. The string shall be suitable for human interpretation.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.message_level"

A *message_level* is the severity of the message.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.message_level.error"

the message is an error message.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.message_level.warning"

the message is an warning message.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.message_level.note"

the message is an informative note.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_3d_state_coordinate_system"

A *surface_3d_state_coordinate_system* is the valid types of coordinate systems in a state definition for a surface 3D element.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_2d_state_coordinate_system"

A *surface_2d_state_coordinate_system* is the valid types of coordinate systems in a state definition for a surface 2D element.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_3d_state_coordinate_system"

A *curve_3d_state_coordinate_system* is the valid types of coordinate systems in a state definition for a curve 3D element.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_2d_state_coordinate_system"

A *curve_2d_state_coordinate_system* is the valid types of coordinate systems in a state definition for a curve 2D element.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.action_type"

An *action_type* is the valid types of nodal actions, that are either forces or moments.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.action_type.applied_loads"

the actions upon the node are applied loads.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.action_type.residual_loads"

the actions upon the node are residual loads resulting from a lack of equilibrium at the node.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_3d_element_output_reference"

A *volume_3d_element_output_reference* is an output request or specification for an element representation, an element group, an element descriptor, or a geometric representation item within the context of a representation, for volume 3D elements. If an element descriptor is referenced then all elements that reference that descriptor will have the same output request or specification.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_2d_element_output_reference"

A *volume_2d_element_output_reference* is an output request or specification for an element representation, an element group, an element descriptor, or a geometric representation item within the context of a representation, for volume 2D elements. If an element descriptor is referenced then all elements that reference that descriptor will have the same output request or specification.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_3d_element_output_reference"

A *surface_3d_element_output_reference* is an output request or specification for an element representation, an element group, an element descriptor, or a geometric representation item within the context of a representation, for surface 3D elements. If an element descriptor is referenced then all elements that reference that descriptor will have the same output request or specification.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_2d_element_output_reference"

A *surface_2d_element_output_reference* is an output request or specification for an element representation, an element group, an element descriptor, or a geometric representation item within the context of a representation, for surface 2D elements. If an element descriptor is referenced then all elements that reference that descriptor will have the same output request or specification.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_3d_element_output_reference"

A *curve_3d_element_output_reference* is an output request or specification for an element representation, an element group, an element descriptor, or a geometric representation item within the context of a representation, for curve 3D elements. If an element descriptor is referenced then all elements that reference that descriptor will have the same output request or specification.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_2d_element_output_reference"

A *curve_2d_element_output_reference* is an output request or specification for an element representation, an element group, an element descriptor, or a geometric representation item within the context of a representation, for curve 2D elements. If an element descriptor is referenced then all elements that reference that descriptor will have the same output request or specification.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.node_output_reference"

A *node_output_reference* is an output reference or specification for a node representation, a node group, a node within a substructure element, or a geometric representation item within the context of a representation.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control,control>> is administrative information for a model, and associates analysis controls and results with a unique model.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control.model_ref"

the model to which the control applies.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control.control_id"

the identifier for the control information.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control.creating_software"

the software used to create the control.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control.description"

additional information about the purpose of this control.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control.user_defined_control"

additional information about the analysis control parameters.

[example]
Analysis code specific information may be input with this attribute, such as solution paramaters, singularity criteria, and restart instructions.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control.intended_analysis_code"

the set of one or many names of the intended analysis code that an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_model,fea_model>> was created for. Each intended analysis code shall have the vendor, version, computer system, operating system and descriptions specified.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control.UR1"

the control identifier shall be unique for the model.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.analysis_step"

An <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.analysis_step,analysis_step>> is a single step or sub-step in an analysis.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.analysis_step.analysis_control"

the control which governs the the analysis step.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control_analysis_step"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control_analysis_step,control_analysis_step>> is a single step in an analysis.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.step_id"

the identifier for the step.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.sequence"

a sequence number that determines the order of processing for the control analysis step.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.initial_state"

the state of the model at the beginning of the step. This includes information such as reference temperatures and initial strains or stresses. For an initial equilibrium state of zero stress or strain it is only necessary to identify the initial state. The initial state will then have no referencing state definitions.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.description"

additional information about the purpose of this control.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.description.UR1"

the sequence number shall be unique for the control.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.description.UR2"

the step identifier shall be unique for the control.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.symmetry_control"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.symmetry_control,symmetry_control>> is the type of symmetry in an analysis.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.no_symmetry_control"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.no_symmetry_control,no_symmetry_control>> is an indication of lack of symmetry control in the analysis.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.cylindrical_symmetry_control"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.cylindrical_symmetry_control,cylindrical_symmetry_control>> is an indication of cylindrical harmonic symmetry in the analysis.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.cylindrical_symmetry_control.harmonic"

the cylindrical harmonic number for an axisymmetric analysis. The initial state may be the zero harmonic, whatever the harmonic of the final state.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.cylindrical_symmetry_control.phase"

the angle stem:[theta] measured from the stem:[i] axis, which gives a factor cos stem:[theta] in the amplitude of all field variables for an axisymmetric analysis.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control_linear_static_analysis_step"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control_linear_static_analysis_step,control_linear_static_analysis_step>> is an analysis step in a linear static analysis.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control_linear_static_analysis_step.process"

the load increment process for the linear static analysis.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control_linear_static_analysis_step_with_harmonic"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control_linear_static_analysis_step_with_harmonic,control_linear_static_analysis_step_with_harmonic>> is an analysis step in a linear static analysis with cylindrical symmetry.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control_linear_static_analysis_step_with_harmonic.symmetry"

the type of symmetry for an analysis.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control_linear_static_analysis_step_with_harmonic.wr:IP1"

the harmonic for a linear static analysis step shall be the same as that for its final state.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control_linear_static_analysis_step_with_harmonic.wr:IP2"

a harmonic number shall be supplied for a state of an axisymmetric model.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control_linear_modes_and_frequencies_analysis_step"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control_linear_modes_and_frequencies_analysis_step,control_linear_modes_and_frequencies_analysis_step>> is an analysis step in a linear nodes and frequencies analysis.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control_linear_modes_and_frequencies_analysis_step.process"

the load increment process for the linear modes and frequencies analysis.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control_linear_modes_and_frequencies_analysis_step.number_of_modes"

the number of modes to be calculated for a step.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control_linear_modes_and_frequencies_analysis_step.frequency_range"

the range of frequencies to consider for a step.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.constraint_element"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.constraint_element,constraint_element>> is a constraint applied to a node or between many nodes.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.constraint_element.element_id"

the identifier for the constraint element.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.constraint_element.steps"

the analysis control steps to which the constraint element applies.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.constraint_element.wr:IP1"

the constraint element identifier shall be unique for the model.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.single_point_constraint_element"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.single_point_constraint_element,single_point_constraint_element>> is a single point constraint which sets values for one or more degrees of freedom at a single node. This equation has the form:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
a_i \cdot x_i = b_i
++++

where:

stem:[x_i]:: are the stem:[n] nodal freedom values;

stem:[a_i]:: are the stem:[n] nodal freedom coefficients;

stem:[b_i]:: are the constraint equation coefficients.

The values of this constraint are set by a <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.single_point_constraint_element_values,single_point_constraint_element_values>> entity.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.single_point_constraint_element.required_node"

the node that is being constrained.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.single_point_constraint_element.coordinate_system"

the coordinate system with respect to which the constraint freedoms are defined.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.single_point_constraint_element.freedoms_and_values"

the degrees of freedom and their coefficients for each term of the linear constraint equation.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.single_point_constraint_element.description"

additional information about the single point constraint element.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.linear_constraint_equation_element"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.linear_constraint_equation_element,linear_constraint_equation_element>> is a linear multi-point constraint specified as a constraint equation. This equation has the form:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
\sum_{i=1}^n \left( a_i \cdot x_i \right)  = b
++++

where:

stem:[x_i]:: are the stem:[n] nodal freedom values;

stem:[a_i]:: are the stem:[n] nodal freedom coefficients;

stem:[b]:: is the constraint equation coefficient.

The value the constraint equation coefficient stem:[b] above is set by a <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.linear_constraint_equation_element_value,linear_constraint_equation_element_value>> entity.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.linear_constraint_equation_element.freedoms_and_coefficients"

the degrees of freedom and their coefficients for each term of the linear constraint equation.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.linear_constraint_equation_element.description"

additional information about the element.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.linear_constraint_equation_nodal_term"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.linear_constraint_equation_nodal_term,linear_constraint_equation_nodal_term>> is the degrees of freedom and their coefficients at a node of the constraint.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.linear_constraint_equation_nodal_term.node"

the node that is associated with the degree of freedom.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.linear_constraint_equation_nodal_term.coordinate_system"

the coordinate system in which the constraint freedom is being defined.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.linear_constraint_equation_nodal_term.freedom_and_coefficient_term"

the constrained freedom at the node, and the coefficient for the constrained freedom at the node (denoted stem:[a_i] in the constraint equation shown above in <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.linear_constraint_equation_element,linear_constraint_equation_element>> ).

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.linear_constraint_equation_nodal_term.dependent"

a flag that indicates whether or not the freedom is to be considered dependent by the analysis application, as follows: TRUE it is the dependent degree of freedom, FALSE it is not.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.freedom_and_coefficient"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.freedom_and_coefficient,freedom_and_coefficient>> is the degree of freedom and the corresponding coefficient value of a constraint equation.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.freedom_and_coefficient.freedom"

the degree of freedom that the value is associated with.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.freedom_and_coefficient.a"

the nodal freedom coefficient stem:[a] associated with the degree of freedom, as defined in <<finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.linear_constraint_equation_element>>.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.nodal_dof_reduction"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.nodal_dof_reduction,nodal_dof_reduction>> is a definition of the degrees of freedom that are to be reduced out for the specified node in dynamic and substructuring analyses.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.nodal_dof_reduction.required_node"

the node that is being reduced.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.nodal_dof_reduction.coordinate_system"

the coordinate system with respect to which the constraint freedoms are defined.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.nodal_dof_reduction.freedoms"

the freedoms to be reduced.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.nodal_dof_reduction.description"

additional information about the reduction definition.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.point_constraint"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.point_constraint,point_constraint>> sets the values for one or more degrees of freedom for all nodes that may be related to the specified point.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.point_constraint.required_point"

the point whose associated nodes are being constrained.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.point_constraint.coordinate_system"

the coordinate system with respect to which the constraint freedoms are defined.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.point_constraint.freedoms_and_coefficients"

the freedom and coefficient pairs imposed by the constraint.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.point_constraint.description"

additional information about the point constraint.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.point_constraint.wr:WR1"

the *geometric_representation_item* shall be a point or a vertex point.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_constraint"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_constraint,curve_constraint>> sets the values for one or more degrees of freedom for all nodes that may be related to the specified curve.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_constraint.required_curve"

the curve whose associated nodes are being constrained.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_constraint.coordinate_system"

the coordinate system with respect to which the constraint freedoms are defined.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_constraint.freedoms_and_coefficients"

the freedom and coefficient pairs imposed by the constraint.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_constraint.description"

additional information about the curve constraint.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_constraint.wr:WR1"

the *geometric_representation_item* shall be a curve or an edge curve.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_constraint"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_constraint,surface_constraint>> sets the values for one or more degrees of freedom for all nodes that may be related to the specified surface.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_constraint.required_surface"

the surface whose associated nodes are being constrained.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_constraint.coordinate_system"

the coordinate system with respect to which the constraint freedoms are defined.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_constraint.freedoms_and_coefficients"

the freedom and coefficient pairs imposed by the constraint.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_constraint.description"

additional information about the surface constraint.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_constraint.wr:WR1"

the *geometric_representation_item* shall be a surface or a face surface.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.solid_constraint"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.solid_constraint,solid_constraint>> sets the values for one or more degrees of freedom for all nodes that may be related to the specified solid model.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.solid_constraint.required_solid"

the solid whose associated nodes are being constrained.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.solid_constraint.coordinate_system"

the coordinate system with respect to which the constraint freedoms are defined.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.solid_constraint.freedoms_and_coefficients"

the freedom and coefficient pairs imposed by the constraint.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.solid_constraint.description"

additional information about the solid constraint.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.solid_constraint.wr:WR1"

the *geometric_representation_item* shall be a solid.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control_process"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control_process,control_process>> is the way in which the model is caused to depart from its initial state.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control_process.process_id"

the identifier for the process.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control_process.description"

additional information about the process.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control_process.wr:IP1"

the process identifier shall be unique for the model.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control_linear_static_load_increment_process"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control_linear_static_load_increment_process,control_linear_static_load_increment_process>> is a process that is a static load increment, and specifies the final state. All loads other than those that specify the initial state (before the process of applying load for the step) are specified with this entity.

The load increment is the difference between the loads for the final state specified by this entity, and those for the initial state specified by entity
<<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control_analysis_step,control_analysis_step>>. The load increment shall include any changes in the constraints.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control_linear_static_load_increment_process.final_input_state"

the final equilibrium state for the static load increment. The final state includes all field and node state definitions applied to the model. This state is a specified state without any analysis output information until an analysis has been carried out.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control_linear_modes_and_frequencies_process"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control_linear_modes_and_frequencies_process,control_linear_modes_and_frequencies_process>> is a process that is a dynamic loading process, and specifies the final state. All loads other than those that specify the initial state (before the process of applying load for the step) are specified with this entity.

The load increment is the difference between the loads for the final state specified by this entity, and those for the initial state specified by entity
<<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control_analysis_step,control_analysis_step>>. The load increment shall include any changes in the constraints.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control_linear_modes_and_frequencies_process.final_input_state"

the final equilibrium state for the dynamicanalysis process.The final state includes all field and node state definitions appliedto the model. This state is a specified state without anyanalysis output information until an analysis has been carried out.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.element_sequence"

An <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.element_sequence,element_sequence>> is an ordered list of elements.

NOTE: Typical uses of the ordered list will be solution optimization orcontrolling the presentation of results.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.element_sequence.oder_id"

the identifier for the ordered element list.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.element_sequence.control_ref"

the control for the ordered element list.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.element_sequence.purpose"

additional information about the ordered element listspecifying its use.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.element_sequence.elements"

the ordered list of elements.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.element_sequence.UR1"

the ordered list identifier shall be unique for the control referencein each of the steps.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.node_sequence"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.node_sequence,node_sequence>> is an ordered list of nodes.

NOTE: Typical uses of the ordered list will be solution optimization orcontrolling the presentation of results.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.node_sequence.order_id"

the identifier for the ordered node list.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.node_sequence.control_ref"

the control for the ordered node list.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.node_sequence.purpose"

additional information about the ordered node listspecifying its use.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.node_sequence.nodes"

the ordered list of nodes.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.node_sequence.UR1"

the ordered list identifier shall be unique for the control referencein each of the steps.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.result"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.result,result>> is the administrative information for analysis results.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.result.result_id"

the identifier for the result.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.result.creating_software"

the software that is used to create the result.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.result.description"

additional information about the result.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.result.wr:IP1"

the result identifier shall be unique for the model.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.result_analysis_step"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.result_analysis_step,result_analysis_step>> is an analysis sub-step. Asresults are calculated, theanalysis step specified by the control is divided into one or more analysissub-steps. The resulting model state is stored for the end of eachsub-step.

For a linear static and dynamic analyses, analysis calculations producea single analysis sub-step which is the final state.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.result_analysis_step.analysis_result"

the result in which the step was calculated.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.result_analysis_step.UR1"

the result shall be unique for the control.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.result_linear_static_analysis_sub_step"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.result_linear_static_analysis_sub_step,result_linear_static_analysis_sub_step>> is a sub-step that is calculated by a linear static analysis,and represents the final state of the step.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.result_linear_static_analysis_sub_step.state"

the calculated state resulting from the linear static analysis sub-step.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.result_linear_modes_and_frequencies_analysis_sub_step"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.result_linear_modes_and_frequencies_analysis_sub_step,result_linear_modes_and_frequencies_analysis_sub_step>> is a sub-step that is calculated by a linear modes and frequencies analysis,
and represents the final state of the step. The final state is described by a series of calculated states, one state for each mode and frequency pair.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.result_linear_modes_and_frequencies_analysis_sub_step.states"

the set of calculated states resulting from the linear modes and frequencies analysis sub-step. There is one <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.calculated_state,calculated_state>> per mode and frequency pair.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.result_linear_modes_and_frequencies_analysis_sub_step.wr:IP1"

there shall be exactly one <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.whole_model_modes_and_frequencies_analysis_message,whole_model_modes_and_frequencies_analysis_message>> for each <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.result_linear_modes_and_frequencies_analysis_sub_step,result_linear_modes_and_frequencies_analysis_sub_step>> that defines the mode number and frequency value.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control_result_relationship"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control_result_relationship,control_result_relationship>> is the relationship of a result step to a control step (and the associated model) that formed the input to the analysis that created the calculated state for the result step.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control_result_relationship.control"

the control for a given analysis step.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control_result_relationship.result"

the result for a given analysis control.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.state"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.state,state>> is an aggregation of state definitions that describe the model at an instant as follows:

* the attributes of the entity provide administrative information for the state;
* details of the state are supplied by the <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.state_definition,state_definition>> entities that reference it.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.state.state_id"

the identifier for the state.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.state.description"

additional information about the state.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.state.wr:IP1"

the state identifier shall be unique for the model.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.state_with_harmonic"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.state_with_harmonic,state_with_harmonic>> is the state of a model for an analysis that requires the specification of the type of symmetry and a corresponding harmonic.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.state_with_harmonic.symmetry"

the type of symmetry for an analysis.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.specified_state"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.specified_state,specified_state>> is all the information for the state that is specified, and that none of it is the result of a previous calculation represented within the information model.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.calculated_state"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.calculated_state,calculated_state>> is some of the information for the state that is calculated by a previous analysis step.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.linearly_superimposed_state"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.linearly_superimposed_state,linearly_superimposed_state>> is some of the information for the state that is calculated by a combination of previously calculated and/or specified steps.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.linearly_superimposed_state.components"

the states from which this state is created.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.state_component"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.state_component,state_component>> is a component of a linearly superimposed state.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.state_component.state"

the state that aggregates the state components.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.state_component.factor"

a weighting factor to scale information in the state.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.output_request_state"

An <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.output_request_state,output_request_state>> is the computer readable output to be produced by an finite element analysis system as follows:

* the attributes of the entity provide administrative information for the state of output;
* details of the information to be produced by the finite element analysis system are supplied by the
<<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.state_definition,state_definition>> entities that reference it.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.output_request_state.steps"

the analysis control steps to which the output requests apply.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.state_relationship"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.state_relationship,state_relationship>> is an association between a relating state and a related state, such that all the information about the related state is also about the relating state. The related state is an aspect of the relating state.

[example]
The <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.state_relationship,state_relationship>> may be used to associate <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.state,state>> entities to one or more <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.state,state>> - <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control_analysis_step,control_analysis_step>> pairs thereby providing an unordered grouping capability for *state_definitions*.

NOTE: A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.state_relationship,state_relationship>> enables different aspects of a state such as boundary conditions, external loads, and thermal loads to be managed as separate states. The initial state for a <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.control_analysis_step,control_analysis_step>> can be defined as a combination of different aspects. The partitioning of a state into aspects is solely for information management convenience, and has no engineering significance.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.state_relationship.name"

the word or group of words by which the <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.state_relationship,state_relationship>> is referred to.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.state_relationship.description"

text that relates the nature of the <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.state_relationship,state_relationship>>.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.state_relationship.relating_state"

one of the <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.state,state>>s which is a part of the relationship.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.state_relationship.related_state"

the other <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.state,state>> which is a part of the relationship. If one state in the relationship is dependent upon the other, then this attribute shall be the dependent one.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.state_definition"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.state_definition,state_definition>> is both information known before and after an analysis and therefore either requests or represents information calculated by the analysis. In this manner a <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.state_definition,state_definition>> output from one *step* may be used as input for a subsequent <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.state_definition,state_definition>>.

[example]
External loadings and prescribed values of variables at a boundary are types of information known before and after an analysis.

[example]
Element stresses and values of variables at unconstrained nodes are types of information calculated by the analysis.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.state_definition.defined_state"

the model state that aggregated the state definitions.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.field_variable_definition"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.field_variable_definition,field_variable_definition>> is a state of the model that specifies values for a field variable pertaining to the elements of the model.

The field variable information shall be either:

* evaluated a point within the volume of an element;
* aggregated through the section of a surface or curve element at a point on the element;
* aggregated within an element, a group of elements, or an entire model;
* evaluated at a point on an element boundary (element face of a volume element or element edge of a surface element);
* aggregated over an element boundary.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.field_variable_element_definition"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.field_variable_element_definition,field_variable_element_definition>> defines the state of the model by specifying the values of a variable within an element.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_3d_element_field_variable_definition"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_3d_element_field_variable_definition,volume_3d_element_field_variable_definition>> is a state of the model that specifies the values of a variable within a volume 3D element.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_3d_element_field_variable_definition.element"

the element for which the values are specified, or the element for which values are to be calculated.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_3d_element_location_point_variable_values"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_3d_element_location_point_variable_values,volume_3d_element_location_point_variable_values>> is a state of the model that specifies the values of a variable at location points within a volume 3D element.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_3d_element_location_point_variable_values.basis"

if *basis* is TRUE then the value set contains only basis locations for the field variable within the element, and no others.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_3d_element_location_point_variable_values.values_and_locations"

the values and locations of the field variable.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_3d_element_location_point_variable_values.variable"

the type of field variable being specified.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_3d_element_location_point_variable_values.wr:WR1"

each variable shall have a corresponding value of the proper type.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_3d_element_location_point_variable_values.wr:WR2"

the value shall be unspecified when the *state_definition.defined_state* is an <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.output_request_state,output_request_state>>.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_3d_element_value_and_location"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_3d_element_value_and_location,volume_3d_element_value_and_location>> is the value of a variable at a location point within a volume 3D element.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_3d_element_value_and_location.simple_value"

the value of the field variable.

*)

