Values are supplied for either the vertex nodes or all nodes of the element,
in the order established graphically in <<sub-eltopo>>.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_2d_element_nodal_specified_variable_values.values"

the values of the field variable.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_2d_element_nodal_specified_variable_values.additional_node_values"

indicates whether values are given for all nodes of the element (TRUE), or for just the vertex nodes (FALSE).

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_2d_element_nodal_specified_variable_values.variable"

the type of field variable being specified.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_2d_element_nodal_specified_variable_values.wr:WR1"

each variable shall have a corresponding value of the proper type.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_2d_element_nodal_specified_variable_values.wr:WR2"

the values shall be unspecified when the *state_definition.defined_state* is an <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.output_request_state,output_request_state>>.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_2d_element_boundary_location_point_variable_values"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_2d_element_boundary_location_point_variable_values,volume_2d_element_boundary_location_point_variable_values>> is a state of the model that specifies the values of a variable at points over the element face of a volume 2D element.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_2d_element_boundary_location_point_variable_values.basis"

if *basis* is TRUE then the value set contains only basis locations for the field variable within the element, and no others.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_2d_element_boundary_location_point_variable_values.values_and_locations"

the values and locations of the field variable.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_2d_element_boundary_location_point_variable_values.variable"

the type of field variable being specified.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_2d_element_boundary_location_point_variable_values.element_face"

the element face for which the values are specified.

The relationship between the element face number and the element node sequence numbers is established graphically in <<sub-eltopo>>.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_2d_element_boundary_location_point_variable_values.wr:WR1"

each variable shall have a corresponding value of the proper type.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_2d_element_boundary_location_point_variable_values.wr:WR2"

the values shall be unspecified when the *state_definition.defined_state* is an <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.output_request_state,output_request_state>>.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_2d_element_boundary_location_point_variable_values.wr:IP1"

each location in the list shall lie on the specified element face.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_2d_element_boundary_whole_face_variable_value"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_2d_element_boundary_whole_face_variable_value,volume_2d_element_boundary_whole_face_variable_value>> is a state of the model that specifies the value of a variable which is obtained by aggregation over the element face of a volume 2D element.

