the simple value shall be unspecified when the *state_definition.defined_state* is an <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.output_request_state,output_request_state>>.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.nodal_freedom_and_value_definition"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.nodal_freedom_and_value_definition,nodal_freedom_and_value_definition>> is a state of the model that specifies information at a node of the model with respect to the solution degrees of freedom that are not a part of an element field discretization. The information may be:

* values for the solution degrees of freedom, such as x translation, or z rotation;

* loads applied in the direction of the solutions degrees of freedom such as values for x force, or z moment. These may be loads applied to a node by elements of the model, or loads applied to a node from outside the model.

NOTE: The purpose of this entity IS to represent information such as loads and displacements at nodes. The purpose of this entity is NOT to represent an element field that has been discretized at the model nodes. The <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.field_variable_node_definition,field_variable_node_definition>> should be used for that purpose.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.nodal_freedom_and_value_definition.node"

the node for which the values are specified, or the node for which the values are to be calculated.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.nodal_freedom_and_value_definition.coordinate_system"

the coordinate system in which the nodal degrees of freedom are defined.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.nodal_freedom_and_value_definition.degrees_of_freedom"

the degrees of freedom at the node.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.nodal_freedom_and_value_definition.values"

the matching values at the node.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.nodal_freedom_and_value_definition.wr:WR1"

the number of degrees of freedom shall match the number of values.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.nodal_freedom_values"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.nodal_freedom_values,nodal_freedom_values>> is a state of the model that specifies the values for degrees of freedom at a node.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.nodal_freedom_action_definition"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.nodal_freedom_action_definition,nodal_freedom_action_definition>> is a state of the model that specifies the values for the actions applied directly to a node of the model. The type of action is indicated with the *action* attribute.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.nodal_freedom_action_definition.action"

the type of values (external applied loads or residual loads at the node) that the action represents.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.element_nodal_freedom_actions"

An <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.element_nodal_freedom_actions,element_nodal_freedom_actions>> is the values of nodal action for an element. This action is applied by the element to the node.

NOTE: This entity is used to represent the reactions of a single or multi-point constraint.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.element_nodal_freedom_actions.element"

the element for which the values are specified or calculated. This can be either an element or a constraint.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.element_nodal_freedom_actions.nodal_action"

the values and associated degrees of freedom at the nodes of an element. The terms in the LIST correspond to the nodes in the *required_node_list* and the *additional_node_list* for the element.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.element_nodal_freedom_terms"

An <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.element_nodal_freedom_terms,element_nodal_freedom_terms>> is a list of degrees of freedom and corresponding values at a node of an element, and a reference coordinate system in which the values are defined.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.element_nodal_freedom_terms.coordinate_system"

the coordinate system in which the values are defined.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.element_nodal_freedom_terms.degree_of_freedom"

the degrees of freedom at the node.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.element_nodal_freedom_terms.values"

the values corresponding to the degrees of freedom at the node.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.point_freedom_and_value_definition"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.point_freedom_and_value_definition,point_freedom_and_value_definition>> is a state of the model that specifies information at all nodes that may be associated with a point with respect to the solution degrees of freedom that are not a part of an element field discretization. The intent of this entity is identical to a <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.nodal_freedom_and_value_definition,nodal_freedom_and_value_definition>>, however it is applied to all nodes associated to a point, rather than to a single node.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.point_freedom_and_value_definition.required_point"

the point whose associated nodes are for which the values are specified, or whose associated nodes for which the values are to be calculated.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.point_freedom_and_value_definition.coordinate_system"

the coordinate system in which the nodal degrees of freedom are defined.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.point_freedom_and_value_definition.degrees_of_freedom"

the degrees of freedom at the node.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.point_freedom_and_value_definition.values"

the matching values at the node.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.point_freedom_and_value_definition.wr:WR1"

the number of degrees of freedom shall match the number of values.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.point_freedom_and_value_definition.wr:WR2"

the *geometric_representation_item* shall be a point or a vertex point.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.point_freedom_values"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.point_freedom_values,point_freedom_values>> is a state of the model that specifies the values for degrees of freedom at a node that is associated with a point.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.point_freedom_action_definition"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.point_freedom_action_definition,point_freedom_action_definition>> is a state of the model that specifies the values for the actions applied directly to nodes associated with a point. The type of action is indicated with the *action* attribute.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.point_freedom_action_definition.action"

the type of values (external applied loads or residual loads at the nodes associated with the point) that the action represents.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_freedom_and_value_definition"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_freedom_and_value_definition,curve_freedom_and_value_definition>> is a state of the model that specifies information at all nodes that may be associated with a curve with respect to the solution degrees of freedom that are not a part of an element field discretization. The intent of this entity is identical to a <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.nodal_freedom_and_value_definition,nodal_freedom_and_value_definition>>, however it is applied to all nodes associated to a curve, rather than to a single node.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_freedom_and_value_definition.required_curve"

the curve whose associated nodes have the values specified, or whose associated node values are to be calculated.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_freedom_and_value_definition.coordinate_system"

the coordinate system in which the nodal degrees of freedom are defined.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_freedom_and_value_definition.degrees_of_freedom"

the degrees of freedom at the node.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_freedom_and_value_definition.values"

the matching values at the node.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_freedom_and_value_definition.wr:WR1"

the number of degrees of freedom shall match the number of values.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_freedom_and_value_definition.wr:WR2"

the *geometric_representation_item* shall be a curve or an edge curve.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_freedom_values"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_freedom_values,curve_freedom_values>> is a state of the model that specifies the values for degrees of freedom at a node that is associated with a curve.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_freedom_action_definition"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_freedom_action_definition,curve_freedom_action_definition>> is a state of the model that specifies the values for the actions applied directly to nodes associated with a curve. The type of action is indicated with the *action* attribute.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.curve_freedom_action_definition.action"

the type of values (external applied loads or residual loads at the nodes associated with the curve) that the action represents.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_freedom_and_value_definition"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_freedom_and_value_definition,surface_freedom_and_value_definition>> is a state of the model that specifies information at all nodes that may be associated with a surface with respect to the solution degrees of freedom that are not a part of an element field discretization. The intent of this entity is identical to a <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.nodal_freedom_and_value_definition,nodal_freedom_and_value_definition>>, however it is applied to all nodes associated to a surface, rather than to a single node.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_freedom_and_value_definition.required_surface"

the surface whose associated nodes are have the values specified, or whose associated node values are to be calculated.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_freedom_and_value_definition.coordinate_system"

the coordinate system in which the nodal degrees of freedom are defined.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_freedom_and_value_definition.degrees_of_freedom"

the degrees of freedom at the node.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_freedom_and_value_definition.values"

the matching values at the node.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_freedom_and_value_definition.wr:WR1"

the number of degrees of freedom shall match the number of values.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_freedom_and_value_definition.wr:WR2"

the *geometric_representation_item* shall be a surface or a face surface.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_freedom_values"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_freedom_values,surface_freedom_values>> is a state of the model that specifies the values for degrees of freedom at a node that is associated with a surface.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_freedom_action_definition"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_freedom_action_definition,surface_freedom_action_definition>> is a state of the model that specifies the values for the actions applied directly to nodes associated with a surface. The type of action is indicated with the *action* attribute.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_freedom_action_definition.action"

the type of values (external applied loads or residual loads at the nodes associated with the surface) that the action represents.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.solid_freedom_and_value_definition"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.solid_freedom_and_value_definition,solid_freedom_and_value_definition>> is a state of the model that specifies information at all nodes that may be associated with a solid with respect to the solution degrees of freedom that are not a part of an element field discretization. The intent of this entity is identical to a <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.nodal_freedom_and_value_definition,nodal_freedom_and_value_definition>>, however it is applied to all nodes associated to a solid, rather than to a single node.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.solid_freedom_and_value_definition.required_solid"

the solid whose associated nodes have the values specified, or whose associated node values are to be calculated.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.solid_freedom_and_value_definition.coordinate_system"

the coordinate system in which the nodal degrees of freedom are defined.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.solid_freedom_and_value_definition.degrees_of_freedom"

the degrees of freedom at the node.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.solid_freedom_and_value_definition.values"

the matching values at the node.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.solid_freedom_and_value_definition.wr:WR1"

the number of degrees of freedom shall match the number of values.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.solid_freedom_and_value_definition.wr:WR2"

the *geometric_representation_item* shall be a solid model.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.solid_freedom_values"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.solid_freedom_values,solid_freedom_values>> is a state of the model that specifies the values for degrees of freedom at a node that is associated with a solid.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.solid_freedom_action_definition"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.solid_freedom_action_definition,solid_freedom_action_definition>> is a state of the model that specifies the values for the actions applied directly to nodes associated with a solid. The type of action is indicated with the *action* attribute.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.solid_freedom_action_definition.action"

the type of values (external applied loads or residual loads at the nodes associated with the solid) that the action represents.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.freedoms_list"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.freedoms_list,freedoms_list>> is a list of the degrees of freedom at a node.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.freedoms_list.freedoms"

the degrees of freedom.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.linear_constraint_equation_element_value"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.linear_constraint_equation_element_value,linear_constraint_equation_element_value>> is the specified constraint equation coefficient stem:[b] associated with the freedoms (stem:[x_i]) and coefficients (stem:[a_i]) as shown in the equation in <<finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.linear_constraint_equation_element>>.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.linear_constraint_equation_element_value.element"

the linear constraint equation element to which the coefficient is applied.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.linear_constraint_equation_element_value.b"

the constraint equation coefficient stem:[b] as above.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.single_point_constraint_element_values"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.single_point_constraint_element_values,single_point_constraint_element_values>> is the set of specified constraint equation coefficients and corresponding freedoms for a single point constraint.

NOTE: The freedoms are specified with the values to allow the correlation of the constraint coefficient with the nodal freedom coefficient in a <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.single_point_constraint_element,single_point_constraint_element>> entity.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.single_point_constraint_element_values.element"

the single point constraint element to which the coefficients and freedoms are applied.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.single_point_constraint_element_values.degrees_of_freedom"

the degrees of freedom at the node of the element.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.single_point_constraint_element_values.b"

the constraint equation coefficients corresponding to the freedoms list.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.single_point_constraint_element_values.wr:WR1"

the number of degrees of freedom shall match the number of values.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.analysis_message"

An <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.analysis_message,analysis_message>> is message information that may be attached to an element, a node, or an entire model.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.analysis_message.level"

the severity of analysis message.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.analysis_message.message_text"

the message text.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.whole_model_analysis_message"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.whole_model_analysis_message,whole_model_analysis_message>> is message information that may be attached to the entire <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_model,fea_model>>.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.whole_model_modes_and_frequencies_analysis_message"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.whole_model_modes_and_frequencies_analysis_message,whole_model_modes_and_frequencies_analysis_message>> is message information about a mode number and matching frequency that may be attached to the entire <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_model,fea_model>>.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.whole_model_modes_and_frequencies_analysis_message.mode"

the mode number that the message concerns.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.whole_model_modes_and_frequencies_analysis_message.frequency"

the frequency that matches the mode number that the message concerns.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.element_analysis_message"

An <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.element_analysis_message,element_analysis_message>> is message information that may be attached to an element.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.element_analysis_message.element"

the element that the message concerns.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.node_analysis_message"

A <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.node_analysis_message,node_analysis_message>> is message information that may be attached to a node.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.node_analysis_message.node"

the node or node group that the message concerns.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.element_group_analysis_message"

An <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.element_group_analysis_message,element_group_analysis_message>> is message information that may be attached to an element group.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.element_group_analysis_message.group"

the group of elements that the message concerns.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_3d_substructure_element_reference"

An <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_3d_substructure_element_reference,volume_3d_substructure_element_reference>> is the reference of a volume 3D element within the contet of a substructure for output request or specification.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_3d_substructure_element_reference.substructure_element_ref"

the substructure element that the volume 3D element information references.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_3d_substructure_element_reference.element_ref"

the volume 3D element for output request or specification.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_2d_substructure_element_reference"

An <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_2d_substructure_element_reference,volume_2d_substructure_element_reference>> is the reference of a volume 2D element within the context of a substructure for output request or specification.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_2d_substructure_element_reference.substructure_element_ref"

the substructure element that the volume 2D element information references.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_2d_substructure_element_reference.element_ref"

the volume 2D element for output request or specification.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_3d_substructure_element_reference"

An <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_3d_substructure_element_reference,surface_3d_substructure_element_reference>> is the reference of a surface 3D element within the context of a substructure for output request or specification.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_3d_substructure_element_reference.substructure_element_ref"

the substructure element that the surface 3D element information references.

*)

