(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.necessary_value_coordinate_system"

A *necessary_value_coordinate_system* ensures that a coordinate system is supplied for the value of a non-scalar variable.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.necessary_value_coordinate_system.value"

identifies the value being checked.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.necessary_value_coordinate_system.coordinate_system"

identifies the coordinate system being checked for existence.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.consistent_set_values"

A *consistent_set_values* ensures the SET of variables and values are consistent.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.consistent_set_values.values_and_locations"

identifies the SET of values to be compared with the variable to ensure consistency.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.consistent_set_values.variable"

identifies the variable to be compared with the SET of values to ensure a consistency.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.consistent_list_values"

A *consistent_list_values* ensures the LIST of variables and values are consistent.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.consistent_list_values.values_and_locations"

identifies the LIST of values to be compared with the variable to ensure consistency.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.consistent_list_values.variable"

identifies the variable to be compared with the LIST of values to ensure a consistency.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.consistent_value"

A *consistent_value* ensures the variable and value are consistent.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.consistent_value.value"

identifies the value to be compared with the variable to ensure consistency.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.consistent_value.variable"

identifies the variable to be compared with the value to ensure a consistency.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.variable_value_type"

A *variable_value_type* calculates the corresponding value for a supplied variable.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.variable_value_type.variable"

identifies used to calculate the appropriately corresponding type of value.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.variable_value_type.vv_type"

output argument that is the value for a corresponding variable.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.appropriate_set_value_existence"

A *appropriate_set_value_existence* ensures the value is unspecified only when the *state_definition.defined_state* is an <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.output_request_state,output_request_state>> for a SET of *values_and_locations*.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.appropriate_set_value_existence.values_and_locations"

identifies the SET of values to be checked for existence.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.appropriate_set_value_existence.type_self"

identifies the <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.state_definition,state_definition>>.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.appropriate_list_value_existence"

A *appropriate_set_value_existence* ensures the value is unspecified only when the *state_definition.defined_state* is an <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.output_request_state,output_request_state>> for a LIST of *values_and_locations*.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.appropriate_list_value_existence.values"

identifies the LIST of values to be checked for existence.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.appropriate_list_value_existence.type_self"

identifies the <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.state_definition,state_definition>>.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.appropriate_value_existence"

An *appropriate_value_existence* ensures the value is unspecified only when the *state_definition.defined_state* is an <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.output_request_state,output_request_state>>.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.appropriate_value_existence.a_value_e"

identifies the value to be checked for proper type.

*)

(*"finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.appropriate_value_existence.type_self"

identifies the <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.state_definition,state_definition>>.

*)

