* <<geometric_model_schema_expg12>>; 12
* <<geometric_model_schema_expg11>>; 13
* <<geometric_model_schema_expg10>>; 14
* <<geometric_model_schema_expg13>>; 15
* <<geometric_model_schema_expg10>>; 16
* <<geometric_model_schema_expg11>>; 17
* <<express:geometry_schema.curve>>; 18
* <<express:geometry_schema.surface>>; 19
* <<express:geometry_schema.point>>; 20
* <<express:product_property_representation_schema.shape_representation>>; 21
* <<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_item>>; 22
* <<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_item>>; 23
* <<express:topology_schema.vertex_point>>; 24
* <<express:topology_schema.advanced_face>>; 25
* <<express:product_property_representation_schema.shape_representation>>; 26
* <<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_context>>; 27
* <<express:representation_schema.mapped_item>>; 28
* <<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_item>>; 29
* <<express:topology_schema.face_surface>>; 30
* <<express:topology_schema.edge_curve>>; 31
* <<express:geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_edge_assignment>>; 32
* <<express:geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_vertex_assignment>>; 33
* <<express:geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_shape_representation>>; 34
* <<express:geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_face_assignment>>; 35
====
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.angular_deviation"
An **angular_deviation** type specifies the maximum angular deviation of any facet in a tessellated shape model. Angular deviation is a measure of the angle between the normal vectors at two points on a shape. The angular deviation for a given facet is the maximum angular deviation for all pairs of points on the shape in the region being approximated by the facet.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.angular_deviation.__note"
The angular deviation of a facet may be approximated by the maximum angular deviation between the pairs of vertex normals.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_facet_long_short_edge_ratio"
A **tessellated_facet_long_short_edge_ratio** type specifies the maximum aspect ratio of any facet in a tessellated shape model. A **tessellated_facet_long_short_edge_ratio** is the ratio of the longest to shortest edge of a facet.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_facet_long_short_edge_ratio.__note"
*tessellated_facet_long_short_edge_ratio* is an easily calculated criterion used to verify that the individual facets in a tessellated geometry have edges of similar lengths.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.boolean_operand"
A **boolean_operand** type identifies all those types of entities which may participate in a boolean operation to form a CSG solid. This includes provision for the special case of a two dimensional 'solid' which is an arcwise connected finite region in two dimensional space defined by boolean operations with 2D operands.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.boolean_operator"
A **boolean_operator** type defines the three boolean operators used in the definition of CSG solids.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.boolean_operator.union"
the operation of constructing the regularised set theoretic union of the volumes defined by two solids;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.boolean_operator.intersection"
the operation of constructing the regularised set theoretic intersection of the volumes defined by two solids;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.boolean_operator.difference"
the regularised set theoretic difference between the volumes defined by two solids;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.bounded_primitive_2d"
A **bounded_primitive_2d** extensible select type defines the set of two dimensional CSG primitives of finite size which may participate in boolean operations or be used as <<express:geometric_model_schema.csg_solid.tree_root_expression,tree_root_expression>> to directly define a two dimensional CSG solid.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.chordal_deviation"
A **chordal_deviation** type specifies the maximum chordal deviation of any facet in a tessellated shape model. Chordal deviation is the maximum value of the minimum distance from any point on the edge of a facet to the closest point on the surface being approximated by the facets.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.csg_primitive"
A **csg_primitive** select type defines the set of CSG primitives which may participate in boolean operations or be used as <<express:geometric_model_schema.csg_solid.tree_root_expression,tree_root_expression>> to directly define a CSG solid.

The 3D CSG primitives are <<express:geometric_model_schema.sphere,sphere>>, <<express:geometric_model_schema.ellipsoid,ellipsoid>>, <<express:geometric_model_schema.right_circular_cone,right_circular_cone>>, <<express:geometric_model_schema.eccentric_cone,eccentric_cone>>, <<express:geometric_model_schema.right_circular_cylinder,right_circular_cylinder>>, <<express:geometric_model_schema.torus,torus>>, <<express:geometric_model_schema.block,block>>, <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive,faceted_primitive>>, <<express:geometric_model_schema.rectangular_pyramid,rectangular_pyramid>>, and <<express:geometric_model_schema.right_angular_wedge,right_angular_wedge>>. The <<express:geometric_model_schema.bounded_primitive_2d,bounded_primitive_2d>> instances which are all types of <<express:geometric_model_schema.primitive_2d,primitive_2d>> may participate in boolean operations with other two dimensional entities.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.csg_select"
A **csg_select** select type identifies the types of entity which may be selected as the root of a CSG tree including a single CSG primitive as a special case.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.edge_or_curve"
An **edge_or_curve** select type identifies the types of entity which may be selected as the underlying geometry of a tessellated edge.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.face_or_surface"
A **face_or_surface** select type identifies the types of entity which may be selected as the underlying geometry of a tessellated face.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.geometric_set_select"
A **geometric_set_select** type identifies the types of entities which can occur in a <<express:geometric_model_schema.geometric_set,geometric_set>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.length_to_height_ratio"
A **length_to_height_ratio** type specifies the maximum ratio of height to length of any facets in a tessellated shape model. The height is measured in a direction perpendicular to the longest edge of a facet.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.length_to_height_ratio.__note"
*length_to_height_ratio* is a criterion used to ensure reasonable proportions of the facets and thus, ensure the regularity of a set of facets in a tessellated geometry.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.maximum_edge_length"
A **maximum_edge_length** type specifies the maximum length of any edge off any facet of a tessellated shape model.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.path_or_composite_curve"
A **path_or_composite_curve** select type identifies the types of entities in a geometric model which can be linked to a <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_wire,tessellated_wire>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.surface_model"
A **surface_model** select type collects all possible surface model entities.

Some product model representations consist of collections of surfaces which do not necessarily form the complete boundary of a solid. Such a model can be represented by a collection of <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> instances or <<express:topology_schema.shell,shell>> instances.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge_or_vertex"
A **tessellated_edge_or_vertex** select type identifies the types of entities that are used as items in the definition of a <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_wire,tessellated_wire>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellation_accuracy_parameter_item"
A **tessellation_accuracy_parameter_item** select type identifies the types of entities that are used as items in the definition of <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_shape_representation_with_accuracy_parameters.tessellation_accuracy_parameters,tessellation_accuracy_parameters>> of a <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_shape_representation_with_accuracy_parameters,tessellated_shape_representation_with_accuracy_parameters>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.wireframe_model"
A **wireframe_model** type collects all possible wireframe model entities.

A wireframe representation of a geometric model contains information only about the intersections of the surfaces forming the boundary but does not contain information about the surfaces themselves.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.solid_model"
A **solid_model** is a type of <<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_item,geometric_representation_item>> which is a complete representation of the nominal shape of a product such that all points in the interior are connected. Any point can be classified as being inside, outside or on the boundary of a solid.

There are several different types of solid model representations including 'solid's defined as connected regions in two dimensional space.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep"
A **manifold_solid_brep** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.solid_model,solid_model>> which is is a finite, arcwise connected volume bounded by one or more surfaces, each of which is a connected, oriented, finite, closed 2-manifold. There is no restriction on the number of through holes, nor on the number of voids within the volume. The Boundary Representation (B-rep) of a manifold solid utilises a graph of edges and vertices embedded in a connected, oriented, finite, closed two manifold surface. The embedded graph divides the surface into arcwise connected areas known as faces. The edges and vertices, therefore, form the boundaries of the faces and the domain of a face does not include its boundaries. The embedded graph may be disconnected and may be a pseudograph. The graph is labelled; that is, each entity in the graph has a unique identity. The geometric surface definition used to specify the geometry of a face shall be 2-manifold embeddable in the plane within the domain of the face. In other words, it shall be connected, oriented, finite, non-self-intersecting, and of surface genus 0. Faces do not intersect except along their boundaries. Each edge along the boundary of a face is shared by at most one other face in the assemblage. The assemblage of edges in the B-rep do not intersect except at their boundaries (i.e., vertices). The geometric curve definition used to specify the geometry of an edge shall be arcwise connected and shall not self-intersect or overlap within the domain of the edge. The geometry of an edge shall be consistent with the geometry of the faces of which it forms a partial bound. The geometry used to define a vertex shall be consistent with the geometry of the faces and edges of which it forms a partial bound. A B-rep is represented by one or more <<express:topology_schema.closed_shell,closed_shell>> instances which shall be disjoint. One shell, the outer, shall completely enclose all the other shells and no other shell may enclose a shell. The facility to define a B-rep with one or more internal voids is provided by the <<express:geometric_model_schema.brep_with_voids,brep_with_voids>> subtype. The following version of the Euler formula shall be satisfied

[[eqnGM1]]

[stem]
++++
chi_{ms} = V - E + 2F - L_{l} - 2(S - G^{s}) = 0
++++

where stem:[V], stem:[E], stem:[F], stem:[L_{l}] and stem:[S] are the numbers of unique vertices, edges, faces, face bounds and shells in the model and stem:[G^s] is the sum of the genus of the shells. More specifically, the topological entities shall conform to the following constraints, where stem:[B] denotes a manifold solid B-rep:

* The shells shall be unique
[stem]
++++
(B)[S] = (B){S}
++++

* Each face in the B-rep is unique
[stem]
++++
((B)[S])[F] = ((B)[S]){F}
++++

* Each loop is unique
[stem]
++++
(((B)[S])[F])[L] = (((B)[S])[F]){L}
++++

* Each (edge + logical) pair is unique
[stem]
++++
((((B)[S])[F])[L])[E_{l}] = ((((B)[S])[F])[L]) E_{l}
++++

* Each edge in the B-rep is either used by exactly two loops or twice by one loop
[stem]
++++
|((((B)[S])[F])[L]){E_{l} }| = 2 |((((B)[S])[F])[L])[E_{l}]|
++++
+
That is, in the list stem:[((((B)[S\])[F\])[L\])[E\]] each edge appears exactly twice.

* Equation <<eqnGM1>> shall be satisfied
[stem]
++++
2|(B)[S]| - 2 Sigma G^{s} = |(((((B)[S])[F]){L ^{e} }){E}){V}| + |((((B)[S])[F]){L ^{v} } ){V}| - |((((B)[S])[F]){L}){E}| + 2|((B)[S])[F]| - |(((B)[S])[F])[L]|
++++

The topological normal of the B-rep at each point on its boundary is the surface normal direction that points away from the solid material. The <<express:topology_schema.closed_shell,closed_shell>> normals, as used, shall be consistent with the topological normal of the B-rep. The **manifold_solid_brep** has two subtypes, <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_brep,faceted_brep>> and <<express:geometric_model_schema.brep_with_voids,brep_with_voids>>, with which there exists a default ANDOR relationship. The following can all be instantiated:

* **manifold_solid_brep**
* <<express:geometric_model_schema.brep_with_voids,brep_with_voids>>
* <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_brep,faceted_brep>>
* <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_brep,faceted_brep>> AND <<express:geometric_model_schema.brep_with_voids,brep_with_voids>>
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep.outer"
a <<express:topology_schema.closed_shell,closed_shell>> defining the exterior boundary of the solid; the shell normal shall point away from the interior of the solid
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep.wr:IP1"
The dimensionality of a **manifold_solid_brep** shall be 3.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep.wr:IP2"
The extent of the **manifold_solid_brep** shall be finite and non-zero.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep.wr:IP3"
No <<express:topology_schema.vertex_point,vertex_point>>, undirected <<express:topology_schema.edge_curve,edge_curve>> (i.e., one which is not an <<express:topology_schema.oriented_edge,oriented_edge>> ), or undirected <<express:topology_schema.face_surface,face_surface>> (i.e., one which is not an <<express:topology_schema.oriented_face,oriented_face>> ) referenced by a **manifold_solid_brep** shall intersect any other <<express:topology_schema.vertex_point,vertex_point>>, undirected <<express:topology_schema.edge_curve,edge_curve>>, or undirected <<express:topology_schema.face_surface,face_surface>> referenced by the same **manifold_solid_brep**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep.wr:IP4"
// Distinct

// <express_ref linkend="topology_schema:ir_express:topology_schema.loop"/>

// s referenced by the same

// <express_ref linkend="topology_schema:ir_express:topology_schema.face"/>

// shall have no common

// <express_ref linkend="topology_schema:ir_express:topology_schema.vertex"/>

No
// tessellated_vertex_point
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_vertex_point,tessellated_vertex_point>>, undirected
// tessellated_edge_curve
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge_curve,tessellated_edge_curve>> (i.e., one which is not an
// oriented_edge
<<express:topology_schema.oriented_edge,oriented_edge>>), or undirected
// tessellated_face_surface
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face_surface,tessellated_face_surface>> (i.e., one which is not an
// oriented_face
<<express:topology_schema.oriented_face,oriented_face>>) referenced by a **manifold_solid_brep** shall intersect any other
// tessellated_vertex_point
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_vertex_point,tessellated_vertex_point>>, undirected
// tessellated_edge_curve
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge_curve,tessellated_edge_curve>> , or undirected
// tessellated_face_surface
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face_surface,tessellated_face_surface>> referenced by the same **manifold_solid_brep**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep.wr:IP4.__note"
This implies that distinct loops of the same face have no common edges. If geometry is present, distinct loops of the same face do not intersect.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep.wr:IP5"
All topological elements of the **manifold_solid_brep** shall have defined associated geometry.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep.wr:IP6"
The shell normals shall agree with the B-rep normal and point away from the solid represented by the B-rep.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep.wr:IP7"
Each face shall be referenced only once by the shells of the **manifold_solid_brep**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep.wr:IP8"
Each <<express:topology_schema.oriented_edge,oriented_edge>> in the **manifold_solid_brep** shall be referenced only once.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep.wr:IP9"
Each undirected edge shall be referenced exactly twice by the loops in the faces of the **manifold_solid_brep**'s shells.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep.wr:IP10"
The Euler equation shall be satisfied for the boundary representation, where the genus term shell-genus is the sum of the genus values for the shells of the B-rep.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep.wr:IP11"
A **manifold_solid_brep**, which is not a <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_brep,faceted_brep>>, shall not reference <<express:topology_schema.poly_loop,poly_loop>> instances.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep.wr:IP12"
A <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_brep,faceted_brep>> can reference only <<express:topology_schema.poly_loop,poly_loop>> instances as face boundaries.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.brep_with_voids"
A **brep_with_voids** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep,manifold_solid_brep>> which contains one or more voids in its interior. The voids are represented by <<express:topology_schema.oriented_closed_shell,oriented_closed_shell>> instances which are defined so that the <<express:topology_schema.oriented_closed_shell,oriented_closed_shell>> normals point into the void, that is, with <<express:topology_schema.oriented_closed_shell.orientation,orientation>> FALSE. A **brep_with_voids** can also be a <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_brep,faceted_brep>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.brep_with_voids.voids"
a set of <<express:topology_schema.oriented_closed_shell,oriented_closed_shell>> instances defining voids within the solid. The set may contain one or more shells.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.brep_with_voids.wr:IP1"
Each void shell shall be disjoint from the outer shell and from every other void shell.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.brep_with_voids.wr:IP2"
Each void shell shall be enclosed within the outer shell but not within any other void shell. In particular, the outer shell is not in the set of void shells.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.brep_with_voids.wr:IP3"
Each shell in the **brep_with_voids** shall be referenced only once.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.faceted_brep"
A **faceted_brep** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep,manifold_solid_brep>> which is a simple form of boundary representation model in which all faces are planar and all edges are straight lines.

Unlike the B-rep model, edges and vertices are not represented explicitly in the model but are implicitly available through the <<express:topology_schema.poly_loop,poly_loop>> entity. A **faceted_brep** has to meet the same topological constraints as the <<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep,manifold_solid_brep>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.faceted_brep.__note"
The *faceted_brep* has been introduced in order to support the large number of systems that allow boundary type solid representations with planar surfaces only. Faceted models may be represented by <<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep,manifold_solid_brep>> but their representation as a *faceted_brep* will be more compact.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.faceted_brep.wr:IP1"
All the bounding loops of all the faces of all the shells in the **faceted_brep** shall be of type <<express:topology_schema.poly_loop,poly_loop>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.faceted_brep.wr:IP2"
The faces in the shells may have implicit or explicit surface geometry. If explicit, the face surface shall be a plane. All polyloops defining the face shall be coplanar.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.brep_2d"
A **brep_2d** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.solid_model,solid_model>> which is a bounded two-dimensional region defined by a face. Any two-dimensional point can be classified as being inside, outside or on the boundary of a **brep_2d**. A **brep_2d** shall have an outer boundary and may have any number of holes.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.brep_2d.extent"
the face which defines the region of two-dimensional space occupied by the **brep_2d** ;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.brep_2d.wr:WR1"
**extent** shall not be a <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> of type <<express:topology_schema.face_surface,face_surface>>, <<express:topology_schema.subface,subface>>, or
// oriented_face
<<express:topology_schema.oriented_face,oriented_face>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.brep_2d.wr:WR2"
Each <<express:topology_schema.face_bound,face_bound>> used to define the **extent** shall be of type <<express:topology_schema.edge_loop,edge_loop>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.brep_2d.wr:WR3"
Precisely one of the bounds of the <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> shall be of type <<express:topology_schema.face_outer_bound,face_outer_bound>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.brep_2d.wr:WR4"
Each <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> used to define the bounds shall be of type <<express:topology_schema.edge_curve,edge_curve>> and shall be two-dimensional.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.csg_solid"
A **csg_solid** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.solid_model,solid_model>> which is a solid represented as a CSG model defined by a collection of so-called primitive solids, combined using regularised boolean operations. The allowed operations are intersection, union and difference. As a special case a **csg_solid** can also consist of a single CSG primitive.

A regularised subset of space is the closure of its interior, where this phrase is interpreted in the usual sense of point set topology. For <<express:geometric_model_schema.boolean_result,boolean_result>> instances regularisation has the effect of removing dangling edges and other anomalies produced by the original operations.

A CSG solid requires two kinds of information for its complete definition: geometric and structural. The geometric information is conveyed by <<express:geometric_model_schema.solid_model,solid_model>> instances. These typically are primitive volumes such as cylinders, wedges and extrusions, but can include general B-rep models. <<express:geometric_model_schema.solid_model,solid_model>> instances can also be <<express:geometric_model_schema.solid_replica,solid_replica>> instances (transformed solids) and <<express:geometric_model_schema.half_space_solid,half_space_solid>> instances. The structural information is in a tree (strictly, an acyclic directed graph) of <<express:geometric_model_schema.boolean_result,boolean_result>> and CSG solids, which represent a `recipe' for building the solid. The terminal nodes are the geometric primitives and other solids. Every **csg_solid** has precisely one <<express:geometric_model_schema.boolean_result,boolean_result>> associated with it which is the root of the tree that defines the solid. (There may be further <<express:geometric_model_schema.boolean_result,boolean_result>> instances within the tree as operands). The significance of a **csg_solid** entity is that the solid defined by the associated tree is thus identified as a significant object in itself, and in this way it is distinguished from other <<express:geometric_model_schema.boolean_result,boolean_result>> entities representing intermediate results during the construction process.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.csg_solid.tree_root_expression"
a boolean expression of primitives and regularised operators describing the solid; the root of the tree of boolean expressions is given here explicitly as a <<express:geometric_model_schema.boolean_result,boolean_result>> entity, or as a <<express:geometric_model_schema.csg_primitive,csg_primitive>>;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.boolean_result"
A **boolean_result** is a type of <<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_item,geometric_representation_item>> which is the result of a regularised operation on two solids to create a new solid. Valid operations are regularised union, regularised intersection, and regularised difference. For purposes of Boolean operations, a solid is considered to be a regularised set of points. The final **boolean_result** depends upon the operation and the two operands. In the case of the difference operator the order of the operands is also significant. The operator can be either union, intersection or difference. The effect of these operators is described below.

_union_ on two solids is the new solid that contains all the points that are in either the **first_operand** or the **second_operand** or both.

_intersection_ on two solids is the new solid that is the regularisation of the set of all points that are in both the **first_operand** and the **second_operand**.

The result of the _difference_ operation on two solids is the regularisation of the set of all points which are in the **first_operand**, but not in the **second_operand**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.boolean_result.__note"
For example if the first operand is a block and the second operand is a solid cylinder of suitable dimensions and location the *boolean_result* produced with the difference operator would be a block with a circular hole.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.boolean_result.operator"
the boolean operator used in the operation to create the result;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.boolean_result.first_operand"
the first operand to be operated upon by the boolean operation;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.boolean_result.second_operand"
the second operand to be operated upon by the boolean operation.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.block"
A **block** is a type of <<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_item,geometric_representation_item>> which is a solid rectangular parallelepiped, defined with a locationand placement coordinate system. The **block** is specified by the positive lengths **x**, **y**, and **z** along the axes of the placement coordinate system, and has one vertex at the origin of the placement coordinate system.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.block.position"
the location and orientation of the axis system for the primitive; the block has one vertex at position.location and its edges aligned with the placement axes in the positive sense;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.block.x"
the size of the block along the placement X axis, (position.p[1]);
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.block.y"
the size of the block along the placement Y axis, (position.p[21]);
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.block.z"
the size of the block along the placement Z axis, (position.p[3]);
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.right_angular_wedge"
A **right_angular_wedge** is a type of <<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_item,geometric_representation_item>> which can be envisioned as the result of intersecting a block with a plane perpendicular to one of its faces. It is defined with a location and local coordinate system. A triangular/trapezoidal face lies in the plane defined by the placement X and Y axes. This face is defined by positive lengths **x** and **y** along the placement X and Y axes, by the length **ltx** (if nonzero) parallel to the X axis at a distance **y** from the placement origin, and by the line connecting the ends of the **x** and **ltx** segments. The remainder of the wedge is specified by the positive length **z** along the placement Z axis which defines a distance through which the trapezoid or triangle is extruded. If **ltx** = 0, the wedge has five faces; otherwise, it has six faces.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.right_angular_wedge.__figure"
[[figure-geometric_model_schema-GMfig24]]
.Right angular wedge and its attributes
====
image::GMfig24.gif[]
====
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.right_angular_wedge.__note"
See <<figure-geometric_model_schema-GMfig24>> for interpretation of attributes.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.right_angular_wedge.position"
the location and orientation of the axis system for the primitive; the **right_angular_wedge** has one vertex at position.location and its edges aligned with the placement axes in the positive sense;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.right_angular_wedge.x"
the size of the **right_angular_wedge** along the placement X axis, (position.p[1]);
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.right_angular_wedge.y"
the size of the wedge along the placement Y axis, (position.p[21]);
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.right_angular_wedge.z"
the size of the wedge along the placement Z axis, (position.p[3]);
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.right_angular_wedge.ltx"
the length in the positive X direction of the smaller surface of the wedge;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.right_angular_wedge.wr:WR1"
**ltx** shall be non-negative and less than **x**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.rectangular_pyramid"
A **rectangular_pyramid** is a type of <<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_item,geometric_representation_item>> which is a solid pyramid with a rectangular base. The apex of the pyramid is directly above the centre point of the base. The **rectangular_pyramid** is specified by its position, which provides a placement coordinate system, its length, depth and height.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.rectangular_pyramid.position"
the location and orientation of the pyramid. **position** defines a placement coordinate system for the pyramid. The pyramid has one corner of its base at position.location and the edges of the base are aligned with the first two placement axes in the positive sense;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.rectangular_pyramid.xlength"
the length of the base along the placement X axis, (position.p[1]);
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.rectangular_pyramid.ylength"
the length of the base along the placement Y axis, (position.p[21]);
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.rectangular_pyramid.height"
the height of the apex above the plane of the base, measured in the direction of the placement Z axis (position.p[3]);
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive"
A **faceted_primitive** is a type of <<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_item,geometric_representation_item>> which is a type of CSG primitive with planar faces. It is defined by a list of four or more points which locate the vertices. These points shall not be coplanar.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points"
the <<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_point,cartesian_point>> instances that locate the vertices of the **faceted_primitive** ;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.wr:WR1"
The coordinate space dimension of **points** [1] shall be 3.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.wr:WR1.__note"
The rule <<express:geometry_schema.compatible_dimension,compatible_dimension>> ensures that all the <<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_point,cartesian_point>> attributes of this entity have the same dimension.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.wr:IP1"
The points in the list **points** shall not be coplanar.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.wr:IP2"
The **points** shall define a closed solid with planar faces.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tetrahedron"
A **tetrahedron** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive,faceted_primitive>> with 4 vertices and 4 triangular faces. It is defined by the four points which locate the vertices. These points shall not be coplanar.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tetrahedron.points"
the <<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_point,cartesian_point>> instances that locate the vertices of the **tetrahedron** ;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tetrahedron.wr:WR1"
The list of <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> shall contain 4 <<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_point,cartesian_point>> instances.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tetrahedron.wr:WR2"
The <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> shall not be coplanar. This is tested by verifying that the fourth point is either above, or below, the plane of the other 3 points.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.convex_hexahedron"
A **convex_hexahedron** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive,faceted_primitive>> primitive with 8 vertices and 6 four-sided faces. It is defined by the 8 points which locate the vertices.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.convex_hexahedron.__figure"
[[figure-geometric_model_schema-GMfig25]]
.Convex_hexahedron
====
image::Geomfig22.gif[]
====
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.convex_hexahedron.__note"
See <<figure-geometric_model_schema-GMfig25>> for further information about the faces and vertices.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.convex_hexahedron\faceted_primotive.points"
the <<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_point,cartesian_point>> instances that locate the vertices of the **tetrahedron** ; these points are ordered such that **points[1], points[2], points[3], points[4]** define, in anti-clockwise order, when viewed from outside the solid, one planar face of the solid. **points[5], points[6], points[7], points[8]** define the opposite face, each of these points being connected by an edge to the corresponding point, with index reduced by 4, on the opposite face;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.convex_hexahedron.wr:WR1"
The list of <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> shall contain 8 <<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_point,cartesian_point>> instances.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.convex_hexahedron.wr:WR2"
The first 4 <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> shall be coplanar.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.convex_hexahedron.wr:WR3"
The final 4 <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> shall be coplanar.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.convex_hexahedron.wr:WR4"
<<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [1], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [4], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [8], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [5], shall be coplanar.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.convex_hexahedron.wr:WR5"
<<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [4], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [3], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [7], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [8], shall be coplanar.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.convex_hexahedron.wr:WR6"
<<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [3], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [2], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [6], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [7], shall be coplanar.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.convex_hexahedron.wr:WR7"
<<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [1], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [5], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [6], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [2], shall be coplanar.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.convex_hexahedron.wr:WR8"
<<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [5], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [6], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [7], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [8], shall all lie on the same side of the plane of <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [1], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [2], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [3].
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.convex_hexahedron.wr:WR9"
<<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [4], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [3], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [7], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [8], shall be coplanar.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.convex_hexahedron.wr:WR10"
<<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [4], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [3], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [7], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [8], shall all lie on the same side of the plane of <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [1], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [2], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [5].
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.convex_hexahedron.wr:WR11"
<<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [1], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [2], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [3], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [4], shall all lie on the same side of the plane of <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [5], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [6], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [7].
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.convex_hexahedron.wr:WR12"
<<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [1], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [4], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [8], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [5], shall all lie on the same side of the plane of <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [3], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [7], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [6].
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.convex_hexahedron.wr:WR13"
<<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [1], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [5], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [6], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [2], shall all lie on the same side of the plane of <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [3], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [7], <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> [8].
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.convex_hexahedron.wr:WR13.__note"
The final 6 rules ensure that the <<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_primitive.points,points>> define a convex figure.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.sphere"
A **sphere** is a type of <<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_item,geometric_representation_item>> which is a CSG primitive with a spherical shape defined by a centre and a radius.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.sphere.radius"
the radius of the **sphere** ;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.sphere.centre"
the location of the centre of the **sphere** ;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.right_circular_cone"
A **right_circular_cone** is a type of <<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_item,geometric_representation_item>> which is a CSG primitive in the form of a cone which may be truncated. It is defined by an axis, a point on the axis, the semi-angle of the cone, and a distance giving the location in the negative direction along the axis from the point to the base of the cone. In addition, a radius is given, which, if nonzero, gives the size and location of a truncated face of the cone.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.right_circular_cone.position"
the location of a point on the axis and the direction of the axis; position.location is a point on the axis of the cone and at the centre of one of the planar circular faces, or, if radius is zero, at the apex; **position.axis** is the direction of the central axis of symmetry of the cone. The direction of the axis is out of the closed solid from the point at the centre of the top face, if truncated, or from the apex if the **radius** is zero.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.right_circular_cone.height"
the distance between the planar circular faces of the cone, if **radius** is greater than zero; or from the base to the apex, if radius equals zero;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.right_circular_cone.radius"
the radius of the cone at the point on the axis (position.location); if the **radius** is zero, the cone has an apex at this point,. if the **radius** is greater than zero, the cone is truncated;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.right_circular_cone.semi_angle"
one half the angle of the cone; this is the angle between the axis and a generator of the conical surface;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.right_circular_cone.wr:WR1"
The **radius** shall be non-negative.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.right_circular_cone.wr:IP1"
The **semi_angle** shall be between 0 and 90 degrees.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.right_circular_cylinder"
A **right_circular_cylinder** is a type of <<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_item,geometric_representation_item>> which is a CSG primitive in the form of a solid cylinder of finite height. It is defined by an axis point at the centre of one planar circular face, an axis, a height, and a radius. The faces are perpendicular to the axis and are circular discs with the specified radius. The height is the distance from the first circular face centre in the positive direction of the axis to the second circular face centre.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.right_circular_cylinder.position"
the location of a point on the axis and the direction of the axis; position.location is a point on the axis and position.axis is the direction of the central axis of symmetry of the cylinder;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.right_circular_cylinder.height"
the distance between the planar circular faces of the cylinder;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.right_circular_cylinder.radius"
the radius of the **right_circular_cylinder** ;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.eccentric_cone"
A **eccentric_cone** is a type of <<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_item,geometric_representation_item>> which is a CSG primitive which is a generalisation of the <<express:geometric_model_schema.right_circular_cone,right_circular_cone>>. The **eccentric_cone** may have an elliptic cross section, and may have a central axis which is not perpendicular to the base. Depending upon the value of the **ratio** attribute it may be truncated, or may take the form of a generalised cylinder. When truncated the top face of the cone is parallel to the plane of the base and has a similar cross section.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.eccentric_cone.__note"
In the placement coordinate system defined by *position* the central point of the top face of the *eccentric_cone* has coordinates (x_offset, y_offset, height).
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.eccentric_cone.__note"
If *ratio* = 0.0 the *eccentric_cone* includes the apex. If *ratio* = 1.0 the *eccentric_cone* is in the form of a generalised cylinder with all cross sections of the same dimensions.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.eccentric_cone.position"
the location of the central <<express:geometry_schema.point,point>> on the axis and the direction of **semi_axis_1**. This defines the centre and plane of the base of the **eccentric_cone** ; **position.p[3]** is normal to the base of the **eccentric_cone** ;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.eccentric_cone.semi_axis_1"
the length of the first radius of the base of the cone in the direction of **position.p[1]**
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.eccentric_cone.semi_axis_2"
the length of the second radius of the base of the cone in the direction of **position.p[2]**
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.eccentric_cone.height"
the height of the cone above the base measured in the direction of **position.p[3]**;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.eccentric_cone.x_offset"
the distance, in the direction of **position.p[1]**, to the central point of the top face of the cone from the point in the plane of this face directly above the central point of the base;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.eccentric_cone.y_offset"
the distance, in the direction of **position.p[2]**, to the central point of the top face of the cone from the point in the plane of this face directly above the central point of the base;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.eccentric_cone.ratio"
the ratio of a radius of the top face to the corresponding radius of the base of the cone;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.eccentric_cone.wr:WR1"
The **ratio** shall not be negative.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.torus"
A **torus** is a type of <<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_item,geometric_representation_item>> which is a solid primitive defined by sweeping the area of a circle (the generatrix) about a larger circle (the directrix). The directrix is defined by a location and direction <<express:geometry_schema.axis1_placement,axis1_placement>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.torus.position"
the location of the central <<express:geometry_schema.point,point>> on the axis and the direction of the axis. This defines the centre and plane of the directrix
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.torus.major_radius"
the radius of the directrix;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.torus.minor_radius"
the radius of the generatrix;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.torus.wr:WR1"
The **major_radius** shall be greater than the **minor_radius**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.ellipsoid"
A **ellipsoid** is a type of <<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_item,geometric_representation_item>> which is a type of CSG primitive in the form of a solid ellipsoid. It is defined by its location and orientation and by the lengths of the three semi-axes.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.ellipsoid.position"
the location and orientation of the ellipsoid. position.location is a <<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_point,cartesian_point>> at the centre of the ellipsoid and the axes of the ellipsoid are aligned with the directions position.p;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.ellipsoid.semi_axis_1"
the length of the semi-axis of the ellipsoid in the direction **position.p[1]**;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.ellipsoid.semi_axis_2"
the length of the semi-axis of the ellipsoid in the direction **position.p[2]**;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.ellipsoid.semi_axis_3"
the length of the semi-axis of the ellipsoid in the direction **position.p[3]**;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.cyclide_segment_solid"
A **cyclide_segment_solid** is a type of <<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_item,geometric_representation_item>> which is a partial Dupin cyclide solid (see <<express:geometry_schema.dupin_cyclide_surface,dupin_cyclide_surface>>). This solid has two planar circular faces that in general have different radii and different normal directions. Around the boundary of each of these faces the curved surface of the solid is tangent to a right circular cone. In the following definition the semi-vertex angle of the cone is in each case specified with respect to the outward normal to its corresponding circular face.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.cyclide_segment_solid.__figure"
[[figure-geometric_model_schema-GMfig_Cyclide_segment_solid]]
.Cyclide_segment_solid
====
image::GMfig25.gif[]
====
*)
(*"geometric_model_schema.cyclide_segment_solid.__figure"
[[figure-geometric_model_schema-GMfig26]]
.Cross section of cyclide_segment_solid
====
image::GMfig26.gif[]
====
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.cyclide_segment_solid.__note"
See <<figure-geometric_model_schema-GMfig_Cyclide_segment_solid>> for further information about the attributes.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.cyclide_segment_solid.position"
the location and orientation of the solid; **position.location** is at the centre of the first circular end face of the solid; **position.p[3] = position.axis** is in the direction of the normal to the plane of symmetry passing through the centres of both circular end faces **position.p[1]** lies in the plane of the first circular end face and **position.p[2]** is directed into the solid;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.cyclide_segment_solid.radius2"
the radius of the first circular end face of the solid;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.cyclide_segment_solid.radius1"
the radius of the second circular end face of the solid;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.cyclide_segment_solid.cone_angle1"
the semi-vertex angle of the cone tangent to the curved surface around the first circular end face of the solid, taken as positive if the cone vertex lies in the direction of the outward-facing normal from that face;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.cyclide_segment_solid.cone_angle2"
the semi-vertex angle of the cone tangent to the curved surface around the second circular end face of the solid, taken as positive if the cone vertex lies in the direction of the outward-facing normal from the centre of that face;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.cyclide_segment_solid.turn_angle"
the angle between the planes of the two circular faces of the solid, measured in the sector containing the solid;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.cyclide_segment_solid.wr:IP1"
The **turn_angle** shall lie in the range 0 to 360 degrees (see NOTE 2).
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.cyclide_segment_solid.wr:IP1.__note"
In terms of the definition of the <<express:geometry_schema.dupin_cyclide_surface,dupin_cyclide_surface>>, the *turn_angle* is the difference in the values of stem:[u] between the isoparametric lines corresponding to the boundaries of the two end faces of the solid.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.cyclide_segment_solid.wr:IP2"
The two tangent cones at the ends of the segment have generators lying in the plane containing the directrix of the Dupin cyclide that define a quadrilateral circumscribing a circle. When one cone reduces to a cylinder its generators become a pair of parallel lines. When both cones are cylinders all four generators are parallel and the circumscribed circle lies at infinity (see NOTE 3).
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.cyclide_segment_solid.wr:IP2.__note"
The attributes of the *cyclide_segment_solid* are not mutually independent. Informal proposition IP2 expresses this fact, and states the simplest geometric characterisation of the dependency. Any correctly generated *cyclide_segment_solid* will satisfy IP2. The condition is illustrated in <<figure-geometric_model_schema-GMfig26>>.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.half_space_solid"
A **half_space_solid** is a type of <<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_item,geometric_representation_item>> which is defined by the half space which is the regular subset of the domain which lies on one side of an unbounded surface. The domain is limited by an orthogonal box in the <<express:geometric_model_schema.boxed_half_space,boxed_half_space>> subtype. The side of the surface which is in the half space is determined by the surface normals and the agreement flag. If the agreement flag is TRUE, then the subset is the one the normals point away from. If the agreement flag is FALSE, then the subset is the one the normals point into. For a valid **half_space_solid**, the surface shall divide the domain into exactly two subsets. Also, within the domain the surface shall be manifold and all the surface normals shall point into the same subset.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.half_space_solid.__note"
A *half_space_solid* is not a subtype of <<express:geometric_model_schema.solid_model,solid_model>>; *half_space_solid* instances are only useful as operands in Boolean expressions.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.half_space_solid.base_surface"
a <<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> defining the boundary of the half space;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.half_space_solid.agreement_flag"
the **agreement_flag** is TRUE if the normal to the **base_surface** points away from the material of the **half_space_solid** ;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.half_space_solid.wr:IP1"
The **base_surface** shall divide the domain into exactly two subsets. If the **half_space_solid** is of subtype <<express:geometric_model_schema.boxed_half_space,boxed_half_space>>, the domain in question is that of the attribute <<express:geometric_model_schema.boxed_half_space.enclosure,enclosure>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.boxed_half_space"
A **boxed_half_space** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.half_space_solid,half_space_solid>> that is trimmed by a surrounding rectangular box. The box has its edges parallel to the coordinate axes of the geometric coordinate system.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.boxed_half_space.__note"
The purpose of the box is to facilitate CSG computations by producing a solid of finite size.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.boxed_half_space.enclosure"
the box which bounds the half space for computational purposes only;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.box_domain"
A **box_domain** is a type of <<express:representation_schema.founded_item,founded_item>> which is an orthogonal box oriented parallel to the axes of the geometric coordinate system which may be used to limit the domain of a <<express:geometric_model_schema.half_space_solid,half_space_solid>>. The **box_domain** is specified by the point at the corner of the box with minimum coordinates, and the lengths of the sides measured in the directions of the coordinate axes.e normals shall point into the same subset.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.box_domain.corner"
a <<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_point,cartesian_point>> at the corner of box with minimum coordinate values;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.box_domain.xlength"
the length of the **box_domain** along the edge parallelto the x axis;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.box_domain.ylength"
the length of the **box_domain** along the edge parallelto the y ayis;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.box_domain.zlength"
the length of the **box_domain** along the edge parallelto the z azis;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.box_domain.wr:WR1"
The only use of the box domain shall be to define the limits for a <<express:geometric_model_schema.boxed_half_space,boxed_half_space>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.primitive_2d"
A **primitive_2d** is a type of <<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_item,geometric_representation_item>> which is a two-dimensional CSG primitive represented as either a <<express:geometric_model_schema.circular_area,circular_area>>, <<express:geometric_model_schema.elliptic_area,elliptic_area>>, <<express:geometric_model_schema.rectangular_area,rectangular_area>>, <<express:geometric_model_schema.polygonal_area,polygonal_area>>, or <<express:geometric_model_schema.half_space_2d,half_space_2d>>. **primitive_2d** instances may be used with other two-dimensional objects to create <<express:geometric_model_schema.csg_solid,csg_solid>> instances in 2D.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.primitive_2d.__note"
The combination of *primitive_2d* instances and any of the three-dimensional <<express:geometric_model_schema.csg_primitive,csg_primitive>> instances in a <<express:geometric_model_schema.boolean_result,boolean_result>> is prohibited by the constraints on <<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_item,geometric_representation_item>> in the geometry schema.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.primitive_2d.wr:WR1"
The coordinate space dimensionality of a **primitive_2d** shall be 2.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.circular_area"
A **circular_area** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.primitive_2d,primitive_2d>> which has the form of a circular disk. It is defined by a centre point and a radius.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.circular_area.centre"
the <<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_point,cartesian_point>> at the centre of the **circular_area** ;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.circular_area.radius"
the radius of the **circular_area** ;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.elliptic_area"
A **elliptic_area** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.primitive_2d,primitive_2d>> which has an ellipse as outer boundary. It is defined by its position and the lengths of the semi-axes of the bounding ellipse.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.elliptic_area.position"
the location and orientation of the **elliptic_area** ; the **elliptic_area** has its centre at position.location and its principal axes are aligned with the placement axes;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.elliptic_area.semi_axis_1"
the length of the semi-axis aligned with the placement X axis ( {blank}**position.p[1]** );
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.elliptic_area.semi_axis_2"
the length of the semi-axis aligned with the placement Y axis ( {blank}**position.p[2]** );
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.rectangular_area"
A **rectangular_area** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.primitive_2d,primitive_2d>> with a rectangular shape. It is defined by a placement coordinate system and linear dimensions. It is specified by the positive lengths x and y along the axes of the placement coordinate system, and has one corner at the origin of the placement coordinate system.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.rectangular_area.position"
the location and orientation of the **rectangular_area** ; the **rectangular_area** has one vertex (with minimum coordinate values) at position.location and its edges are aligned with the placement axes in the positive sense;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.rectangular_area.x"
the length of the **rectangular_area** along the placement X axis ( {blank}**position.p[1]** );
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.rectangular_area.y"
the length of the **rectangular_area** along the placement Y axis ( {blank}**position.p[2]** );
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.polygonal_area"
A **polygonal_area** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.primitive_2d,primitive_2d>> with straight edges. It is defined by a list of three or more <<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_point,cartesian_point>> instances which implicitly define edges connecting consecutive points. The final edge is from the last point in the list of **bounds** to the first.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.polygonal_area.bounds"
the two dimensional <<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_point,cartesian_point>> that are at the vertices of the **polygonal_area** ; the linear segments joining consecutive points form the boundary of the **polygonal_area** ;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.polygonal_area.wr:IP1"
The implicit edges of the **polygonal_area** shall not intersect each other.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.area_with_outer_boundary"
An **area_with_outer_boundary** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.half_space_2d,half_space_2d>> which is the finite interior of a closed curve. It is defined by its boundary, a <<express:geometry_schema.composite_curve,composite_curve>> which is required to be closed.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.area_with_outer_boundary.base_curve"
the two dimensional <<express:geometry_schema.composite_curve,composite_curve>> that forms the boundary of the **area_with_outer_boundary** ;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.area_with_outer_boundary.wr:WR1"
The <<express:geometry_schema.composite_curve.closed_curve,closed_curve>> flag of the <<express:geometric_model_schema.half_space_2d.base_curve,base_curve>> shall have the value TRUE.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.area_with_outer_boundary.wr:IP1"
The <<express:geometric_model_schema.half_space_2d.agreement_flag,agreement_flag>> shall have the value which ensures that the <<express:geometric_model_schema.half_space_2d,half_space_2d>> defined is the finite region inside the closed <<express:geometry_schema.composite_curve,composite_curve>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.half_space_2d"
A **half_space_2d** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.primitive_2d,primitive_2d>> which is a partially bounded region of two-dimensional space. It is defined as the half plane which is the regular subset of the domain that lies on one side of an unbounded curve, or, of a closed curve. The domain is limited by a rectangle in the <<express:geometric_model_schema.rectangled_half_space,rectangled_half_space>> subtype. The side of the curve which is in the half plane is determined by the curve direction and an **agreement_flag**. For a valid **half_space_2d**, the curve shall divide the 2D space into exactly two connected regions. Within the domain of the **half_space_2d** the **base_curve** shall be manifold.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.half_space_2d.__note"
A *half_space_2d* may be used as an operand in a Boolean operation provided the final CSG object is finite and arcwise connected; only subtypes which are also of type <<express:geometric_model_schema.bounded_primitive_2d,bounded_primitive_2d>> may define a simple CSG solid with no Boolean operation.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.half_space_2d.base_curve"
the two dimensional curve defining the boundary of the half plane;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.half_space_2d.agreement_flag"
a BOOLEAN value indicating to which side of the curve the **half_space_2d** lies; if the **agreement_flag** is TRUE, then the region defined is the one on the left as the curve is traversed in the direction of increasing parameter; if the **agreement_flag** is FALSE, then the region is on the right as the curve is traversed in the direction of increasing parameter;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.half_space_2d.wr:IP1"
The **base_curve** shall not be self-intersecting.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.half_space_2d.wr:IP2"
The **base_curve** shall divide the domain into exactly two connected subsets. This implies that, unless the **half_space_2d** is of type <<express:geometric_model_schema.rectangled_half_space,rectangled_half_space>>, the **base_curve** shall be unbounded or closed.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.rectangled_half_space"
A **rectangled_half_space** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.half_space_2d,half_space_2d>> which is trimmed by a surrounding rectangle. The trimming rectangle has its edges parallel to the coordinate axes of the geometric coordinate system.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.rectangled_half_space.enclosure"
the rectangle which bounds the half plane for computational purposes;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.rectangle_domain"
A **rectangle_domain** is a type of <<express:representation_schema.founded_item,founded_item>> which is a rectangular area in two-dimensional space with its edges parallel to the coordinate axes. It may be used to limit the domain of a <<express:geometric_model_schema.half_space_2d,half_space_2d>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.rectangle_domain.corner"
a <<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_point,cartesian_point>> at the corner of box with minimum coordinate values;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.rectangle_domain.xlength"
the length of the **rectangle_domain** along the edge parallelto the x axis;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.rectangle_domain.ylength"
the length of the **rectangle_domain** along the edge parallelto the y ayis;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.rectangle_domain.wr:WR1"
The only use of the **rectangle_domain** shall be to define the limits for a <<express:geometric_model_schema.rectangled_half_space,rectangled_half_space>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.swept_face_solid"
A **swept_face_solid** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.solid_model,solid_model>> which collects the entities which are defined procedurally by a sweeping action on planar figures. The position in space of the swept solid will be dependent upon the position of the **swept_face**. The **swept_face** will be a face of the **swept_face_solid**, except in the case of a solid of revolution with angle equal to 360 degrees.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.swept_face_solid.swept_face"
the <<express:topology_schema.face_surface,face_surface>> defining the area to be swept. The extent of this face is defined by the <<express:topology_schema.face.bounds,bounds>> attribute of the referenced <<express:topology_schema.face_surface,face_surface>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.swept_face_solid.wr:WR1"
The **swept_face** shall be planar. The <<express:topology_schema.face_surface.face_geometry,face_geometry>> attribute of the <<express:topology_schema.face_surface,face_surface>> referenced shall be a <<express:geometry_schema.plane,plane>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.extruded_face_solid"
A **extruded_face_solid** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_face_solid,swept_face_solid>> which is a solid defined by sweeping a planar <<express:topology_schema.face_surface,face_surface>>. The direction of translation is defined by a <<express:geometry_schema.direction,direction>>, and the length of the translation is defined by a distance **depth**. The planar face may have holes which will sweep into holes in the solid.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.extruded_face_solid.extruded_direction"
the <<express:geometry_schema.direction,direction>> in which the face is to be swept;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.extruded_face_solid.depth"
the distance the face is to be swept;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.extruded_face_solid.wr:WR1"
**extruded_direction** shall not be perpendicular to the normal to the plane of the <<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_face_solid.swept_face,swept_face>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.revolved_face_solid"
A **revolved_face_solid** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_face_solid,swept_face_solid>> which is a solid of revolution formed by revolving a planar <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> about an axis. The axis shall be in the plane of the face and the axis shall not intersect the interior of the face. The planar face may have holes which will sweep into holes in the solid. The direction of revolution is clockwise when viewed along the axis in the positive direction. More precisely if stem:[A] is the axis location and stem:[d] is the axis direction and stem:[C] is an arc on the surface of revolution generated by an arbitrary point stem:[p] on the boundary of the face, then stem:[C] leaves stem:[p] in direction stem:[d xx (p - A)] as the face is revolved.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.revolved_face_solid.__figure"
[[figure-geometric_model_schema-GMfig27]]
.Revolved face solid
====
image::GMfig27.gif[]
====
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.revolved_face_solid.__note"
See <<figure-geometric_model_schema-GMfig27>> for illustration of attributes.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.revolved_face_solid.axis"
the axis about which revolution will take place;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.revolved_face_solid.angle"
the angle through which the sweep will be made; this angle is measured from the plane of the swept face;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.revolved_face_solid.axis_line"
the line of the axis of revolution;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.revolved_face_solid.wr:IP1"
**axis_line** shall lie in plane of <<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_face_solid.swept_face,swept_face>> attribute of the <<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_face_solid,swept_face_solid>> supertype.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.revolved_face_solid.wr:IP2"
The **axis_line** shall not intersect the interior of the <<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_face_solid.swept_face,swept_face>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.revolved_face_solid.wr:IP3"
**angle** shall lie in the range stem:[0 < angle le 360 "P{degree}"].
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.surface_curve_swept_face_solid"
A **surface_curve_swept_face_solid** is a type of
// swept_face_solid
<<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_face_solid,swept_face_solid>> which is the result of sweeping a face along a **directrix** lying on a **reference_surface**. The orientation of the
// swept_face
<<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_face_solid.swept_face,swept_face>> is related to the direction of the surface normal. The
// swept_face
<<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_face_solid.swept_face,swept_face>> is required to be a
// face_surface
<<express:topology_schema.face_surface,face_surface>> lying in the plane z = 0 and this is swept along the **directrix** in such a way that the origin of the local coordinate system used to define the
// swept_face
<<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_face_solid.swept_face,swept_face>> is on the **directrix** and the local X axis is in the direction of the normal to the **reference_surface** at the current point. The resulting solid has the property that the cross section of the surface by the normal plane to the **directrix** at any point is a copy of the <<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_face_solid.swept_face,swept_face>>.

The orientation of the
// swept_face
<<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_face_solid.swept_face,swept_face>> geometry as it sweeps along the **directrix** is precisely defined by a
// cartesian_transformation_operator_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_transformation_operator_3d,cartesian_transformation_operator_3d>> with attributes:

// local_origin
<<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_transformation_operator.local_origin,local_origin>> as point (0,0,0).

// axis1
<<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_transformation_operator.axis1,axis1>> as the normal **N** to the **reference_surface** at the point of the **directrix** with parameter stem:[u].

// axis3
<<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_transformation_operator_3d.axis3,axis3>> as the direction of the tangent vector **t** at the point of the **directrix** with parameter stem:[u].

The remaining attributes are defaulted to define a corresponding transformation matrix **T** (stem:[u]), which varies with the **directrix** parameter stem:[u].
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.surface_curve_swept_face_solid.__note"
The geometric shape of the solid is not dependent upon the curve parametrisation; the volume depends upon the area of the face and the length of the *directrix*.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.surface_curve_swept_face_solid.directrix"
the curve used to define the sweeping operation; the solid is generated by sweeping the
// swept_face
<<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_face_solid.swept_face,swept_face>> along the **directrix**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.surface_curve_swept_face_solid.start_param"
the parameter value on the **directrix** at which the sweeping operation commences.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.surface_curve_swept_face_solid.end_param"
the parameter value on the **directrix** at which the sweeping operation ends.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.surface_curve_swept_face_solid.reference_surface"
the surface containing the **directrix**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.surface_curve_swept_face_solid.wr:WR1"
If the **directrix** is a
// surface_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve,surface_curve>> then the **reference_surface** shall be in the
// basis_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve.basis_surface,basis_surface>> set for this curve.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.surface_curve_swept_face_solid.wr:IP1"
The
// swept_face
<<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_face_solid.swept_face,swept_face>> shall lie in the plane stem:[z = 0].
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.surface_curve_swept_face_solid.wr:IP2"
The **directrix** shall lie on the **reference_surface**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.surface_curve_swept_face_solid.wr:IP2.__note"
In the description above the normal to the *reference_surface* at the current point is denoted *N*.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.swept_area_solid"
A **swept_area_solid** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.solid_model,solid_model>> which collects the entities which are defined procedurally by a sweeping action on planar bounded surfaces. The position in space of the swept solid will be dependent upon the position of the **swept_area**. The **swept_area** will be a face of the resulting **swept_area_solid**, except for the case of a <<express:geometric_model_schema.revolved_area_solid,revolved_area_solid>> with angle equal to 360 degrees.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.swept_area_solid.swept_area"
the <<express:geometry_schema.curve_bounded_surface,curve_bounded_surface>> defining the area to be swept; the extent of this area is defined by the <<express:geometry_schema.curve_bounded_surface.boundaries,boundaries>> attribute of the referenced <<express:geometry_schema.curve_bounded_surface,curve_bounded_surface>>;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.swept_area_solid.wr:WR1"
The **swept_area** shall be planar. The <<express:geometry_schema.curve_bounded_surface.basis_surface,basis_surface>> attribute of the <<express:geometry_schema.curve_bounded_surface,curve_bounded_surface>> referenced shall be a <<express:geometry_schema.plane,plane>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.extruded_area_solid"
A **extruded_area_solid** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_area_solid,swept_area_solid>> which is a solid defined by sweeping a bounded planar surface. The direction of translation is defined by a <<express:geometry_schema.direction,direction>>, and the length of the translation is defined by a distance **depth**. The planar area may have holes which will sweep into holes in the solid.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.extruded_area_solid.extruded_direction"
the <<express:geometry_schema.direction,direction>> in which the area is to be swept;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.extruded_area_solid.depth"
the distance the area is to be swept;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.extruded_area_solid.wr:WR1"
**extruded_direction** shall not be perpendicular to the normal to the plane of the <<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_area_solid.swept_area,swept_area>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.revolved_area_solid"
A **revolved_area_solid** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_area_solid,swept_area_solid>> which is a solid formed by revolving a planar bounded surface about an axis. The axis shall be in the plane of the surface and the axis shall not intersect the interior of the bounded surface. The bounded surface may have holes which will sweep into holes in the solid. The direction of revolution is clockwise when viewed along the axis in the positive direction. More precisely if stem:[A] is the axis location and stem:[d] is the axis direction and stem:[C] is an arc on the surface of revolution generated by an arbitrary point stem:[p] on the boundary of the <<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_area_solid.swept_area,swept_area>>, then stem:[C] leaves stem:[p] in direction stem:[d xx (p - A)] as the area is revolved.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.revolved_area_solid.axis"
the axis about which revolution will take place;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.revolved_area_solid.angle"
the angle through which the sweep will be made; this angle is measured from the plane of the <<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_area_solid.swept_area,swept_area>>;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.revolved_area_solid.axis_line"
the line of the axis of revolution;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.revolved_area_solid.wr:IP1"
**axis_line** shall lie in plane of <<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_area_solid.swept_area,swept_area>> attribute of the <<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_area_solid,swept_area_solid>> supertype.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.revolved_area_solid.wr:IP2"
The **axis_line** shall not intersect the interior of the <<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_area_solid.swept_area,swept_area>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.revolved_area_solid.wr:IP3"
**angle** shall lie in the range stem:[0 < angle le 360 "P{degree}"].
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.surface_curve_swept_area_solid"
A **surface_curve_swept_area_solid** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_area_solid,swept_area_solid>> which is the result of sweeping a face along a **directrix** lying on a **reference_surface**. The orientation of the <<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_area_solid.swept_area,swept_area>> is related to the direction of the surface normal.

The <<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_area_solid.swept_area,swept_area>> is required to be a <<express:geometry_schema.curve_bounded_surface,curve_bounded_surface>> lying in the plane z = 0 and this is swept along the **directrix** in such a way that the origin of the local coordinate system used to define the <<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_area_solid.swept_area,swept_area>>. is on the **directrix** and the local X axis is in the direction of the normal to the **reference_surface** at the current point. The resulting solid has the property that the cross section of the surface by the normal plane to the **directrix** at any point is a copy of the <<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_area_solid.swept_area,swept_area>>.

The orientation of the <<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_area_solid.swept_area,swept_area>> as it sweeps along the **directrix** is precisely defined by a <<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_transformation_operator_3d,cartesian_transformation_operator_3d>> with attributes:

<<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_transformation_operator.local_origin,local_origin>> as point (0,0,0),

<<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_transformation_operator.axis1,axis1>> as the normal **N** to the **reference_surface** at the point of the **directrix** with parameter stem:[u].

<<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_transformation_operator_3d.axis3,axis3>> as the direction of the tangent vector **t** at the point of the **directrix** with parameter stem:[u].

The remaining attributes are defaulted to define a corresponding transformation matrix **T** ( stem:[u] ), which varies with the **directrix** parameter stem:[u].
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.surface_curve_swept_area_solid.__note"
The geometric shape of the solid is not dependent upon the curve parametrisation; the volume depends upon the area swept and the length of the *directrix*.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.surface_curve_swept_area_solid.directrix"
the curve used to define the sweeping operation; the solid is generated by sweeping the <<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_area_solid.swept_area,swept_area>> along the **directrix** ;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.surface_curve_swept_area_solid.start_param"
the parameter value on the **directrix** at which the sweeping operation commences;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.surface_curve_swept_area_solid.end_param"
the parameter value on the **directrix** at which the sweeping operation ends;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.surface_curve_swept_area_solid.reference_surface"
the surface containing the **directrix** ;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.surface_curve_swept_area_solid.wr:WR1"
If the **directrix** is a <<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve,surface_curve>> then the **reference_surface** shall be in the <<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve.basis_surface,basis_surface>> set for this curve.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.surface_curve_swept_area_solid.wr:IP1"
The <<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_area_solid.swept_area,swept_area>> shall lie in the plane z = 0.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.surface_curve_swept_area_solid.wr:IP2"
The **directrix** shall lie on the **reference_surface**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.swept_disk_solid"
A **swept_disk_solid** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_area_solid,swept_area_solid>> which is the solid produced by sweeping a circular disk along a three dimensional curve. During the sweeping operation the normal to the plane of the circular disk is in the direction of the tangent to the **directrix** curve and the centre of the disk lies on the **directrix**. The circular disk may, optionally, have a central hole, in this case the resulting solid has a through hole, or, an internal void when the directrix forms a close curve.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.swept_disk_solid.__example"
A solid in the form of a toroidal shell of major radius stem:[R_1], minor radius stem:[R_2] and shell thickness stem:[t] could be defined as an instance of *swept_disk_solid* with the following attributes:



directrix:: a circle in 3D space of radius R_{1},


radius:: R_{2},


inner_radius:: R_{2}- t,

[stem]
++++
"start_param": 0,
++++



[stem]
++++
"end_param": 360 degrees.
++++
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.swept_disk_solid.directrix"
the curve used to define the sweeping operation. The solid is generated by sweeping a circular disk along the **directrix** ;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.swept_disk_solid.radius"
the radius of the circular disk to be swept along the directrix;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.swept_disk_solid.inner_radius"
an optional attribute, if present it defines the radius of a circular hole in the centre of the disk;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.swept_disk_solid.start_param"
the parameter value on the **directrix** at which the sweeping operation starts;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.swept_disk_solid.end_param"
the parameter value on the **directrix** at which the sweeping operation ends;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.swept_disk_solid.wr:WR1"
The **directrix** shall be a curve in three dimensional space.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.swept_disk_solid.wr:WR1.__note"
A simple solid with no self-intersections will be produced if the *directrix* is an open curve with radius of curvature at all points greater than *radius*.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.swept_disk_solid.wr:WR2"
If **inner_radius** exists then **radius** shall be greater than **inner_radius**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.trimmed_volume"
A **trimmed_volume** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.solid_model,solid_model>> for which the boundaries are the 6 constant parameter surfaces stem:[u = u1], stem:[u = u2], stem:[v = v1], stem:[v = v2], stem:[w = w1], and stem:[w = w2], of the **basis_volume**. In the three dimensional parameter space of the **basis_volume** the domain of the **trimmed_volume** is a cuboid.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.trimmed_volume.__example"
If refcyl is a reference to a <<express:geometry_schema.cylindrical_volume,cylindrical_volume>> then:



trimmed_volume(refcyl, 0.0, 0.5, 0.0, 1,0, 0.0, 1.0) defines a solid half cylinder whose vertical face is defined by the plane  stem:[u = 0],



trimmed_volume(refcyl, 0.875, 0.125, 0.0, 1.0, 0.9, 1.0) defines a quadrant of a cylindrical shell of thickness (0.1 radius 1) centred on  stem:[u = 0] . The trimming values for stem:[u] are from 0.875 to 0.125 (equivalent to 1.125).
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.trimmed_volume.__note"
A *trimmed_volume* for which the *basis_volume* is not closed in any parameter direction will satisfy the additional constraints stem:[u1 < u2, v1 < v2, w1 < w2].
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.trimmed_volume.__note"
If the *basis_volume* is closed in one or more parameter directions and uses circular functions (sine and cosine) in its definition the second value of a parameter may be less than the first value of that parameter. This is interpreted as a periodic definition of a portion of the volume from the second parameter boundary to the first including the `seam' of the parameter value.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.trimmed_volume.basis_volume"
the <<express:geometry_schema.volume,volume>> to be trimmed;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.trimmed_volume.u1"
the first value for the The two trimming values for stem:[u] shall be distinct.parameter;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.trimmed_volume.u2"
the second value for the stem:[u] parameter;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.trimmed_volume.v1"
the first value for the stem:[v] parameter;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.trimmed_volume.v2"
the second value for the stem:[v] parameter;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.trimmed_volume.w1"
the first value for the stem:[w] parameter;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.trimmed_volume.w2"
the second value for the stem:[w] parameter;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.trimmed_volume.wr:WR1"
The two trimming values for The two trimming values for stem:[u] shall be distinct.shall be distinct.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.trimmed_volume.wr:WR2"
The two trimming values for The two trimming values for stem:[v] shall be distinct.shall be distinct.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.trimmed_volume.wr:WR3"
The two trimming values for The two trimming values for stem:[u] shall be distinct.shall be distinct.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.solid_replica"
A **solid_replica** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.solid_model,solid_model>> which is a copy of another solid at a new location.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.solid_replica.parent_solid"
the solid model which is being copied to create the **solid_replica** ;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.solid_replica.transformation"
a <<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_transformation_operator_3d,cartesian_transformation_operator_3d>> which defines the location and orientation of the **solid_replica** and any associated scaling factor;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.solid_replica.wr:WR1"
A **solid_replica** shall not participate in its own definition.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.solid_replica.wr:WR2"
The **parent_solid** shall be of dimension 3.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.shell_based_surface_model"
A **shell_based_surface_model** is a type of <<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_item,geometric_representation_item>> which is described by a set of open or closed shells of dimensionality 2. The shells shall not intersect except at edges and vertices. In particular, distinct faces shall not intersect. A complete face of one shell may be shared with another shell. Coincident portions of shells shall both reference the same faces, edges and vertices defining the coincident region.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.shell_based_surface_model.__note"
A <<express:topology_schema.shell,shell>> may exist independently of a *shell_based_surface_model*.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.shell_based_surface_model.sbsm_boundary"
the set of <<express:topology_schema.shell,shell>> instances which define the **shell_based_surface_model**
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.shell_based_surface_model.wr:WR1"
The <<express:topology_schema.shell,shell>> instances which make up the **shell_based_surface_model** shall be of type <<express:topology_schema.closed_shell,closed_shell>> or <<express:topology_schema.closed_shell,closed_shell>> only.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.shell_based_surface_model.wr:IP1"
The topological dimensionality of the **shell_based_surface_model** is 2.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.shell_based_surface_model.wr:IP2"
The <<express:topology_schema.shell,shell>> instances shall not overlap or intersect except at common <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> instances, <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> instances, or <<express:topology_schema.vertex,vertex>> instances.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.shell_based_surface_model.wr:IP3"
There shall be at least one <<express:topology_schema.shell,shell>> in a **shell_based_surface_model**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.face_based_surface_model"
A **face_based_surface_model** is a type of <<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_item,geometric_representation_item>> which is described by a set of <<express:topology_schema.connected_face_set,connected_face_set>> instances of dimensionality 2. The <<express:topology_schema.connected_face_set,connected_face_set>> instances shall not intersect except at edges and vertices, except that a <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> in one connected face set may overlap a <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> in another connected face set, provided the face boundaries are identical. There shall be at least one <<express:topology_schema.connected_face_set,connected_face_set>>. A <<express:topology_schema.connected_face_set,connected_face_set>> may exist independently of a **face_based_surface_model**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.face_based_surface_model.fbsm_faces"
the set of <<express:topology_schema.connected_face_set,connected_face_set>> instances which define the **face_based_surface_model** ;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.face_based_surface_model.wr:IP1"
The <<express:topology_schema.connected_face_set,connected_face_set>> instances shall not overlap or intersect except at common <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> instances, <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> instances or <<express:topology_schema.vertex,vertex>> instances.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.face_based_surface_model.wr:IP2"
The topological dimensionality of the **fbsm_faces** is 2.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.shell_based_wireframe_model"
A **shell_based_wireframe_model** is a type of <<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_item,geometric_representation_item>> which is described by a graph of edges and vertices embedded in stem:[RR^3]. The graph may be disconnected. Within the graph the edges do not intersect except at their boundaries (i.e., vertices). The geometry associated with a vertex shall be consistent with the geometry associated with any of the edges of which the vertex forms a boundary. A **shell_based_wireframe_model** is represented by one or more <<express:topology_schema.shell,shell>> instances of dimensionality 0 or 1. There shall be at least one <<express:topology_schema.shell,shell>>. A <<express:topology_schema.shell,shell>> may exist independently of a **shell_based_wireframe_model**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.shell_based_wireframe_model.sbwm_boundary"
the set of <<express:topology_schema.vertex_shell,vertex_shell>> instances and/or <<express:topology_schema.wire_shell,wire_shell>> instances which define the **shell_based_wireframe_model** ;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.shell_based_wireframe_model.wr:WR1"
Each <<express:topology_schema.shell,shell>> shall be either of type <<express:topology_schema.vertex_shell,vertex_shell>> or <<express:topology_schema.wire_shell,wire_shell>>. The function <<express:geometric_model_schema.constraints_geometry_shell_based_wireframe_model,constraints_geometry_shell_based_wireframe_model>> returns TRUE, where the function evaluates these geometric constraints and finds them satisfied.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.shell_based_wireframe_model.wr:IP1"
The topological dimensionality of **sbwm_boundary** is less than 2.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.shell_based_wireframe_model.wr:IP2"
The **shell_based_wireframe_model** has positive and finite extent.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.shell_based_wireframe_model.wr:IP3"
The <<express:topology_schema.shell,shell>> instances shall not overlap or intersect except at common <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> instances or <<express:topology_schema.vertex,vertex>> instances.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.edge_based_wireframe_model"
An **edge_based_wireframe_model** is a type of <<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_item,geometric_representation_item>> which is described by a graph of edges and vertices embedded in stem:[RR^3]. The graph may be disconnected. Within the graph the edges do not intersect except at their boundaries (i.e., vertices). The geometry associated with a vertex shall be consistent with the geometry associated with any of the edges of which the vertex forms a boundary. An **edge_based_wireframe_model** is represented by one or more <<express:topology_schema.connected_edge_set,connected_edge_set>> instances of dimensionality 1. There shall be at least one <<express:topology_schema.connected_edge_set,connected_edge_set>>. A <<express:topology_schema.connected_edge_set,connected_edge_set>> may exist independently of an **edge_based_wireframe_model**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.edge_based_wireframe_model.ebwm_boundary"
the set of <<express:topology_schema.connected_edge_set,connected_edge_set>> instances comprising the **edge_based_wireframe_model** ;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.edge_based_wireframe_model.wr:IP1"
The dimensionality of **edge_based_wireframe_model** is 1.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.edge_based_wireframe_model.wr:IP2"
The <<express:topology_schema.connected_edge_set,connected_edge_set>> instances shall not overlap or intersect except at common <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> instances or <<express:topology_schema.vertex,vertex>> instances.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.geometric_set"
A **geometric_set** is a type of <<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_item,geometric_representation_item>> which is intended for the transfer of models when a topological structure is not available.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.geometric_set.elements"
the geometric elements which make up the **geometric_set**, these may be <<express:geometry_schema.point,point>> instances, <<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> instances or <<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> instances; but are required to be of the same coordinate space dimensionality;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.geometric_curve_set"
A **geometric_curve_set** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.geometric_set,geometric_set>> which is a collection of two-dimensional or three-dimensional <<express:geometry_schema.point,point>> instances and <<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> instances.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.geometric_curve_set.wr:WR1"
Only curves and points shall be included in a **geometric_curve_set**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.sectioned_spine"
An **sectioned_spine** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.geometric_curve_set,geometric_curve_set>> which is a representation of the shape of a three dimensional object composed of a spine curve and a number of planar **cross_sections**. The shape is defined between the first element of **cross_sections** and the last element of this set.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.sectioned_spine.__note"
A *sectioned_spine* may be used to represent a surface or a solid but the interpolation of the shape between the cross-sections is not defined. For the representation of a solid all cross-sections are closed curves.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.sectioned_spine.cross_sections"
the set of 2 or more planar cross-sections; each cross-section is defined in its correct location relative to the spine curve;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.sectioned_spine.spine_points"
the set of <<express:geometry_schema.point,point>> instances on the spine, each point lies in the plane of the corresponding cross-section;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.sectioned_spine.wr:WR1"
The <<express:geometric_model_schema.geometric_set.elements,elements>> set shall contain a single item.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.sectioned_spine.wr:WR2"
The <<express:geometric_model_schema.geometric_set.elements,elements>> set shall contain a single item.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.sectioned_spine.wr:WR3"
The set of **cross_sections** and the set of **spine_points** shall be of the same size.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.sectioned_spine.wr:WR4"
The space dimensionality of the **sectioned_spine** shall be 3.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.sectioned_spine.wr:IP1"
Each curve in the **cross_sections** set shall be a planar curve.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.sectioned_spine.wr:IP2"
Each point in the **spine_points** set shall lie in the plane of the corresponding curve from the **cross_sections**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.geometric_set_replica"
An **geometric_set_replica** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.geometric_set,geometric_set>> which defines a replica of a <<express:geometric_model_schema.geometric_set,geometric_set>> in a different location. Each element of the set is transformed by the same **transformation** which may include scaling. The type of set produced will correspond to that of the **parent_set**
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.geometric_set_replica.parent_set"
a <<express:geometric_model_schema.geometric_set,geometric_set>> which is being copied to create the **geometric_set_replica** ;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.geometric_set_replica.transformation"
a Cartesian transformation operator which defines the location and orientation of the **geometric_set_replica** ;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.geometric_set_replica.elements"
the set of elements resulting from the transformation of the **parent_set** ;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.geometric_set_replica.wr:WR1"
A **geometric_set_replica** shall not participate in its own definition.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_shape_representation"
A **tessellated_shape_representation** is a type of <<express:product_property_representation_schema.shape_representation,shape_representation>> in which the geometry is approximately represented by a tessellated model with planar facets.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_shape_representation.wr:WR1"
The context of the **tessellated_shape_representation** shall be a <<express:measure_schema.global_unit_assigned_context,global_unit_assigned_context>>. This ensures that the coordinates used to define the points of the tessellated geometry have defined units.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_shape_representation.wr:WR2"
The **tessellated_shape_representation** shall contain at least 1 <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_item,tessellated_item>> in the <<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> set.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_shape_representation_with_accuracy_parameters"
A **tessellated_shape_representation_with_accuracy_parameters** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_shape_representation,tessellated_shape_representation>> which has additional parameters to define the accuracy of the tessellated approximation to the corresponding exact geometric shape.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_shape_representation_with_accuracy_parameters.tessellation_accuracy_parameters"
the set of parameters defining the accuracy of the <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_shape_representation_with_accuracy_parameters,tessellated_shape_representation_with_accuracy_parameters>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_item"
A **tessellated_item** is a type of <<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_item,geometric_representation_item>> used in the description of a tessellated shape.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_item.wr:WR1"
A **tessellated_item** shall only be used in a <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_shape_representation,tessellated_shape_representation>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.repositioned_tessellated_item"
A **repositioned_tessellated_item** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_item,tessellated_item>> which has been re-postioned by defining the coordinates with respect to a new axis system.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.repositioned_tessellated_item.location"
an <<express:geometry_schema.axis2_placement_3d,axis2_placement_3d>> defining the origin and axis direction for the coordinates of the referenced points in the **repositioned_tessellated_item** ;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.repositioned_tessellated_item.wr:WR1"
A **repositioned_tessellated_item** shall only be used as a complex subtype with one of the following types of <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_item,tessellated_item>>:

<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_curve_set,tessellated_curve_set>>, <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_geometric_set,tessellated_geometric_set>>, <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_point_set,tessellated_point_set>>, <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_surface_set,tessellated_surface_set>>, <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_shell,tessellated_shell>>, <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_solid,tessellated_solid>>, <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_wire,tessellated_wire>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_structured_item"
A **tessellated_structured_item** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.geometric_set,geometric_set>> which has a topological structure. The links to topological components of an exact geometric model are defined with the subtypes.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.coordinates_list"
A **coordinates_list** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_item,tessellated_item>> that defines the coordinate values for points used in a <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_shape_representation,tessellated_shape_representation>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.coordinates_list.npoints"
the number of points with coordinates in the list;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.coordinates_list.position_coords"
the list of real triples defining the coordinates of the points;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.coordinates_list.position_coords.__note"
These real triples have the semantics of <<express:measure_schema.length_measure,length_measure>> instances, but are not formally defined as such, the units for these are defined since a <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_item,tessellated_item>> is required to be used in a <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_shape_representation,tessellated_shape_representation>> having a <<express:measure_schema.global_unit_assigned_context,global_unit_assigned_context>>.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.coordinates_list.wr:WR1"
The value of **npoints** shall be equal to the size of the **position_coords** list.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.coordinates_list.wr:WR2"
This entity shall not be instantiated as a complex subtype with <<express:geometric_model_schema.repositioned_tessellated_item,repositioned_tessellated_item>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.coordinates_list.wr:WR2.__note"
This rule together with the ONEOF rule on the supertype <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_item,tessellated_item>> ensures that it is not instantiated with any subtype of <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_item,tessellated_item>>.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_vertex"
A **tessellated_vertex** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_structured_item,tessellated_structured_item>> and is a single vertex in a tessellated model.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_vertex.coordinates"
the <<express:geometric_model_schema.coordinates_list,coordinates_list>> giving the vertex coordinate values;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_vertex.topological_link"
an optional link to a topological <<express:topology_schema.vertex_point,vertex_point>> entity;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_vertex.point_index"
the location in the **coordinates** list of the coordinates for this vertex;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge"
A **tessellated_edge** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_structured_item,tessellated_structured_item>>. The geometry of the **tessellated_edge** is approximated by straight line segments joining the points listed.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge.__note"
A *tessellated_edge* may be used as the boundary between two <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face,tessellated_face>> instances.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge.coordinates"
the <<express:geometric_model_schema.coordinates_list,coordinates_list>> giving the coordinate values for points of the **tessellated_edge**
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge.geometric_link"
the <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> or <<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> of an exact model to which this **tessellated_edge** corresponds;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge.line_strip"
the list of integers giving the locations in the **coordinates** list of consecutive points of this edge;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_connecting_edge"
A **tessellated_connecting_edge** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge,tessellated_edge>>. The **tessellated_connecting_edge** connects two faces and contains information relating to the face normals at corresponding points on the 2 faces.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_connecting_edge.smooth"
a LOGICAL variable; if TRUE, there is tangent continuity where two faces join along this edge
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_connecting_edge.face1"
the first <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face,tessellated_face>> using this edge;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_connecting_edge.face2"
the second <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face,tessellated_face>> using this edge;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_connecting_edge.line_strip_face1"
the list of integers giving the locations in the normals list of **face1** of the normals on the **face1** side at consecutive points of this edge, and, for connection checking, if required, the locations in the **face1** coordinates list or **face1** pnindex of consecutive points of this edge; in cases where normals are not defined for **face1** the locations in the coordinates list are given;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_connecting_edge.line_strip_face2"
the list of integers giving the locations in the normals list of **face2** of the normals on the **face2** side at consecutive points of this edge, and, for connection checking, if required, the locations in the **face2** coordinates list or **face2** pnindex of consecutive points of this edge; in cases where normals are not defined for **face2** the locations in the coordinates list are given.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_connecting_edge.wr:WR1"
**line_strip_face1** and **line_strip_face2** shall be of the same size.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_connecting_edge.wr:WR2"
**line_strip_face1** shall be of the same size as the inherited <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge.line_strip,line_strip>> attribute.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_connecting_edge.wr:WR3"
**face1** shall not be of type <<express:geometric_model_schema.cubic_bezier_triangulated_face,cubic_bezier_triangulated_face>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_connecting_edge.wr:WR4"
**face2** shall not be of type <<express:geometric_model_schema.cubic_bezier_triangulated_face,cubic_bezier_triangulated_face>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.cubic_bezier_tessellated_edge"
A **cubic_bezier_tessellated_edge** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge,tessellated_edge>> which takes the form of a piecewise cubic bezier curve. The **cubic_bezier_tessellated_edge** has its geometry defined by a list of control points, referenced by the inherited <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge.line_strip,line_strip>> attribute; in this list only the points corresponding to ends of segments lie on the edge and the list of pointers is of length 3n +1, where n is the number of segments.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.cubic_bezier_tessellated_edge.line_strip"
the list of 3n + 1 integers, where n is the number of cubic segments, giving the locations in the <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge.coordinates,coordinates>> list of consecutive control points points of this edge.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.cubic_tessellated_connecting_edge"
A **cubic_tessellated_connecting_edge** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.cubic_bezier_tessellated_edge,cubic_bezier_tessellated_edge>> which takes the form of a cubic curve and connects two <<express:geometric_model_schema.cubic_bezier_triangulated_face,cubic_bezier_triangulated_face>> instances. The **cubic_tessellated_connecting_edge** has its geometry defined by a list of control points contained in the inherited <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge.line_strip,line_strip>> attribute; in this list only the points corresponding to vertices of the cubic triangles of the adjacent faces lie on the edge and the list of pointers is of length 3n +1, where n is the number of triangles with adjacent edges on each side of the connecting edge.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.cubic_tessellated_connecting_edge.smooth"
a LOGICAL variable; if TRUE, there is tangent continuity where two faces join along this edge;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.cubic_tessellated_connecting_edge.face1"
the <<express:geometric_model_schema.cubic_bezier_triangulated_face,cubic_bezier_triangulated_face>> to the left of this edge;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.cubic_tessellated_connecting_edge.face2"
the <<express:geometric_model_schema.cubic_bezier_triangulated_face,cubic_bezier_triangulated_face>> to the right of this edge.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face"
A **tessellated_face** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_structured_item,tessellated_structured_item>> that represents a face of a tessellated model.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face.coordinates"
the <<express:geometric_model_schema.coordinates_list,coordinates_list>> giving the coordinate values for points of the **tessellated_face**
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face.pnmax"
the larger of the number of points defined with the face or the number of unique point and normal combinations in the face;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face.normals"
the list of REAL triples defining the normals at the points of the face. If the size of this list is greater than one the ordering of the normals is the same as the ordering used for the points via <<express:geometric_model_schema.triangulated_face.pnindex,pnindex>> in one of the subtypes.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face.geometric_link"
the <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> or <<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> of an exact model to which this **tessellated_face** corresponds;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face.wr:WR1"
The size of **normals** shall be 0, 1 or equal to **pnmax**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face.wr:WR1.__note"
If size = 0 normals are undefined at all face points, if size = 1 the normal has the same value at each face point and the underlying surface is planar, if size is greater than 1 each point on the face has an individual underlying surface normal defined.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.triangulated_face"
A **triangulated_face** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face,tessellated_face>> that has its geometry defined by a set of triangles.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.triangulated_face.__figure"
[[figure-geometric_model_schema-GMfig28]]
.Use of pnindex to locate coordinates
====
image::GMfig28.gif[]
====
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.triangulated_face.pnindex"
the list of integers defining the locations in the <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face.coordinates,coordinates>> list of the points and normals of the triangles of the face
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.triangulated_face.triangles"
the list of INTEGER triples, in the range 1 to pnmax, giving the locations of the coordinate values in the <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face.coordinates,coordinates>> list or in **pnindex** for each triangle. The stem:[i] th triple in the list defines the orders in the appropriate list of the 3 vertices of the stem:[i] th triangle;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.triangulated_face.triangles.__note"
See <<figure-geometric_model_schema-GMfig28>> for further details of use of pnindex.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.triangulated_face.triangles.__note"
In the simplest case where no point is associated with more than 1 normal and the size of <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face.coordinates,coordinates>> is <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face.pnmax,pnmax>> the triangles refer directly to the <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face.coordinates,coordinates>> list and *pnindex* is empty. In all other cases *pnindex* is required to identify points and normals for the triangles.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.triangulated_face.triangles.__note"
In the the simple case where each vertex point is defined with a unique normal this entity is equivalent to a set of curved triangles with normals at the vertices as defined in the AMF standard [4]
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.triangulated_face.wr:WR1"
The size of **pnindex**, if non-zero, shall be equal to <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face.pnmax,pnmax>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.triangulated_face.wr:WR2"
**pnindex** shall not be empty unless <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face.pnmax,pnmax>> is equal to the size of the <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face.coordinates,coordinates>> list.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.triangulated_face.wr:WR2.__note"
This option can only be used in the simple case of a local <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face.coordinates,coordinates>> list and 0 or 1 normals per point.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.complex_triangulated_face"
A **complex_triangulated_face** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face,tessellated_face>> defining the geometry as a set of triangles arranged in strips and fans.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.complex_triangulated_face.__figure"
[[figure-geometric_model_schema-GMfig29]]
.Ordering of points for complex_triangulated_face
====
image::GMfig29.gif[]
====
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.complex_triangulated_face.__note"
The ordering of the points used to define the strips or fans of triangles is shown in <<figure-geometric_model_schema-GMfig29>>.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.complex_triangulated_face.pnindex"
the list of integers defining the locations in the <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face.coordinates,coordinates>> list of the points and normals of the triangles of the face
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.complex_triangulated_face.triangle_strips"
the list of lists of INTEGERs giving the locations of the coordinate values in the <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face.coordinates,coordinates>> list for each strip of triangles. Each sublist defines the orders in the <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face.coordinates,coordinates>> list, via the **pnindex** if used, of the vertices of the stem:[i] th strip of triangles.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.complex_triangulated_face.triangle_strips.__note"
If required a single triangle can be included in this structure as a strip of one triangle, in which case the sublist will contain 3 INTEGERs.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.complex_triangulated_face.triangle_fans"
the list of lists of INTEGERs giving the locations of the coordinate values in the <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face.coordinates,coordinates>> list for each fan of triangles. Each sublist defines the orders in the <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face.coordinates,coordinates>> list of the vertices of the stem:[i] th fan of triangles.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.complex_triangulated_face.triangle_fans.__note"
In the simplest case where no point is associated with more than 1 normal and the size of <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face.coordinates,coordinates>> is <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face.pnmax,pnmax>> the triangles defined by the strips and fans refer directly to the <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face.coordinates,coordinates>> list and *pnindex* is empty. In all other cases *pnindex* is required to identify points and normals for the triangles.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.complex_triangulated_face.wr:WR1"
The size of **pnindex**, if non-zero, shall be equal to <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face.pnmax,pnmax>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.complex_triangulated_face.wr:WR2"
**pnindex** shall not be empty unless <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face.pnmax,pnmax>> is equal to the size of the <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face.coordinates,coordinates>> list.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.complex_triangulated_face.wr:WR2.__note"
This option can only be used in the simple case of a local <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face.coordinates,coordinates>> list and 0 or 1 normals per point.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.complex_triangulated_face.wr:WR3"
The **triangle_strips** list and the **triangle_fans** list shall not both be empty.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.cubic_bezier_triangulated_face"
A **cubic_bezier_triangulated_face** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face,tessellated_face>> that has its geometry defined by a set of curved triangles. Each of the triangles is a 3 sided Bezier cubic surface defined by a list of 10 control points, 9 near the edges and one above the centre. The control points stem:[bbP_1], stem:[bb(P_2)], stem:[bb(P_3)], are at the vertices of the triangle. Each triangle is a bi-parametric surface with equation:

[stem]
++++
s (u,v) = (1 - u -v) ^{3} P_{1} + u ^{3} P_{2} + v ^{3} P_{3} + 3(1 - u -v) ^{2} u P_{4} + 3(1 - u -v)u ^{2} P_{5} + 3u ^{2} v P_{6} + 3uv ^{2} P_{7} + 3(1 - u -v)v ^{2} P_{8} + 3(1 - u -v) ^{2} v P_{9} + 6uv(1 - u -v) P_{10}
++++

The parametric range for each triangle is stem:[0 le u le 1; 0 le v le 1]; with stem:[u+v le 1]._

// <p>

// At each vertex the tangent along the edge of the triangle is in the

// direction of the next conrol point along this edge and has a

// magnnitude equal to 3 times this distance. At vertex

// <b>

// P

// <sub>1</sub>

// </b>

// the tangent vector along the edge

// <it> u = 0 </it>

// is

// <b> t </b>

// = 3(

// <b>

// P

// <sub>4</sub>

// </b>

// -

// <b>

// P

// <sub>1</sub>

// </b>

// ), other tangent vectors are defined in a similar way.

// </p>

Continuity of geometry between adjacent triangles is assured provided the adjacent edges reference the same 4 control points. Each edge of the triangle is a Bezier cubic curve of parametric length 1 defined by the 4 control points along that edge. stem:[bb(P_1)], stem:[bb(P_4)], stem:[bb(P_5)], stem:[bb(P_2)] define the cubic curve of the first edge of the triangle, other edges are defined in a similar manner.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.cubic_bezier_triangulated_face.__figure"
[[figure-geometric_model_schema-beziertri]]
.Relationship between control points and triangular surface
====
image::beziertri.gif[]
====
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.cubic_bezier_triangulated_face.__note"
See <<figure-geometric_model_schema-beziertri>> for illustration of the numbering of the control points.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.cubic_bezier_triangulated_face.ctriangles"
the list of list of 10 INTEGER pointers, giving the locations of the coordinate values of the control points for each triangle in the <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face.coordinates,coordinates>> list.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.cubic_bezier_triangulated_face.ctriangles.__note"
The control points for each triangle are ordered as shown in <<figure-geometric_model_schema-beziertri>>
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.cubic_bezier_triangulated_face.wr:WR1"
The size of <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face.normals,normals>> list. shall be zero, the geometry of each triangle is completely defined by the control points.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_solid"
A **tessellated_solid** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_item,tessellated_item>> that is a tessellated representation of a solid model. Its geometry is defined as a set of <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_structured_item,tessellated_structured_item>> instances.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_solid.__note"
The <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_structured_item,tessellated_structured_item>> instances defining the geometry may be relocated in a local coordinate system by defining a complex instance of this entity with a <<express:geometric_model_schema.repositioned_tessellated_item,repositioned_tessellated_item>>.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_solid.items"
the set of <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_structured_item,tessellated_structured_item>> instances defining the faces of the solid;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_solid.geometric_link"
a corresponding exact model of the solid;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_shell"
A **tessellated_shell** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_item,tessellated_item>> that is a tessellated representation of a shell. Its geometry is defined as a set of <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_structured_item,tessellated_structured_item>> instances.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_shell.__note"
The <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_structured_item,tessellated_structured_item>> instances defining the geometry may be relocated in a local coordinate system by defining a complex instance of this entity with a <<express:geometric_model_schema.repositioned_tessellated_item,repositioned_tessellated_item>>.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_shell.items"
the set of <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_structured_item,tessellated_structured_item>> instances defining the faces of the shell;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_shell.topological_link"
a <<express:topology_schema.connected_face_set,connected_face_set>> representing the exact geometry of the shell;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_wire"
A **tessellated_wire** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_item,tessellated_item>> that is a tessellated representation of a collection of bounded curves joined end to end. Its geometry is defined as a set of tessellated edges and vertices.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_wire.__note"
The edges and vertices defining the geometry may be relocated in a local coordinate system by defining a complex instance of this entity with a <<express:geometric_model_schema.repositioned_tessellated_item,repositioned_tessellated_item>>.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_wire.items"
the set of <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge_or_vertex,tessellated_edge_or_vertex>> instances defining the geometry of the wire;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_wire.geometric_model_link"
the corresponding exact geometry which may be a <<express:topology_schema.path,path>> or <<express:geometry_schema.composite_curve,composite_curve>>;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_surface_set"
A **tessellated_surface_set** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_item,tessellated_item>> that is a tessellated representation of a collection of surfaces.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_surface_set.__note"
If the surfaces are triangulated the geometry of the surfaces is fully defined by creating an instance of one of the subtypes.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_surface_set.coordinates"
the <<express:geometric_model_schema.coordinates_list,coordinates_list>> for the vertices of the triangles;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_surface_set.pnmax"
the larger of the number of points defined with the triangles or the number of unique point and normal combinations in the set of triangles;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_surface_set.pnmax.__note"
In the case of a *tessellated_surface_set* with a discontinuous boundary between faces it is possible to have more than one normal defined at a point on the boundary.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_surface_set.normals"
the list of REAL triples defining the normals at the vertices of the triangles. If the size of this list is greater than one the ordering of the normals is the same as the ordering used for the <<express:geometric_model_schema.triangulated_surface_set.pnindex,pnindex>>;
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_surface_set.wr:WR1"
The size of **normals** shall be 0, 1 or equal to **pnmax**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_surface_set.wr:WR1.__note"
If size = 0 normals are undefined at all vertices, if size = 1 the normal has the same value at each vertex and the underlying surface is planar, if size is greater than 1 each triangle vertex has an individual underlying surface normal defined.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.triangulated_surface_set"
A **triangulated_surface_set** is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_surface_set,tessellated_surface_set>> defining the geometry of the surface set as a set of triangles. The individual triangles are defined by listing the coordinates of their vertices. Normals to the surfaces defined by the set of triangles may be included.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.triangulated_surface_set.pnindex"
