(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_surface_shape_representation"
A **manifold_surface_shape_representation** is a type of
// shape_representation
<<express:product_property_representation_schema.shape_representation,shape_representation>> that describes the shape or portions of the shape of a product using 2-manifolds with boundaries.

// REVIEW_ITEM

// This item is deferred to TCSC410303-227:

// Geometric Model Schema Reorganization

// REVIEW_ITEM

// THIS IS THE MISSING PARAGRAPH INFORMATION

// NOTE 2 - Entity product is not included in this document.

//

// A manifold_surface_shape_representation is a shape_representation as defined in ISO 10303-41 that

// consists of one or many shell_based_surface_models. Each shell_based_surface_model is built up of

// open_shells and closed_shells which are sets of faces. Connected_face_set, which is the supertype

// of open_shell and closed_shell, shall not be instantiated. Faces use edges and vertexs; all of these

// shall reference geometric entities such as points, curves, and surfaces. The link between topology and

// geometry may be established by either using face_surface or advanced_face as defined in ISO 10303-

// 511. The two options differ both in the selection of valid point, curve, and surface subtypes and in

// constraints on references to underlying geometry.

//

// NOTE 3 - The representation of face_surfaces as advanced_faces is recommended for manifold surface

// models that are intended to be used together with boundary representation solid models; the integration of

// such a manifold surface model into, for example, an advanced boundary representation model, which is

// defined in ISO 10303-514, will be easier.

All geometric entities shall be of dimensionality three except for two-dimensional geometry that is used for the purpose of defining
// pcurve
<<express:geometry_schema.pcurve,pcurve>> instances. The use of one-dimensional
// cartesian_point
<<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_point,cartesian_point>> instances is excluded.

All unbounded geometry shall be trimmed by using topological constructs.

The
// item
<<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> of a **manifold_surface_shape_representation** may also be of type
// mapped_item
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>>, or
// axis2_placement_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.axis2_placement_3d,axis2_placement_3d>>. These are used to assemble one or several **manifold_surface_shape_representation** instances into one other **manifold_surface_shape_representation**.

In WR5 and WR9, these functions validate the
// curves
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> instances and
// surface
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> instances of all
// edge
<<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> instances and
// faces
<<express:topology_schema.face,face>> instances that are in the scope of a **manifold_surface_shape_representation** except for those that are in the reference tree of an
// advanced_face
<<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>>; the geometry of an
// advanced_face
<<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>> is validated by a different set of rules. The functions automatically assess all underlying geometry; for this they are called recursively.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_surface_shape_representation.__example"
A
// pcurve
<<express:geometry_schema.pcurve,pcurve>> may reference both a
// curve
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> and a
// surface
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>>. Function
// msf_curve_check
<<express:geometric_model_schema.msf_curve_check,msf_curve_check>> validates not only the
// pcurve
<<express:geometry_schema.pcurve,pcurve>>, but also this underlying geometry. It will, therefore, not only call itself, but also
// msf_surface_check
<<express:geometric_model_schema.msf_surface_check,msf_surface_check>>.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_surface_shape_representation.__note"
2-manifolds are topologically constrained in a way that makes them suitable for inclusion into solid representations. Within a 2-manifold, for example, only a maximum of two
// faces
<<express:topology_schema.face,face>> instances may share the same
// edge
<<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>>.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_surface_shape_representation.__note"
The representation of
// face_surface
<<express:topology_schema.face_surface,face_surface>> instances as
// advanced_faces
<<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>> instances is recommended for manifold surface models that are intended to be used together with boundary representation solid models; the integration of such a manifold surface model into, for example, an advanced boundary representation model, will be easier.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_surface_shape_representation.__note"
This document does not include a function for the validation of
// points
<<express:geometry_schema.point,point>> instances and their underlying
// curves
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> instances and
// surfaces
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> instances. This is because all
// curves
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> instances and
// surfaces
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> instances of a *manifold_surface_shape_representation* are referenced from
// edges
<<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> instances and
// faces
<<express:topology_schema.face,face>> instances and are, thus, covered by the two existing functions already.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_surface_shape_representation.items"
one or more of:
// shell_based_surface_models
<<express:geometric_model_schema.shell_based_surface_model,shell_based_surface_model>> instances,
// mapped_item
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>> instances, or
// axis2_placement_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.axis2_placement_3d,axis2_placement_3d>> instances.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_surface_shape_representation.items.__note"
// axis2_placement_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.axis2_placement_3d,axis2_placement_3d>> is a valid
// mapped_item.mapping_target
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item.mapping_target,mapping_target>>. To include another
// representation
<<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> into the list of
// representation.items
<<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> of a *manifold_surface_shape_representation* (see WR3 for valid
// mapped_item
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>> instances), the
// mapped_representation
<<express:representation_schema.representation_map.mapped_representation,mapped_representation>>
// geometric_representation_item
<<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_item,geometric_representation_item>> may be any entity that is geometrically founded in the
// geometric_representation_context
<<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_context,geometric_representation_context>> of the
// mapped_representation
<<express:representation_schema.representation_map.mapped_representation,mapped_representation>>.



If this entity is an
// axis2_placement_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.axis2_placement_3d,axis2_placement_3d>>, the operator that maps the
// mapped_representation
<<express:representation_schema.representation_map.mapped_representation,mapped_representation>> into the *manifold_surface_shape_representation* corresponds to a transformation matrix with only translation and rotation enabled. If a
// cartesian_transformation_operator_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_transformation_operator_3d,cartesian_transformation_operator_3d>> is used as
// mapped_item.mapping_source.mapping_origin
<<express:representation_schema.representation_map.mapping_origin,mapping_origin>>, scaling and mirroring are possible.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:WR1"
At least one of the
// representation.items
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_surface_shape_representation.items,items>> in a **manifold_surface_shape_representation** shall be either a
// shell_based_surface_model
<<express:geometric_model_schema.shell_based_surface_model,shell_based_surface_model>> or a
// mapped_item
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:WR2"
If there is a
// mapped_item
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>> in a **manifold_surface_shape_representation**, the
// mapped_representation
<<express:representation_schema.representation_map.mapped_representation,mapped_representation>> of its
// mapping_source
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item.mapping_source,mapping_source>> shall also be a **manifold_surface_shape_representation**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:WR3"
The boundary of a
// shell_based_surface_model
<<express:geometric_model_schema.shell_based_surface_model,shell_based_surface_model>>, that is its attribute
// sbsm_boundary
<<express:geometric_model_schema.shell_based_surface_model.sbsm_boundary,sbsm_boundary>>, shall be defined by using only
// open_shells
<<express:topology_schema.open_shell,open_shell>> instances,
// closed_shells
<<express:topology_schema.closed_shell,closed_shell>> instances, or
// oriented_closed_shells
<<express:topology_schema.oriented_closed_shell,oriented_closed_shell>> instances;
// oriented_open_shells
<<express:topology_schema.oriented_open_shell,oriented_open_shell>> instances are not valid.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:WR4"
A
// face
<<express:topology_schema.face,face>> shall be instantiated as a
// face_surface
<<express:topology_schema.face_surface,face_surface>>, this may include the
// advanced_face
<<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>> subtype. An
// oriented_face
<<express:topology_schema.oriented_face,oriented_face>> is not a valid instantiation of a
// face
<<express:topology_schema.face,face>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:WR5"
All basis geometry that is referenced by
// surfaces
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> instances shall be either within the reference tree of an
// advanced_face
<<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>> or shall be valid
// curves
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> instances and
// surfaces
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> instances.

The
// basis_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve.basis_surface,basis_surface>> of an
// offset_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_surface,offset_surface>> shall be either an
// elementary_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.elementary_surface,elementary_surface>>,
// b_spline_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_surface,b_spline_surface>>,
// offset_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_surface,offset_surface>>,
// swept_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.swept_surface,swept_surface>>, or
// surface_replica
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_replica,surface_replica>>.

The
// parent_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_replica.parent_surface,parent_surface>> of a
// surface_replica
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_replica,surface_replica>> shall be either an
// elementary_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.elementary_surface,elementary_surface>>,
// b_spline_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_surface,b_spline_surface>>,
// offset_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_surface,offset_surface>>,
// swept_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.swept_surface,swept_surface>>, or
// surface_replica
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_replica,surface_replica>>.

The
// swept_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.swept_surface.swept_curve,swept_curve>> of a
// swept_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.swept_surface,swept_surface>> shall be either a
// line
<<express:geometry_schema.line,line>>,
// conic
<<express:geometry_schema.conic,conic>>,
// pcurve
<<express:geometry_schema.pcurve,pcurve>>,
// surface_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve,surface_curve>>,
// offset_curve_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_curve_3d,offset_curve_3d>>,
// b_spline_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_curve,b_spline_curve>>,
// polyline
<<express:geometry_schema.polyline,polyline>>, or
// curve_replica
<<express:geometry_schema.curve_replica,curve_replica>>.

The attribute
// self_intersect
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_surface.self_intersect,self_intersect>> for
// b_spline_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_surface,b_spline_surface>> instances and
// self_intersect
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_surface.self_intersect,self_intersect>> for
// offset_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_surface,offset_surface>> instances shall be set to FALSE or UNKNOWN.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:WR5.__note"
A
// surface
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> is validated against these constraints by the function
// msf_surface_check
<<express:geometric_model_schema.msf_surface_check,msf_surface_check>>.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:WR6"
The
// bound
<<express:topology_schema.face_bound.bound,bound>> of a
// face_bound
<<express:topology_schema.face_bound,face_bound>>, which is referenced from a
// face
<<express:topology_schema.face,face>>, shall be either within the reference tree of an
// advanced_face
<<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>> or shall be an
// edge_loop
<<express:topology_schema.edge_loop,edge_loop>> or a
// vertex_loop
<<express:topology_schema.vertex_loop,vertex_loop>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:WR7"
The geometry of a bounding
// edge
<<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>>, that is the
// edge_element
<<express:topology_schema.oriented_edge.edge_element,edge_element>> of an
// oriented_edge
<<express:topology_schema.oriented_edge,oriented_edge>>, shall be either within the reference tree of an
// advanced_face
<<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>> or shall be an
// edge_curve
<<express:topology_schema.edge_curve,edge_curve>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:WR8"
The
// curve
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> used to define the geometry of an
// edge
<<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>>, that is the
// edge_geometry
<<express:topology_schema.edge_curve.edge_geometry,edge_geometry>> of an
// edge_curve
<<express:topology_schema.edge_curve,edge_curve>> of an
// edge
<<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>>, shall be either a
// b_spline_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_curve,b_spline_curve>>, a
// conic
<<express:geometry_schema.conic,conic>>, a
// curve_replica
<<express:geometry_schema.curve_replica,curve_replica>>, a
// line
<<express:geometry_schema.line,line>>, an
// offset_curve_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_curve_3d,offset_curve_3d>>, a
// pcurve
<<express:geometry_schema.pcurve,pcurve>>, a
// polyline
<<express:geometry_schema.polyline,polyline>>, a
// surface_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve,surface_curve>>, or a
// curve
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> in the reference tree of an
// advanced_face
<<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>>.
*)


