(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:WR10"
The
// edge.edge_start
<<express:topology_schema.edge.edge_start,edge_start>> and
// edge.edge_end
<<express:topology_schema.edge.edge_end,edge_end>> of an
// edge
<<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> shall be either within the reference tree of an
// advanced_face
<<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>> or shall be
// vertex_points
<<express:topology_schema.vertex_point,vertex_point>> instances.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:WR11"
The
// vertex_geometry
<<express:topology_schema.vertex_point.vertex_geometry,vertex_geometry>> of a
// vertex
<<express:topology_schema.vertex,vertex>> that is part of an
// edge_loop
<<express:topology_schema.edge_loop,edge_loop>> shall be either within the reference tree of an
// advanced_face
<<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>> or shall be a
// cartesian_point
<<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_point,cartesian_point>>,
// point_on_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.point_on_curve,point_on_curve>>,
// point_on_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.point_on_surface,point_on_surface>>, or
// degenerate_pcurve
<<express:geometry_schema.degenerate_pcurve,degenerate_pcurve>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:WR12"
The
// vertex_loop.loop_vertex
<<express:topology_schema.vertex_loop.loop_vertex,loop_vertex>> of a
// vertex_loop
<<express:topology_schema.vertex_loop,vertex_loop>> shall be either within the reference tree of an
// advanced_face
<<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>> or shall be a
// vertex_points
<<express:topology_schema.vertex_point,vertex_point>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:WR13"
The
// vertex_geometry
<<express:topology_schema.vertex_point.vertex_geometry,vertex_geometry>> of a
// vertex
<<express:topology_schema.vertex,vertex>> that is part of a
// vertex_loop
<<express:topology_schema.vertex_loop,vertex_loop>> shall be either within the reference tree of an
// advanced_face
<<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>> or shall be a
// cartesian_point
<<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_point,cartesian_point>>,
// point_on_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.point_on_curve,point_on_curve>>,
// point_on_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.point_on_surface,point_on_surface>>, or
// degenerate_pcurve
<<express:geometry_schema.degenerate_pcurve,degenerate_pcurve>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:IP1"
The portion of a
// b_spline_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_curve,b_spline_curve>> that is within the topological domain of a **manifold_surface_shape_representation** shall not self-intersect.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:IP2"
The portion of a
// b_spline_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_surface,b_spline_surface>> that is within the topological domain of a **manifold_surface_shape_representation** shall not self-intersect.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:IP3"
The portion of a
// offset_curve_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_curve_3d,offset_curve_3d>> that is within the topological domain of a **manifold_surface_shape_representation** shall not self-intersect.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:IP4"
The portion of a
// offset_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_surface,offset_surface>> that is within the topological domain of a **manifold_surface_shape_representation** shall not self-intersect.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:IP5"
If a
// face
<<express:topology_schema.face,face>> has only one connected outer bound, the corresponding
// loop
<<express:topology_schema.loop,loop>> shall be represented as
// face_outer_bound
<<express:topology_schema.face_outer_bound,face_outer_bound>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:IP6"
If the outer bound is not connected,
// face_outer_bound
<<express:topology_schema.face_outer_bound,face_outer_bound>> shall not be used.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.msf_curve_check"
The **msf_curve_check** function checks a
// curve
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> instance for validity in the context of a
// manifold_surface_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_surface_shape_representation,manifold_surface_shape_representation>>. Each geometric instance that is referenced by that
// curve
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> instance is also validated.

Where appropriate an instance is investigated recursively. This means if a
// curve
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> references another
// curve
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> as a basis curve or parent curve, the **msf_curve_check** function is called again. If a
// surface
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>>
// express_ref linkend
is referenced, the
// msf_surface_check
<<express:geometric_model_schema.msf_surface_check,msf_surface_check>> function is called. The recursive process terminates at entity types that do not reference any
// curves
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> instances or
// surfaces
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> instances.

The following curve types and their subtypes are within the scope of the
// manifold_surface_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_surface_shape_representation,manifold_surface_shape_representation>> and are, thus, valid input to this function:

*
// b_spline_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_curve,b_spline_curve>>;
*
// conic
<<express:geometry_schema.conic,conic>>;
*
// curve_replica
<<express:geometry_schema.curve_replica,curve_replica>>;
*
// line
<<express:geometry_schema.line,line>>;
*
// offset_curve_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_curve_3d,offset_curve_3d>>;
*
// pcurve
<<express:geometry_schema.pcurve,pcurve>>;
*
// polyline
<<express:geometry_schema.polyline,polyline>>;
*
// surface_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve,surface_curve>>.

Four of these
// curve
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> types reference basis or parent
// curves
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> instances. The lists below indicate the valid references.

The
// parent_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.curve_replica.parent_curve,parent_curve>> of a
// curve_replica
<<express:geometry_schema.curve_replica,curve_replica>> and the
// basis_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_curve_3d.basis_curve,basis_curve>> of an
// offset_curve_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_curve_3d,offset_curve_3d>> shall be of one of the following types:

*
// b_spline_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_curve,b_spline_curve>>;
*
// conic
<<express:geometry_schema.conic,conic>>;
*
// curve_replica
<<express:geometry_schema.curve_replica,curve_replica>> (recursive);
*
// line
<<express:geometry_schema.line,line>>;
*
// offset_curve_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_curve_3d,offset_curve_3d>> (recursive);
*
// pcurve
<<express:geometry_schema.pcurve,pcurve>> (recursive);
*
// polyline
<<express:geometry_schema.polyline,polyline>>;
*
// surface_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve,surface_curve>> (recursive).

The one instance in the set of
// items
<<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> attribute (inherited from
// representation
<<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>>) of a
// definitional_representation
<<express:representation_schema.definitional_representation,definitional_representation>> where that
// definitional_representation
<<express:representation_schema.definitional_representation,definitional_representation>> is referenced as
// reference_to_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.pcurve.reference_to_curve,reference_to_curve>> by a
// pcurve
<<express:geometry_schema.pcurve,pcurve>> shall be one of the following types:

*
// b_spline_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_curve,b_spline_curve>>;
*
// conic
<<express:geometry_schema.conic,conic>>;
*
// curve_replica
<<express:geometry_schema.curve_replica,curve_replica>> (recursive);
*
// line
<<express:geometry_schema.line,line>>;
*
// polyline
<<express:geometry_schema.polyline,polyline>>.

The
// curve_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve.curve_3d,curve_3d>> of a
// surface_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve,surface_curve>> shall be of one of the following types:

*
// b_spline_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_curve,b_spline_curve>>;
*
// conic
<<express:geometry_schema.conic,conic>>;
*
// curve_replica
<<express:geometry_schema.curve_replica,curve_replica>> (recursive);
*
// line
<<express:geometry_schema.line,line>>;
*
// offset_curve_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_curve_3d,offset_curve_3d>> (recursive);
*
// polyline
<<express:geometry_schema.polyline,polyline>>;
*
// surface_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve,surface_curve>> (recursive).

Each
// pcurve
<<express:geometry_schema.pcurve,pcurve>> instance and
// surface_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve,surface_curve>> instance reference
// surface
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> instances. Function
// msf_surface_check
<<express:geometric_model_schema.msf_surface_check,msf_surface_check>> is called for validation of these
// surfaces
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> instances.

A valid
// polyline
<<express:geometry_schema.polyline,polyline>> shall consist of at least three
// cartesian_point
<<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_point,cartesian_point>> instances.

The attributes
// self_intersect
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_surface.self_intersect,self_intersect>> for
// b_spline_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_surface,b_spline_surface>> instances and
// offset_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_surface.self_intersect,self_intersect>> for
// offset_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_surface,offset_surface>> instances shall be set to FALSE or UNKNOWN.

This function returns TRUE, if the types of all referenced geometries are within the scope of the
// manifold_surface_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_surface_shape_representation,manifold_surface_shape_representation>>. and if all constraints are fulfilled, otherwise the function returns FALSE.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.msf_curve_check.__example"
One of the constraints that is validated by this function is whether the self-intersection flag of a
// b_spline_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_curve,b_spline_curve>> instance is set to TRUE, FALSE, or UNKNOWN; only FALSE and UNKNOWN are valid.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.msf_curve_check.__note"
This function applies to those entity types that are marked in the lists below a recursive process to check their entity references for valid instantiations.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.msf_curve_check.cv"
(input) a
// representation_item
<<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> that is supposed to be a
// curve
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> that is checked for being valid in the context of a <<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_surface_shape_representation,manifold_surface_shape_representation>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.msf_surface_check"
The **msf_surface_check** function checks a
// surface
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> instance for validity in the context of a
// manifold_surface_shape_representation?
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_surface_shape_representation,manifold_surface_shape_representation>> Each geometric instance that is referenced by that
// surface
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> instance is also validated.

Where appropriate an instance is investigated recursively. This means if a
// surface
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> references another <<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> as a basis surface or parent surface the **msf_surface_check** function is called again. If a
// curve
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> is referenced, the
// msf_curve_check
<<express:geometric_model_schema.msf_curve_check,msf_curve_check>> function is called. The recursive process terminates at entity types that do not reference any
// curve
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> instances or
// surfaces
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> instances.

The following surface types and their subtypes are within the scope of the
// manifold_surface_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_surface_shape_representation,manifold_surface_shape_representation>> and are, thus, valid input to this function:

*
// b_spline_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_surface,b_spline_surface>>;
*
// elementary_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.elementary_surface,elementary_surface>>;
*
// offset_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_surface,offset_surface>>;
*
// surface_replica
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_replica,surface_replica>>;
*
// swept_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.swept_surface,swept_surface>>.

Two of these
// surface
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> types reference basis or parent
// surfaces
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> instances. The
// parent_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_replica.parent_surface,parent_surface>> of a
// surface_replica
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_replica,surface_replica>> and the
// basis_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_surface.basis_surface,basis_surface>> of an
// offset_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_surface,offset_surface>> shall both be one of the following types:

*
// b_spline_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_surface,b_spline_surface>>;
*
// elementary_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.elementary_surface,elementary_surface>>;
*
// offset_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_surface,offset_surface>> (recursive);
*
// surface_replica
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_replica,surface_replica>> (recursive);
*
// swept_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.swept_surface,swept_surface>>.

Each
// swept_surfaces
<<express:geometry_schema.swept_surface,swept_surface>> references
// curve
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> instances. Function
// msf_curve_check
<<express:geometric_model_schema.msf_curve_check,msf_curve_check>> is called for validation of these
// curves
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> instances. All
// curves
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> instances that are in the scope of a
// manifold_surface_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_surface_shape_representation,manifold_surface_shape_representation>> are valid as
// swept_surface.swept_curves
<<express:geometry_schema.swept_surface.swept_curve,swept_curve>> instances.

The attributes
// self_intersect
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_surface.self_intersect,self_intersect>> for
// b_spline_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_surface,b_spline_surface>> instances and
// offset_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_surface.self_intersect,self_intersect>> for
// offset_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_surface,offset_surface>> instances shall be set to FALSE or UNKNOWN.

This function returns TRUE, if the types of all referenced geometries are within the scope of the
// manifold_surface_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_surface_shape_representation,manifold_surface_shape_representation>> and if all constraints are fulfilled, otherwise the function returns FALSE.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.msf_surface_check.__example"
One of the constraints that is validated by this function is whether the self-intersection flag of a
// b_spline_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_surface,b_spline_surface>> instance is set to TRUE, FALSE, or UNKNOWN; only FALSE and UNKNOWN are valid.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.msf_surface_check.__note"
This function applies to those entity types that are marked in the list above a recursive process to check their entity references for valid instantiations.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.msf_surface_check.__note"
This function does not check the correctness of references with respect to requirements specified by <<express:product_property_representation_schema.shape_representation,shape_representation>>. Only additional requirements due to the scope of the <<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_surface_shape_representation,manifold_surface_shape_representation>> are checked.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.msf_surface_check.surf"
(input) the
// surface
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> that is being checked for a valid surface in a
// manifold_surface_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_surface_shape_representation,manifold_surface_shape_representation>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.non_manifold_surface_shape_representation"
A **non_manifold_surface_shape_representation** is a type of
// shape_representation
<<express:product_property_representation_schema.shape_representation,shape_representation>> that describes the shape or portions of the shape of a product using non-manifolds with boundaries.

A **non_manifold_surface_shape_representation** is a
// shape_representation
<<express:product_property_representation_schema.shape_representation,shape_representation>> that consists of one or many
// face_based_surface_models
<<express:geometric_model_schema.face_based_surface_model,face_based_surface_model>> instances. Each
// face_based_surface_model
<<express:geometric_model_schema.face_based_surface_model,face_based_surface_model>> is built up of
// connected_face_sets
<<express:topology_schema.connected_face_set,connected_face_set>> instances, which in the context of this document may be instantiated as a
// connected_face_set
<<express:topology_schema.connected_face_set,connected_face_set>> or as one of its subtypes
// open_shells
<<express:topology_schema.open_shell,open_shell>> or
// closed_shell
<<express:topology_schema.closed_shell,closed_shell>>.
// connected_face_sets
All <<express:topology_schema.connected_face_set,connected_face_set>> instaces consist of
// faces
<<express:topology_schema.face,face>> instances which use
// edges
<<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> instances and
// vertexs
<<express:topology_schema.vertex,vertex>> instances; the latter three shall reference geometric entities, such as
// points
<<express:geometry_schema.point,point>> instances,
// curves
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> instances, and
// surfaces
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> instances. The link between topology and geometry may be established by either using
// face_surface
<<express:topology_schema.face_surface,face_surface>> or
// advanced_face
<<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>>. The two options differ both in the selection of valid
// point
<<express:geometry_schema.point,point>>,
// curve
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>>, and
// surface
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> subtypes and in constraints on references to underlying geometry.

All geometric entities shall be of dimensionality three except for two-dimensional geometry that is used for the purpose of defining
// pcurve
<<express:geometry_schema.pcurve,pcurve>> instances. The use of one-dimensional
// cartesian_point
<<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_point,cartesian_point>> instances is excluded.

All unbounded geometry shall be trimmed by using topological constructs.

The
// items
<<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> of a **non_manifold_surface_shape_representation** may also be of type
// mapped_item
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>>, or
// axis2_placement_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.axis2_placement_3d,axis2_placement_3d>>. These are used to assemble one or several **non_manifold_surface_shape_representation** instances into one other **non_manifold_surface_shape_representation** instances.

In WR4, WR5 and WR9, these functions validate the
// curves
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> instances and
// surface
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> instances of all
// edge
<<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> instances and
// faces
<<express:topology_schema.face,face>> instances that are in the scope of a **non_manifold_surface_shape_representation** except for those that are in the reference tree of an
// advanced_face
<<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>>; the geometry of an
// advanced_face
<<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>> is validated by a different set of rules. The functions automatically assess all underlying geometry; for this they are called recursively.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.non_manifold_surface_shape_representation.__example"
A
// pcurve
<<express:geometry_schema.pcurve,pcurve>> references both a
// curve
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> and a
// surface
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>>. The function
// nmsf_curve_check
<<express:geometric_model_schema.nmsf_curve_check,nmsf_curve_check>> validates not only the
// pcurve
<<express:geometry_schema.pcurve,pcurve>>, but also the
// curve
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> and the
// surface
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>>. It will, therefore, not only call itself, but also
// nmsf_surface_check
<<express:geometric_model_schema.nmsf_surface_check,nmsf_surface_check>>.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.non_manifold_surface_shape_representation.__note"
Non-manifolds are topologically less constrained than manifolds. For example, the restriction that only a maximum of two
// faces
<<express:topology_schema.face,face>> instances may share the same
// edge
<<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> instance does not apply. They are, therefore, not necessarily suitable for building solid models. They are, however, often found in applications that support the finite element analysis method.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.non_manifold_surface_shape_representation.__note"
A *non_manifold_surface_shape_representation* may well hold a manifold surface model, but not vice versa.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.non_manifold_surface_shape_representation.__note"
The representation of
// face_surfaces
<<express:topology_schema.face_surface,face_surface>> instances as
// advanced_faces
<<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>> instances is recommended for non-manifold surface models that are intended to be used together with boundary-representation solid models to reduce integration complexity.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.non_manifold_surface_shape_representation.__note"
This document does not include a function for the validation of
// points
<<express:geometry_schema.point,point>> instances and their underlying
// curves
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> instances and
// surfaces
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> instances. This is because all
// curves
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> instances and
// surfaces
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> insances of a *non_manifold_surface_shape_representation* are referenced from
// edges
<<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> instances and
// faces
<<express:topology_schema.face,face>> instances and are, thus, covered by the two existing functions already.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.non_manifold_surface_shape_representation.items"
one or more of:
// face_based_surface_models
<<express:geometric_model_schema.face_based_surface_model,face_based_surface_model>> instances,
// mapped_items
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>> instances, or
// axis2_placement_3ds
<<express:geometry_schema.axis2_placement_3d,axis2_placement_3d>> instances.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.non_manifold_surface_shape_representation.items.__note"
An
// axis2_placement_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.axis2_placement_3d,axis2_placement_3d>> is a valid
// mapped_item.mapping_target
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item.mapping_target,mapping_target>> item. To include another
// representation
<<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> into the list of
// representation.items
<<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> of a *non_manifold_surface_shape_representation* (see *WR2* for valid
// mapped_item
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>> instances), the entity specified by the
// mapped_item.mapping_source.mapping_origin
<<express:representation_schema.representation_map.mapping_origin,mapping_origin>> attribute of the
// representation_map
<<express:representation_schema.representation_map,representation_map>> specified by the
// mapped_item
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>> may be any entity that is geometrically founded in the
// geometric_representation_context
<<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_context,geometric_representation_context>> of the
// mapped_representation
<<express:representation_schema.representation_map.mapped_representation,mapped_representation>>. If that entity is an
// axis2_placement_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.axis2_placement_3d,axis2_placement_3d>>, the operator that maps the
// mapped_representation
<<express:representation_schema.representation_map.mapped_representation,mapped_representation>>, into the *non_manifold_surface_shape_representation* corresponds to a transformation matrix with only translation and rotation enabled. If a
// cartesian_transformation_operator_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_transformation_operator_3d,cartesian_transformation_operator_3d>> is used as
// mapping_origin
<<express:representation_schema.representation_map.mapping_origin,mapping_origin>>, scaling and mirroring are possible.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.non_manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:WR1"
At least one of the
// representation.items
<<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> in a **non_manifold_surface_shape_representation** shall be either a
// face_based_surface_model
<<express:geometric_model_schema.face_based_surface_model,face_based_surface_model>> or a
// mapped_item
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.non_manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:WR2"
If there is a
// mapped_item
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>> in a **non_manifold_surface_shape_representation** the
// mapped_representation
<<express:representation_schema.representation_map.mapped_representation,mapped_representation>> of its
// mapping_source
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item.mapping_source,mapping_source>> shall be a **non_manifold_surface_shape_representation**. This
// shape_representation
<<express:product_property_representation_schema.shape_representation,shape_representation>> shall include at least one
// face_based_surface_model
<<express:geometric_model_schema.face_based_surface_model,face_based_surface_model>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.non_manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:WR3"
A
// face
<<express:topology_schema.face,face>> shall be instantiated as either a
// face_surface
<<express:topology_schema.face_surface,face_surface>>, its subtype
// advanced_face
<<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>>, or an
// oriented_face
<<express:topology_schema.oriented_face,oriented_face>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.non_manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:WR4"
All basis geometry that via a
// face_surface
<<express:topology_schema.face_surface,face_surface>> is referenced by
// surfaces
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> instances shall be either within the reference tree of an
// advanced_face
<<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>> or shall be valid
// curves
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> instances and
// surfaces
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> instances.

The
// basis_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve.basis_surface,basis_surface>> of an
// offset_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_surface,offset_surface>> shall be either an
// elementary_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.elementary_surface,elementary_surface>>,
// b_spline_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_surface,b_spline_surface>>,
// offset_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_surface,offset_surface>>,
// swept_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.swept_surface,swept_surface>>, or
// surface_replica
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_replica,surface_replica>>.

The
// parent_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_replica.parent_surface,parent_surface>> of a
// surface_replica
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_replica,surface_replica>> shall be either an
// elementary_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.elementary_surface,elementary_surface>>,
// b_spline_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_surface,b_spline_surface>>,
// offset_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_surface,offset_surface>>,
// swept_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.swept_surface,swept_surface>>, or
// surface_replica
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_replica,surface_replica>>.

The
// swept_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.swept_surface.swept_curve,swept_curve>> of a
// swept_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.swept_surface,swept_surface>> shall be either a
// line
<<express:geometry_schema.line,line>>,
// conic
<<express:geometry_schema.conic,conic>>,
// pcurve
<<express:geometry_schema.pcurve,pcurve>>,
// surface_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve,surface_curve>>,
// offset_curve_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_curve_3d,offset_curve_3d>>,
// b_spline_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_curve,b_spline_curve>>,
// polyline
<<express:geometry_schema.polyline,polyline>>, or
// curve_replica
<<express:geometry_schema.curve_replica,curve_replica>>.

The attribute
// self_intersect
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_surface.self_intersect,self_intersect>> for
// b_spline_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_surface,b_spline_surface>> instances and
// self_intersect
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_surface.self_intersect,self_intersect>> for
// offset_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_surface,offset_surface>> instances shall be set to FALSE or UNKNOWN.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.non_manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:WR4.__note"
A
// surface
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> is validated against these constraints by the function
// nmsf_surface_check
<<express:geometric_model_schema.nmsf_surface_check,nmsf_surface_check>>.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.non_manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:WR5"
All basis geometry that is referenced via a
// oriented_face.face_element
<<express:topology_schema.oriented_face.face_element,face_element>> shall be either within the reference tree of an
// advanced_face
<<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>> or shall be valid
// curves
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> instances and
// surfaces
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> instances.

The
// basis_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve.basis_surface,basis_surface>> of an
// offset_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_surface,offset_surface>> shall be either an
// elementary_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.elementary_surface,elementary_surface>>,
// b_spline_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_surface,b_spline_surface>>,
// offset_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_surface,offset_surface>>,
// swept_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.swept_surface,swept_surface>>, or
// surface_replica
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_replica,surface_replica>>.

The
// parent_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_replica.parent_surface,parent_surface>> of a
// surface_replica
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_replica,surface_replica>> shall be either an
// elementary_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.elementary_surface,elementary_surface>>,
// b_spline_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_surface,b_spline_surface>>,
// offset_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_surface,offset_surface>>,
// swept_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.swept_surface,swept_surface>>, or
// surface_replica
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_replica,surface_replica>>.

The
// swept_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.swept_surface.swept_curve,swept_curve>> of a
// swept_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.swept_surface,swept_surface>> shall be either a
// line
<<express:geometry_schema.line,line>>,
// conic
<<express:geometry_schema.conic,conic>>,
// pcurve
<<express:geometry_schema.pcurve,pcurve>>,
// surface_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve,surface_curve>>,
// offset_curve_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_curve_3d,offset_curve_3d>>,
// b_spline_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_curve,b_spline_curve>>,
// polyline
<<express:geometry_schema.polyline,polyline>>, or
// curve_replica
<<express:geometry_schema.curve_replica,curve_replica>>.

The attribute
// self_intersect
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_surface.self_intersect,self_intersect>> for
// b_spline_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_surface,b_spline_surface>> instances and
// self_intersect
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_surface.self_intersect,self_intersect>> for
// offset_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_surface,offset_surface>> instances shall be set to FALSE or UNKNOWN.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.non_manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:WR6"
The
// face_bound.bound
<<express:topology_schema.face_bound.bound,bound>> of a
// face_bound
<<express:topology_schema.face_bound,face_bound>>, that is referenced by a
// face
<<express:topology_schema.face,face>> that is referenced either directly by a
// connected_face_set
<<express:topology_schema.connected_face_set,connected_face_set>> or via an
// oriented_face
<<express:topology_schema.oriented_face,oriented_face>> shall be either within the reference tree of an
// advanced_face
<<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>> or shall be an
// edge_loop
<<express:topology_schema.edge_loop,edge_loop>> or a
// vertex_loop
<<express:topology_schema.vertex_loop,vertex_loop>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.non_manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:WR7"
The geometry of a bounding
// edge
<<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> that is the
// edge_element
<<express:topology_schema.oriented_edge.edge_element,edge_element>> of an
// oriented_edge
<<express:topology_schema.oriented_edge,oriented_edge>> that is referenced by a
// face
<<express:topology_schema.face,face>> that is referenced either directly by a
// connected_face_set
<<express:topology_schema.connected_face_set,connected_face_set>> or via an
// oriented_face
<<express:topology_schema.oriented_face,oriented_face>> shall be either within the reference tree of an
// advanced_face
<<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>> or shall be an
// edge_curve
<<express:topology_schema.edge_curve,edge_curve>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.non_manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:WR8"
The
// curve
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> used to define the geometry of an
// edge
<<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> that is the <<express:topology_schema.edge_curve.edge_geometry,edge_geometry>> of an
// edge_curve
<<express:topology_schema.edge_curve,edge_curve>> of an
// edge
<<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> that is referenced by a
// face
<<express:topology_schema.face,face>> that is referenced either directly by a
// connected_face_set
<<express:topology_schema.connected_face_set,connected_face_set>> or via an
// oriented_face
<<express:topology_schema.oriented_face,oriented_face>> shall be either a
// b_spline_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_curve,b_spline_curve>>, a
// conic
<<express:geometry_schema.conic,conic>>, a
// curve_replica
<<express:geometry_schema.curve_replica,curve_replica>>, a
// line
<<express:geometry_schema.line,line>>, an
// offset_curve_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_curve_3d,offset_curve_3d>>, a
// pcurve
<<express:geometry_schema.pcurve,pcurve>>, a
// polyline
<<express:geometry_schema.polyline,polyline>>, a
// surface_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve,surface_curve>>, or a
// curve
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> in the reference tree of an
// advanced_face
<<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.non_manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:WR9"
All basis geometry that is referenced by
// curves
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> instances shall be either within the reference tree of an
// advanced_face
<<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>> or shall be valid
// curves
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> instances and
// surfaces
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> instances.

The
// parent_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.curve_replica.parent_curve,parent_curve>> of a
// curve_replica
<<express:geometry_schema.curve_replica,curve_replica>> shall be either a
// line
<<express:geometry_schema.line,line>>,
// conic
<<express:geometry_schema.conic,conic>>,
// pcurve
<<express:geometry_schema.pcurve,pcurve>>,
// surface_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve,surface_curve>>,
// offset_curve_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_curve_3d,offset_curve_3d>>,
// b_spline_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_curve,b_spline_curve>>,
// polyline
<<express:geometry_schema.polyline,polyline>>, or
// curve_replica
<<express:geometry_schema.curve_replica,curve_replica>>.

The
// basis_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_curve_3d.basis_curve,basis_curve>> of an
// offset_curve_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_curve_3d,offset_curve_3d>> shall be either a
// line
<<express:geometry_schema.line,line>>,
// conic
<<express:geometry_schema.conic,conic>>,
// pcurve
<<express:geometry_schema.pcurve,pcurve>>,
// surface_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve,surface_curve>>,
// offset_curve_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_curve_3d,offset_curve_3d>>,
// b_spline_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_curve,b_spline_curve>>,
// polyline
<<express:geometry_schema.polyline,polyline>>, or
// curve_replica
<<express:geometry_schema.curve_replica,curve_replica>>.

The
// curve_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve.curve_3d,curve_3d>> of a
// surface_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve,surface_curve>> shall be either a
// line
<<express:geometry_schema.line,line>>,
// conic
<<express:geometry_schema.conic,conic>>,
// offset_curve_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_curve_3d,offset_curve_3d>>,
// b_spline_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_curve,b_spline_curve>>,
// polyline
<<express:geometry_schema.polyline,polyline>>, or
// curve_replica
<<express:geometry_schema.curve_replica,curve_replica>>.

The
// basis_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve.basis_surface,basis_surface>> of a
// surface_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve,surface_curve>> shall be either a
// b_spline_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_surface,b_spline_surface>>,
// elementary_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.elementary_surface,elementary_surface>>,
// offset_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_surface,offset_surface>>,
// surface_replica
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_replica,surface_replica>>, or
// swept_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.swept_surface,swept_surface>>.

Each
// polylines
<<express:geometry_schema.polyline,polyline>> instance shall contain at least three
// cartesian_points
<<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_point,cartesian_point>> instances.

The attribute
// self_intersect
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_curve.self_intersect,self_intersect>> for
// b_spline_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_curve,b_spline_curve>> instances and
// self_intersect
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_curve_3d.self_intersect,self_intersect>> for
// offset_curve_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_curve_3d,offset_curve_3d>> instances shall be set to FALSE or UNKNOWN.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.non_manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:WR9.__note"
A
// curve
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> is validated against these constraints by the function
// nmsf_curve_check
<<express:geometric_model_schema.nmsf_curve_check,nmsf_curve_check>>.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.non_manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:WR10"
The
// edge_start
<<express:topology_schema.edge.edge_start,edge_start>> and
// edge_end
<<express:topology_schema.edge.edge_end,edge_end>> of an
// edge
<<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> shall be either within the reference tree of an
// advanced_face
<<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>> or shall be
// vertex_points
<<express:topology_schema.vertex_point,vertex_point>> instances.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.non_manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:WR11"
The
// vertex_geometry
<<express:topology_schema.vertex_point.vertex_geometry,vertex_geometry>> of a
// vertex
<<express:topology_schema.vertex,vertex>> that is part of an
// edge_loop
<<express:topology_schema.edge_loop,edge_loop>> shall be either within the reference tree of an
// advanced_face
<<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>> or shall be a
// cartesian_point
<<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_point,cartesian_point>>,
// point_on_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.point_on_curve,point_on_curve>>,
// point_on_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.point_on_surface,point_on_surface>>, or
// degenerate_pcurve
<<express:geometry_schema.degenerate_pcurve,degenerate_pcurve>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.non_manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:WR12"
The
// loop_vertex
<<express:topology_schema.vertex_loop.loop_vertex,loop_vertex>> of a
// vertex_loop
<<express:topology_schema.vertex_loop,vertex_loop>> shall be either within the reference tree of an
// advanced_face
<<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>> or shall be a
// vertex_points
<<express:topology_schema.vertex_point,vertex_point>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.non_manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:WR13"
The
// vertex_geometry
<<express:topology_schema.vertex_point.vertex_geometry,vertex_geometry>> of a
// vertex
<<express:topology_schema.vertex,vertex>> that is part of a
// vertex_loop
<<express:topology_schema.vertex_loop,vertex_loop>> shall be either within the reference tree of an
// advanced_face
<<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>> or shall be a
// cartesian_point
<<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_point,cartesian_point>>,
// point_on_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.point_on_curve,point_on_curve>>,
// point_on_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.point_on_surface,point_on_surface>>, or
// degenerate_pcurve
<<express:geometry_schema.degenerate_pcurve,degenerate_pcurve>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.non_manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:IP1"
The portion of a
// b_spline_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_curve,b_spline_curve>> that is within the topological domain of a **non_manifold_surface_shape_representation** shall not self-intersect.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.non_manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:IP2"
The portion of a
// b_spline_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_surface,b_spline_surface>> that is within the topological domain of a **non_manifold_surface_shape_representation** shall not self-intersect.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.non_manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:IP3"
The portion of a
// offset_curve_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_curve_3d,offset_curve_3d>> that is within the topological domain of a **non_manifold_surface_shape_representation** shall not self-intersect.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.non_manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:IP4"
The portion of a
// offset_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_surface,offset_surface>> that is within the topological domain of a **non_manifold_surface_shape_representation** shall not self-intersect.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.non_manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:IP5"
If a
// face
<<express:topology_schema.face,face>> has only one connected outer bound, the corresponding
// loop
<<express:topology_schema.loop,loop>> shall be represented as
// face_outer_bound
<<express:topology_schema.face_outer_bound,face_outer_bound>>. If the outer bound is not connected,
// face_outer_bound
<<express:topology_schema.face_outer_bound,face_outer_bound>> shall not be used.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.nmsf_curve_check"
The **nmsf_curve_check** function checks a
// curve
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> instance for validity in the context of a
// non_manifold_surface_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.non_manifold_surface_shape_representation,non_manifold_surface_shape_representation>>. Each geometric instance that is referenced by that
// curve
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> instance is also validated.

Where appropriate an instance is investigated recursively. This means if a
// curve
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> references another
// curve
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> as a basis curve or parent curve, the **nmsf_curve_check** function is called again. If a
// surface
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> is referenced, the
// nmsf_surface_check
<<express:geometric_model_schema.nmsf_surface_check,nmsf_surface_check>> function is called. The recursive process terminates at entity types that do not reference any
// curves
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> instances or
// surfaces
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> instances.

The following curve types and their subtypes are within the scope of the
// non_manifold_surface_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.non_manifold_surface_shape_representation,non_manifold_surface_shape_representation>> and are, thus, valid input to this function:

*
// b_spline_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_curve,b_spline_curve>>;
*
// conic
<<express:geometry_schema.conic,conic>>;
*
// curve_replica
<<express:geometry_schema.curve_replica,curve_replica>>;
*
// line
<<express:geometry_schema.line,line>>;
*
// offset_curve_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_curve_3d,offset_curve_3d>>;
*
// pcurve
<<express:geometry_schema.pcurve,pcurve>>;
*
// polyline
<<express:geometry_schema.polyline,polyline>>;
*
// surface_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve,surface_curve>>.

Four of these
// curve
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> types reference basis or parent
// curves
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> instances. The lists below indicate the valid references.

The
// parent_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.curve_replica.parent_curve,parent_curve>> of a
// curve_replica
<<express:geometry_schema.curve_replica,curve_replica>> shall be of one of the following types:

*
// b_spline_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_curve,b_spline_curve>>;
*
// conic
<<express:geometry_schema.conic,conic>>;
*
// curve_replica
<<express:geometry_schema.curve_replica,curve_replica>> (recursive);
*
// line
<<express:geometry_schema.line,line>>;
*
// offset_curve_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_curve_3d,offset_curve_3d>> (recursive);
*
// pcurve
<<express:geometry_schema.pcurve,pcurve>> (recursive);
*
// polyline
<<express:geometry_schema.polyline,polyline>>;
*
// surface_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve,surface_curve>> (recursive).

The
// offset_curve_3d.basis_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_curve_3d.basis_curve,basis_curve>> of an
// offset_curve_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_curve_3d,offset_curve_3d>> shall be of one of the following types:

*
// b_spline_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_curve,b_spline_curve>>;
*
// conic
<<express:geometry_schema.conic,conic>>;
*
// curve_replica
<<express:geometry_schema.curve_replica,curve_replica>> (recursive);
*
// line
<<express:geometry_schema.line,line>>;
*
// offset_curve_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_curve_3d,offset_curve_3d>> (recursive);
*
// pcurve
<<express:geometry_schema.pcurve,pcurve>> (recursive);
*
// surface_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve,surface_curve>> (recursive).

The instance specified by the
// items
<<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> attribute (inherited from
// representation
<<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>>) of a
// definitional_representation
<<express:representation_schema.definitional_representation,definitional_representation>> where that
// definitional_representation
<<express:representation_schema.definitional_representation,definitional_representation>> is referenced as
// reference_to_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.pcurve.reference_to_curve,reference_to_curve>> by a
// pcurve
<<express:geometry_schema.pcurve,pcurve>> shall be one of the following types:

*
// b_spline_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_curve,b_spline_curve>>;
*
// conic
<<express:geometry_schema.conic,conic>>;
*
// curve_replica
<<express:geometry_schema.curve_replica,curve_replica>> (recursive);
*
// line
<<express:geometry_schema.line,line>>;
*
// polyline
<<express:geometry_schema.polyline,polyline>>.

The
// curve_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve.curve_3d,curve_3d>> of a
// surface_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve,surface_curve>> shall be of one of the following types:

*
// b_spline_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_curve,b_spline_curve>>;
*
// conic
<<express:geometry_schema.conic,conic>>;
*
// curve_replica
<<express:geometry_schema.curve_replica,curve_replica>> (recursive);
*
// line
<<express:geometry_schema.line,line>>;
*
// offset_curve_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_curve_3d,offset_curve_3d>> (recursive);
*
// polyline
<<express:geometry_schema.polyline,polyline>>;
*
// surface_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve,surface_curve>> (recursive).

Each
// pcurve
<<express:geometry_schema.pcurve,pcurve>> instance and
// surface_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve,surface_curve>> instance reference
// surfaces
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> instances. Function
// nmsf_surface_check
<<express:geometric_model_schema.nmsf_surface_check,nmsf_surface_check>> is called for validation of these
// surfaces
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> instances.

A valid
// polyline
<<express:geometry_schema.polyline,polyline>> shall consist of at least three
// cartesian_points
<<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_point,cartesian_point>> instances.

The attributes
// self_intersect
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_surface.self_intersect,self_intersect>> shall for B-spline and offset geometry be set to FALSE or UNKNOWN.

This function returns TRUE, if the types of all referenced geometries are within the scope of the
// non_manifold_surface_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.non_manifold_surface_shape_representation,non_manifold_surface_shape_representation>> and if all constraints are fulfilled, otherwise the function returns FALSE.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.nmsf_curve_check.__example"
One of the constraints that is validated by this function is whether the self-intersection flag of a
// b_spline_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_curve,b_spline_curve>> instance is set to TRUE, FALSE, or UNKNOWN; only FALSE and UNKNOWN are valid.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.nmsf_curve_check.__note"
This function applies to those entity types that are marked in the lists below a recursive process to check their entity references for valid instantiations.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.nmsf_curve_check.cv"
(input) a
// representation_item
<<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> that is required to be a
// curve
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> that is checked for being valid in the context of a
// non_manifold_surface_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.non_manifold_surface_shape_representation,non_manifold_surface_shape_representation>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.nmsf_surface_check"
The **nmsf_surface_check** function checks a
// surface
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> instance for validity in the context of a
// non_manifold_surface_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.non_manifold_surface_shape_representation,non_manifold_surface_shape_representation>>. Each geometric instance that is referenced by that
// surface
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> instance is also validated.

Where appropriate, an instance is investigated recursively. This means if a
// surface
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> references another
// surface
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> as a basis surface or parent surface the **nmsf_surface_check** function is called again. If a
// curve
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> is referenced, the
// nmsf_curve_check
<<express:geometric_model_schema.nmsf_curve_check,nmsf_curve_check>>. function is called. The recursive process terminates at entity types that do not reference any
// curve
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> instances or
// surfaces
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> instances.

The following surface types and their subtypes are within the scope of the
// non_manifold_surface_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.non_manifold_surface_shape_representation,non_manifold_surface_shape_representation>>. and are, thus, valid input to this function:

*
// b_spline_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_surface,b_spline_surface>>;
*
// elementary_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.elementary_surface,elementary_surface>>;
*
// offset_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_surface,offset_surface>>;
*
// surface_replica
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_replica,surface_replica>>;
*
// swept_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.swept_surface,swept_surface>>.

Two of these
// surface
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> types reference basis or parent
// surfaces
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> instances. The
// parent_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_replica.parent_surface,parent_surface>> of a
// surface_replica
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_replica,surface_replica>> and the
// basis_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve.basis_surface,basis_surface>> of an
// offset_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_surface,offset_surface>> shall both be of one of the following types:

*
// b_spline_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_surface,b_spline_surface>>;
*
// elementary_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.elementary_surface,elementary_surface>>;
*
// offset_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.offset_surface,offset_surface>> (recursive);
*
// surface_replica
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_replica,surface_replica>> (recursive);
*
// swept_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.swept_surface,swept_surface>>.

Each
// swept_surfaces
<<express:geometry_schema.swept_surface,swept_surface>> references
// curves
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> instances. The function
// nmsf_curve_check
<<express:geometric_model_schema.nmsf_curve_check,nmsf_curve_check>> is called for validation of these
// curves
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> instances. All
// curves
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> instances that are in the scope of a
// non_manifold_surface_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.non_manifold_surface_shape_representation,non_manifold_surface_shape_representation>>. are valid as
// swept_surface.swept_curves
<<express:geometry_schema.swept_surface.swept_curve,swept_curve>> instances.

The attributes
// self_intersect
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_surface.self_intersect,self_intersect>> shall for b_spline and offset geometry be set to FALSE or UNKNOWN.

This function returns TRUE, if the types of all referenced geometries are within the scope of the
// non_manifold_surface_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.non_manifold_surface_shape_representation,non_manifold_surface_shape_representation>> and if all constraints are fulfilled, otherwise the function returns FALSE.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.nmsf_surface_check.__example"
One of the constraints that is validated by this function is whether the self-intersection flag of a
// b_spline_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_surface,b_spline_surface>> instance is set to TRUE, FALSE, or UNKNOWN; only FALSE and UNKNOWN are valid.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.nmsf_surface_check.__note"
This function applies to those entity types that are marked in the list above a recursive process to check their entity references for valid instantiations.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.nmsf_surface_check.surf"
(input) the
// surface
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> that is being checked for a valid
// surface
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> in a
// non_manifold_surface_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.non_manifold_surface_shape_representation,non_manifold_surface_shape_representation>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.faceted_brep_shape_representation"
A **faceted_brep_shape_representation** is a type of
// shape_representation
<<express:product_property_representation_schema.shape_representation,shape_representation>> in which the representation item instances are specialisations of
// faceted_brep
<<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_brep,faceted_brep>> entities. These differ from the more general B-rep in having only planar faces and implicit edge geometry.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.faceted_brep_shape_representation.items"
one or more of:
// face_based_surface_models
<<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_brep,faceted_brep>> instances,
// mapped_items
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>> instances, or
// axis2_placement_3ds
<<express:geometry_schema.axis2_placement_3d,axis2_placement_3d>> instances.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.faceted_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR1"
At least one item in the
// item
<<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> set shall be a
// faceted_brep
<<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_brep,faceted_brep>> entity, or a
// mapped_item
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>>, (See also WR6).
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.faceted_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR2"
For each
// faceted_brep
<<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_brep,faceted_brep>> in the
// item
<<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> instance set: the faces shall be
// face_surface
<<express:topology_schema.face_surface,face_surface>> instances, the associated surface for each face shall be a
// plane
<<express:geometry_schema.plane,plane>>, and each
// plane
<<express:geometry_schema.plane,plane>> shall use a
// cartesian_point
<<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_point,cartesian_point>> for its location.

// REVIEW_ITEM

// This item is deferred to TCSC410303-227:

// Geometric Model Schema Reorganization

// REVIEW_ITEM

// `fbrep' is currently hardcoded in the document

// deferring appropriate links for REORG phase
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.faceted_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR2.__note"
The call to function
// msb_shells
<<express:geometric_model_schema.msb_shells,msb_shells>> in WR2 and WR3 is correct since, although the generic type of the argument `fbrep' is
// representation_item
<<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> `fbrep' has been selected by QUERY to be a subtype of
// manifold_solid_brep
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep,manifold_solid_brep>>
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.faceted_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR3"
An explicit outer bound shall be specifed for each
// face
<<express:topology_schema.face,face>> of the
// faceted_brep
<<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_brep,faceted_brep>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.faceted_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR4"
For each
// manifold_solid_brep
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep,manifold_solid_brep>> in the
// item
<<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> instance set the
// outer
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep.outer,outer>> shell attribute shall not be of the oriented subtype.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.faceted_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR5"
If the
// manifold_solid_brep
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep,manifold_solid_brep>> is also a
// brep_with_voids
<<express:geometric_model_schema.brep_with_voids,brep_with_voids>> then each shell in the
// voids
<<express:geometric_model_schema.brep_with_voids.voids,voids>> set shall be an
// oriented_closed_shell
<<express:topology_schema.oriented_closed_shell,oriented_closed_shell>> with orientation value FALSE.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.faceted_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR6"
If a
// mapped_item
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>> is included in the
// items
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_surface_shape_representation.items,items>> instance set then the
// mapped_representation
<<express:representation_schema.representation_map.mapped_representation,mapped_representation>> of the
// mapping_source
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item.mapping_source,mapping_source>> attribute shall be a **faceted_brep_shape_representation**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.faceted_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR6.__note"
If a
// cartesian_transformation_operator_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_transformation_operator_3d,cartesian_transformation_operator_3d>> is included as
// mapped_item.mapping_target
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item.mapping_target,mapping_target>> with an
// axis2_placement_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.axis2_placement_3d,axis2_placement_3d>>, the operator that maps the that corresponds to the original coordinate system as
// mapped_representation.mapping_origin
<<express:representation_schema.representation_map.mapping_origin,mapping_origin>>, then the resulting
// mapped item
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>> is a transformed copy of the *faceted brep shape representation*. The precise definition of the transformation, including translation, rotation, scaling and, if appropriate, mirroring, is given by the transformation operator.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.csg_shape_representation"
A **csg_shape_representation** is a type of
// shape_representation
<<express:product_property_representation_schema.shape_representation,shape_representation>> that is three-dimensional and that represents the shape of a product using constructive solid geometry operations and techniques. The solid objects may be either solid primitives, swept face solids, half-space solids, faceted B-rep solids (consistent with
// faceted_brep_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_brep_shape_representation,faceted_brep_shape_representation>>), or advanced B-rep solids (consistent with
// advanced_brep_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.advanced_brep_shape_representation,advanced_brep_shape_representation>>).
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.csg_shape_representation.__note"
An application protocol that uses *csg_shape_representation* may ensure that the <<express:product_property_representation_schema.shape_representation,shape_representation>> entity is instantiated as a *csg_shape_representation*.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.csg_shape_representation.items"
one or more of:
// csg_solid
<<express:geometric_model_schema.csg_solid,csg_solid>> instances,
// extruded_face_solid
<<express:geometric_model_schema.extruded_face_solid,extruded_face_solid>> instances,
// revolved_face_solid
<<express:geometric_model_schema.revolved_face_solid,revolved_face_solid>> instances,
// solid_replica
<<express:geometric_model_schema.solid_replica,solid_replica>> instances,
// mapped_item
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>> instances, or
// axis2_placement_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.axis2_placement_3d,axis2_placement_3d>> instances.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.csg_shape_representation.wr:WR1"
The
// geometric_representation_context
<<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_context,geometric_representation_context>> of the **csg_shape_representation** shall have a
// geometric_representation_context.coordinate_space_dimension
<<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_context.coordinate_space_dimension,coordinate_space_dimension>> equal to three.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.csg_shape_representation.wr:WR2"
The
// mapped_item.mapping_source
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item.mapping_source,mapping_source>> of any
// mapped_item
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>>, in the
// items
<<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> set of a **csg_shape_representation** shall be of type **csg_shape_representation**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.csg_shape_representation.wr:WR3"
The
// solid_replica.parent_solid
<<express:geometric_model_schema.solid_replica.parent_solid,parent_solid>> of any
// solid_replica
<<express:geometric_model_schema.solid_replica,solid_replica>> in the
// items
<<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> set of a **csg_shape_representation** shall be either of type
// csg_solid
<<express:geometric_model_schema.csg_solid,csg_solid>>,
// revolved_face_solid
<<express:geometric_model_schema.revolved_face_solid,revolved_face_solid>> or
// extruded_face_solid
<<express:geometric_model_schema.extruded_face_solid,extruded_face_solid>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.csg_shape_representation.wr:WR4"
There shall be at least one element in the
// items
<<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> set of a **csg_shape_representation**, which is not of type
// axis2_placement_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.axis2_placement_3d,axis2_placement_3d>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.csg_shape_representation.wr:IP1"
Any instance of
// solid_model
<<express:geometric_model_schema.solid_model,solid_model>> used directly, or indirectly, as
// boolean_result.first_operand
<<express:geometric_model_schema.boolean_result.first_operand,first_operand>> or
// boolean_result.second_operand
<<express:geometric_model_schema.boolean_result.second_operand,second_operand>> of a
// boolean_result
<<express:geometric_model_schema.boolean_result,boolean_result>> to define a
// csg_solid
<<express:geometric_model_schema.csg_solid,csg_solid>> in the
// items
<<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> set of a **csg_shape_representation** shall be either of type
// extruded_face_solid
<<express:geometric_model_schema.extruded_face_solid,extruded_face_solid>>,
// revolved_face_solid
<<express:geometric_model_schema.revolved_face_solid,revolved_face_solid>>,
// manifold_solid_brep
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep,manifold_solid_brep>>, or
// solid_replica
<<express:geometric_model_schema.solid_replica,solid_replica>>. If it is of type
// solid_replica
<<express:geometric_model_schema.solid_replica,solid_replica>>, its
// solid_replica.parent_solid
<<express:geometric_model_schema.solid_replica.parent_solid,parent_solid>> shall be of type
// csg_solid
<<express:geometric_model_schema.csg_solid,csg_solid>>,
// extruded_face_solid
<<express:geometric_model_schema.extruded_face_solid,extruded_face_solid>>,
// revolved_face_solid
<<express:geometric_model_schema.revolved_face_solid,revolved_face_solid>> or
// manifold_solid_brep
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep,manifold_solid_brep>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.csg_shape_representation.wr:IP2"
Any instance of
// manifold_solid_brep
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep,manifold_solid_brep>> used directly, or indirectly, as
// boolean_result.first_operand
<<express:geometric_model_schema.boolean_result.first_operand,first_operand>> or
// boolean_result.second_operand
<<express:geometric_model_schema.boolean_result.second_operand,second_operand>> of a
// boolean_result
<<express:geometric_model_schema.boolean_result,boolean_result>> to define a
// csg_solid
<<express:geometric_model_schema.csg_solid,csg_solid>> occurring in a **csg_shape_representation** shall be compatible with either the rules defined for its use in an
// advanced_brep_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.advanced_brep_shape_representation,advanced_brep_shape_representation>> or, the rules defined for its use in a
// faceted_brep_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_brep_shape_representation,faceted_brep_shape_representation>>. In particular each
// face
<<express:topology_schema.face,face>> shall either be of type
// advanced_face
<<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>> or, in the case of a
// faceted_brep
<<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_brep,faceted_brep>>, shall be a
// face_surface
<<express:topology_schema.face_surface,face_surface>> bounded by
// poly_loop
<<express:topology_schema.poly_loop,poly_loop>> instances and with a
// plane
<<express:geometry_schema.plane,plane>> as
// face_surface.face_geometry
<<express:topology_schema.face_surface.face_geometry,face_geometry>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_subsurface_shape_representation"
A **manifold_subsurface_shape_representation** is a type of
// shape_representation
<<express:product_property_representation_schema.shape_representation,shape_representation>> in which the shape of a product is represented by
// connected_face_sub_set
<<express:topology_schema.connected_face_sub_set,connected_face_sub_set>> instances.

Each
// connected_face_sub_set
<<express:topology_schema.connected_face_sub_set,connected_face_sub_set>> is also a type of <<express:topology_schema.open_shell,open_shell>>.

The <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> instances of the
// connected_face_sub_set
<<express:topology_schema.connected_face_sub_set,connected_face_sub_set>> are required to be of type <<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>> or of type <<express:topology_schema.subface,subface>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_subsurface_shape_representation.items"
one or more of:
// connected_face_sub_set
<<express:topology_schema.connected_face_sub_set,connected_face_sub_set>> instances,
// mapped_item
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>> instances, or
// axis2_placement_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.axis2_placement_3d,axis2_placement_3d>> instances.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_subsurface_shape_representation.wr:WR1"
At least one of the <<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> shall be either a <<express:topology_schema.connected_face_sub_set,connected_face_sub_set>> or a <<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_subsurface_shape_representation.wr:WR2"
For any <<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>>, the <<express:representation_schema.representation_map.mapped_representation,mapped_representation>> of its <<express:representation_schema.mapped_item.mapping_source,mapping_source>> shall be a **manifold_subsurface_shape_representation**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_subsurface_shape_representation.wr:WR3"
Any instance of <<express:topology_schema.connected_face_sub_set,connected_face_sub_set>> in the <<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> set shall be of type <<express:topology_schema.connected_face_sub_set,connected_face_sub_set>> and <<express:topology_schema.open_shell,open_shell>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_subsurface_shape_representation.wr:WR4"
For any instance of <<express:topology_schema.connected_face_sub_set,connected_face_sub_set>> the <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> instances of the <<express:topology_schema.connected_face_sub_set.parent_face_set,parent_face_set>> shall be of type <<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>> or the <<express:topology_schema.connected_face_sub_set.parent_face_set,parent_face_set>> shall be an instance of <<express:topology_schema.connected_face_sub_set,connected_face_sub_set>> whose faces are related to <<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_subsurface_shape_representation.wr:WR4.__note"
The <<express:topology_schema.connected_face_sub_set.parent_face_set,parent_face_set>> may be one of the subtypes, <<express:topology_schema.open_shell,open_shell>>, or <<express:topology_schema.closed_shell,closed_shell>> of <<express:topology_schema.connected_face_set,connected_face_set>>.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_subsurface_shape_representation.wr:WR5"
For any instance of <<express:topology_schema.connected_face_sub_set,connected_face_sub_set>> each <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> of the <<express:topology_schema.connected_face_set.cfs_faces,cfs_faces>> attribute shall be of type <<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>> or of type <<express:topology_schema.subface,subface>> and, directly or indirectly, reference an <<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_subsurface_shape_representation.wr:WR5.__note"
This property is verified by the <<express:geometric_model_schema.advanced_face_properties,advanced_face_properties>> function.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_subsurface_shape_representation.wr:WR6"
For any instance of <<express:topology_schema.subface,subface>> in the <<express:topology_schema.connected_face_set.cfs_faces,cfs_faces>> of a <<express:topology_schema.connected_face_sub_set,connected_face_sub_set>> instance the bounding <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> instances shall be of type <<express:topology_schema.subedge,subedge>> or of type <<express:topology_schema.edge_curve,edge_curve>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_subsurface_shape_representation.wr:WR7"
For any instance of <<express:topology_schema.subface,subface>> in the <<express:topology_schema.connected_face_set.cfs_faces,cfs_faces>> of a <<express:topology_schema.connected_face_sub_set,connected_face_sub_set>> instance all vertices used in the <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> definition shall be of type <<express:topology_schema.vertex_point,vertex_point>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_subsurface_shape_representation.wr:WR8"
The bounds of any <<express:topology_schema.subface,subface>> in the <<express:topology_schema.connected_face_set.cfs_faces,cfs_faces>> of a <<express:topology_schema.connected_face_sub_set,connected_face_sub_set>> instance shall be of type <<express:topology_schema.edge_loop,edge_loop>> or of type <<express:topology_schema.vertex_loop,vertex_loop>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_subsurface_shape_representation.wr:WR9"
The types of <<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> used to define the geometry of an <<express:topology_schema.edge_curve,edge_curve>> used in the definition of a <<express:topology_schema.subface,subface>> shall be restricted to <<express:geometry_schema.line,line>> instances, <<express:geometry_schema.conic,conic>> instances, <<express:geometry_schema.polyline,polyline>> instances, <<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve,surface_curve>> instances, or <<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_curve,b_spline_curve>> instances.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_subsurface_shape_representation.wr:WR10"
If a <<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve,surface_curve>> is used as part of a face bound of a <<express:topology_schema.subface,subface>> the <<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve.associated_geometry,associated_geometry>> attribute shall reference a <<express:geometry_schema.pcurve,pcurve>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_subsurface_shape_representation.wr:WR11"
If a <<express:geometry_schema.polyline,polyline>> is used as part of a face bound of a <<express:topology_schema.subface,subface>> it shall contain at least 3 points.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.manifold_subsurface_shape_representation.wr:WR11.__note"
Rules WR6 to WR11 ensure that the definition of the bounds of a <<express:topology_schema.subface,subface>> are consistent with those of an <<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>>.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.advanced_face_properties"
The **advanced_face_properties** function checks the properties of a <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> to determine if it is of type <<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>>, or, if it is a <<express:topology_schema.subface,subface>> directly, or indirectly, referencing an <<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>> as <<express:topology_schema.subface.parent_face,parent_face>>. This check is carried out recursively and a TRUE result is returned if the <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> either is an <<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>>, or, via the <<express:topology_schema.subface.parent_face,parent_face>> attribute of a <<express:topology_schema.subface,subface>> references an <<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>>. In all other cases a FALSE result is returned.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.advanced_face_properties.testface"
the <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> which is to be tested for <<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>> properties.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.elementary_brep_shape_representation"
A **elementary_brep_shape_representation** is a type of
// shape_representation
<<express:product_property_representation_schema.shape_representation,shape_representation>> in which the representation items are specialisations of
// manifold_solid_brep
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep,manifold_solid_brep>> entities. These differ from the more general B-rep in having only explicit geometric forms for their faces and edges. The face geometry is restricted to
// elementary_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.elementary_surface,elementary_surface>>, instances, and the edge curves to
// lines
<<express:geometry_schema.line,line>> instances,
// polyline
<<express:geometry_schema.polyline,polyline>> instances, or
// conic
<<express:geometry_schema.conic,conic>> instances.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.elementary_brep_shape_representation.items"
one or more of:
// shell_based_surface_models
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep,manifold_solid_brep>> instances,
// mapped_item
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>> instances, or
// axis2_placement_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.axis2_placement_3d,axis2_placement_3d>> instances.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.elementary_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR1"
At least one item in the
// item
<<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> set shall be a
// manifold_solid_brep
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep,manifold_solid_brep>> entity or a
// mapped_item
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>> (see also WR10).
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.elementary_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR2"
All faces used in constructing a
// manifold_solid_brep
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep,manifold_solid_brep>>. shall be of type
// face_surface
<<express:topology_schema.face_surface,face_surface>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.elementary_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR2.__note"
The call to function
// msb_shells
<<express:geometric_model_schema.msb_shells,msb_shells>> in WR2, and later rules, is correct since, although the generic type of the argument 'msb' is
// representation_item
<<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>>, 'msb' has been selected by QUERY to be of type
// manifold_solid_brep
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep,manifold_solid_brep>>.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.elementary_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR3"
For each
// manifold_solid_brep
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep,manifold_solid_brep>> in the
// item
<<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> set, the associated surface for each face shall be an
// elementary_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.elementary_surface,elementary_surface>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.elementary_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR4"
For each
// manifold_solid_brep
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep,manifold_solid_brep>> in the
// items
<<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> set, the edges used to define the boundaries shall all be of type
// edge_curve
<<express:topology_schema.edge_curve,edge_curve>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.elementary_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR5"
For each
// manifold_solid_brep
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep,manifold_solid_brep>> in the
// items
<<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> set, each curve used to define the face bounds shall be either a
// conic
<<express:geometry_schema.conic,conic>>, a
// line
<<express:geometry_schema.line,line>>, or a
// polyline
<<express:geometry_schema.polyline,polyline>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.elementary_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR6"
For each
// manifold_solid_brep
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep,manifold_solid_brep>> in the
// items
<<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> set, the edges used to define the boundaries shall all be trimmed by vertices of type
// vertex_point
<<express:topology_schema.vertex_point,vertex_point>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.elementary_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR7"
For each
// manifold_solid_brep
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep,manifold_solid_brep>> in the
// items
<<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> set, each
// polyline
<<express:geometry_schema.polyline,polyline>> used to define part of the face bounds shall contain 3 or more points.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.elementary_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR8"
For each
// manifold_solid_brep
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep,manifold_solid_brep>> in the
// items
<<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> set, the outer shell attribute shall not be of type
// oriented_closed_shell
<<express:topology_schema.oriented_closed_shell,oriented_closed_shell>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.elementary_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR9"
If a
// brep_with_voids
<<express:geometric_model_schema.brep_with_voids,brep_with_voids>> is included in the
// items
<<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> set, each shell in the
// voids
<<express:geometric_model_schema.brep_with_voids.voids,voids>> set shall be an
// oriented_closed_shell
<<express:topology_schema.oriented_closed_shell,oriented_closed_shell>> with orientation value FALSE.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.elementary_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR10"
If a
// mapped_item
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>> is included in the
// items
<<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> set, the
// mapped_representation
<<express:representation_schema.representation_map.mapped_representation,mapped_representation>> of the
// mapping_source
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item.mapping_source,mapping_source>> attribute shall be an
// elementary_brep_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.elementary_brep_shape_representation,elementary_brep_shape_representation>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.elementary_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR10.__note"
If a
// cartesian_transformation_operator_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_transformation_operator_3d,cartesian_transformation_operator_3d>> is included as
// mapped_item.mapping_target
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item.mapping_target,mapping_target>> with an
// axis2_placement_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.axis2_placement_3d,axis2_placement_3d>> that corresponds to the original coordinate system as
// mapped_representation.mapping_origin
<<express:representation_schema.representation_map.mapping_origin,mapping_origin>>, the resulting
// mapped_item
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>> is a transformed copy of the
// elementary_brep_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.elementary_brep_shape_representation,elementary_brep_shape_representation>>. The precise definition of the transformation, including translation, rotation, scaling and, if appropriate, mirroring, is given by the transformation operator.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.elementary_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR11"
For each
// manifold_solid_brep
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep,manifold_solid_brep>> in the
// items
<<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> set, any
// vertex_loop
<<express:topology_schema.vertex_loop,vertex_loop>> used to define a face bound shall reference a
// vertex_point
<<express:topology_schema.vertex_point,vertex_point>> with the geometry defined by a
// cartesian_point
<<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_point,cartesian_point>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.advanced_brep_shape_representation"
An **advanced_brep_shape_representation** is a type of
// shape_representation
<<express:product_property_representation_schema.shape_representation,shape_representation>> in which the representation items are specialisations of
// manifold_solid_brep
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep,manifold_solid_brep>> entities. These specialisations differ from the more general B-rep in that they shall only use explicit geometric forms for their face and edge geometry. The face geometry is restricted to elementary surfaces, swept surfaces or B-spline surfaces.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.advanced_brep_shape_representation.items"
one or more of:
// shell_based_surface_models
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep,manifold_solid_brep>> instances,
// mapped_item
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>> instances, or
// axis2_placement_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.axis2_placement_3d,axis2_placement_3d>> instances.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.advanced_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR1"
At least one item in the
// item
<<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> set shall be a
// manifold_solid_brep
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep,manifold_solid_brep>> entity or a
// mapped_item
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>> (see also WR5).
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.advanced_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR2"
For each
// manifold_solid_brep
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep,manifold_solid_brep>> in the
// item
<<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> set each face shall be an
// advanced_face
<<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>>. This ensures that the following conditions are met:

* each
// face
<<express:topology_schema.face,face>> is a
// face_surface
<<express:topology_schema.face_surface,face_surface>>;
* each
// face_surface
<<express:topology_schema.face_surface,face_surface>> has its geometry defined by an
// elementary_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.elementary_surface,elementary_surface>>,
// swept_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.swept_surface,swept_surface>> or a
// b_spline_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_surface,b_spline_surface>>;
* the
// edge
<<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> instances used to define the boundaries of the
// face
<<express:topology_schema.face,face>> shall all reference an
// edge_curve
<<express:topology_schema.edge_curve,edge_curve>>;
* each curve used to define the geometry of the faces and face bounds shall be either a
// conic
<<express:geometry_schema.conic,conic>>, or a
// line
<<express:geometry_schema.line,line>> or a
// polyline
<<express:geometry_schema.polyline,polyline>> or a
// b_spline_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_curve,b_spline_curve>>;
* the
// edge
<<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> instances used to define the
// face
<<express:topology_schema.face,face>> boundaries shall all be trimmed by vertices of type
// vertex_points
<<express:topology_schema.vertex_point,vertex_point>>;
* no loop used to define a
// face_bound
<<express:topology_schema.face_bound,face_bound>> shall be of the oriented subtype.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.advanced_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR2.__note"
The call to function
// msb_shells
<<express:geometric_model_schema.msb_shells,msb_shells>> is correct since, although the generic type of the argument `msb' is
// representation_item
<<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>>, `msb' has been selected by QUERY to be of type
// manifold_solid_brep
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep,manifold_solid_brep>>.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.advanced_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR3"
For each
// manifold_solid_brep
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep,manifold_solid_brep>> in the
// item
<<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> set the outer shell attribute shall not be of the oriented subtype.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.advanced_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR4"
If a
// brep_with_voids
<<express:geometric_model_schema.brep_with_voids,brep_with_voids>> is included in the
// items
<<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> set then each shell in the
// voids
<<express:geometric_model_schema.brep_with_voids.voids,voids>> set shall be an
// oriented_closed_shell
<<express:topology_schema.oriented_closed_shell,oriented_closed_shell>>. with orientation value FALSE.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.advanced_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR5"
If a
// mapped_item
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>> is included in the
// items
<<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> set then the
// mapped_representation
<<express:representation_schema.representation_map.mapped_representation,mapped_representation>> of the
// mapping_source
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item.mapping_source,mapping_source>> attribute shall be an **advanced_brep_shape_representation**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.advanced_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR5.__note"
If a
// cartesian_transformation_operator_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_transformation_operator_3d,cartesian_transformation_operator_3d>> is included as
// mapped_item.mapping_target
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item.mapping_target,mapping_target>> with an
// axis2_placement_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.axis2_placement_3d,axis2_placement_3d>> corresponding to the original coordinate system as
// mapped_representation.mapping_origin
<<express:representation_schema.representation_map.mapping_origin,mapping_origin>>, then the resulting
// mapped_item
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>> is a transformed copy of the *advanced_brep_shape_representation*. The precise definition of the transformation, including translation, rotation, scaling and, if appropriate, mirroring, is given by the transformation operator.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_brep_shape_representation"
A **tessellated_brep_shape_representation** is a type of
// shape_representation
<<express:product_property_representation_schema.shape_representation,shape_representation>> in which tessellated elements are used to compose the
// shape_representation
<<express:product_property_representation_schema.shape_representation,shape_representation>>. These differ from the more general B-rep in having only explicit tessellated geometric forms associated with their faces, edges, and vertices. The faces are restricted to
// tessellated_face_surface
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face_surface,tessellated_face_surface>> instances. The edges are restricted to
// tessellated_edge_curve
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge_curve,tessellated_edge_curve>> instances. The vertices are restricted to
// tessellated_vertex_point
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_vertex_point,tessellated_vertex_point>> instances.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_brep_shape_representation.items"
one or more of:
// manifold_solid_brep
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep,manifold_solid_brep>> instances,
// mapped_item
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>> instances or,
// axis2_placement_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.axis2_placement_3d,axis2_placement_3d>> instances.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR1"
At least one item in the
// item
<<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> set shall be a
// manifold_solid_brep
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep,manifold_solid_brep>> entity or a
// mapped_item
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR2"
All faces used in constructing a
// manifold_solid_brep
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep,manifold_solid_brep>> shall be of type
// tessellated_face_surface
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face_surface,tessellated_face_surface>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR2.__note"
The call to function
// msb_shells
<<express:geometric_model_schema.msb_shells,msb_shells>> in later rules is correct since, although the generic type of the argument 'msb' is
// representation_item
<<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>>, 'msb' has been selected by QUERY to be of type
// manifold_solid_brep
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep,manifold_solid_brep>>.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR3"
For each
// manifold_solid_brep
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep,manifold_solid_brep>> in the
// items
<<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> set, the edges used to define the boundaries shall all be of type
// tessellated_edge_curve
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge_curve,tessellated_edge_curve>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR4"
For each
// manifold_solid_brep
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep,manifold_solid_brep>> in the
// items
<<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> set, the edges used to define the boundaries shall all be trimmed by vertices of type
// tessellated_vertex_point
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_vertex_point,tessellated_vertex_point>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR5"
For each
// manifold_solid_brep
<<express:geometric_model_schema.manifold_solid_brep,manifold_solid_brep>> in the
// items
<<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> set, the outer shell attribute shall not be of type
// oriented_closed_shell
<<express:topology_schema.oriented_closed_shell,oriented_closed_shell>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR6"
If a
// brep_with_voids
<<express:geometric_model_schema.brep_with_voids,brep_with_voids>> is included in the
// items
<<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> set, each shell in the
// voids
<<express:geometric_model_schema.brep_with_voids.voids,voids>> set shall be an
// oriented_closed_shell
<<express:topology_schema.oriented_closed_shell,oriented_closed_shell>>. with orientation value FALSE.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR7"
If a
// mapped_item
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>> is included in the
// items
<<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> set, the
// mapped_representation
<<express:representation_schema.representation_map.mapped_representation,mapped_representation>> of the
// mapping_source
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item.mapping_source,mapping_source>> attribute shall be an
// tessellated_brep_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_brep_shape_representation,tessellated_brep_shape_representation>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR7.__note"
If a
// cartesian_transformation_operator_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_transformation_operator_3d,cartesian_transformation_operator_3d>> is included as
// mapped_item.mapping_target
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item.mapping_target,mapping_target>> with an
// axis2_placement_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.axis2_placement_3d,axis2_placement_3d>>, that corresponds to the original coordinate system as
// mapped_representation.mapping_origin
<<express:representation_schema.representation_map.mapping_origin,mapping_origin>>, the resulting
// mapped_item
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>> is a transformed copy of the
// tessellated_brep_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_brep_shape_representation,tessellated_brep_shape_representation>>. The precise definition of the transformation, including translation, rotation, scaling and, if appropriate, mirroring, is given by the transformation operator.
*)

(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_manifold_subsurface_shape_representation"
A **tessellated_manifold_subsurface_shape_representation** is a type of
// shape_representation
<<express:product_property_representation_schema.shape_representation,shape_representation>> in which the shape of a product is represented by a combination of specialisations of
// connected_face_sub_set
<<express:topology_schema.connected_face_sub_set,connected_face_sub_set>> and tessellated entities.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_manifold_subsurface_shape_representation.items"
one or more of
// connected_face_sub_set
<<express:topology_schema.connected_face_sub_set,connected_face_sub_set>>,
// mapped_item
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>> or,
// axis2_placement_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.axis2_placement_3d,axis2_placement_3d>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_manifold_subsurface_shape_representation.wr:WR1"
At least one of the
// items
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_manifold_subsurface_shape_representation.items,items>> shall be either a
// connected_face_sub_set
<<express:topology_schema.connected_face_sub_set,connected_face_sub_set>> or a
// mapped_item
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_manifold_subsurface_shape_representation.wr:WR2"
Each
// mapped_item
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>> shall indirectly reference a **tessellated_manifold_subsurface_shape_representation**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_manifold_subsurface_shape_representation.wr:WR3"
Any instance of
// connected_face_sub_set
<<express:topology_schema.connected_face_sub_set,connected_face_sub_set>> in the
// items
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_manifold_subsurface_shape_representation.items,items>> set shall be of type
// connected_face_sub_set
<<express:topology_schema.connected_face_sub_set,connected_face_sub_set>> AND
// tessellated_open_shell
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_open_shell,tessellated_open_shell>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_manifold_subsurface_shape_representation.wr:WR4"
For any instance of
// subface
<<express:topology_schema.subface,subface>> in the
// cfs_faces
<<express:topology_schema.connected_face_set.cfs_faces,cfs_faces>> of a
// connected_face_sub_set
<<express:topology_schema.connected_face_sub_set,connected_face_sub_set>> instance, the bounding edge instances shall be of type
// tessellated_subedge_curve
<<express:topology_schema.subedge,subedge>> or of type
// tessellated_edge_curve
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge_curve,tessellated_edge_curve>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_manifold_subsurface_shape_representation.wr:WR5"
For any instance of
// subface
<<express:topology_schema.subface,subface>> in the
// cfs_faces
<<express:topology_schema.connected_face_set.cfs_faces,cfs_faces>> of a
// connected_face_sub_set
<<express:topology_schema.connected_face_sub_set,connected_face_sub_set>> instance, all vertices used in the
// face
<<express:topology_schema.face,face>> definition shall be of type
// tessellated_vertex_point
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_vertex_point,tessellated_vertex_point>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_manifold_subsurface_shape_representation.wr:WR6"
The bounds of any
// subface
<<express:topology_schema.subface,subface>> in the
// cfs_faces
<<express:topology_schema.connected_face_set.cfs_faces,cfs_faces>> of a
// connected_face_sub_set
<<express:topology_schema.connected_face_sub_set,connected_face_sub_set>> instance shall be of type
// edge_loop
<<express:topology_schema.edge_loop,edge_loop>>, or of type
// vertex_loop
<<express:topology_schema.vertex_loop,vertex_loop>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_manifold_surface_shape_representation"
A **tessellated_manifold_surface_shape_representation** is a type of
// shape_representation
<<express:product_property_representation_schema.shape_representation,shape_representation>> that describes the shape or portions of the shape of a product
// product
using 2-manifolds with boundaries. A **tessellated_manifold_surface_shape_representation** consists of one or many
// shell_based_surface_models
<<express:geometric_model_schema.shell_based_surface_model,shell_based_surface_model>> instances. Each
// shell_based_surface_model
<<express:geometric_model_schema.shell_based_surface_model,shell_based_surface_model>> is built up of
// open_shells
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_open_shell,tessellated_open_shell>> and
// closed_shells
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_closed_shell,tessellated_closed_shell>> instances.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_manifold_surface_shape_representation.items"
one or more of:
// shell_based_surface_models
<<express:geometric_model_schema.shell_based_surface_model,shell_based_surface_model>> instances,
// mapped_item
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>> instances, or
// axis2_placement_3d
<<express:geometry_schema.axis2_placement_3d,axis2_placement_3d>> instances.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:WR1"
At least one of the
// items
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_manifold_surface_shape_representation.items,items>> shall be either a
// shell_based_surface_model
<<express:geometric_model_schema.shell_based_surface_model,shell_based_surface_model>> or a
// mapped_item
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:WR2"
If there is a
// mapped_item
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>> in a **tessellated_manifold_surface_shape_representation**, the
// mapped_representation
<<express:representation_schema.representation_map.mapped_representation,mapped_representation>> of its
// mapping_source
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item.mapping_source,mapping_source>> shall also be a **tessellated_manifold_surface_shape_representation** and there shall be at least one
// shell_based_surface_model
<<express:geometric_model_schema.shell_based_surface_model,shell_based_surface_model>> included in that **tessellated_manifold_surface_shape_representation**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_manifold_surface_shape_representation.wr:WR3"
The boundary of a
// shell_based_surface_model
<<express:geometric_model_schema.shell_based_surface_model,shell_based_surface_model>>, that is its attribute
// sbsm_boundary
<<express:geometric_model_schema.shell_based_surface_model.sbsm_boundary,sbsm_boundary>>, shall be defined by using only
// tessellated_open_shells
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_open_shell,tessellated_open_shell>> instances, or
// tessellated_closed_shells
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_closed_shell,tessellated_closed_shell>> instances.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_vertex_point"
A **tessellated_vertex_point** is a type of
// geometric_representation_item
<<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_item,geometric_representation_item>> that is a tessellated form of
// vertex_point
<<express:topology_schema.vertex_point,vertex_point>>, but is not a type of
// vertex_point
<<express:topology_schema.vertex_point,vertex_point>>, for use in
// tessellated_brep_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_brep_shape_representation,tessellated_brep_shape_representation>> instances. The geometry is defined by the associated
// tessellated_vertex
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_vertex,tessellated_vertex>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_vertex_point.tessellated_vertex_geometry"
a
// tessellated_vertex
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_vertex,tessellated_vertex>> provides the geometric representation for the **tessellated_vertex_point**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_vertex_point.wr:WR1"
The
// topological_link
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_vertex.topological_link,topological_link>> of the
// tessellated_vertex
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_vertex,tessellated_vertex>> referenced by
// tessellated_vertex_geometry
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_vertex_point.tessellated_vertex_geometry,tessellated_vertex_geometry>> shall not be provided.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_vertex_point.wr:WR2"
A **tessellated_vertex_point** shall not be a
// vertex_point
<<express:topology_schema.vertex_point,vertex_point>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_vertex_point.wr:IP1"
The domain of the **tessellated_vertex_point** is formally defined to be the domain of its
// tessellated_vertex_geometry
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_vertex_point.tessellated_vertex_geometry,tessellated_vertex_geometry>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge_curve"
A **tessellated_edge_curve** is a type of
// geometric_representation_item
<<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_item,geometric_representation_item>> that is a tessellated form of
// edge_curve
<<express:topology_schema.edge_curve,edge_curve>>, but is not a type of
// edge_curve
<<express:topology_schema.edge_curve,edge_curve>>, for use in
// tessellated_brep_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_brep_shape_representation,tessellated_brep_shape_representation>> instances. The geometry is defined by the associated
// tessellated_edge
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge,tessellated_edge>>. As the topological and geometric directions may be opposed, an indicator
// same_sense
(<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge_curve.same_sense,same_sense>>) is used to identify whether the directions of the edge topology and
// tessellated_edge
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge,tessellated_edge>> geometry agree or are opposed. The Boolean value indicates whether the
// tessellated_edge
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge,tessellated_edge>>. direction agrees with (TRUE) or is in the opposite direction (FALSE) to the
// edge
<<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> direction. Any geometry associated with the vertices of the
// edge
<<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> shall be consistent with the edge geometry.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge_curve.tessellated_edge_geometry"
a
// tessellated_edge
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge,tessellated_edge>> provides a geometric representation for the **tessellated_edge_curve**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge_curve.same_sense"
the relationship of the topological sense of this entity to that of the **tessellated_edge_geometry** ; if TRUE, the topological sense as used coincides with the sense of the **tessellated_edge_geometry**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge_curve.wr:WR1"
If the optional
// geometric_link
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge.geometric_link,geometric_link>> of the
// tessellated_edge
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge,tessellated_edge>> is provided, then the type of that link shall be
// curve
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge_curve.wr:WR2"
A **tessellated_edge_curve** shall not be a
// edge_curve
<<express:topology_schema.edge_curve,edge_curve>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge_curve.wr:WR3"
Both
// edge_start
<<express:topology_schema.edge.edge_start,edge_start>> and
// edge_end
<<express:topology_schema.edge.edge_end,edge_end>> of the **tessellated_edge_curve** shall be
// vertex_point
<<express:topology_schema.vertex_point,vertex_point>> instances.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge_curve.wr:WR4"
If a **tessellated_edge_curve** is a
// subedge
<<express:topology_schema.subedge,subedge>> then the
// parent_edge
<<express:topology_schema.subedge.parent_edge,parent_edge>> shall be a **tessellated_edge_curve**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge_curve.wr:IP1"
The domain of the **tessellated_edge_curve** is formally defined to be the domain of its **tessellated_edge_geometry** as trimmed by the vertices. This domain does not include the vertices.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge_curve.wr:IP2"
The extent of a **tessellated_edge_curve** shall be finite and nonzero.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge_curve.wr:IP3"
A **tessellated_edge_curve** is a manifold.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge_curve.wr:IP4"
A **tessellated_edge_curve** is arcwise connected.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge_curve.wr:IP5"
The edge start is not part of the edge domain.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge_curve.wr:IP6"
The edge end is not part of the edge domain.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge_curve.wr:IP7"
Vertex geometry shall be consistent with edge geometry.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face_surface"
A **tessellated_face_surface** is a type of
// geometric_representation_item
<<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_item,geometric_representation_item>> that is a tessellated form of
// face_surface
<<express:topology_schema.face_surface,face_surface>>, but is not a type of
// face_surface
<<express:topology_schema.face_surface,face_surface>>, for use in
// tessellated_brep_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_brep_shape_representation,tessellated_brep_shape_representation>> instances. The geometry is defined by the associated
// tessellated_face
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face,tessellated_face>>. As both the face topology and the
// tessellated_face
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face,tessellated_face>> geometry have defined normal directions, a BOOLEAN flag (the orientation attribute) is used to indicate whether the
// tessellated_face
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face,tessellated_face>> geometric normal agrees with (TRUE) or is opposed to (FALSE) the topological face normal direction. The tessellated geometry associated with any component of the loops of the face shall be consistent with the
// tessellated_face
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face,tessellated_face>> geometry, in the sense that each domain of the vertex and edge geometric references is completely contained in the
// tessellated_face
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face,tessellated_face>> geometry.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face_surface.tessellated_face_geometry"
a
// tessellated_face
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face,tessellated_face>> provides a geometric representation for the **tessellated_face_surface**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face_surface.same_sense"
the relationship of the topological sense of this entity to that of the **tessellated_face_geometry** ; if TRUE, the topological sense as used coincides with the sense of the **tessellated_face_geometry**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face_surface.wr:WR1"
If the optional
// geometric_link
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face.geometric_link,geometric_link>> of the
// tessellated_face
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face,tessellated_face>> is provided, then the type of that link shall be
// surface
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face_surface.wr:WR2"
A **tessellated_face_surface** shall not be a
// face_surface
<<express:topology_schema.face_surface,face_surface>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face_surface.wr:WR3"
If a **tessellated_face_surface** is a
// subface
<<express:topology_schema.subface,subface>>, the
// parent_face
<<express:topology_schema.subface.parent_face,parent_face>> shall be a **tessellated_face_surface**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face_surface.wr:IP1"
The domain of the **tessellated_face_surface** is formally defined to be the domain of its **tessellated_face_geometry** geometry as trimmed by the loops, this domain does not include the bounding loops.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face_surface.wr:IP2"
A **tessellated_face_surface** has nonzero finite extent.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face_surface.wr:IP3"
A **tessellated_face_surface** is a manifold.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face_surface.wr:IP4"
A **tessellated_face_surface** is arcwise connected.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face_surface.wr:IP5"
A **tessellated_face_surface** has surface genus 0.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face_surface.wr:IP6"
The loops are not part of the face domain.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face_surface.wr:IP7"
Loop geometry shall be consistent with face geometry. This implies that any
// tessellated_edge_curve
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge_curve,tessellated_edge_curve>> instances or
// tessellated_vertex_point
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_vertex_point,tessellated_vertex_point>> instances used in defining the loops bounding the **tessellated_face_surface** shall lie on the **tessellated_face_geometry**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face_surface.wr:IP8"
The loops of the face shall not intersect.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_face_assignment"
A **hybrid_brep_face_assignment** is a type of
// geometric_representation_item
<<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_item,geometric_representation_item>> that associates a topological form of a face with a geometric surface.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_face_assignment.associated_topological_representation_item"
one of
// advanced_face
<<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>>, or
// face_surface
<<express:topology_schema.face_surface,face_surface>>, or
// tessellated_face_surface
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face_surface,tessellated_face_surface>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_face_assignment.hybrid_brep_surface"
one of
// surface
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> or
// tessellated face
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face,tessellated_face>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_face_assignment.owner"
an inverse relationship that specifies thata the **hybrid_brep_face_assignment** is existence dependent on the instance of
// hybrid_brep_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_shape_representation,hybrid_brep_shape_representation>> that specifies the **hybrid_brep_face_assignment** as a member of the
// items
<<express:geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_shape_representation.items,items>> attribute.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_face_assignment.wr:WR1"
The
// hybrid_brep_shape_representation.reference_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_shape_representation.reference_representation,reference_representation>> of the
// hybrid_brep_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_shape_representation,hybrid_brep_shape_representation>> in the role of owner shall directly or indirectly reference the
// hybrid_brep_face_assignment.associated_topological_representation_item
<<express:geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_face_assignment.associated_topological_representation_item,associated_topological_representation_item>> and the
// hybrid_brep_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_shape_representation,hybrid_brep_shape_representation>> in the role of owner shall directly or indirectly reference the instance specified by the
// hybrid_brep_face_assignment.hybrid_brep_surface
<<express:geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_face_assignment.hybrid_brep_surface,hybrid_brep_surface>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_edge_assignment"
A **hybrid_brep_edge_assignment** is a type of
// geometric_representation_item
<<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_item,geometric_representation_item>> that associates a topological form of an edge with a geometric curve.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_edge_assignment.associated_topological_representation_item"
one of <<express:topology_schema.edge_curve,edge_curve>> or <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge_curve,tessellated_edge_curve>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_edge_assignment.hybrid_brep_curve"
one of
// surface
<<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> or
// tessellated face
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge_curve,tessellated_edge_curve>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_edge_assignment.owner"
an inverse relationship that specifies that a **hybrid_brep_edge_assignment** is existence dependent on the instance of
// hybrid_brep_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_shape_representation,hybrid_brep_shape_representation>> that specifies the **hybrid_brep_edge_assignment** as a member of the
// items
<<express:geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_shape_representation.items,items>> attribute.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_edge_assignment.wr:WR1"
The
// hybrid_brep_shape_representation.reference_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_shape_representation.reference_representation,reference_representation>> of the
// hybrid_brep_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_shape_representation,hybrid_brep_shape_representation>> in the role of owner shall directly or indirectly reference the
// hybrid_brep_edge_assignment.associated_topological_representation_item
<<express:geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_edge_assignment.associated_topological_representation_item,associated_topological_representation_item>> and the
// hybrid_brep_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_shape_representation,hybrid_brep_shape_representation>> in the role of owner shall directly or indirectly reference the instance specified by the
// hybrid_brep_edge_assignment.hybrid_brep_curve
<<express:geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_edge_assignment.hybrid_brep_curve,hybrid_brep_curve>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_vertex_assignment"
A **hybrid_brep_vertex_assignment** is a type of
// geometric_representation_item
<<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_item,geometric_representation_item>> that associates a topological form of a vertex with a geometric point.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_vertex_assignment.associated_topological_representation_item"
one of
// vertex_point
<<express:topology_schema.vertex_point,vertex_point>> or
// tessellated_vertex_point
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_vertex_point,tessellated_vertex_point>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_vertex_assignment.hybrid_brep_point"
one of
// surface
<<express:geometry_schema.point,point>> or
// tessellated face
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_vertex,tessellated_vertex>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_vertex_assignment.owner"
an inverse relationship that specifies that a **hybrid_brep_vertex_assignment** is existence dependent on the instance of
// hybrid_brep_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_shape_representation,hybrid_brep_shape_representation>> that specifies the **hybrid_brep_vertex_assignment** as a member of the
// items
<<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> attribute.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_vertex_assignment.wr:WR1"
The
// hybrid_brep_shape_representation.reference_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_shape_representation.reference_representation,reference_representation>> of the
// hybrid_brep_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_shape_representation,hybrid_brep_shape_representation>> in the role of owner shall directly or indirectly reference the
// hybrid_brep_vertex_assignment.associated_topological_representation_item
<<express:geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_vertex_assignment.associated_topological_representation_item,associated_topological_representation_item>> and the
// hybrid_brep_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_shape_representation,hybrid_brep_shape_representation>> in the role of owner shall directly or indirectly reference the instance specified by the
// hybrid_brep_vertex_assignment.hybrid_brep_point
<<express:geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_vertex_assignment.hybrid_brep_point,hybrid_brep_point>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_shape_representation"
A **hybrid_brep_shape_representation** is a type of
// shape_representation
<<express:product_property_representation_schema.shape_representation,shape_representation>> in which the geometry is represented by one or more of:
// hybrid_brep_face_assignment
<<express:geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_face_assignment,hybrid_brep_face_assignment>>, or
// hybrid_brep_edge_assignment
<<express:geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_edge_assignment,hybrid_brep_edge_assignment>>, or
// hybrid_brep_vertex_assignment
<<express:geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_vertex_assignment,hybrid_brep_vertex_assignment>>, or
// mapped_item
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_shape_representation.associated_geometric_representation"
a set of
// shape_representation
<<express:product_property_representation_schema.shape_representation,shape_representation>> instances that provide the geometric model or the **hybrid_brep_shape_representation**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_shape_representation.items"
one or more
// hybrid_brep_face_assignment
<<express:geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_face_assignment,hybrid_brep_face_assignment>>, or
// hybrid_brep_edge_assignment
<<express:geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_edge_assignment,hybrid_brep_edge_assignment>>, or
// hybrid_brep_vertex_assignment
<<express:geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_vertex_assignment,hybrid_brep_vertex_assignment>>, or
// mapped_item
<<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_shape_representation.context_of_items"
a
// geometric_representation_context
<<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_context,geometric_representation_context>> provided to establish a unified context for the **hybrid_brep_shape_representation**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_shape_representation.reference_representation"
one of
// advanced_brep_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.advanced_brep_shape_representation,advanced_brep_shape_representation>>, or
// faceted_brep_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.faceted_brep_shape_representation,faceted_brep_shape_representation>>, or
// hybrid_brep_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_shape_representation,hybrid_brep_shape_representation>>, or
// tessellated_brep_shape_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_brep_shape_representation,tessellated_brep_shape_representation>>, that provides a topological reference model for the **hybrid_brep_shape_representation**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR1"
The dimensionality of the geometric context shall be 3.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR2"
The **hybrid_brep_shape_representation** shall not be included in the <<express:geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_shape_representation.associated_geometric_representation,associated_geometric_representation>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR3"
The
// reference_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_shape_representation.reference_representation,reference_representation>> shall not be included in the
// associated_geometric_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_shape_representation.associated_geometric_representation,associated_geometric_representation>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_shape_representation.wr:WR4"
The **hybrid_brep_shape_representation** shall not also be the
// reference_representation
<<express:geometric_model_schema.hybrid_brep_shape_representation.reference_representation,reference_representation>>.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_open_shell"
A **tessellated_open_shell** is a type of
// open_shell
<<express:topology_schema.open_shell,open_shell>> that contains only tessellated forms of geometry associated with the faces, edges, and vertices.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_open_shell.wr:WR1"
Only
// tessellated_face_surface
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face_surface,tessellated_face_surface>> instances shall be in the set of face instances for a **tessellated_open_shell**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_open_shell.wr:WR2"
Only
// tessellated_edge_curve
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge_curve,tessellated_edge_curve>> instances shall be in the face bound instancess for a **tessellated_open_shell**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_open_shell.wr:WR3"
Only
// tessellated_vertex_point
<<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_vertex_point,tessellated_vertex_point>> instances shall be in the role of start or end for a face bound for a **tessellated_open_shell**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_closed_shell"
A **tessellated_closed_shell** is a type of
// closed_shell
<<express:topology_schema.closed_shell,closed_shell>> that contains only tessellated forms of geometry associated with the faces, edges, and vertices.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_closed_shell.wr:WR1"
Only <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_face_surface,tessellated_face_surface>> instances shall be in the set of face instances for a **tessellated_closed_shell**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_closed_shell.wr:WR2"
Only <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_edge_curve,tessellated_edge_curve>> instances shall be in the face bound instances for a **tessellated_closed_shell**.
*)


(*"geometric_model_schema.tessellated_closed_shell.wr:WR3"
Only <<express:geometric_model_schema.tessellated_vertex_point,tessellated_vertex_point>> instances shall be in the role of start or end for a face bound for a **tessellated_closed_shell**.
*)


