the entity instance for which an **reference_in** is defined.
*)


(*"management_resources_schema.reference_in.ur:UR1"
Within an exchange set all **id** s shall be unique.
*)


(*"management_resources_schema.reference_in.ur:UR2"
For a **target** instance at most one **reference_in** shall be defined.
*)


(*"management_resources_schema.security_classification_assignment"
A **security_classification_assignment** is an association of a <<express:security_classification_schema.security_classification,security_classification>> with product data.
*)


(*"management_resources_schema.security_classification_assignment.assigned_security_classification"
the instance of the <<express:security_classification_schema.security_classification,security_classification>> entity data type that is to be associated with product data.
*)


(*"management_resources_schema.security_classification_assignment.role"
the <<express:basic_attribute_schema.object_role,object_role>> that specifies the purpose of the association of the **security_classification_assignment** with product data.
*)


(*"management_resources_schema.security_classification_assignment.role.__note"
This attribute is an enhancement to the definition of *security_classification_assignment* using a method that is upwardly compatible with ISO 10303-41:1994
*)

(*"management_resources_schema.security_classification_assignment.wr:WR1"
Each **security_classification_assignment** shall be the <<express:basic_attribute_schema.role_association.item_with_role,item_with_role>> in at most one <<express:basic_attribute_schema.role_association,role_association>>.
*)


(*"management_resources_schema.security_classification_assignment.wr:WR1.__note"
A template for constraining the population of the entity data types defined in the <<express:basic_attribute_schema,basic_attribute_schema>> is described in annex E.
*)

(*"management_resources_schema.time_assignment"
A **time_assignment** is an association of a <<express:date_time_schema.local_time,local_time>> with product data.
*)


(*"management_resources_schema.time_assignment.assigned_time"
the instance of the <<express:date_time_schema.local_time,local_time>> entity data type that is to be associated with product data.
*)


(*"management_resources_schema.time_assignment.role"
the <<express:date_time_schema.time_role,time_role>> that specifies the purpose of the association of the **time_assignment** with product data.
*)

(*"management_resources_schema.time_assignment.role.__example"
'Start time' is an example of a role that may be used to characterize the fact that the *assigned_time* defines the time when some action was expected to start.
*)

(*"management_resources_schema.time_interval_assignment"
A **time_interval_assignment** is an association of a <<express:date_time_schema.time_interval,time_interval>> with product data.
*)


(*"management_resources_schema.time_interval_assignment.assigned_time_interval"
the instance of the <<express:date_time_schema.time_interval,time_interval>> entity data type that is to be associated with product data.
*)


(*"management_resources_schema.time_interval_assignment.role"
the <<express:date_time_schema.time_interval_role,time_interval_role>> that specifies the purpose of the association of the **time_interval_assignment** with product data.
*)


(*"management_resources_schema.acyclic_identification_assignment_relationship"
The **acyclic_identification_assignment_relationship** function determines whether the graph of instances of the entity data type <<express:management_resources_schema.identification_assignment,identification_assignment>> that contains relation as one of its links contains a cycle. This function may be used to evaluate either an <<express:management_resources_schema.identification_assignment_relationship,identification_assignment_relationship>> or any of its subtypes.

The function returns TRUE if no cycle has been detected. Otherwise it returns FALSE.
*)


(*"management_resources_schema.acyclic_identification_assignment_relationship.__note"
The algorithm of the function is explained in annex E.2.
*)

(*"management_resources_schema.acyclic_identification_assignment_relationship.__note"
This function is not used in this schema. It is defined here because other ISO 10303 integrated resources and application protocols that use the <<express:management_resources_schema.identification_assignment_relationship,identification_assignment_relationship>> entity include rules that use this function.
*)

(*"management_resources_schema.acyclic_identification_assignment_relationship.relation"
