(*"material_property_definition_schema.generic_property_relationship"
A **generic_property_relationship** is an association between two members of <<express:material_property_definition_schema.generic_property_definition_select,generic_property_definition_select>>. The meaning of the relationship for a context is specified by the value of the **relation_type** attribute.
*)


(*"material_property_definition_schema.generic_property_relationship.__note"
Relationships captured using this entity may be parent-to-child relationships. Specialisations of this entity state this fact if it is true for the specialisation.
*)

(*"material_property_definition_schema.generic_property_relationship.__note"
This entity, in conjunction with the members of the <<express:material_property_definition_schema.generic_property_definition_select,generic_property_definition_select>> type is based on the relationship template that is described in ISO 10303-41.
*)

(*"material_property_definition_schema.generic_property_relationship.name"
the word or group of words by which the generic property relationship is referred to.
*)


(*"material_property_definition_schema.generic_property_relationship.description"
text that relates the nature of the generic property relationship.
*)


(*"material_property_definition_schema.generic_property_relationship.relating"
one of the members of <<express:material_property_definition_schema.generic_property_definition_select,generic_property_definition_select>> which is a part of the relationship.
*)


(*"material_property_definition_schema.generic_property_relationship.related"
the other member of <<express:material_property_definition_schema.generic_property_definition_select,generic_property_definition_select>> which is part of the relationship.
*)


(*"material_property_definition_schema.generic_property_relationship.related.__note"
If one element of the relationship is dependent on the other then this attribute shall be the dependent one.
*)

(*"material_property_definition_schema.generic_property_relationship.related.__note"
The roles of the *related* and the *relating* is defined in the part of ISO 10303 that uses or specialises this entity.
*)

(*"material_property_definition_schema.generic_property_relationship.relation_type"
the meaning of the relationship.
*)


(*"material_property_definition_schema.generic_property_relationship.wr:WR1"
A **generic_property_relationship** shall not participate in its own definition.
*)


(*"material_property_definition_schema.material_designation"
A **material_designation** is the association of a material designation with a product or a part of a product or with an unrealised product.
*)

(*"material_property_definition_schema.material_designation.__example"
'3105' could be the name of a *material_designation* assigned by an agreement that identifies a class of products containing specified amounts of aluminium, copper, magnesium and manganese.
*)
(*"material_property_definition_schema.material_designation.__example"
'copper' could be the name of a *material_designation* associated with an unrealised product at the design stage to indicate the intention to use a substance with the range of electrical conductivity expected from copper metal.
*)

(*"material_property_definition_schema.material_designation.name"
the word or group of words by which the **material_designation** is referred to.
*)


(*"material_property_definition_schema.material_designation.definitions"
the definition of the product or parts of the product for which the **material_designation** is specified.
*)


(*"material_property_definition_schema.material_designation_characterization"
A **material_designation_characterization** is the characterization of a material designation through its association with either a <<express:material_property_representation_schema.material_property_representation,material_property_representation>> or a <<express:material_property_definition_schema.product_material_composition_relationship,product_material_composition_relationship>>.
*)


(*"material_property_definition_schema.material_designation_characterization.name"
the word or group of words by which the **material_designation_characterization** is referred to.
*)


(*"material_property_definition_schema.material_designation_characterization.description"
a narrative description of the **material_designation_characterization**.
*)


(*"material_property_definition_schema.material_designation_characterization.designation"
the definition of the material designation for which the **material_designation_characterization** is specified.
*)


(*"material_property_definition_schema.material_designation_characterization.property"
the definition of the property for which the **material_designation_characterization** is specified.
*)


(*"material_property_definition_schema.material_property"
A **material_property** is a type of <<express:product_property_definition_schema.property_definition,property_definition>> which shall have conditions that determine its validity when it specifies a property of a <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>>, <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect,shape_aspect>>, or <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect_relationship,shape_aspect_relationship>>.
*)


(*"material_property_definition_schema.material_property.ur:UR1"
The name of each <<express:material_property_definition_schema.material_property,material_property>> that is related to a single <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> or <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect,shape_aspect>> (through their definition attribute) shall be unique within the collection of <<express:material_property_definition_schema.material_property,material_property>> entities which are related through that <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> or <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect,shape_aspect>>.
*)


(*"material_property_definition_schema.material_property.wr:WR1"
If a <<express:material_property_definition_schema.material_property,material_property>> is not to be assigned to a <<express:product_property_definition_schema.characterized_object,characterized_object>> through its <<express:product_property_definition_schema.property_definition.definition,definition>> attribute , all of the <<express:product_property_representation_schema.property_definition_representation,property_definition_representation>> that reference it shall also be <<express:material_property_representation_schema.material_property_representation,material_property_representation>> and will therefore, have associated <<express:material_property_representation_schema.data_environment,data_environment>>.
*)


(*"material_property_definition_schema.product_material_composition_relationship"
A **product_material_composition_relationship** is a type of <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship,product_definition_relationship>>. The **product_material_composition_relationship** associates a material constituent with a product. The product participates in a <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship,product_definition_relationship>> as a <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition,relating_product_definition>>. The constituent participates in a <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship,product_definition_relationship>> as a <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition,related_product_definition>>.
*)


(*"material_property_definition_schema.product_material_composition_relationship.__note"
The spatial location and orientation of the material constituents in the product are specified by their <<express:product_property_definition_schema.product_definition_shape,product_definition_shape>>. By this means the material structure of the product is described.
*)

(*"material_property_definition_schema.product_material_composition_relationship.class"
the name or identifier for the kind of relationship between a constituent and a product.
*)

(*"material_property_definition_schema.product_material_composition_relationship.class.__example"
Possible values of a class include: 'mixture', 'chemically bonded', and 'alloyed'.
*)

(*"material_property_definition_schema.product_material_composition_relationship.constituent_amount"
the quantity of the material constituent in a product and the units in which the quantity is expressed.
*)


(*"material_property_definition_schema.product_material_composition_relationship.constituent_amount.__note"
Examples of elements of the set could be the minimum value, maximum value, typical value. The description of the values as maximum, minimum or typical may be achieved by using the constructs in the <<express:qualified_measure_schema,qualified_measure_schema>>.
*)

(*"material_property_definition_schema.product_material_composition_relationship.composition_basis"
the basis on which a product is decomposed into its constituents.
*)

(*"material_property_definition_schema.product_material_composition_relationship.composition_basis.__example"
Expected values for composition basis include: 'volume', 'weight', 'moles', and 'atoms'.
*)

(*"material_property_definition_schema.product_material_composition_relationship.determination_method"
a description of the procedure by which the constituent amount is determined.
*)


(*"material_property_definition_schema.property_definition_relationship"
A **property_definition_relationship** is an association between two <<express:product_property_definition_schema.property_definition,property_definition>>. The meaning of the relationship for a context is defined in the specialisations of this resource construct.
*)


(*"material_property_definition_schema.property_definition_relationship.__note"
Relationships captured using this entity may be parent-to-child relationships. Specialisations of this entity state this fact if it is true for the specialisation.
*)

(*"material_property_definition_schema.property_definition_relationship.__note"
This entity, in conjunction with the <<express:product_property_definition_schema.property_definition,property_definition>> entity is based on the relationship template that is described in ISO 10303-41.
*)

(*"material_property_definition_schema.property_definition_relationship.name"
the word or group of words by which the property definition relationship is referred to.
*)


(*"material_property_definition_schema.property_definition_relationship.description"
text that relates the nature of the property definition relationship.
*)


(*"material_property_definition_schema.property_definition_relationship.relating_property_definition"
one of the <<express:product_property_definition_schema.property_definition,property_definition>> which is a part of the relationship.
*)


(*"material_property_definition_schema.property_definition_relationship.related_property_definition"
the other <<express:product_property_definition_schema.property_definition,property_definition>> which is part of the relationship.
*)


(*"material_property_definition_schema.property_definition_relationship.related_property_definition.__note"
If one element of the relationship is dependent on the other then this attribute shall be the dependent one.
*)

(*"material_property_definition_schema.property_definition_relationship.related_property_definition.__note"
The roles of the *related_property_definition* and the *relating_property_definition* is defined in the part of ISO 10303 that uses or specialises this entity.
*)

(*"material_property_definition_schema.acyclic_generic_property_relationship"
The **acyclic_generic_property_relationship** function determines whether the graph of instances of members of the select data type <<express:material_property_definition_schema.generic_property_definition_select,generic_property_definition_select>> that contains relation as one of its links contains a cycle. This function may be used to evaluate either a <<express:material_property_definition_schema.generic_property_relationship,generic_property_relationship>> or any of its subtypes.

The function returns TRUE if no cycle has been detected. Otherwise it returns FALSE.
*)


(*"material_property_definition_schema.acyclic_generic_property_relationship.__note"
The algorithm of the function is explained in <<ISO_10303_41,annex=E.2>>.
*)

(*"material_property_definition_schema.acyclic_generic_property_relationship.relation"
(input) the candidate <<express:material_property_definition_schema.generic_property_relationship,generic_property_relationship>> to be checked.
*)


(*"material_property_definition_schema.acyclic_generic_property_relationship.relatives"
(input) the set of instances of members of the select data type <<express:material_property_definition_schema.generic_property_definition_select,generic_property_definition_select>> for which the function is searching in the <<express:material_property_definition_schema.generic_property_relationship.relating,relating>> parameter of the relation argument.
*)


(*"material_property_definition_schema.acyclic_generic_property_relationship.specific_relation"
(input) the fully qualified name of a subtype of the <<express:material_property_definition_schema.generic_property_relationship,generic_property_relationship>> entity.
*)


(*"material_property_definition_schema.acyclic_property_definition_relationship"
The **acyclic_property_definition_relationship** function determines whether or not the given property definitions have been self-defined by the associations made in the specified <<express:material_property_definition_schema.property_definition_relationship,property_definition_relationship>>. This function may be used to evaluate either a <<express:material_property_definition_schema.property_definition_relationship,property_definition_relationship>> or any of its subtypes.
*)


(*"material_property_definition_schema.acyclic_property_definition_relationship.__note"
A specified type of the <<express:material_property_definition_schema.property_definition_relationship,property_definition_relationship>> entity is either a <<express:material_property_definition_schema.property_definition_relationship,property_definition_relationship>> or one of its subtypes. The function returns a value of TRUE is none of the elements of the relatives argument occur in the relation argument which is given in the *specific_relation* argument. Otherwise it returns a value of FALSE.
*)

(*"material_property_definition_schema.acyclic_property_definition_relationship.__note"
This function is not used in this schema. It is defined here because other parts of ISO 10303 that use the <<express:material_property_definition_schema.property_definition_relationship,property_definition_relationship>> entity define rules that use this function.
*)

(*"material_property_definition_schema.acyclic_property_definition_relationship.relation"
(input) the candidate <<express:material_property_definition_schema.property_definition_relationship,property_definition_relationship>> that is to be checked.
*)


(*"material_property_definition_schema.acyclic_property_definition_relationship.relatives"
(input) the set of <<express:product_property_definition_schema.property_definition,property_definition>> which the function is searching for in the <<express:material_property_definition_schema.property_definition_relationship.relating_property_definition,relating_property_definition>> parameter of the relation argument.
*)


(*"material_property_definition_schema.acyclic_property_definition_relationship.specific_relation"
(input) the fully qualified name of a subtype of the <<express:material_property_definition_schema.property_definition_relationship,property_definition_relationship>> entity.
*)


(*"material_property_definition_schema.__schema_file"
data/resource_docs/material_and_other_engineering_properties/resource.xml
*)


