(*"mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.maths_space_context_relationship"
A **maths_space_context_relationship** is a relationship between two instances of <<express:mathematical_context_schema.maths_space_context,maths_space_context>>.
*)


(*"mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.maths_space_context_relationship.id"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> for **the maths_space_context_relationship**.
*)


(*"mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.maths_space_context_relationship.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **maths_space_context_relationship** is known.
*)


(*"mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.maths_space_context_relationship.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **maths_space_context_relationship**. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.maths_space_context_relationship.related_context"
the instance of <<express:mathematical_context_schema.maths_space_context,maths_space_context>> that has a relationship with the <<express:mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.maths_space_context_relationship.relating_context,relating_context>>.
*)


(*"mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.maths_space_context_relationship.relating_context"
the instance of <<express:mathematical_context_schema.maths_space_context,maths_space_context>> that has a relationship with the <<express:mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.maths_space_context_relationship.related_context,related_context>>.
*)


(*"mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.maths_space_context_relationship_description"
A **maths_space_context_relationship_description** i3s a specification that a <<express:mathematical_functions_schema.maths_function,maths_function>> defines the relationship between two instances of <<express:mathematical_context_schema.maths_space_context,maths_space_context>>.

Let:

the relating <<express:mathematical_context_schema.maths_space_context,maths_space_context>> be stem:[A : P -> S_1] ;

the related <<express:mathematical_context_schema.maths_space_context,maths_space_context>> be stem:[B : P -> S_2];

P be a physical space;

stem:[S_1] and stem:[S_2] be two instances of <<express:mathematical_functions_schema.maths_space,maths_space>>;

the description of the relationship between the instances of <<express:mathematical_context_schema.maths_space_context,maths_space_context>> be stem:[T : S_1 -> S_2] (a <<express:mathematical_functions_schema.maths_function,maths_function>>).

An instance of **maths_space_context_relationship_description** specifies that:

stem:[B(p) = T(A(p))] for each p in P.
*)


(*"mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.maths_space_context_relationship_description.id"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> for the <<express:mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.maths_space_context_relationship_description,maths_space_context_relationship_description>>.
*)


(*"mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.maths_space_context_relationship_description.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the <<express:mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.maths_space_context_relationship_description,maths_space_context_relationship_description>> is known.
*)


(*"mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.maths_space_context_relationship_description.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the <<express:mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.maths_space_context_relationship_description,maths_space_context_relationship_description>>. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.maths_space_context_relationship_description.described_relationship"
the <<express:mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.maths_space_context_relationship_description,maths_space_context_relationship_description>> that is described by the description.
*)


(*"mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.maths_space_context_relationship_description.describing_relationship"
the <<express:mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.maths_space_context_relationship,maths_space_context_relationship>> that is described by the description.
*)


(*"mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.normalized_property_distribution_description"
A **normalized_property_distribution_description** is a specification of how a <<express:mathematical_functions_schema.maths_function,maths_function>> describes a property distribution with respect to a reference property distribution.

Let:

* the domain of the property distribution be P (a <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>>, <<express:action_schema.action,action>>, <<express:action_schema.action_method,action_method>>, <<express:process_property_schema.resource_property.resource,resource>> or <<express:product_property_definition_schema.general_property,general_property>>);
* the range of the property distribution be C (a <<express:product_property_definition_schema.general_property,general_property>> as a physical quantity space);
* the property distribution be D:P⟴C (a <<express:product_property_definition_schema.property_definition,property_definition>>, <<express:process_property_schema.action_property,action_property>>, <<express:product_property_definition_schema.general_property_relationship,general_property_relationship>> or <<express:process_property_schema.resource_property,resource_property>>);
* the reference property distribution be stem:[D0 : P -> C] (a <<express:product_property_definition_schema.property_definition,property_definition>>, <<express:process_property_schema.action_property,action_property>>, <<express:product_property_definition_schema.general_property_relationship,general_property_relationship>> or <<express:process_property_schema.resource_property,resource_property>>);
* the parameterisation of the domain of the property distribution be stem:[A : P -> S_1] (a <<express:mathematical_context_schema.maths_space_context,maths_space_context>>);
* the description of the property distribution be stem:[F : S_1 -> S_2] (a <<express:mathematical_functions_schema.maths_function,maths_function>>);
* the domain and range of the maths function be the maths spaces stem:[S_1] and stem:[S_2].

An instance of **normalized_property_distribution_description** specifies that:

stem:[D(p) = F(A(p)).D0(p)] for each p in P.
*)

(*"mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.normalized_property_distribution_description.id"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> for the **normalized_property_distribution_description**.
*)


(*"mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.normalized_property_distribution_description.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **normalized_property_distribution_description** is referenced.
*)


(*"mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.normalized_property_distribution_description.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **normalized_property_distribution_description**. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.normalized_property_distribution_description.abstract_function"
the <<express:mathematical_functions_schema.maths_function,maths_function>> that describes the <<express:mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.normalized_property_distribution_description.physical_function,physical_function>>.
*)


(*"mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.normalized_property_distribution_description.domain_context"
the <<express:mathematical_context_schema.maths_space_context,maths_space_context>> that is used to interpret the domain of the <<express:mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.normalized_property_distribution_description.abstract_function,abstract_function>>.
*)


(*"mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.normalized_property_distribution_description.normalization_basis"
the reference property distribution that is the basis for the description of the <<express:mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.normalized_property_distribution_description.physical_function,physical_function>>.
*)


(*"mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.normalized_property_distribution_description.normalization_basis.__note"
The <<express:mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.normalized_property_distribution_description.physical_function,physical_function>> equals the *normalization_basis* wherever the <<express:mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.normalized_property_distribution_description.abstract_function,abstract_function>> evaluates to 1.
*)

(*"mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.normalized_property_distribution_description.physical_function"
the property distribution that is described by the <<express:mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.normalized_property_distribution_description.physical_function,physical_function>>.
*)


(*"mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.property_distribution_description"
A **property_distribution_description** is a specificiation of how a <<express:mathematical_functions_schema.maths_function,maths_function>> describes a property distribution. Let:

* the domain of the property distribution be P (a <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>>, <<express:action_schema.action,action>>, <<express:action_schema.action_method,action_method>>, resource or <<express:product_property_definition_schema.general_property,general_property>>);
* the range of the property distribution be C (ag <<express:product_property_definition_schema.general_property,general_property>> as a physical quantity space);
* the property distribution be stem:[D : P -> C] (a <<express:product_property_definition_schema.property_definition,property_definition>> , <<express:process_property_schema.action_property,action_property>>, <<express:product_property_definition_schema.general_property_relationship,general_property_relationship>> or <<express:process_property_schema.resource_property,resource_property>>);
* the parameterisation of the domain of the property distribution be stem:[A : P -> S_1] (a <<express:mathematical_context_schema.maths_space_context,maths_space_context>>);
* the scale of the range of the property distribution be stem:[U : C -> S_2] (a <<express:mathematical_context_schema.maths_space_context,maths_space_context>>);
* the description of the property distribution be stem:[F : S_1 -> S_2] (a <<express:mathematical_functions_schema.maths_function,maths_function>>);
* the domain and range of the maths function be the maths spaces stem:[S_1] and stem:[S_2].
* An instance of **property_distribution_description** specifies that:

stem:[D(p) = U-1(F(A(p)))] for each p in P].
*)

(*"mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.property_distribution_description.__note"
U-1 is well defined because U is a 1-1 mapping.
*)

(*"mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.property_distribution_description.id"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> for the **property_distribution_description**.
*)


(*"mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.property_distribution_description.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **property_distribution_description** is known.
*)


(*"mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.property_distribution_description.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **property_distribution_description**. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.property_distribution_description.abstract_function"
the <<express:mathematical_functions_schema.maths_function,maths_function>> that describes the <<express:mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.property_distribution_description.physical_function,physical_function>>.
*)


(*"mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.property_distribution_description.domain_context"
the <<express:mathematical_context_schema.maths_space_context,maths_space_context>> that is used to interpret the domain of the <<express:mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.property_distribution_description.abstract_function,abstract_function>>.
*)


(*"mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.property_distribution_description.physical_function"
the property distribution that is described by the <<express:mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.property_distribution_description.abstract_function,abstract_function>>.
*)


(*"mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.property_distribution_description.range_context"
the <<express:mathematical_context_schema.maths_space_context,maths_space_context>> that is used to interpret the range of the <<express:mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.property_distribution_description.abstract_function,abstract_function>>.
*)


(*"mathematical_description_of_distribution_schema.__schema_file"
data/resource_docs/mathematical_representation/resource.xml
*)


--
-- MATHEMATICAL_FUNCTIONS_SCHEMA (/Users/mulgogi/src/mn/iso-10303/schemas/resources/mathematical_functions_schema/mathematical_functions_schema.exp)
--
