(*"measure_schema.absorbed_dose_measure"
An **absorbed_dose_measure** is the value of an absorbed dose of radiation.
*)


(*"measure_schema.acceleration_measure"
An **acceleration_measure** is the value of the rate of change of velocity.
*)


(*"measure_schema.amount_of_substance_measure"
An **amount_of_substance_measure** is the value for the quantity of a substance when compared with the number of atoms in 0.012 kilogram of carbon 12.
*)


(*"measure_schema.area_measure"
An **area_measure** is the value of the extent of a surface.
*)


(*"measure_schema.capacitance_measure"
A **capacitance_measure** is the value of capacitance.
*)


(*"measure_schema.celsius_temperature_measure"
A **celsius_temperature_measure** is the value for the degree of heat of a body.
*)


(*"measure_schema.conductance_measure"
A **conductance_measure** is the value of an electrical conductance.
*)


(*"measure_schema.context_dependent_measure"
A **context_dependent_measure** is the value of a physical quantity that may be interpreted based on the context in which it is used.
*)


(*"measure_schema.count_measure"
A **count_measure** is the value of a count.
*)


(*"measure_schema.descriptive_measure"
A **descriptive_measure** is a textual value of a physical quantity.
*)


(*"measure_schema.dose_equivalent_measure"
A **dose_equivalent_measure** is the value of the radiation dose equivalent.
*)


(*"measure_schema.electric_charge_measure"
An **electric_charge_measure** is the value of an electrical charge.
*)


(*"measure_schema.electric_current_measure"
An **electric_current_measure** is the value for the movement of electrically charged particles.
*)


(*"measure_schema.electric_potential_measure"
An **electric_potential_measure** is the value of an electrical potential.
*)


(*"measure_schema.energy_measure"
An **energy_measure** is the value of energy, or work done, in a system.
*)


(*"measure_schema.force_measure"
A **force_measure** is the value of a force.
*)


(*"measure_schema.frequency_measure"
A **frequency_measure** is the value of a frequency.
*)


(*"measure_schema.illuminance_measure"
An **illuminance_measure** is the value of illuminance.
*)


(*"measure_schema.inductance_measure"
An **inductance_measure** is the value of inductance.
*)


(*"measure_schema.length_measure"
A **length_measure** is the value of a distance.
*)


(*"measure_schema.luminous_flux_measure"
A **luminous_flux_measure** is the value of luminous flux.
*)


(*"measure_schema.luminous_intensity_measure"
A **luminous_intensity_measure** is the value for the brightness of a body.
*)


(*"measure_schema.magnetic_flux_density_measure"
A **magnetic_flux_density_measure** is the value of magnetic flux density.
*)


(*"measure_schema.magnetic_flux_measure"
A **magnetic_flux_measure** is the value of magnetic flux.
*)


(*"measure_schema.mass_measure"
A **mass_measure** is the value of the amount of matter that a body contains.
*)


(*"measure_schema.measure_value"
A **measure_value** is a value as defined in ISO 31-0.
*)


(*"measure_schema.non_negative_length_measure"
A **non_negative_length_measure** type is a <<express:measure_schema.length_measure,length_measure>> whose value is greater than or equal to zero.
*)


(*"measure_schema.non_negative_length_measure.wr:WR1"
A **non_negative_length_measure** shall be positive or zero.
*)


(*"measure_schema.numeric_measure"
A **numeric_measure** is the numeric value of a physical quantity.
*)


(*"measure_schema.numeric_measure.__note"
In order to define measure quantities that are not included as specific types in this standard a *numeric_measure* may be used as the <<express:measure_schema.measure_with_unit.value_component,value_component>> of a <<express:measure_schema.measure_with_unit,measure_with_unit>>, the corresponding <<express:measure_schema.measure_with_unit.unit_component,unit_component>> being an <<express:measure_schema.si_unit,si_unit>> or a <<express:measure_schema.derived_unit,derived_unit>>.
*)

(*"measure_schema.parameter_value"
A **parameter_value** is the value that specifies the amount of a parameter in a parameter space.
*)


(*"measure_schema.plane_angle_measure"
A **plane_angle_measure** is the value of an angle in a plane.
*)


(*"measure_schema.positive_length_measure"
A **positive_length_measure** is a <<express:measure_schema.length_measure,length_measure>> that is greater than zero.
*)


(*"measure_schema.positive_length_measure.wr:WR1"
The value shall be positive.
*)


(*"measure_schema.positive_plane_angle_measure"
A **positive_plane_angle_measure** is a <<express:measure_schema.plane_angle_measure,plane_angle_measure>> that is greater than zero.
*)


(*"measure_schema.positive_plane_angle_measure.wr:WR1"
The value shall be positive.
*)


(*"measure_schema.positive_ratio_measure"
A **positive_ratio_measure** is a <<express:measure_schema.ratio_measure,ratio_measure>> that is greater than zero.
*)


(*"measure_schema.positive_ratio_measure.wr:WR1"
The value shall be positive.
*)


(*"measure_schema.power_measure"
A **power_measure** is the value of power, or the rate of doing work.
*)


(*"measure_schema.pressure_measure"
A **pressure_measure** is the value of force per unit area.
*)


(*"measure_schema.radioactivity_measure"
A **radioactivity_measure** is the value of the radioactive disintegration.
*)


(*"measure_schema.ratio_measure"
A **ratio_measure** is the value of the relation between two physical quantities that are of the same kind.
*)


(*"measure_schema.resistance_measure"
A **resistance_measure** is the value of electrical resistance.
*)


(*"measure_schema.si_prefix"
An **si_prefix** is the name of a prefix that may be associated with an <<express:measure_schema.si_unit,si_unit>>. The definitions of SI prefixes are specified in ISO 1000.
*)


(*"measure_schema.si_prefix.exa"
see ISO 1000;
*)


