(*"measure_schema.measure_with_unit"
A **measure_with_unit** is the specification of a physical quantity as defined in ISO 31. A **measure_with_unit** may be either a <<express:measure_schema.length_measure_with_unit,length_measure_with_unit>> or a <<express:measure_schema.mass_measure_with_unit,mass_measure_with_unit>>, or a <<express:measure_schema.time_measure_with_unit,time_measure_with_unit>>, or an <<express:measure_schema.electric_current_measure_with_unit,electric_current_measure_with_unit>>, or a <<express:measure_schema.thermodynamic_temperature_measure_with_unit,thermodynamic_temperature_measure_with_unit>>, or a <<express:measure_schema.celsius_temperature_measure_with_unit,celsius_temperature_measure_with_unit>>, or an <<express:measure_schema.amount_of_substance_measure_with_unit,amount_of_substance_measure_with_unit>>, or a <<express:measure_schema.luminous_intensity_measure_with_unit,luminous_intensity_measure_with_unit>>, or a <<express:measure_schema.plane_angle_measure_with_unit,plane_angle_measure_with_unit>>, or a <<express:measure_schema.solid_angle_measure_with_unit,solid_angle_measure_with_unit>>, or an <<express:measure_schema.area_measure_with_unit,area_measure_with_unit>>, or a <<express:measure_schema.volume_measure_with_unit,volume_measure_with_unit>>, or a <<express:measure_schema.ratio_measure_with_unit,ratio_measure_with_unit>>, or an <<express:measure_schema.acceleration_measure_with_unit,acceleration_measure_with_unit>>, or a <<express:measure_schema.capacitance_measure_with_unit,capacitance_measure_with_unit>>, or an <<express:measure_schema.electric_charge_measure_with_unit,electric_charge_measure_with_unit>>, or a <<express:measure_schema.conductance_measure_with_unit,conductance_measure_with_unit>>, or an <<express:measure_schema.electric_potential_measure_with_unit,electric_potential_measure_with_unit>>, or an <<express:measure_schema.energy_measure_with_unit,energy_measure_with_unit>>, or a <<express:measure_schema.magnetic_flux_density_measure_with_unit,magnetic_flux_density_measure_with_unit>>, or a <<express:measure_schema.force_measure_with_unit,force_measure_with_unit>>, or a <<express:measure_schema.frequency_measure_with_unit,frequency_measure_with_unit>>, or an <<express:measure_schema.illuminance_measure_with_unit,illuminance_measure_with_unit>>, or an <<express:measure_schema.inductance_measure_with_unit,inductance_measure_with_unit>>, or a <<express:measure_schema.luminous_flux_measure_with_unit,luminous_flux_measure_with_unit>>, or a <<express:measure_schema.magnetic_flux_measure_with_unit,magnetic_flux_measure_with_unit>>, or a <<express:measure_schema.power_measure_with_unit,power_measure_with_unit>>, or a <<express:measure_schema.pressure_measure_with_unit,pressure_measure_with_unit>>, or a <<express:measure_schema.resistance_measure_with_unit,resistance_measure_with_unit>>, or a <<express:measure_schema.velocity_measure_with_unit,velocity_measure_with_unit>>, or an <<express:measure_schema.absorbed_dose_measure_with_unit,absorbed_dose_measure_with_unit>>, or a <<express:measure_schema.radioactivity_measure_with_unit,radioactivity_measure_with_unit>>, or a <<express:measure_schema.dose_equivalent_measure_with_unit,dose_equivalent_measure_with_unit>>.
*)


(*"measure_schema.measure_with_unit.value_component"
the value of the physical quantity if expressed with respect to the **unit_component**.
*)


(*"measure_schema.measure_with_unit.unit_component"
the unit in which the physical quantity is expressed.
*)


(*"measure_schema.measure_with_unit.wr:WR1"
The **unit_component** shall be a valid unit for the kind of measure specified by the **value_component**.
*)


(*"measure_schema.named_unit"
A **named_unit** is a unit quantity. A **named_unit** may be either a <<express:measure_schema.si_unit,si_unit>> or a <<express:measure_schema.conversion_based_unit,conversion_based_unit>>, or a <<express:measure_schema.context_dependent_unit,context_dependent_unit>>, and additionally may be a <<express:measure_schema.length_unit,length_unit>> or a <<express:measure_schema.mass_unit,mass_unit>>, or a <<express:measure_schema.time_unit,time_unit>>, or an <<express:measure_schema.electric_current_unit,electric_current_unit>>, or a <<express:measure_schema.thermodynamic_temperature_unit,thermodynamic_temperature_unit>>, or an <<express:measure_schema.amount_of_substance_unit,amount_of_substance_unit>>, or a <<express:measure_schema.luminous_flux_unit,luminous_flux_unit>>, or a <<express:measure_schema.luminous_intensity_unit,luminous_intensity_unit>>, or a <<express:measure_schema.plane_angle_unit,plane_angle_unit>>, or a <<express:measure_schema.solid_angle_unit,solid_angle_unit>>, or a <<express:measure_schema.ratio_unit,ratio_unit>>.
*)


(*"measure_schema.named_unit.dimensions"
the exponents of the base properties by which the **named_unit** is defined.
*)


(*"measure_schema.plane_angle_measure_with_unit"
A **plane_angle_measure_with_unit** is a type of <<express:measure_schema.measure_with_unit,measure_with_unit>> in which the physical quantity is a plane angle as defined in ISO 31.
*)


(*"measure_schema.plane_angle_measure_with_unit.wr:WR1"
The unit shall be a <<express:measure_schema.plane_angle_unit,plane_angle_unit>>.
*)


(*"measure_schema.plane_angle_unit"
