*)


(*"measure_schema.si_unit.prefix"
the <<express:measure_schema.si_prefix,si_prefix>> that specifies the ratio with the unit specified by name. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"measure_schema.si_unit.name"
the <<express:measure_schema.si_unit_name,si_unit_name>> by which the **si_unit** is known.
*)


(*"measure_schema.si_unit.dimensions"
the <<express:measure_schema.dimensional_exponents,dimensional_exponents>> for the **si_unit**.
*)


(*"measure_schema.si_unit.wr:WR1"
If the **si_unit** is a <<express:measure_schema.mass_unit,mass_unit>> it shall not be used by a <<express:measure_schema.derived_unit_element,derived_unit_element>> unless the prefix is <<express:measure_schema.si_prefix.kilo,kilo>>.
*)


(*"measure_schema.solid_angle_measure_with_unit"
A **solid_angle_measure_with_unit** is a type of <<express:measure_schema.measure_with_unit,measure_with_unit>> in which the physical quantity is a solid angle as defined in ISO 31.
*)


(*"measure_schema.solid_angle_measure_with_unit.wr:WR1"
The unit shall be a <<express:measure_schema.solid_angle_unit,solid_angle_unit>>.
*)


(*"measure_schema.solid_angle_unit"
A **solid_angle_unit** is a type of <<express:measure_schema.named_unit,named_unit>> in which solid angles are expressed.
*)


(*"measure_schema.solid_angle_unit.wr:WR1"
All the dimensional exponents shall be equal to zero.
*)


(*"measure_schema.thermodynamic_temperature_measure_with_unit"
A **thermodynamic_temperature_measure_with_unit** is a type of <<express:measure_schema.measure_with_unit,measure_with_unit>> in which the physical quantity is a thermodynamic temperature as defined in ISO 31.
*)


(*"measure_schema.thermodynamic_temperature_measure_with_unit.wr:WR1"
The unit shall be a <<express:measure_schema.thermodynamic_temperature_unit,thermodynamic_temperature_unit>>.
*)


(*"measure_schema.thermodynamic_temperature_unit"
A **thermodynamic_temperature_unit** is a type of <<express:measure_schema.named_unit,named_unit>> in which the degree of heat of a body is expressed.
*)


(*"measure_schema.thermodynamic_temperature_unit.__note"
This unit corresponds to one of the seven fundamental quantities as specified in ISO 1000.
*)

(*"measure_schema.thermodynamic_temperature_unit.wr:WR1"
The dimensional exponent of thermodynamic temperature shall be equal to one and the other dimensional exponents shall be equal to zero.
*)


(*"measure_schema.time_measure_with_unit"
A **time_measure_with_unit** is a type of <<express:measure_schema.measure_with_unit,measure_with_unit>> in which the physical quantity is a time as defined in ISO 31.
*)


(*"measure_schema.time_measure_with_unit.wr:WR1"
The unit shall be a <<express:measure_schema.time_unit,time_unit>>.
*)


(*"measure_schema.time_unit"
A **time_unit** is a type of <<express:measure_schema.named_unit,named_unit>> in which the duration of periods is expressed.
*)


(*"measure_schema.time_unit.__note"
This unit corresponds to one of the seven fundamental quantities as specified in ISO 1000.
*)

(*"measure_schema.time_unit.wr:WR1"
The dimensional exponent of time shall be equal to one and all the other dimensional exponents shall be equal to zero.
*)


(*"measure_schema.velocity_measure_with_unit"
A **velocity_measure_with_unit** is a type of <<express:measure_schema.measure_with_unit,measure_with_unit>> in which the quantity measured is a velocity.
*)


(*"measure_schema.velocity_measure_with_unit.wr:WR1"
The <<express:measure_schema.measure_with_unit.unit_component,unit_component>> shall be of type <<express:measure_schema.velocity_unit,velocity_unit>>.
*)


(*"measure_schema.velocity_unit"
A **velocity_unit** is a type of <<express:measure_schema.derived_unit,derived_unit>> in which the velocity is expressed.
*)


(*"measure_schema.velocity_unit.wr:WR1"
The dimensional exponent of length shall be equal to one, the dimensional exponent of time shall be equal to minus one, and all the other dimensional exponents shall be equal to zero.
*)


(*"measure_schema.volume_measure_with_unit"
A **volume_measure_with_unit** is a type of <<express:measure_schema.measure_with_unit,measure_with_unit>> in which the physical quantity is a volume as defined in ISO 31.
*)


(*"measure_schema.volume_measure_with_unit.wr:WR1"
The unit shall be a <<express:measure_schema.volume_unit,volume_unit>>.
*)


(*"measure_schema.volume_unit"
A **volume_unit** is a type of <<express:measure_schema.derived_unit,derived_unit>> used to measure the extent of a solid.
*)


(*"measure_schema.volume_unit.wr:WR1"
The dimensional exponent of length shall be equal to three and all the other dimensional exponents shall be equal to zero.
*)


(*"measure_schema.derive_dimensional_exponents"
The **derive_dimensional_exponents** function determines the dimensional exponents of a unit. For named units the dimensions attribute is returned and for derived units the dimensional exponents are calculated from its elements.
*)


(*"measure_schema.derive_dimensional_exponents.x"
(input) the <<express:measure_schema.unit,unit>> that the <<express:measure_schema.dimensional_exponents,dimensional_exponents>> are being derived from.
*)


(*"measure_schema.dimensions_for_si_unit"
The **dimensions_for_si_unit** function returns the <<express:measure_schema.dimensional_exponents,dimensional_exponents>> of the given <<express:measure_schema.si_unit,si_unit>>.
*)


(*"measure_schema.dimensions_for_si_unit.n"
(input) the name of the <<express:measure_schema.si_unit_name,si_unit_name>> for which the <<express:measure_schema.dimensional_exponents,dimensional_exponents>> will be returned.
*)


(*"measure_schema.valid_units"
The **valid_units** function validates a <<express:measure_schema.measure_with_unit,measure_with_unit>>. If the unit of the <<express:measure_schema.measure_with_unit,measure_with_unit>> is valid the function returns TRUE. Otherwise, it returns FALSE.
*)


(*"measure_schema.valid_units.m"
(input) the candidate <<express:measure_schema.measure_with_unit,measure_with_unit>> that is to be checked.
*)


