--
-- PROCESS_PROPERTY_REPRESENTATION_SCHEMA (/Users/mulgogi/src/mn/iso-10303/schemas/resources/process_property_representation_schema/process_property_representation_schema.exp)
--
SCHEMA process_property_representation_schema '{ iso standard 10303 part(49) version(1) object(1) process-property-representation-schema(3) }';

REFERENCE FROM support_resource_schema
  (label,
   text);

REFERENCE FROM representation_schema
  (representation);

REFERENCE FROM process_property_schema
  (action_property,
   resource_property);

ENTITY action_property_representation;
  name           : label;
  description    : text;
  property       : action_property;
  representation : representation;
END_ENTITY;

ENTITY resource_property_representation;
  name           : label;
  description    : text;
  property       : resource_property;
  representation : representation;
END_ENTITY;

END_SCHEMA; -- process_property_representation_schema



(*"process_property_representation_schema"

The subject of the *process_property_representation_schema* is the representation of the properties required by either a resource, an action, or a potential action to affect a process.

*)

(*"process_property_representation_schema.__fund_cons"

This clause supports the representation of a process property. A process property representation may be one of the following:

* resource parameter values;
* action parameter values.

NOTE: Usage of parameter values is not specified in this document.

A given process property may be represented in different ways.

*)

(*"process_property_representation_schema.action_property_representation"

An <<express:process_property_representation_schema.action_property_representation,action_property_representation>> is the representation of the property of an *action* or the *action_method* to affect a process. The representation specifies the realization of the property that the *action* exhibits or the *action_method* exhibits to affect a process.

[EXAMPLE]
====
Spindle speed is an <<express:process_property_schema.action_property,action_property>>. The parameter value "2200 r.p.m." is the *descriptive_representation_item.description* of the property spindle speed.
====

[EXAMPLE]
====
The value "20 days" is the *descriptive_representation_item.description* of the <<express:process_property_schema.action_property,action_property>> "time to complete".
====

*)

(*"process_property_representation_schema.action_property_representation.name"

the word or group of words by which the <<express:process_property_representation_schema.action_property_representation,action_property_representation>> is referred to.

*)

(*"process_property_representation_schema.action_property_representation.description"

a description of the property representation.

*)

(*"process_property_representation_schema.action_property_representation.property"

the characteristic of the *action* or the *action_method* to effect a process that is being represented.

*)

(*"process_property_representation_schema.action_property_representation.representation"

the <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> of the *property* of the *action* or the *action_method* to effect a process.

*)

(*"process_property_representation_schema.resource_property_representation"

A <<express:process_property_representation_schema.resource_property_representation,resource_property_representation>> is the representation of the property of a resource. The representation specifies the realization of the property that the resource exhibits.

NOTE: There are different ways that a given property may be equivalently represented.

[EXAMPLE]
====
A laser inspection machine is an *action_resource*. The table size is the <<express:process_property_schema.resource_property,resource_property>>; the text "1 meter by 2 meters" is the value of a <<express:process_property_representation_schema.resource_property_representation,resource_property_representation>> of the table size.
====

[EXAMPLE]
====
A person is an *action_resource_requirement*. The person's "typing speed" is the <<express:process_property_schema.resource_property,resource_property>>. The value of "20 words per minute" is the <<express:process_property_representation_schema.resource_property_representation,resource_property_representation>>. This is represented through <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>>.
====

*)

(*"process_property_representation_schema.resource_property_representation.name"

the word or group of words by which the <<express:process_property_representation_schema.resource_property_representation,resource_property_representation>> is referred to.

*)

(*"process_property_representation_schema.resource_property_representation.description"

a description of the representation.

*)

(*"process_property_representation_schema.resource_property_representation.property"

the characteristic of the resource being represented.

*)

(*"process_property_representation_schema.resource_property_representation.representation"

the <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> of the property of the resource.

*)

(*"process_property_representation_schema.__expressg"
[[process_property_representation_schema_expg1]]
[.svgmap]
====
image::images/process_property_representation_schemaexpg1.svg[]
====
*)


--
-- PROCESS_PROPERTY_SCHEMA (/Users/mulgogi/src/mn/iso-10303/schemas/resources/process_property_schema/process_property_schema.exp)
--
(*
ISO 10303 TC184/SC4/WG12 N8548

EXPRESS Source:
ISO 10303-49 ed1 Process structure and properties - Process property schema

The following permission notice and disclaimer shall be included in all copies of this EXPRESS schema ("the Schema"),
and derivations of the Schema:

Copyright ISO 2014  All rights reserved
Permission is hereby granted, free of charge in perpetuity, to any person obtaining a copy of the Schema,
to use, copy, modify, merge and distribute free of charge, copies of the Schema for the purposes of developing,
implementing, installing and using software based on the Schema, and to permit persons to whom the Schema is furnished to do so,
subject to the following conditions:

THE SCHEMA IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED,
INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT.
IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM,
DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE,
ARISING FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SCHEMA OR THE
USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE SCHEMA.

In addition, any modified copy of the Schema shall include the following notice:

THIS SCHEMA HAS BEEN MODIFIED FROM THE SCHEMA DEFINED IN
ISO 10303-49 ed1 Process structure and properties - Process property schema
AND SHOULD NOT BE INTERPRETED AS COMPLYING WITH THAT STANDARD
*)

SCHEMA process_property_schema '{iso standard 10303 part(49) version(1) object(1) process-property-schema(3)}';

REFERENCE FROM action_schema
    (action,
     action_method,
     action_method_relationship,
     action_relationship,
     action_resource,
     action_resource_relationship,
     acyclic_action_relationship);

REFERENCE FROM product_property_definition_schema
    (characterized_product_definition,
     property_definition,
     shape_definition);

REFERENCE FROM support_resource_schema
    (identifier,
     label,
     text);

TYPE characterized_action_definition = SELECT
   (action,
   action_method,
   action_method_relationship,
   action_relationship);
END_TYPE;

TYPE characterized_resource_definition = SELECT
  (action_resource,
   action_resource_relationship,
   action_resource_requirement,
   action_resource_requirement_relationship);
END_TYPE;

TYPE property_or_shape_select = SELECT
     (property_definition,
      shape_definition);
END_TYPE;

ENTITY action_property;
  name        : label;
  description : text;
  definition  : characterized_action_definition;
END_ENTITY;

ENTITY product_definition_process
  SUBTYPE OF (action);
  identification : identifier;
INVERSE
  product_definitions : SET [1:?] OF process_product_association FOR process;
END_ENTITY;

ENTITY process_product_association;
  name            : label;
  description     : text;
  defined_product : characterized_product_definition;
  process         : product_definition_process;
END_ENTITY;

ENTITY property_process
  SUBTYPE OF (action);
  identification : identifier;
INVERSE
  properties : SET [1:?] OF process_property_association FOR process;
END_ENTITY;

ENTITY process_property_association;
  name              : label;
  description       : text;
  process           : property_process;
  property_or_shape : property_or_shape_select;
END_ENTITY;

ENTITY replacement_relationship
  SUBTYPE OF (action_relationship);
WHERE
  WR1: acyclic_action_relationship (SELF,
       [SELF\action_relationship.related_action],
       'PROCESS_PROPERTY_SCHEMA.REPLACEMENT_RELATIONSHIP');
END_ENTITY;

ENTITY resource_property;
  name        : label;
  description : text;
  resource    : characterized_resource_definition;
END_ENTITY;

ENTITY action_resource_requirement;
  name        : label;
  description : text;
  kind        : resource_requirement_type;
  operations  : SET [1:?] OF characterized_action_definition;
END_ENTITY;

ENTITY action_property_relationship;
  name                     : label;
  description              : text;
  relating_action_property : action_property;
  related_action_property  : action_property;
WHERE
  WR1: relating_action_property :<>: related_action_property;
END_ENTITY;

ENTITY requirement_for_action_resource
  SUBTYPE OF (action_resource_requirement);
  resources : SET [1:?] OF action_resource;
END_ENTITY;

ENTITY resource_property_relationship;
  name                       : label;
  description                : text;
  relating_resource_property : resource_property;
  related_resource_property  : resource_property;
WHERE
  WR1: relating_resource_property :<>: related_resource_property;
END_ENTITY;

ENTITY action_resource_requirement_relationship;
  name                                 : label;
  description                          : text;
  relating_action_resource_requirement : action_resource_requirement;
  related_action_resource_requirement  : action_resource_requirement;
WHERE
  WR1: relating_action_resource_requirement :<>:
       related_action_resource_requirement;
END_ENTITY;

ENTITY resource_requirement_type;
  name        : label;
  description : text;
END_ENTITY;

ENTITY resource_requirement_type_relationship;
  name                      : label;
  description               : text;
  relating_requirement_type : resource_requirement_type;
  related_requirement_type  : resource_requirement_type;
WHERE
  WR1: relating_requirement_type :<>: related_requirement_type;
END_ENTITY;

END_SCHEMA; -- process_property_schema



(*"process_property_schema"

The subject of the *process_property_schema* is the definition of:

* the properties of the actions that effect the process;
* the properties of the action_methods that effect the process;
* the properties of the resources to be used in the execution of the process;
* the association between the properties of the product and the process.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.__fund_cons"

The primary components of a process are:

* the actions that compose the process;
* the resources used within the process.

The results of a process are:

* the product or the intermediate product that will result from the process;
* the product properties that result from the process.

Process properties are the properties of the actions, resources, and products that effect or are part of the process.

Process properties include the description of the properties of the action that effect the process. Properties of the action are the characteristics that describe or specify operational information of the action that effect the process; the property is a description of the action.

Processes that establish product properties either specify a process for some aspect of the product definition or associate a process with the relevant property of a product.

Process properties may assign a resource to perform a particular action that effects a process. Resources can be assigned to an action at different levels of abstraction. More abstract definitions provide a means of deferring the specification of an actual instance of a resource until process time. Less abstract definitions provide an actual resource instance.

NOTE: Several representations of a property exist such as numeric values, parametric or fundamental equations, graphical values, and non-numeric values. A numeric value of a property makes use of representation.

NOTE: See <<iso10303-41>> for further information related to <<express:action_schema.action,action>>.

The *process_property_schema* includes definitions which enable the identification of acceptable substitutions for a process.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.characterized_action_definition"

A *characterized_action_definition* identifies either an <<express:action_schema.action,action>>, an <<express:action_schema.action_method,action_method>>, an <<express:action_schema.action_method_relationship,action_method_relationship>>, or an <<express:action_schema.action_relationship,action_relationship>>.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.characterized_resource_definition"

A *characterized_resource_definition* identifies either an <<express:action_schema.action_resource,action_resource>>, an <<express:process_property_schema.action_resource_requirement,action_resource_requirement>>, an <<express:process_property_schema.action_resource_requirement_relationship,action_resource_requirement_relationship>>, or an <<express:action_schema.action_resource_relationship,action_resource_relationship>>.

NOTE: An <<express:action_schema.action_resource,action_resource>> is a specification of an resource, while an <<express:process_property_schema.action_resource_requirement,action_resource_requirement>> identifies requirements that an <<express:action_schema.action_resource,action_resource>> shall satisfy.

[EXAMPLE]
====
An <<express:action_schema.action_resource,action_resource>> is a 'personal computer'. The <<express:process_property_schema.requirement_for_action_resource,requirement_for_action_resource>> is '4MB of memory'.
====

[EXAMPLE]
====
An <<express:process_property_schema.action_resource_requirement,action_resource_requirement>> is a 'machine capable of lifting 500 kg'.
====

*)

(*"process_property_schema.property_or_shape_select"

A *property_or_shape_select* identifies either a <<express:product_property_definition_schema.property_definition,property_definition>> or a <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_definition,shape_definition>>.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.action_property"

An <<express:process_property_schema.action_property,action_property>> is the description of the behavior, capabilities, or performance measures that are pertinent to a process, an action to effect a process, or a potential action to effect a process. An <<express:process_property_schema.action_property,action_property>> is a characteristic of either an <<express:action_schema.action,action>> or an <<express:action_schema.action_method,action_method>>.

[EXAMPLE]
====
If the heat treatment of a part is an <<express:action_schema.action,action>>, an <<express:process_property_schema.action_property,action_property>> is the temperature, the time, or some other characteristic of the <<express:action_schema.action,action>> that is required to describe the heat treatment.
====

[EXAMPLE]
====
The movement of an object from point A to point B is an <<express:action_schema.action,action>>. An <<express:process_property_schema.action_property,action_property>> of the movement is the speed at which the object moves.
====

*)

(*"process_property_schema.action_property.name"

the word or group of words by which the <<express:process_property_schema.action_property,action_property>> is referred to.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.action_property.description"

a description of the property.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.action_property.definition"

the <<express:action_schema.action,action>>, <<express:action_schema.action_method,action_method>>, <<express:action_schema.action_method_relationship,action_method_relationship>>, or <<express:action_schema.action_relationship,action_relationship>> that is to be characterized.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.product_definition_process"

A <<express:process_property_schema.product_definition_process,product_definition_process>> is an <<express:action_schema.action,action>> that defines or is part of the definition of a <<express:product_property_definition_schema.characterized_product_definition,characterized_product_definition>>. The <<express:process_property_schema.product_definition_process,product_definition_process>> establishes either the product definition of a product or an aspect of the product definition of a product.

NOTE: The aspect of the *product_definition* of a product may be an input or an output to the <<express:process_property_schema.product_definition_process,product_definition_process>>. The <<express:process_property_schema.process_product_association,process_product_association>> may specify the role of the <<express:process_property_schema.product_definition_process,product_definition_process>>.

NOTE: The product definition may be a single product or may be the process that brings several products together to form another product.

[EXAMPLE]
====
The assembly of components is specified by the process that produces the final product.
====

*)

(*"process_property_schema.product_definition_process.identification"

a descriptive identifier of the <<express:process_property_schema.product_definition_process,product_definition_process>>.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.product_definition_process.product_definitions"

the set of one or more <<express:process_property_schema.process_product_association,process_product_associations>> that are associated with each <<express:process_property_schema.product_definition_process,product_definition_process>>.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.process_product_association"

A <<express:process_property_schema.process_product_association,process_product_association>> is an association that specifies the product definition characteristic of interest to the <<express:process_property_schema.product_definition_process,product_definition_process>>.

NOTE: The product definition may be a single product or may be the process that brings several products together to form another product.

NOTE: A <<express:process_property_schema.process_product_association,process_product_association>> may specify a process for a specific <<express:product_property_definition_schema.characterized_product_definition,characterized_product_definition>>. Another <<express:process_property_schema.process_product_association,process_product_association>> may specify the same <<express:product_property_definition_schema.characterized_product_definition,characterized_product_definition>> for another process. The two <<express:product_property_definition_schema.characterized_product_definition,characterized_product_definitions>> are the same, but the <<express:process_property_schema.process_product_association,process_product_associations>> are different.

NOTE: The product definition characteristic may be an input or an output to the <<express:process_property_schema.product_definition_process,product_definition_process>>.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.process_product_association.name"

the word or group of words by which the <<express:process_property_schema.process_product_association,process_product_association>> is referred to.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.process_product_association.description"

description of the process.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.process_product_association.defined_product"

the product definition or product definition relationship that the *process* defines or is an aspect of.
*)

(*"process_property_schema.process_product_association.process"

the process associated with the <<express:product_property_definition_schema.characterized_product_definition,characterized_product_definition>>.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.property_process"

A <<express:process_property_schema.property_process,property_process>> is an <<express:action_schema.action,action>> that produces or results in a specific aspect of a product. The process may define a *product_definition*, but need not be specific to a particular product.

NOTE: An aspect of a *product_definition* may be an input or an output to the <<express:process_property_schema.property_process,property_process>>. The <<express:process_property_schema.process_property_association,process_property_association>> may specify the role of the <<express:process_property_schema.property_process,property_process>>.

[EXAMPLE]
====
The <<express:process_property_schema.property_process,property_process>> of "drill hole" is defined. The <<express:process_property_schema.property_process,property_process>> has the *action.chosen_method* of "drill hole". This process is for any product that a drill operation is applied to.
====

*)

(*"process_property_schema.property_process.identification"

a descriptive identifier of the <<express:process_property_schema.property_process,property_process>>.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.property_process.properties"

the set of one or more <<express:process_property_schema.process_property_association,process_property_associations>> that are associated with each <<express:process_property_schema.property_process,property_process>>.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.process_property_association"

A <<express:process_property_schema.process_property_association,process_property_association>> associates a specific <<express:process_property_schema.property_process,property_process>> to a given <<express:product_property_definition_schema.property_definition,property_definition>> or <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_definition,shape_definition>>.

NOTE: The <<express:process_property_schema.process_property_association,process_property_association>> allows for the specification of a process that results in individual properties of a product, but the specific product definition of the product that possesses the property need not be identified.

NOTE: The product definition characteristic may be an input or an output to the <<express:process_property_schema.process_property_association,process_property_association>>.

[EXAMPLE]
====
A <<express:process_property_schema.property_process,property_process>> is a process that produces a geometric form feature that is a slot in a machined part. The action to create the slot is a process that defines shape properties for a product, but it is not specific to a particular product. The product could be made from any of a number of types of materials. A <<express:process_property_schema.process_property_association,process_property_association>> associates the machining action with the slot feature.
====

[EXAMPLE]
====
A <<express:process_property_schema.property_process,property_process>> is a process that applies a heat treatment to a part. A <<express:process_property_schema.process_property_association,process_property_association>> relates the heat treatment process to the material property through the <<express:product_property_definition_schema.property_definition,property_definition>> and the *material_property* relationships. The heat treatment process is not specific to a particular part.
====

*)

(*"process_property_schema.process_property_association.name"

the word or group of words by which the <<express:process_property_schema.process_property_association,process_property_association>> is referred to.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.process_property_association.description"

3 description of the relationship between the <<express:process_property_schema.property_process,property_process>> and the <<express:product_property_definition_schema.property_definition,property_definition>> or the <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_definition,shape_definition>>.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.process_property_association.process"

the process to be associated with the property.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.process_property_association.property_or_shape"

a characteristic that the *process* defines or is an aspect of.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.replacement_relationship"

A <<express:process_property_schema.replacement_relationship,replacement_relationship>> is an <<express:action_schema.action_relationship,action_relationship>> that specifies that a *related_action* may replace the specified *relating_action*. This replacement may occur within or depend upon a context. The context may be defined by a condition.

[EXAMPLE]
====
A manufacturing process plan is designated as a functional replacement for the specified manufacturing process plan that is to be used to manufacture a product.
====

*)

(*"process_property_schema.replacement_relationship.wr:WR1"

An <<express:action_schema.action_relationship,action_relationship>> shall not replace itself, either directly or indirectly.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.resource_property"

A <<express:process_property_schema.resource_property,resource_property>> is a characteristic of a resource. The characteristic may be the behavior, capability, or performance measure that is pertinent to a process or the actions to effect a process for which the resource is used.

NOTE: The <<express:process_property_schema.resource_property,resource_property>> is not the representation of the property. See clause 6, the *process_property_representation_schema*.

[EXAMPLE]
====
A <<express:process_property_schema.resource_property,resource_property>> for a milling machine might be: the size of the machine bed, the
maximum rotational speed of the tool head, or the accuracy of the machine.
====

*)

(*"process_property_schema.resource_property.name"

the word or group of words by which the <<express:process_property_schema.resource_property,resource_property>> is referred to.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.resource_property.description"

a description of the property.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.resource_property.resource"

the <<express:action_schema.action_resource,action_resource>>, <<express:action_schema.action_resource_relationship,action_resource_relationship>>, <<express:process_property_schema.action_resource_requirement,action_resource_requirement>>, or <<express:process_property_schema.action_resource_requirement_relationship,action_resource_requirement_relationship>> that has or is described by the property.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.action_resource_requirement"

An <<express:process_property_schema.action_resource_requirement,action_resource_requirement>> is a requirement of a resource for the performance of an <<express:action_schema.action,action>> or <<express:action_schema.action_method,action_method>>. The <<express:process_property_schema.action_resource_requirement,action_resource_requirement>> specifies either a particular type of resource or a characteristic possessed by the resource.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.action_resource_requirement.name"

the words or group of words by which the <<express:process_property_schema.action_resource_requirement,action_resource_requirement>> is referred to.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.action_resource_requirement.description"

a description of the requirement.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.action_resource_requirement.kind"

the type of <<express:process_property_schema.action_resource_requirement,action_resource_requirement>> that is being required.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.action_resource_requirement.operations"

the set of one or more <<express:action_schema.action,action>>, <<express:action_schema.action_method_relationship,action_method_relationships>>, <<express:action_schema.action_method,action_methods>>, or <<express:action_schema.action_relationship,action_relationships>> that have the requirement.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.action_property_relationship"

An <<express:process_property_schema.action_property_relationship,action_property_relationship>> is a relationship between two different <<express:process_property_schema.action_property,action_properties>>. The <<express:process_property_schema.action_property_relationship,action_property_relationship>> identifies a relationship that may specify that an <<express:process_property_schema.action_property,action_property>> is an alternative for another <<express:process_property_schema.action_property,action_property>> or may identify a dependency between two <<express:process_property_schema.action_property,action_properties>>.

NOTE: The interpretation of different uses of this entity is not defined in this mm of ISO 10303. Application resources and application protocols provide further distinctions.

[EXAMPLE]
====
A milling operation is an <<express:action_schema.action_method,action_method>>. Duration of the milling operation is an <<express:process_property_schema.action_property,action_property>>. Temperature of the atmosphere for the milling operation is an <<express:process_property_schema.action_property,action_property>>. The <<express:process_property_schema.action_property_relationship,action_property_relationship>> identifies the relationship between the duration and temperature for the milling operation.
====

*)

(*"process_property_schema.action_property_relationship.name"

the word of group of words by which the <<express:process_property_schema.action_property_relationship,action_property_relationship>> is referred to.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.action_property_relationship.description"

a description of the relationship.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.action_property_relationship.relating_action_property"

the <<express:process_property_schema.action_property,action_property>> that is associated with the related <<express:process_property_schema.action_property,action_property>>. If precedence is important in the association, the *relating_action_property* is the independent <<express:process_property_schema.action_property,action_property>>.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.action_property_relationship.related_action_property"

the <<express:process_property_schema.action_property,action_property>> that is associated with the relating <<express:process_property_schema.action_property,action_property>>. If precedence is important in the association, the *related_action_property* is the dependent or alternate <<express:process_property_schema.action_property,action_property>>.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.action_property_relationship.wr:WR1"

The *relating_action_property* and the *related_action_property* shall be different <<express:process_property_schema.action_property,action_properties>>.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.requirement_for_action_resource"

A <<express:process_property_schema.requirement_for_action_resource,requirement_for_action_resource>> is an <<express:process_property_schema.action_resource_requirement,action_resource_requirement>> that specifies one or more <<express:action_schema.action_resource,action_resources>> that will satisfy the requirement.

[EXAMPLE]
====
A milling operation is the <<express:action_schema.action_method,action_method>>. A <<express:process_property_schema.requirement_for_action_resource,requirement_for_action_resource>> specifies an <<express:action_schema.action_resource,action_resource>> of "milling machine" and a description of the milling machine.
====

[EXAMPLE]
====
A machine that can lift 500 kilograms is needed to complete a process. The <<express:process_property_schema.action_resource_requirement,action_resource_requirement>> states the requirement, "machine with the ability to lift 500 kilograms". A specific lifting machine is an <<express:action_schema.action_resource,action_resource>>. If the specific lifting machine can satisfy the requirement, "machine with the ability to lift 500 kilograms", then the <<express:process_property_schema.requirement_for_action_resource,requirement_for_action_resource>> identifies the specific lifting machine.
====

*)

(*"process_property_schema.requirement_for_action_resource.resources"

the set of one or more <<express:action_schema.action_resource,action_resources>> that satisfy the <<express:process_property_schema.action_resource_requirement,action_resource_requirement>>.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.resource_property_relationship"

A <<express:process_property_schema.resource_property_relationship,resource_property_relationship>> is a relationship between two <<express:process_property_schema.resource_property,resource_properties>>.

NOTE: The interpretation of different uses of this entity is not defined in this document. Application resources and application protocols provide further distinctions.

[EXAMPLE]
====
An <<express:action_schema.action_resource,action_resource>> is a milling machine. The machine bed size and the machine milling head (e.g., 5 axis milling machine) are <<express:process_property_schema.resource_property,resource_properties>>. A <<express:process_property_schema.resource_property_relationship,resource_property_relationship>> is the relationship between the machine milling head the machine bed size.
====

*)

(*"process_property_schema.resource_property_relationship.name"

the word or group of words by which the <<express:process_property_schema.resource_property_relationship,resource_property_relationship>> is referred to.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.resource_property_relationship.description"

a description of the relationship.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.resource_property_relationship.relating_resource_property"

the <<express:process_property_schema.resource_property,resource_property>> that is associated with the related <<express:process_property_schema.resource_property,resource_property>>. If precedence is important in the association, the *relating_resource_property* is the independent <<express:process_property_schema.resource_property,resource_property>>.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.resource_property_relationship.related_resource_property"

the <<express:process_property_schema.resource_property,resource_property>> that is associated with the relating <<express:process_property_schema.resource_property,resource_property>>. If precedence is important in the association, the *related_resource_property* is the dependent or alternate <<express:process_property_schema.resource_property,resource_property>>.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.resource_property_relationship.wr:WR1"

The *relating_resource_property* and the *related_resource_property* shall be different <<express:process_property_schema.resource_property,resource_properties>>.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.action_resource_requirement_relationship"

An <<express:process_property_schema.action_resource_requirement_relationship,action_resource_requirement_relationship>> is a relationship between two <<express:process_property_schema.action_resource_requirement,action_resource_requirements>>.

NOTE: The interpretation of different uses of this entity is not defined in this document. Application resources and application protocols can provide further distinctions.

[EXAMPLE]
====
If the <<express:action_schema.action_resource,action_resource>> were for a drill, then a milling machine could be specified as an alternative for the requirement for a hand drill, since the milling machine can perform drilling operations.
====

*)

(*"process_property_schema.action_resource_requirement_relationship.name"

the word or group of words by which the <<express:process_property_schema.action_resource_requirement_relationship,action_resource_requirement_relationship>> is referred to.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.action_resource_requirement_relationship.description"

a description of the relationship.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.action_resource_requirement_relationship.relating_action_resource_requirement"

the <<express:process_property_schema.action_resource_requirement,action_resource_requirement>> that is associated with the related <<express:process_property_schema.action_resource_requirement,action_resource_requirement>>. If precedence is important in the association, the *relating_action_resource_requirement* is the independent <<express:process_property_schema.action_resource_requirement,action_resource_requirement>>.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.action_resource_requirement_relationship.related_action_resource_requirement"

the <<express:process_property_schema.action_resource_requirement,action_resource_requirement>> that is associated with the relating <<express:process_property_schema.action_resource_requirement,action_resource_requirement>>. If precedence is important in the association, the *related_action_resource_requirement* is the dependent or alternate <<express:process_property_schema.action_resource_requirement,action_resource_requirement>>.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.action_resource_requirement_relationship.wr:WR1"

The *relating_action_resource_requirement* and the *related_action_resource_requirement* shall be different <<express:process_property_schema.action_resource_requirement,action_resource_requirements>>.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.resource_requirement_type"

A <<express:process_property_schema.resource_requirement_type,resource_requirement_type>> is a taxonomic designation that is used to distinguish requirements or characteristics of requirements as belonging to an identified group or classification.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.resource_requirement_type.name"

the word or group of words by which the <<express:process_property_schema.resource_requirement_type,resource_requirement_type>> is referred to.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.resource_requirement_type.description"

3 description of the <<express:process_property_schema.resource_requirement_type,resource_requirement_type>>.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.resource_requirement_type_relationship"

A <<express:process_property_schema.resource_requirement_type_relationship,resource_requirement_type_relationship>> is a relationship between two <<express:process_property_schema.resource_requirement_type,resource_requirement_types>>.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.resource_requirement_type_relationship.name"

the word or group of words by which the <<express:process_property_schema.resource_requirement_type_relationship,resource_requirement_type_relationship>> is referred to.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.resource_requirement_type_relationship.description"

a description of the <<express:process_property_schema.resource_requirement_type_relationship,resource_requirement_type_relationship>>.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.resource_requirement_type_relationship.relating_requirement_type"

the <<express:process_property_schema.resource_requirement_type,resource_requirement_type>> that is associated with the related <<express:process_property_schema.resource_requirement_type,resource_requirement_type>>. If precedence is important in the association, the *related_requirement_type* is the independent <<express:process_property_schema.resource_requirement_type,resource_requirement_type>>.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.resource_requirement_type_relationship.related_requirement_type"

the <<express:process_property_schema.resource_requirement_type,resource_requirement_type>> that is associated with the relating <<express:process_property_schema.resource_requirement_type,resource_requirement_type>>. If precedence is important in the association, the *related_requirement_type* is the dependent <<express:process_property_schema.resource_requirement_type,resource_requirement_type>>.

*)

(*"process_property_schema.resource_requirement_type_relationship.wr:WR1"

The *relating_requirement_type* and the *related_requirement_type* shall be different <<express:process_property_schema.resource_requirement_type,resource_requirement_types>>.

*)

