(*"product_structure_schema.alternate_product_relationship"
An **alternate_product_relationship** is an association between two products whereby one product, the alternate product, may be used in place of another product, the base product.

If one product is an alternate for another product it is understood that there is no interest to keep track of which product, the base or any alternates specified, is used as a particular instance of the base product within a product structure.

An **alternate_product_relationship** for which the base product is an assembly specifies that the entire product structure of the alternate product may be used in place of the base product and its product structure.

The relationship established by the **alternate_product_relationship** need not be symmetric. If B is an alternate product for A, A is not implied to be an alternate product for B.
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.alternate_product_relationship.__example"
Two bolts of the same size are products. One bolt has a square head and the other has a hexagonal head. These head shapes are properties of the respective products. The two bolts are considered equivalent with respect to form, fit, and function: they both have sufficiently close physical shape, they take up the same space when used, and they both serve to fasten two things together. Thus, one of these two bolts could be considered to be an alternate part for the other bolt.
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.alternate_product_relationship.__note"
An organization may track design changes for a base part, and establish effectivity conditions for the use of that base part in various assemblies to be manufactured. The use of an alternate product implies that an organization does not specify any particular version of the alternate product or establish effectivities relating to it.
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.alternate_product_relationship.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **alternate_product_relationship** is known.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.alternate_product_relationship.definition"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **alternate_product_relationship**. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.alternate_product_relationship.alternate"
a product that may be used in place of the base product.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.alternate_product_relationship.base"
a product for which another product may be used as an alternate.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.alternate_product_relationship.basis"
a text description to specify the rationale and criteria used to consider the alternate product in place of the base product.
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.alternate_product_relationship.basis.__example"
In the *alternate_product_relationship* for the two bolts defined in example 1, the value of the basis attribute, could be "head shape", while the value of the definition attribute could be "alternate for use as fastener in engine assembly".
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.alternate_product_relationship.wr:WR1"
The instance for the alternate product shall not be the same as the instance of the base product.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.alternate_product_relationship.ur:UR1"
The combination of the alternate product and the base product shall be unique.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage"
An **assembly_component_usage** is a type of <<express:product_structure_schema.product_definition_usage,product_definition_usage>> that should be used to establish a relationship between <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> within one of the following three product structures:

* bill-of-material (BOM) structure;
* parts list structure;
* promissory use structure.

An **assembly_component_usage** relates a constituent to its assembly. An **assembly_component_usage** may be either a <<express:product_structure_schema.next_assembly_usage_occurrence,next_assembly_usage_occurrence>>, or a <<express:product_structure_schema.specified_higher_usage_occurrence,specified_higher_usage_occurrence>>, or a <<express:product_structure_schema.promissory_usage_occurrence,promissory_usage_occurrence>> and in addition may be a <<express:product_structure_schema.quantified_assembly_component_usage,quantified_assembly_component_usage>>.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage.reference_designator"
a distinctive code that serves to identify the usage of the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition,related_product_definition>> as a component in the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition,relating_product_definition>> in a diagram, list, chart, or on a physical piece of equipment. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage.reference_designator.__note"
The *reference_designator* attribute can be made mandatory, or constrained to be unique, or both, in an annotated EXPRESS schema that uses or specializes this entity.
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage_substitute"
An **assembly_component_usage_substitute** is a specification of that one constituent can be used as a substitute for another within the context of a given assembly.

The instance of the substitute constituent does not require the same spatial relationship or the same quantity. A substitute constituent does not require equivalent form, fit, and function of the constituent for which it is a substitute.

This entity defines one-way substitution only. Within a given context, if A is specified as a substitute for B, B is not implied to be a substitute for A.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage_substitute.__note"
The assembly context is specified by the fact that both <<express:product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage,assembly_component_usage>> referred to by the *base* and *substitute* attributes reference the same <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> in their inherited <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition,relating_product_definition>> attribute.
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage_substitute.__note"
The *assembly_component_usage_substitute* entity may be used to eliminate the re-identification of all higher-level assemblies when a new version of a lower-level constituent is created.
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage_substitute.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **assembly_component_usage_substitute** is known.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage_substitute.definition"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **assembly_component_usage_substitute**. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage_substitute.base"
an <<express:product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage,assembly_component_usage>> for which the substitute may be used.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage_substitute.substitute"
an <<express:product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage,assembly_component_usage>> that may be used for the base.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage_substitute.wr:WR1"
The <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition,relating_product_definition>> attribute of both the **base** and the **substitute** attributes shall refer to the same assembly <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>>.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage_substitute.wr:WR2"
The **base** and **substitute** attributes shall not be the same instance.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage_substitute.ur:UR1"
The combination of the **base** and **substitute** attributes shall be unique.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage_substitute_with_ranking"
An **assembly_component_usage_substitute_with_ranking** is a type of <<express:product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage_substitute,assembly_component_usage_substitute>> that specifies a relative preference value for the usage of a particular constituent as a substitute for another among all substitutes within the context of a given assembly.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage_substitute_with_ranking.ranking"
an integer that ranks the preference for use of the substitute <<express:product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage,assembly_component_usage>> among all **assembly_component_usage_substitute_with_ranking** instances with the same value for the base attribute. This value is an integer that only has meaning when comparing it with corresponding values for **assembly_component_usage_substitute_with_ranking** s sharing the same base <<express:product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage,assembly_component_usage>>. It is a relative ranking value, not an absolute ranking. A lower value indicates a higher preference for the substitute <<express:product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage,assembly_component_usage>>, and a higher value indicates a lower preference.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage_substitute_with_ranking.ranking_rationale"
text that describes the rationale used for the ranking.
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage_substitute_with_ranking.ranking_rationale.__example"
Examples of *ranking_rationale* are cost and long lead time.
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.make_from_usage_option"
A **make_from_usage_option** is a type of <<express:product_structure_schema.product_definition_usage,product_definition_usage>> in which one product is the result of applying a process to another product.
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.make_from_usage_option.__example"
Machining, plating, and bending are processes used to make another product.
*)
(*"product_structure_schema.make_from_usage_option.__example"
Consider the case of a shaft that can be machined from either a casting or a forging. All three, the shaft, the forging, and the casting, are represented by separate instances of <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>>. Two instances of the *make_from_usage_option* entity exist, one between the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition,relating_product_definition>> shaft and the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition,related_product_definition>> forging, the other between the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition,relating_product_definition>> shaft and the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition,related_product_definition>> casting.
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.make_from_usage_option.__note"
In situations in which a product is made from another product using a sequence of processes, the intermediate products will be related using the *make_from_usage_option* entity.
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.make_from_usage_option.__note"
A product to be modified may be an assembly. Generally, the <<express:product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage,assembly_component_usage>> differs from the *make_from_usage_option* in that the constituents of an assembly are used in the assembly without any change.
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.make_from_usage_option.__note"
A <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> may be the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition,relating_product_definition>> of many *make_from_usage_option* relationships, and a <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> may be the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition,related_product_definition>> of many *make_from_usage_option* relationships. Further, there may be multiple *make_from_usage_option* instances referencing the same <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition,relating_product_definition>> and <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition,related_product_definition>> pair of <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>>.
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.make_from_usage_option.ranking"
an integer that ranks the preference for use of the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition,related_product_definition>> among all **make_from_usage_option** instances that have the same value for the inherited <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition,relating_product_definition>> attribute. This value is an integer that only has meaning when comparing it with corresponding values for **make_from_usage_option** s sharing the same <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition,relating_product_definition>>. It is a relative ranking value, not an absolute ranking. A lower value indicates a higher preference for the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition,related_product_definition>>, and a higher value indicates a lower preference.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.make_from_usage_option.ranking_rationale"
text that describes the rationale used for the ranking.
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.make_from_usage_option.ranking_rationale.__example"
Examples of *ranking_rationale* are cost and long lead time.
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.make_from_usage_option.quantity"
the amount of the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition,relating_product_definition>> that can be made from the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition,related_product_definition>>.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.make_from_usage_option.wr:WR1"
If the quantity of the constituent is expressed numerically, its value shall be greater than zero.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.make_from_usage_option_group"
A **make_from_usage_option_group** is a collection of <<express:product_structure_schema.make_from_usage_option,make_from_usage_option>> instances that defines one possible combination of <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> that can be made from another single <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>>.

To represent the single product constraint within a single **make_from_usage_option_group**, the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition,related_product_definition>> of all of the instances of the <<express:product_structure_schema.make_from_usage_option,make_from_usage_option>> shall be the same.
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.make_from_usage_option_group.__example"
Suppose a bar stock, represented by <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> D, can be cut twice so as to create three - <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>>, X, Y, and Z. The *make_from_usage_option_group* representing this situation would aggregate three <<express:product_structure_schema.make_from_usage_option,make_from_usage_option>> as shown in Table 1:

[[table-table-product_structure_schema-table_1]]
.Example 1 make_from_usage_option_group
|===
| id | <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition,relating_product_definition>> | <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition,related_product_definition>> | quantity

| 1  | X  | D  | 1
| 2  | Y  | D  | 1
| 3  | Z  | D  | 1

|===
*)
(*"product_structure_schema.make_from_usage_option_group.__example"
The same bar stock <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> D can be cut to produce two <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> X and one <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> T. In this case the corresponding *make_from_usage_option_group* would aggregate two <<express:product_structure_schema.make_from_usage_option,make_from_usage_option>> as shown in Table 2:

[[table-table-product_structure_schema-table_2]]
.Example 2 make_from_usage_option_group
|===
| id | <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition,relating_product_definition>> | <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition,related_product_definition>> | quantity

| 2  | X  | D  | 2
| 1  | T  | D  | 1

|===
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.make_from_usage_option_group.__note"
The *make_from_usage_option_group* is used to indicate that several different products may be made from a single product.
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.make_from_usage_option_group.__note"
It is possible to use a product to make more than one combination of other products.
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.make_from_usage_option_group.__note"
A single <<express:product_structure_schema.make_from_usage_option,make_from_usage_option>> instance may be part of multiple **make_from_usage_option_group**s.
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.make_from_usage_option_group.members"
a collection of at least two <<express:product_structure_schema.make_from_usage_option,make_from_usage_option>> instances whose <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition,relating_product_definition>> instances may be made from the same <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition,related_product_definition>>.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.make_from_usage_option_group.wr:WR1"
All instances of members shall refer to the same instance of <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> in their respective <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition,related_product_definition>> attribute.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.multi_level_reference_designator"
A **multi_level_reference_designator** is a type of <<express:product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage,assembly_component_usage>> that specifies the relationship between an assembly and a constituent if the assembly is not the immediate parent for the constituent and there are several hierarchical levels between the assembly and the constituent. The hierarchical levels are defined by a list of <<express:product_structure_schema.next_assembly_usage_occurrence,next_assembly_usage_occurrence>>s that identifies a connected path in the assembly structure.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.multi_level_reference_designator.__note"
The *multi_level_reference_designator* is used to identify a specific instance of a component within a multi-level assembly structure for which certain properties are to be associated.
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.multi_level_reference_designator.location"
specifies the ordered list of connected <<express:product_structure_schema.next_assembly_usage_occurrence,next_assembly_usage_occurrence>>s that defines an unambiguous path from the assembly to the constituent.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.multi_level_reference_designator.root"
specifies the node in the assembly structure where the path starts.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.multi_level_reference_designator.leaf"
specifies the node in the assembly structure where the path ends.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.multi_level_reference_designator.ur:UR1"
The **location** shall be unique across all instances of **multi_level_reference_designator**.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.multi_level_reference_designator.wr:WR1"
The list of <<express:product_structure_schema.next_assembly_usage_occurrence,next_assembly_usage_occurrence>>s defined by **location** shall be connected.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.multi_level_reference_designator.wr:WR2"
For each element in the **location** list the attribute <<express:product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage.reference_designator,reference_designator>> shall be provided.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.next_assembly_usage_occurrence"
A **next_assembly_usage_occurrence** is a type of <<express:product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage,assembly_component_usage>> that specifies the relationship between a child constituent and its immediate parent assembly in a product structure.
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.next_assembly_usage_occurrence.__example"
The position and orientation of a constituent with respect to its assembly would be computed using a transformation defined in the <<express:representation_schema,representation_schema>> in ISO 10303-43 [2].
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.next_assembly_usage_occurrence.__note"
An instance of *next_assembly_usage_occurrence* represents an individual occurrence of a constituent in an assembly. Each specific use of the same constituent may be represented by another distinct *next_assembly_usage_occurrence* instance for the purpose of assigning property information such as a position and orientation for the constituent. Property information is not provided by any of the entities of this document but by using the appropriate capabilities defined in ISO 10303-42 [1], ISO 10303-43 [2], and ISO 10303-41. The representation of a constituent occurrence in an assembly may be linked to mechanisms in ISO 10303-42 [1] and ISO 10303-43 [2] by means of a <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> entity defined in the <<express:product_definition_schema,product_definition_schema>> in ISO 10303-41.
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.next_assembly_usage_occurrence.__note"
An application algorithm can produce an indented parts list for a product by sequentially tracing through a structure of *next_assembly_usage_occurrence* instances. A similar algorithm can be used to calculate the position and orientation of each occurrence of every constituent relative to its higher-level assemblies within a BOM when used in conjunction with the property information constructs defined ISO 10303-41, ISO 10303-42 [1], and ISO 10303-43 [2].
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.next_assembly_usage_occurrence.__note"
The number of constituents used in the assembly may be specified by composing a complex instance of *next_assembly_usage_occurrence* and <<express:product_structure_schema.quantified_assembly_component_usage,quantified_assembly_component_usage>>.
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.next_assembly_usage_occurrence.product_definition_occurrence_id"
a derived attribute that represents the <<express:product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence.id,id>> of the <<express:product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence,product_definition_occurrence>> when it is referenced by the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition,related_product_definition>> attribute.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.next_assembly_usage_occurrence.ur:UR1"
The combination of <<express:product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage.reference_designator,reference_designator>> and <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition,relating_product_definition>> shall be unique within a population of **next_assembly_usage_occurrence** s.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.next_assembly_usage_occurrence.ur:UR2"
The combination of **product_definition_occurrence_id** and <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition,relating_product_definition>> shall be unique within a population of **next_assembly_usage_occurrence** s.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence"
A **product_definition_occurrence** is an identified occurrence of a <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> or a <<express:product_definition_schema.generic_product_definition_reference,generic_product_definition_reference>> or another **product_definition_occurrence** in one or several product structures.
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence.__example"
The product structures, in which a *product_definition_occurrence* is identified, can be breakdowns and assemblies.
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence.id"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> that distinguishes the **product_definition_occurrence**.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **product_definition_occurrence** is known. The value of the attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **product_definition_occurrence**. The value of the attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence.definition"
the definition of this **product_definition_occurrence**. The value of the attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence.quantity"
the number of objects represented by the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> or <<express:product_definition_schema.generic_product_definition_reference,generic_product_definition_reference>> or <<express:configuration_management_schema.configuration_item,configuration_item>> for this **product_definition_occurrence**. The value of the attribute need not be specified. If the value of this attribute is not defined then there is a single occurrence.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence.descendant_occurrences"
the set of all <<express:product_structure_schema.product_definition_specified_occurrence,product_definition_specified_occurrence>>s that are direct or indirect children of this **product_definition_occurrence**.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence.assembly_usages"
the set of all <<express:product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage,assembly_component_usage>> that reference this **product_definition_occurrence** by the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition,relating_product_definition>> attribute.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence.child_occurrences"
the set of all <<express:product_structure_schema.product_definition_specified_occurrence,product_definition_specified_occurrence>> that are direct children of this **product_definition_occurrence**.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence.wr:WR1"
If **definition** is either a **product_definition_occurrence** or a <<express:product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence_reference,product_definition_occurrence_reference>>, then the **product_definition_occurrence** shall be a <<express:product_structure_schema.product_definition_specified_occurrence,product_definition_specified_occurrence>>.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence.wr:WR2"
When no **definition** is provided, then the definition for this **product_definition_occurrence** shall be provided by a <<express:configuration_management_schema.configuration_item,configuration_item>> that is linked to this **product_definition_occurrence** by a <<express:configuration_management_schema.configuration_design,configuration_design>>.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence.wr:WR3"
If the **quantity** of the constituent is expressed numerically, its value shall be greater than zero.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence_reference"
A **product_definition_occurrence_reference** is a type of <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_reference,product_definition_reference>> that represents an externally defined <<express:product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence,product_definition_occurrence>> by a local <<express:product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence,product_definition_occurrence>>.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence_reference.product_occurrence_id"
specifies the <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> of the externally defined <<express:product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence,product_definition_occurrence>>.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence_reference_with_local_representation"
A **product_definition_occurrence_reference_with_local_representation** is a type of <<express:product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence,product_definition_occurrence>> and of type <<express:product_definition_schema.generic_product_definition_reference,generic_product_definition_reference>> that represents an externally defined <<express:product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence,product_definition_occurrence>> by a local product_definition.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence_relationship"
A **product_definition_occurrence_relationship** is an association between a <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> and an <<express:product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage,assembly_component_usage>> in which the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> referenced by the **occurrence** attribute is a specific instance of the constituent <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> referenced by the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition,related_product_definition>> attribute of the **occurrence_usage** in the assembly <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> referenced by the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition,relating_product_definition>> attribute.
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence_relationship.__example"
A product structure for a car is defined in which entity instances of <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> are defined for the chassis and the wheel. Four <<express:product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage,assembly_component_usage>> instances are then created to represent the four wheels of the chassis in which the <<express:product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage.reference_designator,reference_designator>> has values of 'left front', 'right front', 'left rear', 'right rear'. To represent specific information about the right rear wheel, a <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> of the wheel is created to which the information can be associated. To specify that this <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> is representing the wheel that is implied by the instance of <<express:product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage,assembly_component_usage>> with the <<express:product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage.reference_designator,reference_designator>> attribute value of 'right rear', the *product_definition_occurrence_relationship* is created to associate the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> with the <<express:product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage,assembly_component_usage>>.
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence_relationship.__note"
The identification of the specific instance of the constituent in the assembly can be defined using the <<express:product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage.reference_designator,reference_designator>> attribute of the <<express:product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage,assembly_component_usage>> entity.
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence_relationship.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **product_definition_occurrence_relationship** is known.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence_relationship.description"
the text that provides further information about the **product_definition_occurrence_relationship**. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence_relationship.occurrence"
the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> that represents a specific instance of the product.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence_relationship.occurrence_usage"
the <<express:product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage,assembly_component_usage>> that represents a specific use of the constituent in an assembly.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence_relationship.wr:WR1"
The <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> referenced by the **occurrence** attribute shall not be the assembly <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> in the <<express:product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage,assembly_component_usage>> referenced by the **occurrence_usage** attribute.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence_relationship.wr:WR2"
The <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> referenced by the **occurrence** attribute shall not be the constituent <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> in the <<express:product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage,assembly_component_usage>> referenced by the **occurrence_usage** attribute.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence_relationship.wr:WR3"
The <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> referenced by the **occurrence** attribute and the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> that represents the constituent of the <<express:product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage,assembly_component_usage>> shall be definitions of the same <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation,product_definition_formation>>.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_specified_occurrence"
A **product_definition_specified_occurrence** is a type of <<express:product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence,product_definition_occurrence>> that is defined by another <<express:product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence,product_definition_occurrence>> or <<express:product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence_reference,product_definition_occurrence_reference>> in the context of a higher-level <<express:product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence,product_definition_occurrence>>. The only purpose of a **product_definition_specified_occurrence** is to provide visibility and to identify a specific lower-level product occurrence within a multi-level assembly. A single **product_definition_specified_occurrence** makes a product occurrence visible within an assembly structure of two levels. For more than two assembly levels, a directed graph of several **product_definition_specified_occurrence** s is used. A chain of **product_definition_specified_occurrence** where one is the definition of the other can be used to identify occurrences down in a multi-level assembly tree.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_specified_occurrence.__note"
A *product_definition_specified_occurrence* can be used to relate product data such as properties to a specific lower-level product occurrence.
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_specified_occurrence.__note"
Even without having a *product_definition_specified_occurrence*, a specific lower-level product occurrence will exist in a higher-level assembly.
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_specified_occurrence.definition"
the definition of a **product_definition_specified_occurrence** shall either be of type <<express:product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence,product_definition_occurrence>> or of type <<express:product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence_reference,product_definition_occurrence_reference>>.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_specified_occurrence.occurrence_usage"
a higher-level <<express:product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence,product_definition_occurrence>> or <<express:product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence_reference,product_definition_occurrence_reference>> of which this **product_definition_specified_occurrence** is a child.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_specified_occurrence.ur:UR1"
the **id** of a **product_definition_specified_occurrence** shall be unique among all other **product_definition_specified_occurrence** for the same **occurrence_usage**.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_specified_occurrence.wr:WR1"
A **product_definition_specified_occurrence** shall not be used by the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition,related_product_definition>> attribute of an <<express:product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage,assembly_component_usage>>.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_specified_occurrence.wr:WR2"
The **definition** attribute shall not be cyclic.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_usage"
A **product_definition_usage** is a type of <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship,product_definition_relationship>> that specifies a directed association between two <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> in which the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition,related_product_definition>> is used in the context of the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition,relating_product_definition>>. The **product_definition_usage** establishes a relationship stating that the related product is used in the context of the relating product. This usage is established for the life cycle stages and application contexts in which the two products are described.

A **product_definition_usage** may be either a <<express:product_structure_schema.make_from_usage_option,make_from_usage_option>> or an <<express:product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage,assembly_component_usage>>.
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_usage.__example"
The assembly trees established for production sometimes contain more intermediate levels than the trees established during the design phase. In such a case, the design phase relationship between a component and the assembly in which it is contained may be replaced by several intermediate relationships during production.
*)
(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_usage.__example"
A given product may be used in a support role with respect to another product. A screwdriver may be identified as a resource to be used for the maintenance life cycle stage of a given product. In such a case, the support resource relationship between the screwdriver and the product for which it is identified to be used for maintenance activities may be specified.
*)
(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_usage.__example"
If four identical bolts are used to attach two plates, there may be a need to identify one specific bolt for some purpose. It needs to be torqued to a greater degree than the rest. The inherited <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.id,id>> attribute then is used to identify this specific bolt's requirement, even though the **product_definition_usage**s of all four bolts will have the same attribute pair of <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>>.
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_usage.wr:WR1"
Each **product_definition_usage** shall not relate the same <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition,relating_product_definition>> instance of <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> to the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition,related_product_definition>> or any of its descendants formed by their reference as the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition,relating_product_definition>> in a graph of **product_definition_usage** s.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_usage.wr:WR1.__note"
This rule uses the function <<express:product_definition_schema.acyclic_product_definition_relationship,acyclic_product_definition_relationship>> defined in the <<express:product_definition_schema,product_definition_schema>> in ISO 10303-41.
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_usage.ur:UR1"
The combination of the inherited <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.id,id>>, <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition,relating_product_definition>>, and <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition,related_product_definition>> attributes shall be unique within a scope of **product_definition_usage**.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_usage_relationship"
A **product_definition_usage_relationship** is a type of <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship_relationship,product_definition_relationship_relationship>> that is a relationship between two <<express:product_structure_schema.product_definition_usage,product_definition_usage>> with the same <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition,relating_product_definition>>.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_usage_relationship.relating"
the **relating** attribute shall be of type <<express:product_structure_schema.product_definition_usage,product_definition_usage>>.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_usage_relationship.related"
the **related** attribute shall be of type <<express:product_structure_schema.product_definition_usage,product_definition_usage>>.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.product_definition_usage_relationship.wr:WR1"
the **related** and **relating** <<express:product_structure_schema.product_definition_usage,product_definition_usage>> shall have the same <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition,relating_product_definition>>.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.promissory_usage_occurrence"
A **promissory_usage_occurrence** is a type of <<express:product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage,assembly_component_usage>> in which the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition,related_product_definition>> is in the assembly tree of the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition,relating_product_definition>> regardless of the number of intermediate levels between them.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.promissory_usage_occurrence.__note"
A *promissory_usage_occurrence* is used when the product structure is not completely defined. In such a situation, it is still possible to relate an assembly to a constituent to capture the intent that the constituent will be used in that assembly.
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.quantified_assembly_component_usage"
A **quantified_assembly_component_usage** is a type of <<express:product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage,assembly_component_usage>> that establishes the relationship between an assembly and one of its constituents if there is a need to specify the quantity of the child constituent used in the assembly.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.quantified_assembly_component_usage.__note"
Generally, for production planning or material planning purposes, several occurrences of a constituent are lumped together, and a quantity is specified to account for the several occurrences. A typical example would be the specifying of an occurrence of a rivet used for joining aeroplane structures and denoting the number of such rivets used on the entire aeroplane. If each of the occurrences of the rivets used is to be specified, the <<express:product_structure_schema.next_assembly_usage_occurrence,next_assembly_usage_occurrence>> entity may be used. As many instances of the <<express:product_structure_schema.next_assembly_usage_occurrence,next_assembly_usage_occurrence>> as the number of occurrences of the rivets will exist in this case.
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.quantified_assembly_component_usage.quantity"
a measure that defines how many or how much of the constituent is used in the assembly.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.quantified_assembly_component_usage.wr:WR1"
If the **quantity** of the constituent is expressed numerically, its value shall be greater than zero.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.specified_higher_usage_occurrence"
A **specified_higher_usage_occurrence** is a type of <<express:product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage,assembly_component_usage>> that specifies the relationship between a constituent and an assembly if the assembly is not the immediate parent for the constituent.

The relationship between the constituent and the assembly of the **specified_higher_usage_occurrence** to be specified is captured by the relationship of the inherited attributes <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition,relating_product_definition>> and <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition,related_product_definition>>.

The two attributes ({blank} **upper_usage** and **next_usage** {blank}) within the primary instance of the entity **specified_higher_usage_occurrence** shall respectively specify an <<express:product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage,assembly_component_usage>> and the <<express:product_structure_schema.next_assembly_usage_occurrence,next_assembly_usage_occurrence>> that together will provide the definition of the path from the constituent to the assembly for which the **specified_higher_usage_occurrence** is being specified. To ensure that the <<express:product_structure_schema.next_assembly_usage_occurrence,next_assembly_usage_occurrence>> and the <<express:product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage,assembly_component_usage>> together constitute the entire path desired for the **specified_higher_usage_occurrence**, it is required that the instance of the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition,related_product_definition>> attribute of the <<express:product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage,assembly_component_usage>> entity be the same as the instance of the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition,relating_product_definition>> attribute of the <<express:product_structure_schema.next_assembly_usage_occurrence,next_assembly_usage_occurrence>> entity. The <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition,related_product_definition>> attribute of the <<express:product_structure_schema.next_assembly_usage_occurrence,next_assembly_usage_occurrence>> shall reference the same instance as the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition,related_product_definition>> attribute of the **specified_higher_usage_occurrence** being specified. The <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition,relating_product_definition>> attribute of the <<express:product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage,assembly_component_usage>> entity shall reference the same instance as the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition,relating_product_definition>> attribute of the **specified_higher_usage_occurrence** being specified.

If the <<express:product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage,assembly_component_usage>> referenced by the attribute **upper_usage** is not a <<express:product_structure_schema.next_assembly_usage_occurrence,next_assembly_usage_occurrence>> it shall be a **specified_higher_usage_occurrence**. This **specified_higher_usage_occurrence** shall have its attributes **upper_usage** and **next_usage** defined as described in the previous paragraph to specify further the path of the primary **specified_higher_usage_occurrence**. This recursive specification shall continue until the attribute **upper_usage** references an <<express:product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage,assembly_component_usage>> entity that is a <<express:product_structure_schema.next_assembly_usage_occurrence,next_assembly_usage_occurrence>>. At this point, the primary **specified_higher_usage_occurrence** is fully specified both in terms of its constituents/assembly relationship and the entire path between them.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.specified_higher_usage_occurrence.__note"
The *specified_higher_usage_occurrence* is used to define portions of parts lists that contain a specific constituent within an assembly for which certain properties are to be associated or when the portion is used in more than one assembly structure.
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.specified_higher_usage_occurrence.__note"
<<annex_examples>> contains examples of this entity and figures that depict the relationships between it and the other entities of this schema.
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.specified_higher_usage_occurrence.upper_usage"
an <<express:product_structure_schema.assembly_component_usage,assembly_component_usage>> that is the same instance of the attribute <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition,relating_product_definition>> as this **specified_higher_usage_occurrence** and the same instance of the attribute <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition,related_product_definition>> as the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition,relating_product_definition>> of the <<express:product_structure_schema.next_assembly_usage_occurrence,next_assembly_usage_occurrence>> referenced by the attribute **next_usage**.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.specified_higher_usage_occurrence.next_usage"
a <<express:product_structure_schema.next_assembly_usage_occurrence,next_assembly_usage_occurrence>> that is the same instance of the attribute <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition,related_product_definition>> as this **specified_higher_usage_occurrence** and the same instance of the product definition referenced by the attribute <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition,relating_product_definition>> as the product definition referenced by the attribute <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition,related_product_definition>> of the attribute **upper_usage**.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.specified_higher_usage_occurrence.next_usage.__note"
See Figure E.7 for diagrams illustrating instances of these two attributes.
*)

(*"product_structure_schema.specified_higher_usage_occurrence.wr:WR1"
The instance of **specified_higher_usage_occurrence** shall not be the same as the instance of **upper_usage**.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.specified_higher_usage_occurrence.wr:WR2"
The <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition,relating_product_definition>> attribute (i.e., assembly) of the **specified_higher_usage_occurrence** shall reference the same instance of <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> as the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition,relating_product_definition>> (i.e., assembly) for the **upper_usage**.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.specified_higher_usage_occurrence.wr:WR3"
The <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition,related_product_definition>> attribute (i.e., constituent) of the **specified_higher_usage_occurrence** shall reference the same instance of <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> as the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition,related_product_definition>> for the **next_usage**.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.specified_higher_usage_occurrence.wr:WR4"
The <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition,related_product_definition>> (i.e., constituent) for the **upper_usage** shall reference, or be related to, the same instance of <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> as the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition,relating_product_definition>> (i.e., assembly) for the **next_usage**.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.specified_higher_usage_occurrence.wr:WR5"
The type of the **upper_usage** attribute shall be either <<express:product_structure_schema.next_assembly_usage_occurrence,next_assembly_usage_occurrence>> or **specified_higher_usage_occurrence**.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.specified_higher_usage_occurrence.ur:UR1"
The combination of the **upper_usage** and **next_usage** attributes shall be unique within a population of **specified_higher_usage_occurrence**.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.unambiguously_specified_multi_level_reference_designator.links"
the list of <<express:product_structure_schema.next_assembly_usage_occurrence,next_assembly_usage_occurrence>>s that shall be connected.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.acyclic_product_definition_specified_occurrence"
The **acyclic_product_definition_specified_occurrence** function determines whether the graph of instances of the entity data type <<express:product_structure_schema.product_definition_specified_occurrence,product_definition_specified_occurrence>> connected by their attribute <<express:product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence.definition,definition>> contains a cycle. The function returns TRUE if no cycle has been detected. Otherwise it returns FALSE.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.acyclic_product_definition_specified_occurrence.pdso"
(input) the candidate <<express:product_structure_schema.product_definition_specified_occurrence,product_definition_specified_occurrence>> to be checked.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.acyclic_product_definition_specified_occurrence.definition"
(input) the <<express:product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence,product_definition_occurrence>> to which the candidate is checked against.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.get_descendant_occurrences"
The **getdescendant_occurrences** function determines the set of instances of the entity data type <<express:product_structure_schema.product_definition_specified_occurrence,product_definition_specified_occurrence>> that are descendants of a <<express:product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence,product_definition_occurrence>>.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.get_descendant_occurrences.input"
the <<express:product_structure_schema.product_definition_occurrence,product_definition_occurrence>> for which the descendants are calculated.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.unambiguously_specified_multi_level_reference_designator"
The **unambiguously_specified_multi_level_reference_designator** function determines whether a list of <<express:product_structure_schema.next_assembly_usage_occurrence,next_assembly_usage_occurrence>> is connected.

For each element in the **links** list, the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition,related_product_definition>> shall reference, or be related to, the same instance of <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_or_reference,product_definition_or_reference>> as the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition,relating_product_definition>> of the next element in the list.
*)


(*"product_structure_schema.__schema_file"
data/resource_docs/product_structure_configuration/resource.xml
*)


