(*"qualifications_schema.qualification"
A **qualification** is a particular instance of the formal identification of a capability or aptitude in a specific person or organization.
*)

(*"qualifications_schema.qualification.__example"
John Smith's driving licence.
*)
(*"qualifications_schema.qualification.__example"
Mary Brown's doctorate entitled "Datamodelling Using EXPRESS2".
*)

(*"qualifications_schema.qualification.__note"
A relationship between a <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification_type,qualification_type>> object and one or more *qualification* objects is established by the declaration of a <<express:management_resources_schema.qualification_type_assignment,qualification_type_assignment>> subtype containing a single attribute that references a set of a SELECT type that contains an qualification.
*)

(*"qualifications_schema.qualification.id"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> that distinguishes the **qualification**.
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.qualification.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **qualification** is known.
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.qualification.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **qualification**. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.qualification_relationship"
A **qualification_relationship** is a relationship between two instances of the <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification,qualification>> entity data type and provides for the identification, naming, and description of that relationship.
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.qualification_relationship.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **qualification_relationship**. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.qualification_relationship.id"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> that distinguishes the **qualification_relationship**.
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.qualification_relationship.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **qualification_relationship** is known
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.qualification_relationship.related_qualification"
the other instance of <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification,qualification>> that is a part of the relationship. If one element of the relationship is dependent upon the other, this attribute shall be the dependent one.
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.qualification_relationship.related_qualification.__note"
the meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"qualifications_schema.qualification_relationship.relating_qualification"
one of the instances of <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification,qualification>> that is a part of the relationship.
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.qualification_relationship.relating_qualification.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"qualifications_schema.qualification_type"
An **qualification_type** is the formal identification of a capability or aptitude.
*)

(*"qualifications_schema.qualification_type.__example"
A driving licence.
*)
(*"qualifications_schema.qualification_type.__example"
A university degree.
*)

(*"qualifications_schema.qualification_type.__note"
A relationship between a *qualification_type* object and one or more <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification,qualification>> objects is established by the declaration of an <<express:management_resources_schema.qualification_type_assignment,qualification_type_assignment>> subtype containing a single attribute that references a set of a SELECT type that contains a <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification,qualification>>.
*)

(*"qualifications_schema.qualification_type.id"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> that distinguishes the **qualification_type**.
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.qualification_type.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **qualification_type** is known.
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.qualification_type.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **qualification_type**. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.qualification_type_relationship"
A **qualification_type_relationship** is a relationship between two instances of the <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification_type,qualification_type>> entity data type and provides for the identification, naming, and description of that relationship.
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.qualification_type_relationship.id"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> that distinguishes the **qualification_type_relationship**.
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.qualification_type_relationship.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **qualification_type_relationship** is known.
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.qualification_type_relationship.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **qualification_type_relationship**. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.qualification_type_relationship.related_qualification_type"
the other instance of <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification_type,qualification_type>> that is a part of the relationship. If one element of the relationship is dependent upon the other, this attribute shall be the dependent one.
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.qualification_type_relationship.related_qualification_type.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"qualifications_schema.qualification_type_relationship.relating_qualification_type"
one of the instances of <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification_type,qualification_type>> that is a part of the relationship.
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.qualification_type_relationship.relating_qualification_type.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"qualifications_schema.acyclic_qualification_relationship"
The **acyclic_qualification_relationship** function determines whether the graph of instances of the entity data type <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification,qualification>> that contains relation as one of its links contains a cycle. This function may be used to evaluate either an <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification_relationship,qualification_relationship>> or any of its subtypes.

The function returns TRUE if no cycle has been detected. Otherwise it returns FALSE.
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.acyclic_qualification_relationship.__note"
The algorithm of the function is explained in annex E.2.
*)

(*"qualifications_schema.acyclic_qualification_relationship.__note"
This function is not used in this schema. It is defined here because other ISO 10303 integrated resources and application protocols that use the <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification_relationship,qualification_relationship>> entity include rules that use this function.
*)

(*"qualifications_schema.acyclic_qualification_relationship.relation"
(input) the candidate <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification_relationship,qualification_relationship>> to be checked.
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.acyclic_qualification_relationship.relatives"
(input) the set of instances of the entity data type <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification,qualification>> that the function is searching for in the <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification_relationship.relating_qualification,relating_qualification>> parameter of the **relation** argument.
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.acyclic_qualification_relationship.specific_relation"
(input) the fully qualified name of a subtype of the <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification_relationship,qualification_relationship>> entity.
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.acyclic_qualification_type_relationship"
The **acyclic_qualification_type_relationship** function determines whether the graph of instances of the entity data type <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification_type,qualification_type>> that contains relation as one of its links contains a cycle. This function may be used to evaluate either an <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification_type_relationship,qualification_type_relationship>> or any of its subtypes.

The function returns TRUE if no cycle has been detected. Otherwise it returns FALSE.
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.acyclic_qualification_type_relationship.__note"
The algorithm of the function is explained in annex E.2.
*)

(*"qualifications_schema.acyclic_qualification_type_relationship.__note"
This function is not used in this schema. It is defined here because other ISO 10303 integrated resources and application protocols that use the <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification_type_relationship,qualification_type_relationship>> entity include rules that use this function.
*)

(*"qualifications_schema.acyclic_qualification_type_relationship.relation"
(input) the candidate <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification_type_relationship,qualification_type_relationship>> to be checked.
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.acyclic_qualification_type_relationship.relatives"
(input) the set of instances of the entity data type <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification_type,qualification_type>> that the function is searching for in the <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification_type_relationship.relating_qualification_type,relating_qualification_type>> parameter of the **relation** argument.
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.acyclic_qualification_type_relationship.specific_relation"
(input) the fully qualified name of a subtype of the <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification_type_relationship,qualification_type_relationship>> entity.
*)


