* <<express:representation_schema.binary_representation_item>>; 16
* <<express:representation_schema.set_representation_item>>; 17
* <<express:representation_schema.list_representation_item>>; 18
====
*)

(*"representation_schema.binary_representation_item"
A **binary_representation_item** is a type of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> that specifies a binary value.
*)


(*"representation_schema.binary_representation_item.binary_value"
the value of the element of representation.
*)


(*"representation_schema.bytes_representation_item"
A **bytes_representation_item** is a type of <<express:representation_schema.binary_representation_item,binary_representation_item>> that specifies a byte value.
*)


(*"representation_schema.bytes_representation_item.no_of_bytes"
the number of bytes of the element of representation.
*)


(*"representation_schema.bytes_representation_item.wr:WR1"
The number of bits in <<express:representation_schema.binary_representation_item.binary_value,binary_value>> shall be a multiple of 8.
*)


(*"representation_schema.representation_reference"
A **representation_reference** is an identification based reference to a <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>>.
*)


(*"representation_schema.representation_reference.id"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> that distinguishes the **representation_reference**.
*)


(*"representation_schema.representation_reference.context_of_items"
the <<express:representation_schema.representation_context_reference,representation_context_reference>> in which the items are related to form a **representation_reference** of some concept.
*)


(*"representation_schema.compound_item_definition"
The alternate data types are different aggregations of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>>.
*)


(*"representation_schema.list_item_defined_transformation"
A **list_item_defined_transformation** is an ordered aggregation of two or more <<express:representation_schema.item_defined_transformation,item_defined_transformation>>s defining together the transformation for a <<express:representation_schema.representation_relationship_with_transformation,representation_relationship_with_transformation>>
*)


(*"representation_schema.set_item_defined_transformation"
A **set_item_defined_transformation** is an unordered aggregation of one or more <<express:representation_schema.item_defined_transformation,item_defined_transformation>>s defining together the transformation for a <<express:representation_schema.representation_relationship_with_transformation,representation_relationship_with_transformation>>
*)


(*"representation_schema.get_representations_for_items"
The FUNCTION <<express:representation_schema.get_representations_for_items,get_representations_for_items>> returns the set of <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> that are structurally associated with the input <<express:representation_schema.founded_item_select,founded_item_select>> via direct or indirect reference.
*)


(*"representation_schema.get_representations_for_items.input"
the specified <<express:representation_schema.founded_item_select,founded_item_select>>.
*)


(*"representation_schema.list_representation_item"
A **list_representation_item** is an ordered aggregation of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> instances.
*)


(*"representation_schema.set_representation_item"
A **set_representation_item** is an unordered aggregation of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> instances.
*)


(*"representation_schema.compound_representation_item"
A **compound_representation_item** is a type of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> that is defined by an aggregation of other instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>>. This aggregation is either ordered or unordered.
*)

(*"representation_schema.compound_representation_item.__example"
In an application protocol in the domain of ship design, hydrostatic properties of the ship hull can be represented using a tabular structure composed of instances of <<express:representation_schema.list_representation_item,list_representation_item>>.
*)

(*"representation_schema.compound_representation_item.__note"
A *compound_representation_item* supports the description of aspects of product data using structured collections.
*)

(*"representation_schema.compound_representation_item.__note"
The meaning and usage of a structured collection of instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> can be specified in an annotated EXPRESS listing that uses or specializes this entity data type.
*)

(*"representation_schema.compound_representation_item.item_element"
the <<express:representation_schema.list_representation_item,list_representation_item>> or <<express:representation_schema.set_representation_item,set_representation_item>> whose component instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> define the **compound_representation_item**.
*)


(*"representation_schema.definitional_representation"
A **definitional_representation** is a type of <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> that has a <<express:representation_schema.parametric_representation_context,parametric_representation_context>>.
*)


(*"representation_schema.definitional_representation.wr:WR1"
The context of the **definitional_representation** shall be a <<express:representation_schema.parametric_representation_context,parametric_representation_context>>.
*)


(*"representation_schema.definitional_representation_relationship"
A **definitional_representation_relationship** is a type of <<express:representation_schema.representation_relationship,representation_relationship>>. The representation indicated by <<express:representation_schema.representation_relationship.rep_1,rep_1>> is part of the definition indicated by <<express:representation_schema.representation_relationship.rep_2,rep_2>>.
*)


(*"representation_schema.definitional_representation_relationship.__note"
A <<express:representation_schema.representation_relationship,representation_relationship>> by itself is not making one representation part of the definition of the other like it is the case with <<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>>. The *definitional_representation_relationship* acts in a similar way as <<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>>.
*)

(*"representation_schema.definitional_representation_relationship.wr:WR1"
The **definitional_representation_relationship** shall not participate in cycles.
*)


(*"representation_schema.definitional_representation_relationship.wr:WR2"
Either the or the subtype <<express:representation_schema.definitional_representation_relationship_with_same_context,definitional_representation_relationship_with_same_context>> shall be used.
*)


(*"representation_schema.definitional_representation_relationship_with_same_context"
A **definitional_representation_relationship_with_same_context** is a type of <<express:representation_schema.definitional_representation_relationship,definitional_representation_relationship>> in which the related representations have the same context.
*)


(*"representation_schema.definitional_representation_relationship_with_same_context.wr:WR1"
Two referenced representations shall have the same context instance.
*)


(*"representation_schema.founded_item"
A **founded_item** is an entity data type that represents part of an element of representation. A **founded_item** can be used only as part of the definition of a <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>>, and is founded through the participation of the <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> in a representation. A <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> that is part of a **founded_item** is founded through that participation. A **founded_item** cannot be an item in a <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>>.
*)

(*"representation_schema.founded_item.__example"
A <<express:geometry_schema.bounded_curve,bounded_curve>> that is the parent curve of a <<express:geometry_schema.composite_curve_segment,composite_curve_segment>> is founded as a result of the <<express:geometry_schema.composite_curve_segment,composite_curve_segment>> being a *founded_item* that is part of a <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> (a <<express:geometry_schema.composite_curve,composite_curve>>).
*)

(*"representation_schema.founded_item.__note"
This entity data type allows errors in other parts of ISO 10303 to be corrected in an upwardly compatible manner. Specifically, it is a supertype of the entity data types <<express:geometry_schema.composite_curve_segment,composite_curve_segment>> and <<express:geometry_schema.surface_patch,surface_patch>>, defined in ISO 10303-42 [4], and <<express:presentation_organization_schema.view_volume,view_volume>>, defined in ISO 10303-46 [6].
*)

(*"representation_schema.founded_item.__note"
This entity data type is not intended to be instantiated as a complex instance of two or more of its defined subtypes <<express:geometry_schema.composite_curve_segment,composite_curve_segment>>, <<express:geometry_schema.surface_patch,surface_patch>>, and <<express:presentation_organization_schema.view_volume,view_volume>>.
*)

(*"representation_schema.founded_item.__note"
This entity data type is not intended for any other use apart from the correction of the errors in other parts of ISO 10303 listed in NOTE 1 above.
*)

(*"representation_schema.founded_item.__note"
The <<express:geometry_schema.bounded_curve,bounded_curve>>, <<express:geometry_schema.composite_curve,composite_curve>>, and <<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_context,geometric_representation_context>> entity types are defined in ISO 10303-42 [4].
*)

(*"representation_schema.founded_item.users"
the set of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> or other <<express:representation_schema.founded_item,founded_item>> that directly or indirectly uses this instance.
*)


(*"representation_schema.founded_item.wr:WR1"
There shall be at least one user. Together with WR2 this ensures that a <<express:representation_schema.founded_item,founded_item>> will be used by at least one <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>>.
*)


(*"representation_schema.founded_item.wr:WR2"
The graph of all users shall be acyclic.
*)


(*"representation_schema.functionally_defined_transformation"
A **functionally_defined_transformation** is a transformation operator that helps to compose an explicit transformation function.
*)

(*"representation_schema.functionally_defined_transformation.__example"
Let f be the transformation function between domain A and range B. The function f:A-\>B takes each element a in A and maps it to an element b in B, i.e., f(a)=b, using the transformation operator (-\>).
*)
(*"representation_schema.functionally_defined_transformation.__example"
An annotated EXPRESS schema defines a subtype _x_y_plane_mirror_transformation_operator_ of this entity type; the definition of the subtype would state that the nature of the _x_y_plane_mirror_transformation_operator_ is to mirror all instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> in the x-y plane, when referenced by a member of <<express:representation_schema.representation_relationship_with_transformation,representation_relationship_with_transformation>>.
*)
(*"representation_schema.functionally_defined_transformation.__example"
An annotated EXPRESS schema associates different natural language translation functions with the values 'English to French' and 'French to English', where these are populations of the *description* attribute of *functionally_defined_transformation* when referenced by a member of <<express:representation_schema.representation_relationship_with_transformation,representation_relationship_with_transformation>>.
*)

(*"representation_schema.functionally_defined_transformation.__note"
The transformation operator can be specified in an annotated EXPRESS schema that uses or specializes this entity data type, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"representation_schema.functionally_defined_transformation.__note"
The transformation function is represented by the <<express:representation_schema.representation_relationship_with_transformation,representation_relationship_with_transformation>> that references a *functionally_defined_transformation* in the role of <<express:representation_schema.representation_relationship_with_transformation.transformation_operator,transformation_operator>>.
*)

(*"representation_schema.functionally_defined_transformation.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **functionally_defined_transformation** is known.
*)


(*"representation_schema.functionally_defined_transformation.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **functionally_defined_transformation**. The value of the **description** need not be specified.
*)


(*"representation_schema.global_uncertainty_assigned_context"
A **global_uncertainty_assigned_context** is a type of <<express:representation_schema.representation_context,representation_context>> that specifies uncertainty for the elements of representation that are associated with it. The uncertainty is specified by instances of <<express:representation_schema.uncertainty_measure_with_unit,uncertainty_measure_with_unit>>, and applies to all elements of representation that are expressed in the same measure and that are associated with a representation that has this <<express:representation_schema.global_uncertainty_assigned_context,global_uncertainty_assigned_context>>.
*)

(*"representation_schema.global_uncertainty_assigned_context.__example"
An instance of *global_uncertainty_assigned_context* specifies uncertainty of 0.01m with respect to lengths. Unless modified by the precedence rules specified in 4.2, this uncertainty applies to each length that occurs in each <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> associated with a representation that has this *global_uncertainty_assigned_context*.
*)

(*"representation_schema.global_uncertainty_assigned_context.__note"
The precedence rules that apply to uncertainties in numeric quantities are specified in Clause Fundamental concepts and assumptions, Uncertainty.
*)

(*"representation_schema.global_uncertainty_assigned_context.uncertainty"
the instances of <<express:representation_schema.uncertainty_measure_with_unit,uncertainty_measure_with_unit>> that apply in the <<express:representation_schema.representation_context,representation_context>>.
*)


(*"representation_schema.item_defined_transformation"
An **item_defined_transformation** has two interpretations. The first interpretation is that an **item_defined_transformation** is a transformation operator that is defined by two instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> in which one instance of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> is the result of applying the transformation operator to the other, in the context of a transformation. The transformation operator is not explicitly provided, but it is derived from the relationship between the instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>>. This interpretation applies when an <<express:representation_schema.item_defined_transformation,item_defined_transformation>> is referenced as an individual by a member of <<express:representation_schema.representation_relationship_with_transformation,representation_relationship_with_transformation>>. The second interpretation is that an **item_defined_transformation** is not a transformation operator but is an association between an element in one representation with an element in another representation. In the second interpretation, each element in the collection of the first representation that is not referenced by a member of **item_defined_transformation** is not associated to an element in the second representation. This interpretation applies when an **item_defined_transformation** is referenced as a member of the aggregate <<express:representation_schema.set_item_defined_transformation,set_item_defined_transformation>> by a member of <<express:representation_schema.representation_relationship_with_transformation,representation_relationship_with_transformation>> with the attribute <<express:representation_schema.representation_relationship_with_transformation.transformation_operator,transformation_operator>>.
*)


(*"representation_schema.item_defined_transformation.__note"
A member of <<express:representation_schema.representation_relationship_with_transformation,representation_relationship_with_transformation>> provides the transformation context and directly references an *item_defined_transformation* in the role of <<express:representation_schema.representation_relationship_with_transformation.transformation_operator,transformation_operator>>.
*)

(*"representation_schema.item_defined_transformation.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **item_defined_transformation** is known.
*)


(*"representation_schema.item_defined_transformation.name.__note"
The name could designate a particular instance of *item_defined_transformation*, or the kind of information that an instance of *item_defined_transformation* conveys.
*)

(*"representation_schema.item_defined_transformation.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **item_defined_transformation**. The value of the **description** need not be specified.
*)


(*"representation_schema.item_defined_transformation.transform_item_1"
the first instance of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> that describes the transformation operator.
*)


(*"representation_schema.item_defined_transformation.transform_item_2"
the second instance of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> that describes the transformation operator.
*)

(*"representation_schema.item_defined_transformation.transform_item_2.__example"
This is an example of interpretation one. Consider one <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> having a set of instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> and a context that is a cartesian coordinate space and a second <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> with another set of instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> and a context that is a second cartesian coordinate space. These instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> are related by rigid motion in a <<express:representation_schema.representation_relationship_with_transformation,representation_relationship_with_transformation>> that uses an *item_defined_transformation*. The *transform_item_1* and *transform_item_2* might each be an <<express:geometry_schema.axis2_placement_3d,axis2_placement_3d>> where each is in the respective cartesian coordinate space. The meaning of such a <<express:representation_schema.representation_relationship,representation_relationship>> would be to relate the two instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> such that the transformation between the two instances of <<express:geometry_schema.axis2_placement_3d,axis2_placement_3d>> applies to every element in the representations.
*)
(*"representation_schema.item_defined_transformation.transform_item_2.__example"
This is an example of interpretation two. Consider a graph model having a 
<<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> 
with a set of instances of 
<<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> (representing node names) and a context that is an ISO/IEC 10646[N] character set (cells 21-7E), and a second <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> 
that contains a set of 
<<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>> instances 
with a context that is a cartesian coordinate space. 
These instances of 
<<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> 
are related in a 
<<express:representation_schema.representation_relationship_with_transformation,representation_relationship_with_transformation>> 
that uses an aggregate of 
<<express:representation_schema.item_defined_transformation,item_defined_transformation>> 
through <<express:representation_schema.set_item_defined_transformation,set_item_defined_transformation>>. 
For one member in the set, the *transform_item_1* is a 
<<express:qualified_measure_schema.descriptive_representation_item,descriptive_representation_item>> 
d1 with a *name* value of '1' and a *description* attribute value of 'node name'. 
The *transform_item_2* is an <<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>> 
af1 in the cartesian coordinate space c2. The meaning of such a 
<<express:representation_schema.representation_relationship,representation_relationship>>
 would be to relate the two instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> 
 such that the node '1' is associated with af1.
*)

(*"representation_schema.mapped_item"
A **mapped_item** is a type of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> that specifies the mapping of a <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> as an element of the items of a second <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>>.
*)

(*"representation_schema.mapped_item.__example"
Figure 2 illustrates the use of the *mapped_item* and <<express:representation_schema.representation_map,representation_map>> entity data types. Three instances of representation are shown. The first representation R1 consists of geometry G1 and an <<express:geometry_schema.axis2_placement_3d,axis2_placement_3d>> A1. The second representation R2 consists of geometry G2 and an <<express:geometry_schema.axis2_placement_3d,axis2_placement_3d>> A2. For the purpose of this example, the nature and structure of G1 and G2 are not relevant. R1 represents the shape of a roof. R2 represents the shape of some walls.



[[figure-representation_schema-example_use_of_mapped_item_and_representation_map]]
.Example of the use of *mapped_item* and <<express:representation_schema.representation_map,representation_map>>
====
image::example_use_of_mapped_item_and_representation_map.gif[]
====



Two instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation_map,representation_map>> allow R1 and R2 to be used as elements in a third <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>>, R3. R3 represents the shape of the building. The first instance of <<express:representation_schema.representation_map,representation_map>> RM1 references R1 as its <<express:representation_schema.representation_map.mapped_representation,mapped_representation>> and A1 as its <<express:representation_schema.representation_map.mapping_origin,mapping_origin>>. The second instance of <<express:representation_schema.representation_map,representation_map>> RM2 references R2 as its <<express:representation_schema.representation_map.mapped_representation,mapped_representation>> and A2 as its <<express:representation_schema.representation_map.mapping_origin,mapping_origin>>.



R3 contains as its items an <<express:geometry_schema.axis2_placement_3d,axis2_placement_3d>> and two instances of *mapped_item*, M1 and M2. M1 references RM1 as its *mapping_source* and A3 as its *mapping_target*. M2 references RM2 as its *mapping_source* and A3 as its *mapping_target*. The result is that R3 uses R1 and R2 as parts of its definition. As it is used in R3, R1 is transformed so that A1 is mapped onto A3. As it is used in R3, R2 is transformed so that A2 is mapped onto A3.



This example shows how the *mapped_item* and <<express:representation_schema.representation_map,representation_map>> entity data types can be used to describe the composition of one representation from other instances of representation. See 4.4.14 for an example of the use of <<express:representation_schema.representation_relationship,representation_relationship>> to describe whole-part associations between instances of representation.
*)

(*"representation_schema.mapped_item.__note"
See 4.2 for the fundamental concepts and assumptions that apply to this entity data type.
*)

(*"representation_schema.mapped_item.__note"
The mapping includes a transformation that is derived from the *mapping_source*.<<express:representation_schema.representation_map.mapping_origin,mapping_origin>> and the *mapping_target* attributes. See 4.2 for the fundamental concepts and assumptions that apply to transformation.
*)

(*"representation_schema.mapped_item.__note"
The precise meaning of the mapping can be specified in an annotated EXPRESS schema that uses or specializes this entity data type and the <<express:representation_schema.representation_map,representation_map>> entity data type, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"representation_schema.mapped_item.mapping_source"
the <<express:representation_schema.representation_map,representation_map>> that specifies the source and the origin of the **mapped_item**.
*)


(*"representation_schema.mapped_item.mapping_target"
the <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> that is the target onto which the **mapping_source** is mapped.
*)


(*"representation_schema.mapped_item.wr:WR1"
A **mapped_item** shall not be self-defining by participating in the definition of the <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> being mapped.
*)


(*"representation_schema.parametric_representation_context"
A **parametric_representation_context** is a type of <<express:representation_schema.representation_context,representation_context>> in which instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> are defined in a parametric space.
*)


(*"representation_schema.parametric_representation_context.__note"
The definition of the parametric space can be specified in an annotated EXPRESS schema that uses or specializes this entity data type.
*)

(*"representation_schema.parametric_representation_context.__note"
In a *parametric_representation_context*, length units are dimensionless.
*)

(*"representation_schema.parametric_representation_context.wr:IP1"
If the entity instance is also an instance of <<express:measure_schema.global_unit_assigned_context,global_unit_assigned_context>>, then the <<express:measure_schema.global_unit_assigned_context,global_unit_assigned_context>>.<<express:measure_schema.global_unit_assigned_context.units,units>> attribute shall not include a <<express:measure_schema.length_unit,length_unit>>.
*)


(*"representation_schema.parametric_representation_context.wr:IP1.__note"
The <<express:measure_schema.global_unit_assigned_context,global_unit_assigned_context>> and <<express:measure_schema.length_unit,length_unit>> entity data types are defined in <<ISO_10303-41>>.
*)

(*"representation_schema.representation"
A **representation** is a collection of one or more <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> instances that are related in a specified <<express:representation_schema.representation_context,representation_context>>.

The relationship of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> to <<express:representation_schema.representation_context,representation_context>> is the basis for distinguishing which <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> entities are related.

A <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> can be related to a <<express:representation_schema.representation_context,representation_context>> directly, when it occurs as an element in a representation, or indirectly, when it is referenced through any number of intervening entities, each of type <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> or <<express:representation_schema.founded_item,founded_item>>.

A **representation** relates a <<express:representation_schema.representation_context,representation_context>> to trees of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> instances each tree being rooted in one member of the set of **items**. A <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> or <<express:representation_schema.founded_item,founded_item>> is one node in the tree; a relationship between one <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> or <<express:representation_schema.founded_item,founded_item>> and another is an edge.
*)

(*"representation_schema.representation.__example"
Two cartesian points P and Q (described by instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>>) are related in a context A (they are elements in the same representation in context A, or are elements in different representations that share context A). It is therefore possible to calculate the distance between these points. A third cartesian point R (also described by an instance of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>>) is not related to context A. It is not possible to determine the distance between R and P, or between R and Q.
*)
(*"representation_schema.representation.__example"
Consider a collection of two-dimensional <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> instances used to represent the shape of a machined part. It is not a complete description of the shape, but is suitable for certain applications such as computer-aided draughting.
*)
(*"representation_schema.representation.__example"
Consider a surface that is used in the respective representations of the shape of a casting die and of the shape of the part cast in that die. The same surface is related to two distinct instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation_context,representation_context>> (i.e., coordinate spaces): one for the die and one for the part by the two instances of *representation*. However, the two instances of *representation* are not related; they simply share a common <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>>.
*)

(*"representation_schema.representation.__note"
The use of a *representation*, i.e., that which is being represented, is not specified in this document. It can be specified in an annotated EXPRESS schema that uses or specializes this entity data type.
*)

(*"representation_schema.representation.__note"
Instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item_relationship,representation_item_relationship>> do not form either nodes or edges in this tree; an instance of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> is not part of the tree solely because it is associated with an element in the tree by an instance of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item_relationship,representation_item_relationship>>.
*)

(*"representation_schema.representation.__note"
A *representation* can be incomplete in that it need not fully model the concept that is represented, although it could be adequate for a given application.
*)

(*"representation_schema.representation.__note"
Two instances of *representation* are not related solely because the same instance of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> is referenced directly or indirectly from their sets of *items*.
*)

(*"representation_schema.representation.__note"
Two instances of *representation* are not related solely because instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> in their sets of items are related by an instance of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item_relationship,representation_item_relationship>>.
*)

(*"representation_schema.representation.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **representation** is known.
*)


(*"representation_schema.representation.name.__note"
The name could designate a particular instance of *representation*, or the kind of information that an instance of *representation* conveys.
*)

(*"representation_schema.representation.items"
a set of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> that are related in the **context_of_items**.
*)


(*"representation_schema.representation.context_of_items"
a <<express:representation_schema.representation_context,representation_context>> in which the items are related to form a representation of some concept.
*)


(*"representation_schema.representation.id"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> that distinguishes the **representation**.
*)


(*"representation_schema.representation.id.__note"
This attribute is an upwardly compatible addition to *representation* as specified in the first edition of this document.
*)

(*"representation_schema.representation.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **representation**.
*)


(*"representation_schema.representation.description.__note"
This attribute is an upwardly compatible addition to *representation* as specified in the first edition of this document.
*)

(*"representation_schema.representation.wr:WR1"
Each **representation** shall be the <<express:basic_attribute_schema.id_attribute.identified_item,identified_item>> in at most one <<express:basic_attribute_schema.id_attribute,id_attribute>>.
*)


(*"representation_schema.representation.wr:WR1.__note"
The <<express:basic_attribute_schema.id_attribute,id_attribute>> entity data type is defined in the <<express:basic_attribute_schema,basic_attribute_schema>> in <<ISO_10303-41>>.
*)

(*"representation_schema.representation.wr:WR2"
Each representation shall be the <<express:basic_attribute_schema.name_attribute.named_item,named_item>> in at most one <<express:basic_attribute_schema.name_attribute,name_attribute>>.
*)


(*"representation_schema.representation.wr:WR2.__note"
The <<express:basic_attribute_schema.name_attribute,name_attribute>> entity data type is defined in the <<express:basic_attribute_schema,basic_attribute_schema>> in <<ISO_10303-41>>.
*)

(*"representation_schema.representation.wr:WR2.__note"
A template for constraining the population of the entity data types defined in the <<express:basic_attribute_schema,basic_attribute_schema>> is described in <<ISO_10303-41,annex=E>>.
*)

(*"representation_schema.representation.wr:IP1"
A **set_item_defined_transformation** is in the role of **transformation_operator**, the ordering of the instances of **representation** given for the inherited attributes of <<express:representation_schema.representation_relationship,representation_relationship>> shall be consistent with the ordering of the two instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> given as attributes of members of <<express:representation_schema.item_defined_transformation,item_defined_transformation>> that are in the **set_item_defined_transformation**.
*)


(*"representation_schema.representation_context"
A **representation_context** is a context in which instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> are related.
*)


(*"representation_schema.representation_context.__note"
Two instances of *representation_context* are separate and have no relationship unless a relationship is explicitly specified between them in an annotated EXPRESS schema that uses or specializes this entity data type.
*)

(*"representation_schema.representation_context.context_identifier"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> that distinguishes the **representation_context**.
*)


(*"representation_schema.representation_context.context_type"
a description of the type of the **representation_context**.
*)


(*"representation_schema.representation_context.context_type.__note"
Constraints on the uniqueness of *context_identifier*, or the allowed values of *context_type*, can be specified in an annotated EXPRESS schema that uses or specializes this entity data type.
*)

(*"representation_schema.representation_context.representations_in_context"
the instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> that refer to the **representation_context**.
*)


(*"representation_schema.representation_context_reference"
A **representation_context_reference** is an identification based reference to a <<express:representation_schema.representation_context,representation_context>>.
*)


(*"representation_schema.representation_context_reference.context_identifier"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> that distinguishes the **representation_context_reference**.
*)


(*"representation_schema.representation_context_reference.representations_in_context"
the instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> that refer to the **representation_context_reference**.
*)


(*"representation_schema.representation_item"
A **representation_item** is an element of representation. A **representation_item** participates in one or more instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>>, or contributes to the definition of another **representation_item**.
*)

(*"representation_schema.representation_item.__example"
Consider two instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>>, each having the same value for <<express:representation_schema.representation.context_of_items,context_of_items>>. One is a <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> of the shape of a cube and indirectly references a <<express:geometry_schema.line,line>> as one of its edges. The second simply references the <<express:geometry_schema.line,line>> as one of its <<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>>. There are not two occurrences of the line and its sub-tree of referenced instances of *representation_item* in the <<express:representation_schema.representation_context,representation_context>>. Rather, the use of the line in that <<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_context,geometric_representation_context>> has been asserted twice, once in each <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>>.
*)
(*"representation_schema.representation_item.__example"
The <<express:representation_schema.compound_representation_item,compound_representation_item>> entity data type provides a general capability to define one *representation_item* using other instances of *representation_item*. This can be used to create tabular structures: each cell in the table is a *representation_item* (such as a <<express:qualified_measure_schema.measure_representation_item,measure_representation_item>> that provides a name-value-unit tuple), and the table is itself a *representation_item* that participates in the representation of a product property. The *representation_item* instances that are the cells in the table do not participate directly in the representation.
*)

(*"representation_schema.representation_item.__note"
One *representation_item* contributes to the definition of a second *representation_item* if the first is referenced by the second.
*)

(*"representation_schema.representation_item.__note"
The same *representation_item* could be related multiple times to the same <<express:representation_schema.representation_context,representation_context>> by being used directly or indirectly in several instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>>, each referencing the same <<express:representation_schema.representation_context,representation_context>>. This does not have the meaning that each <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> is creating a new instance of the same *representation_item* in the same <<express:representation_schema.representation_context,representation_context>>. Rather, each <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> reasserts the use of the same instance of *representation_item* in the <<express:representation_schema.representation_context,representation_context>> for different uses.
*)

(*"representation_schema.representation_item.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **representation_item** is known.
*)


(*"representation_schema.representation_item.name.__note"
The name could designate a particular instance of *representation_item* or the kind of information that an instance of *representation_item* conveys.
*)

(*"representation_schema.representation_item.wr:WR1"
The **representation_item** shall participate in at least one <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>>, either as an item in that <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> or being directly or indirectly referenced by an item in the <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>>.
*)


(*"representation_schema.representation_item_relationship"
A **representation_item_relationship** is an association between two instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>>. A **representation_item_relationship** can associate two instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> in the same <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> or in two different instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>>. In this association the two instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> are independent; neither is founded with respect to the other or the instance(s) of <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> in which they participate. If the instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> that are associated are in different instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>>, this association does not relate the instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>>.
*)


(*"representation_schema.representation_item_relationship.__note"
The meaning of the association can be specified in an annotated EXPRESS schema that uses or specializes this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"representation_schema.representation_item_relationship.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **representation_item_relationship** is known.
*)


(*"representation_schema.representation_item_relationship.name.__note"
The name could designate a particular instance of *representation_item_relationship* or the kind of information that an instance of *representation_item_relationship* conveys.
*)

(*"representation_schema.representation_item_relationship.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **representation_item_relationship**. The value of the **description** need not be specified.
*)


(*"representation_schema.representation_item_relationship.relating_representation_item"
one of the instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> that participates in the association.
*)


(*"representation_schema.representation_item_relationship.relating_representation_item.__note"
The role of this attribute can be defined in an annotated EXPRESS schema that uses or specializes this entity data type.
*)

(*"representation_schema.representation_item_relationship.related_representation_item"
the other instance of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> that participates in the association. If one element of the association is dependent upon the other, this attribute shall be the dependent one.
*)


(*"representation_schema.representation_item_relationship.related_representation_item.__note"
The role of this attribute can be defined in an annotated EXPRESS schema that uses or specializes this entity data type.
*)

(*"representation_schema.representation_map"
A **representation_map** is the identification of a <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>>, and of a <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> that is an element within the context of the <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>>, for the purpose of mapping. The <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> defines the origin of the mapping.
*)


(*"representation_schema.representation_map.__note"
An instance of *representation_map* is used as the source of a mapping by an instance of <<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>>. See 4.4.7 for an example of the use of these two entity data types.
*)

(*"representation_schema.representation_map.mapping_origin"
a <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> from which the **mapped_representation** is to be mapped.
*)


(*"representation_schema.representation_map.mapped_representation"
a <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> that is to be mapped to at least one <<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>>.
*)


(*"representation_schema.representation_map.map_usage"
the set of one or more instances of <<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>> to which the **representation_map** is mapped.
*)


(*"representation_schema.representation_map.wr:WR1"
The **mapping_origin** shall be in the <<express:representation_schema.representation_context,representation_context>> of the **mapped_representation**.
*)


(*"representation_schema.representation_relationship"
A **representation_relationship** is the association of two instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation_or_representation_reference,representation_or_representation_reference>>. One <<express:representation_schema.representation_or_representation_reference,representation_or_representation_reference>> is not made part of the definition of the other by participation in a **representation_relationship**.
*)

(*"representation_schema.representation_relationship.__example"
Two instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation_or_representation_reference,representation_or_representation_reference>> each describe a property of a product. The second of these instances is a more complete and accurate description of the property. An instance of *representation_relationship* can be used to denote the second instance of <<express:representation_schema.representation_or_representation_reference,representation_or_representation_reference>> as being the successor of the first.
*)

(*"representation_schema.representation_relationship.__note"
The meaning of the association can be specified in an annotated EXPRESS schema that uses or specializes this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"representation_schema.representation_relationship.__note"
A combination of instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation_or_representation_reference,representation_or_representation_reference>> and *representation_relationship* can form a graph of related instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation_or_representation_reference,representation_or_representation_reference>>. In such a graph, instances of representation are the nodes and instances of *representation_relationship* are the branches connecting the nodes.
*)

(*"representation_schema.representation_relationship.__note"
Constraints can be specified that ensure that such a graph is acyclic, i.e., that no instance of <<express:representation_schema.representation_or_representation_reference,representation_or_representation_reference>> is its own ancestor. Such constraints are outside the scope of this document.
*)

(*"representation_schema.representation_relationship.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **representation_relationship** is known.
*)


(*"representation_schema.representation_relationship.name.__note"
The name could designate a particular instance of *representation_relationship* or the kind of information that an instance of *representation_relationship* conveys.
*)

(*"representation_schema.representation_relationship.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **representation_relationship**. The value of the **description** need not be specified.
*)


(*"representation_schema.representation_relationship.rep_1"
the first of two <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> that are related.
*)


(*"representation_schema.representation_relationship.rep_2"
the second of two <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> that are related.
*)


(*"representation_schema.representation_relationship.rep_2.__note"
There is no significance to the ordering of the two related instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>>. The names *rep_1* and *rep_2* serve only to distinguish the attributes. If any significance to the ordering is needed in any specialization of *representation_relationship*, this significance can be defined in the specialization.
*)

(*"representation_schema.representation_relationship_with_transformation"
A **representation_relationship_with_transformation** is a type of <<express:representation_schema.representation_relationship,representation_relationship>>. A **representation_relationship_with_transformation** defines a functional relationship between the context specified by the two <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>>s when the **transformation_operator** is either a <<express:representation_schema.functionally_defined_transformation,functionally_defined_transformation>> or an <<express:representation_schema.item_defined_transformation,item_defined_transformation>>. A **representation_relationship_with_transformation** defines an association between the contexts specified by the two <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>>s and defines a collection of relationships between one or more of the items specified by the two <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>>s when the **transformation_operator** is a <<express:representation_schema.set_item_defined_transformation,set_item_defined_transformation>>.
*)

(*"representation_schema.representation_relationship_with_transformation.__example"
Figure 3 illustrates the use of the *representation_relationship_with_transformation* entity data type where the *transformation_operator* is an <<express:representation_schema.item_defined_transformation,item_defined_transformation>> Three instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> are shown. The first <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> R1 contains some geometry G1 and an <<express:geometry_schema.axis2_placement_3d,axis2_placement_3d>> A1. The second <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> contains some geometry G2 and an <<express:geometry_schema.axis2_placement_3d,axis2_placement_3d>> A2. For the purpose of this example, the nature and structure of G1 and G2 are not relevant. R1 represents the shape of a roof. R2 represents the shape of some walls.



[[figure-representation_schema-example_use_of_representation_relationship_with_transformation]]
.Example of the use of *representation_relationship_with_transformation*
====
image::example_use_of_representation_relationship_with_transformation.gif[]
====



Two instances of *representation_relationship_with_transformation* allow R1 and R2 to be associated with a third <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>>, R3. R3 represents the shape of the building. R3 contains a single item: an <<express:geometry_schema.axis2_placement_3d,axis2_placement_3d>>. The associations between R1 and R3, and between R2 and R3, do not make R1 and R2 parts of R3. However, the associations between R1 and R3, and between R2 and R3, allow an application to infer that G1 and G2 can be combined and used to describe the shape of the building. An application can make use of the specified transformations to compose the overall shape from G1 and G2.
*)
(*"representation_schema.representation_relationship_with_transformation.__example"
This example illustrates the use of the *representation_relationship_with_transformation* entity data types where the *transformation_operator* is a <<express:representation_schema.functionally_defined_transformation,functionally_defined_transformation>>. Two instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> contain instances of <<express:qualified_measure_schema.descriptive_representation_item,descriptive_representation_item>>, an element of representation that specifies the use of a text string for representation, and two references to <<express:representation_schema.representation_context,representation_context>> instances that define human languages for context. The first instance of <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> contains descriptions in the English language; and the second contains descriptions in the French language. An instance of *representation_relationship_with_transformation* could be used to assert an association between these instances of representation, where the referenced <<express:representation_schema.functionally_defined_transformation,functionally_defined_transformation>> is a language translation table. The <<express:qualified_measure_schema.descriptive_representation_item,descriptive_representation_item>> entity data type is defined in ISO 10303-45 [5].
*)

(*"representation_schema.representation_relationship_with_transformation.__note"
The interpretation of the relationship between the two contexts depends on the value of the *transformation_operator* attribute.
*)

(*"representation_schema.representation_relationship_with_transformation.__note"
See the example given for <<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>> and its use of <<express:representation_schema.representation_map,representation_map>> to describe the composition of one <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> from other instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>>. .
*)

(*"representation_schema.representation_relationship_with_transformation.transformation_operator"
a <<express:representation_schema.transformation,transformation>> that relates the <<express:representation_schema.representation.context_of_items,context_of_items>> of the two related <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>>.
*)


(*"representation_schema.representation_relationship_with_transformation.wr:WR1"
The two related <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> shall not have the same <<express:representation_schema.representation_context,representation_context>>.
*)


(*"representation_schema.representation_relationship_with_transformation.wr:WR2"
If the **transformation_operator** is an <<express:representation_schema.item_defined_transformation,item_defined_transformation>>, the ordering of the instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> given for the inherited attributes of <<express:representation_schema.representation_relationship,representation_relationship>> shall be consistent with the ordering of the two instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> given as attributes of <<express:representation_schema.item_defined_transformation,item_defined_transformation>>.
*)


(*"representation_schema.representation_relationship_with_transformation.wr:IP1"
If the <<express:representation_schema.transformation,transformation>> is an <<express:representation_schema.item_defined_transformation,item_defined_transformation>>, then <<express:representation_schema.item_defined_transformation.transform_item_1,transform_item_1>> shall be in the context of <<express:representation_schema.representation_relationship.rep_1,rep_1>> and <<express:representation_schema.item_defined_transformation.transform_item_2,transform_item_2>> shall be in the context of <<express:representation_schema.representation_relationship.rep_2,rep_2>>.
*)


(*"representation_schema.representation_relationship_with_transformation.wr:IP2"
If a <<express:representation_schema.set_item_defined_transformation,set_item_defined_transformation>> is in the role of <<express:representation_schema.representation_relationship_with_transformation.transformation_operator,transformation_operator>>, no <<express:representation_schema.item_defined_transformation,item_defined_transformation>> that is a member of the set shall reference a placement type in both the **transform_item_1** attribute and the **transform_item_2** attribute.
*)


(*"representation_schema.uncertainty_assigned_representation"
An **uncertainty_assigned_representation** is a type of <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> that specifies uncertainty with respect to the elements of representation that it collects. The **uncertainty** is specified by instances of <<express:representation_schema.uncertainty_measure_with_unit,uncertainty_measure_with_unit>>, and applies to all elements of representation that are expressed in the same measures.
*)

(*"representation_schema.uncertainty_assigned_representation.__example"
This entity data type can be used to specify the uncertainties that apply to the numeric values used to represent a property. For example, in an application protocol whose domain is acoustical engineering, there could be an uncertainty of 1 decibel in the values that represent the relative loudness of sounds.
*)

(*"representation_schema.uncertainty_assigned_representation.__note"
The precedence rules that apply to uncertainty in numeric quantities are specified in 4.2.
*)

(*"representation_schema.uncertainty_assigned_representation.uncertainty"
the set of instances of <<express:representation_schema.uncertainty_measure_with_unit,uncertainty_measure_with_unit>> that apply to instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> in the **uncertainty_assigned_representation**.
*)


(*"representation_schema.uncertainty_measure_with_unit"
An **uncertainty_measure_with_unit** is a type of <<express:measure_schema.measure_with_unit,measure_with_unit>> that specifies the uncertainty that applies to a type of measure. An **uncertainty_measure_with_unit** applies to each <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> that uses the type of measure specified in the <<express:measure_schema.measure_with_unit.value_component,value_component>> of the **uncertainty_measure_with_unit**, in the following cases:

* the <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> is part of an <<express:representation_schema.uncertainty_assigned_representation,uncertainty_assigned_representation>>;
* the <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> is founded in a <<express:measure_schema.global_unit_assigned_context,global_unit_assigned_context>>; or
* the <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> is a <<express:qualified_measure_schema.qualified_representation_item,qualified_representation_item>>.
*)


(*"representation_schema.uncertainty_measure_with_unit.__note"
The <<express:qualified_measure_schema.qualified_representation_item,qualified_representation_item>> entity data type is defined in ISO 10303-45 [5].
*)

(*"representation_schema.uncertainty_measure_with_unit.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **uncertainty_measure_with_unit** is known.
*)


(*"representation_schema.uncertainty_measure_with_unit.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **uncertainty_measure_with_unit**. The value of the **description** need not be specified.
*)


(*"representation_schema.uncertainty_measure_with_unit.wr:WR1"
The <<express:measure_schema.measure_with_unit.value_component,value_component>> of the **uncertainty_measure_with_unit** shall be a positive number if the type of the <<express:measure_schema.measure_with_unit.value_component,value_component>> is a number.
*)


(*"representation_schema.value_representation_item"
A **value_representation_item** is a type of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> that specifies only a measure value. The unit that applies to the specified value is provided by a <<express:measure_schema.global_unit_assigned_context,global_unit_assigned_context>> of the <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> containing the **value_representation_item**.
*)


(*"representation_schema.value_representation_item.__note"
The <<express:measure_schema.global_unit_assigned_context,global_unit_assigned_context>> entity data type, subtype of <<express:representation_schema.representation_context,representation_context>>, is defined in <<ISO_10303-41>>.
*)

(*"representation_schema.value_representation_item.__note"
The <<express:qualified_measure_schema.measure_representation_item,measure_representation_item>> entity data type, specified in ISO 10303-45 [5], is an element of <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> that consists of a value and a unit.
*)

(*"representation_schema.value_representation_item.value_component"
the value of the element of representation when expressed with in the unit specified in the <<express:measure_schema.global_unit_assigned_context,global_unit_assigned_context>>.
*)


(*"representation_schema.value_representation_item.wr:WR1"
Every **value_representation_item** shall be an item in a <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> whose <<express:representation_schema.representation.context_of_items,context_of_items>> attribute references an instance of <<express:representation_schema.representation_context,representation_context>> that is a <<express:measure_schema.global_unit_assigned_context,global_unit_assigned_context>>, or shall participate in the definition of such a <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>>.
*)


(*"representation_schema.value_representation_item.wr:IP1"
If a **value_representation_item** is an item in more than one <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>>, each <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> shall specify the same unit, either by referencing the same <<express:measure_schema.global_unit_assigned_context,global_unit_assigned_context>>, or by referencing different instances of <<express:measure_schema.global_unit_assigned_context,global_unit_assigned_context>> that specify the same unit.
*)


(*"representation_schema.acyclic_mapped_representation"
The function **acyclic_mapped_representation** determines if a given <<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>> is self-defining by virtue of mapping a <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> in which the <<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>> is used. The function checks both the <<express:representation_schema.representation_map.mapped_representation,mapped_representation>> and the <<express:representation_schema.representation_map.mapped_representation,mapped_representation>>.<<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> recursively for any instances of <<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>>, or <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> referencing a <<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>>, that might cause a self defining reference.

This function returns TRUE if the input candidate <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> does not cause self definition. It returns FALSE otherwise. The type of the function is BOOLEAN.
*)


(*"representation_schema.acyclic_mapped_representation.__note"
This function is used to constrain the entity <<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>>.
*)

(*"representation_schema.acyclic_mapped_representation.mi"
the specified <<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>>.
*)


(*"representation_schema.acyclic_representation_relationship"
The **acyclic_representation_relationship** function checks if specified <<express:representation_schema.representation_relationship,representation_relationship>> is not participating in cycle with regards to specified <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>>.
*)


(*"representation_schema.acyclic_representation_relationship.relation"
the specified <<express:representation_schema.representation_relationship,representation_relationship>>.
*)


(*"representation_schema.acyclic_representation_relationship.relatives"
the specified <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>>.
*)


(*"representation_schema.acyclic_representation_relationship.specific_relation"
the specified type of <<express:representation_schema.representation_relationship,representation_relationship>> to be considered.
*)


(*"representation_schema.item_in_context"
The function **item_in_context** determines if a <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> is related to a <<express:representation_schema.representation_context,representation_context>>. The function returns TRUE if the **item** argument is related by a <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> to the input **cntxt** argument. Function **item_in_context** returns FALSE otherwise. The type of the function is BOOLEAN.

A <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> is related to a <<express:representation_schema.representation_context,representation_context>> if it is:

* referenced in the set of <<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> of a <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> where **cntxt** appears as the <<express:representation_schema.representation.context_of_items,context_of_items>>, or
* referenced by a <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> that is an **item_in_context** of the **cntxt**.
*)


(*"representation_schema.item_in_context.__note"
The second condition is a recursive check allowing for a <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> to be related to a <<express:representation_schema.representation_context,representation_context>> by being part of a tree of related instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>>. The tree is rooted in an entity that is related to a <<express:representation_schema.representation_context,representation_context>> by fulfilling the first or second condition.
*)

(*"representation_schema.item_in_context.__note"
The function *item_in_context* only determines if an *item* is related to a specific <<express:representation_schema.representation_context,representation_context>>. The relationship of the *item* to some other <<express:representation_schema.representation_context,representation_context>> is not determined.
*)

(*"representation_schema.item_in_context.item"
the <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> checked for relationship in **cntxt**. This is input to the function.
*)


(*"representation_schema.item_in_context.cntxt"
the <<express:representation_schema.representation_context,representation_context>> for which relationship to **item** is determined. This is input to the function.
*)


(*"representation_schema.using_items"
The function **using_items** returns the set of instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> or <<express:representation_schema.founded_item,founded_item>> that reference a <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> directly or indirectly.
*)


(*"representation_schema.using_items.item"
the <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> for which the referencing instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> and <<express:representation_schema.founded_item,founded_item>> are determined. This is input to the function.
*)


(*"representation_schema.using_items.checked_items"
the set of instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> and <<express:representation_schema.founded_item,founded_item>> that have been checked already in order to ensure termination of the recursive function. This is input to the function.
*)


(*"representation_schema.using_representations"
The function **using_representations** returns the set of representations in which a <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> is used.

A <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> is used in a representation if it is:

* referenced in the set of <<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> of the <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>>,
* referenced by a <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> used in the <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>>, or
* referenced by a <<express:representation_schema.founded_item,founded_item>> used in the <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>>.

A <<express:representation_schema.founded_item,founded_item>> or a <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> is used in a <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> if it is referenced directly, or indirectly, by a <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> in the set of items of the <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>>.
*)


(*"representation_schema.using_representations.__note"
The second and third conditions are checks allowing for a <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> to be used in a <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> by being part of a tree of related <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> or <<express:representation_schema.founded_item,founded_item>>. The tree is rooted in an entity used in a <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> by fulfilling the first condition.
*)

(*"representation_schema.using_representations.item"
the <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> or <<express:representation_schema.founded_item,founded_item>> for which using instances of <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> are determined. This is input to the function.
*)


(*"representation_schema.valid_measure_value"
The function **valid_measure_value** determines whether a <<express:measure_schema.measure_value,measure_value>> is valid. The function returns TRUE if the <<express:measure_schema.measure_value,measure_value>> is numeric and is positive, or if it is textual. Function **valid_measure_value** returns FALSE otherwise.
*)


(*"representation_schema.valid_measure_value.m"
the <<express:measure_schema.measure_value,measure_value>> to be checked. This is the input to the function.
*)


(*"representation_schema.__schema_file"
data/resource_docs/representation_structures/resource.xml
*)


