* <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_dataset>>; 17
* <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_dataset_with_colours>>; 18
====
*)

(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_set_or_superset"
The **point_cloud_set_or_superset** select type collects together, for reference when constructing more complex models, sets and supersets of point clouds.
*)


(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.scanned_data_item"
A **scanned_data_item** is a type of <<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_item,geometric_representation_item>> that represents an element of geometric data produced by a scanner. A **scanned_data_item** is required to be used in a <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.scan_data_shape_representation,scan_data_shape_representation>>.
*)


(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.scanned_data_item.wr:WR1"
Each **scanned_data_item** shall be used in a <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.scan_data_shape_representation,scan_data_shape_representation>>.
*)


(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_dataset"
A **point_cloud_dataset** is a type of <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.scanned_data_item,scanned_data_item>>, and represents the geometry of a cloud of points produced by a scanner.

.
*)


(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_dataset.__note"
The *point_cloud_dataset* has subtypes with additional attributes to permit the creation of instances of a *point_cloud_dataset* with normals, with colours, or with intensities. The and/or relationship between these subtypes enables, for example, the creation as a complex instance, of a *point_cloud_dataset* with normals and colours attached to each point.
*)

(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_dataset.point_coordinates"
the list of real triples defining the coordinates of the points.
*)


(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_dataset.point_coordinates.__note"
These real triples have the semantics of <<express:measure_schema.length_measure,length_measure>>s, but are not formally defined as such, the units for these coordinates are defined since a <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.scanned_data_item,scanned_data_item>> is required to be used in a <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.scan_data_shape_representation,scan_data_shape_representation>> having a <<express:measure_schema.global_unit_assigned_context,global_unit_assigned_context>>.
*)

(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_dataset_with_normals"
A **point_cloud_dataset_with_normals** is a type of <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_dataset,point_cloud_dataset>>, which has a normal defined at each point of the dataset.
*)


(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_dataset_with_normals.normals"
a list of real triples defining the direction ratios of the normals at each point of the <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_dataset,point_cloud_dataset>>.
*)


(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_dataset_with_normals.wr:WR1"
The size of the **normals** list shall be the same as the size of the <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_dataset.point_coordinates,point_coordinates>> list.
*)


(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_dataset_with_colours"
A **point_cloud_dataset_with_colours** is a type of <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_dataset,point_cloud_dataset>>, which has a colour defined at each point of the dataset.
*)


(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_dataset_with_colours.colour_indices"
a list of integer triples defining the RGB integer values of the colours at each point of the <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_dataset,point_cloud_dataset>>.
*)


(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_dataset_with_colours.wr:WR1"
The size of the **colour_indices** list shall be the same as the size of the <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_dataset.point_coordinates,point_coordinates>> list.
*)


(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_dataset_with_intensities"
A **point_cloud_dataset_with_intensities** is a type of <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_dataset,point_cloud_dataset>>, which has an intensity defined at each point of the dataset.
*)


(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_dataset_with_intensities.intensities"
a list of real numbers defining the intensity value at each point of the <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_dataset,point_cloud_dataset>>.
*)


(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_dataset_with_intensities.wr:WR1"
The size of the **intensities** list shall be the same as the size of the <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_dataset.point_coordinates,point_coordinates>> list.
*)


(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_superdataset"
A **point_cloud_superdataset** is a type of <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.scanned_data_item,scanned_data_item>>, which contains a list of <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_dataset,point_cloud_dataset>>s. Each of the <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_dataset,point_cloud_dataset>>s, except, possibly, the last is required to contain the same number of points.
*)


(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_superdataset.pts_per_sublist"
the number of points in each listed <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_dataset,point_cloud_dataset>>, except for the last.
*)


(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_superdataset.sublists"
a list of 2 or more <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_dataset,point_cloud_dataset>>s .
*)


(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_superdataset.wr:WR1"
The number of points in each <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_dataset,point_cloud_dataset>> in **sublists**, except for the last shall be **pts_per_sublist** the last element of the **sublists** shall not contain more than this number of points. These conditions are verified by the <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.consistent_sizes,consistent_sizes>> function.
*)


(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.triangulated_point_cloud_dataset"
A **triangulated_point_cloud_dataset** is a type of <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.scanned_data_item,scanned_data_item>> in which the points of the dataset are arranged into triangles.
*)


(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.triangulated_point_cloud_dataset.points"
the <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_dataset,point_cloud_dataset>> or <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_superdataset,point_cloud_superdataset>> containing the coordinates of the points used to construct the trinagles.
*)


(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.triangulated_point_cloud_dataset.triangles"
a list of integer triples defining the locations in <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.triangulated_point_cloud_dataset.points,points>> of the coordinate values for the 3 vertices of each triangle. If <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.triangulated_point_cloud_dataset.points,points>> is of type <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_dataset,point_cloud_dataset>> the integer directly gives the position in <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_dataset.point_coordinates,point_coordinates>> of the coordinates of the vertex point. If <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.triangulated_point_cloud_dataset.points,points>> is of type <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_superdataset,point_cloud_superdataset>> it is necessary to first determine, by dividing the integer value by <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_superdataset.pts_per_sublist,pts_per_sublist>>, the particular <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_dataset,point_cloud_dataset>> in which to find the coordinates position. The remainder from this division is then the required address.
*)

(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.triangulated_point_cloud_dataset.triangles.__example"
In the case of a superdataset, if the integer value is 5927 and if the value of <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_superdataset.pts_per_sublist,pts_per_sublist>> is 2000, then the required point coordinates will be in position 1927 of the <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.triangulated_point_cloud_dataset.points,points>> coordinates list of the 3rd. <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_dataset,point_cloud_dataset>>. If the integer value is exactly 2000 then the required point coordinates are in the last position in the first <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_dataset,point_cloud_dataset>>. <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.triangulated_point_cloud_dataset.points,points>> list.
*)

(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.scan_3d_model"
A **scan_3d_model** is a type of <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.scanned_data_item,scanned_data_item>>, which represents the data produced by scanning a 3D shape. It contains scanner properties and a set of <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.scanned_data_item,scanned_data_item>>s. Each of the <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.scanned_data_item,scanned_data_item>>s includes point cloud data..
*)


(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.scan_3d_model.scanner_info"
a set of 1 or more <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.scanner_property,scanner_property>>;
*)


(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.scan_3d_model.scanned_points"
a set of 1 or more <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.scanned_data_item,scanned_data_item>>s which contains the point cloud data produced by the scanning operation.;
*)


(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.scan_3d_model.wr:WR1"
The **scanned_points** set shall not contain a <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.scan_3d_model,scan_3d_model>>.
*)


(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.scanner_property"
A **scanner_property** is a type of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>>, which represents one or more properties of a scanner.
*)


(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.scanner_basic_properties"
A **scanner_basic_properties** is a type of <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.scanner_property,scanner_property>>, which represents the basic properties of a scanner.
*)


(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.scanner_basic_properties.__note"
More advanced properties of a scanner may be represented by further subtypes of <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.scanner_property,scanner_property>>
*)

(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.scanner_basic_properties.scanner_identification"
a label which identifies the scanner;
*)


(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.scanner_basic_properties.scanner_location"
a <<express:geometry_schema.axis2_placement_3d,axis2_placement_3d>> which is the location and orientation of the scanner;
*)


(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.scanner_basic_properties.scanner_uncertainty"
an optional <<express:measure_schema.positive_length_measure,positive_length_measure>> which gives the possible error in the coordinate values measured by the scanner.
*)


(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.scan_data_shape_representation"
A **scan_data_shape_representation** is a type of <<express:product_property_representation_schema.shape_representation,shape_representation>> in which the geometry of a 3D shape is approximately represented by a set of point cloud data produced by a scanner.
*)


(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.scan_data_shape_representation.items"
the <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.scanned_data_item,scanned_data_item>>s defining the shape;
*)


(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.scan_data_shape_representation.wr:WR1"
The context of the **scan_data_shape_representation** shall be a <<express:measure_schema.global_unit_assigned_context,global_unit_assigned_context>>. This ensures that the coordinates used to define the points of the scan data geometry have defined units.
*)


(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.consistent_sizes"
The **consistent_sizes** function checks the sizes of the <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_dataset.point_coordinates,point_coordinates>> lists of the input <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_dataset,point_cloud_dataset>>s and returns true if all but the last are of size **max** and the last has a size which is not greater than **max**,
*)


(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.consistent_sizes.max"
(input) the maxinum permitted size of any of the point coordinate lists;
*)


(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.consistent_sizes.point_lists"
(input) A list of <<express:scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.point_cloud_dataset,point_cloud_dataset>>s whose sizes are to be checked.
*)


(*"scan_data_3d_shape_model_schema.__schema_file"
data/resource_docs/geometric_and_topological_representation/resource.xml
*)


