(*"shape_dimension_schema.angle_relator"
An **angle_relator** type is an identification of an angle. This angle is one of a set of possible angles created by:

* the intersection of two <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect,shape_aspect>> elements;
* the virtual intersection formed by extensions of two <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect,shape_aspect>> elements;
* the boundaries of a single angular <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect,shape_aspect>>.
*)


(*"shape_dimension_schema.angle_relator.equal"
the numerical measure of the angles is equal at the point of intersection between two <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect,shape_aspect>> elements.
*)


(*"shape_dimension_schema.angle_relator.large"
the numerical measure of the selected angle at the point of intersection between two <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect,shape_aspect>> elements are the larger absolute value.
*)


(*"shape_dimension_schema.angle_relator.small"
the numerical measure of the selected angle at the point of intersection between two <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect,shape_aspect>> elements are the smaller absolute value.
*)

(*"shape_dimension_schema.angle_relator.small.__figure"
[[figure-shape_dimension_schema-fig_single_angular_shape_aspect]]
.Single angular shape aspect
====
image::single_angular_shape_aspect.gif[]
====
*)
(*"shape_dimension_schema.angle_relator.small.__example"
Figure 8 illustrates a type of single angular <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect,shape_aspect>>. See figure 16 for types of intersections of <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect,shape_aspect>>.
*)

