(*"shape_tolerance_schema.area_unit_type"
The **area_unit_type** is an extensible list of types of area that is used by <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_defined_area_unit,geometric_tolerance_with_defined_area_unit>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.area_unit_type.circular"
the area is circular;
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.area_unit_type.square"
the area is square;
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.area_unit_type.rectangular"
the area is rectangular;
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.area_unit_type.cylindrical"
the area is cylindrical;
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.area_unit_type.spherical"
the area is spherical;
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.chain_based_geometric_item_specific_usage"
A **chain_based_geometric_item_specific_usage** is a type of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_item_specific_usage,geometric_item_specific_usage>> and is a type of <<express:product_property_representation_schema.chain_based_item_identified_representation_usage,chain_based_item_identified_representation_usage>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.directed_tolerance_zone_type"
The **directed_tolerance_zone_type** is an extensible list of modifier types that is used by <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.directed_tolerance_zone,directed_tolerance_zone>> to indicate the direction of an "intersection plane".
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.directed_tolerance_zone_type.angular"
indicates that the "intersection plane" is directed at an angle to the referenced datum.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.directed_tolerance_zone_type.perpendicular"
indicates that the "intersection plane" is directed perpendicular to the referenced datum.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.directed_tolerance_zone_type.parallel"
indicates that the "intersection plane" is directed parallel to the referenced datum.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.directed_tolerance_zone_type.including"
indicates that the "intersection plane" is directed so that it includes the referenced datum.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.directed_tolerance_zone_type.symmetrical_to"
indicates that the "intersection plane" is directed so that it is symmetrical to the referenced datum.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.direction_feature_application_type"
The **direction_feature_application_type** is a list of indicators that is used by <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.direction_feature_tolerance_zone,direction_feature_tolerance_zone>> to define how the "direction feature" is derived from the datum. Unless otherwise specified the rules governing "direction feature" defined in ISO 1101 shall apply.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.direction_feature_application_type.perpendicular"
indicates that the "direction feature" is perpendicular to the referenced datum.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.direction_feature_application_type.parallel"
indicates that the "direction feature" is parallel to the referenced datum.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.direction_feature_application_type.inclined"
indicates that the "direction feature" is inclined to the referenced datum.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.direction_feature_application_type.runout"
indicates that the "direction feature" is the surface of the toleranced feature.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_item_specific_usage"
A **geometric_item_specific_usage** is a type of <<express:product_property_representation_schema.item_identified_representation_usage,item_identified_representation_usage>>. In this specialization of <<express:product_property_representation_schema.item_identified_representation_usage,item_identified_representation_usage>>, the <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_item_specific_usage.identified_item,identified_item>> is directly included in the set of items of the <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_item_specific_usage.used_representation,used_representation>> and is a <<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_item,geometric_representation_item>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_item_specific_usage.definition"
an attribute inherited from the <<express:product_property_representation_schema.item_identified_representation_usage,item_identified_representation_usage>> shall be redeclared as the <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_item_specific_usage_select,geometric_item_specific_usage_select>> for the **geometric_item_specific_usage**.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_item_specific_usage.used_representation"
an attribute inherited from the <<express:product_property_representation_schema.item_identified_representation_usage,item_identified_representation_usage>> shall be redeclared as the <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.shape_model,shape_model>> for the **geometric_item_specific_usage**.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_item_specific_usage.identified_item"
an attribute inherited from the <<express:product_property_representation_schema.item_identified_representation_usage,item_identified_representation_usage>> shall be redeclared as the <<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_item,geometric_representation_item>> for the **geometric_item_specific_usage**.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier"
The **geometric_tolerance_modifier** is the list of modifiers that is used by <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_modifiers,geometric_tolerance_with_modifiers>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.any_cross_section"
indicates that any cross section applies in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.any_cross_section.__note"
The symbol for any cross section is ACS.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.associated_least_square_feature"
indicates that the toleranced feature specification element is the least squares (Gaussian) feature in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.associated_least_square_feature.__note"
The symbol for least squares (Gaussian) feature is Ⓖ.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.associated_maximum_inscribed_feature"
indicates that the toleranced feature specification element is the maximum inscribed feature in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.associated_maximum_inscribed_feature.__note"
The symbol for maximum inscribed feature is Ⓧ.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.associated_minimum_inscribed_feature"
indicates that the toleranced feature specification element is the associated minimum circumscribed feature in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.associated_minimum_inscribed_feature.__note"
The symbol for minimum circumscribed feature is Ⓝ.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.associated_minmax_feature"
indicates that the toleranced feature specification element is the associated minimax (Chebyshev) feature in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.associated_minmax_feature.__note"
The symbol for minimax (Chebyshev) feature is Ⓒ.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.associated_tangent_feature"
indicates that the toleranced feature specification element is the associated tangent feature in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.associated_tangent_feature.__note"
The symbol for tangent feature is Ⓣ.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.associated_tangent_feature.__note"
The tangent_plane is used for ASME Y14.5-2009 or later editions of that standard.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.circle_a"
indicates that the toleranced feature is a median feature in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.circle_a.__note"
The symbol for median feature is Ⓐ.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.common_zone"
indicates that common zone applies in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.common_zone.__note"
The symbol for common zone is CZ.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.continuous_features"
indicates that the tolerance is based on continuous features as defined in ASME Y14.5-2009 or later editions of that standard.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.continuous_features.__note"
The symbol for continuous features is CF.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.derived_feature"
indicates that the toleranced feature is a median feature in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.derived_feature.__note"
The symbol for median feature is Ⓐ.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.each_element"
indicates that the tolerance zone is applied to indiviudual line elements of a surface as defined in ASME Y14.5-2009 or later editions of that standard.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.each_element.__note"
This is indicated by EACH ELEMENT.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.each_radial_element"
indicates that the tolerance zone is applied to indiviudual radial line elements of a surface as defined in ASME Y14.5-2009 or later editions of that standard.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.each_radial_element.__note"
This is indicated by EACH RADIAL ELEMENT.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.free_state"
indicates that free state applies in accordance with ISO 10579 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.free_state.__note"
The symbol for free state is Ⓕ.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.individually"
indicates that one or more tolerances are controlled independently of a composite tolerance as defined in ASME Y14.5-2009 or later editions of that standard..
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.individually.__note"
This is indicated by INIDIVIDUALLY.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.least_material_requirement"
indicates that least material requirement applies in accordance with ISO 2692 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.least_material_requirement.__note"
The symbol for least material requirement is Ⓛ.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.line_element"
indicates that line element applies in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.line_element.__note"
The symbol for line element is LE.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.major_diameter"
indicates that major diameter applies in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.major_diameter.__note"
The symbol for major diameter is MD.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.maximum_material_requirement"
indicates that maximum material requirement applies in accordance with ISO 2692 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.maximum_material_requirement.__note"
The symbol for maximum material requirement is Ⓜ.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.minor_diameter"
indicates that minor diameter applies in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.minor_diameter.__note"
The symbol for minor diameter is LD.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.not_convex"
indicates that not convex applies in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.not_convex.__note"
The symbol for not convex is NC.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.peak_height"
indicates that the parameter specification elements is the peak height in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.peak_height.__note"
The symbol for peak height is P.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.pitch_diameter"
indicates that pitch diameter applies in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.pitch_diameter.__note"
The symbol for pitch diameter is PD.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.reciprocity_requirement"
indicates that reciprocity requirement applies in accordance with ISO 2692 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.reciprocity_requirement.__note"
The symbol for reciprocity requirement is Ⓡ.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.reference_least_square_feature_with_external_material_constraint"
indicates that the toleranced feature specification element is the least squares (Gaussian) association with the constraint external to the material in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.reference_least_square_feature_with_external_material_constraint.__note"
The symbol for least squares (Gaussian) feature with external material constraintis is GE.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.reference_least_square_feature_with_internal_material_constraint"
indicates that the toleranced feature specification element is the least squares (Gaussian) association with the constraint internal to the material in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.reference_least_square_feature_with_internal_material_constraint.__note"
The symbol for least squares (Gaussian) feature with internal material constraintis is GI.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.reference_least_square_feature_without_constraint"
indicates that the toleranced feature specification element is the least squares (Gaussian) association in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.reference_least_square_feature_without_constraint.__note"
The symbol for least squares (Gaussian) feature is G.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.reference_maximum_inscribed_feature"
indicates that the toleranced feature specification element is the minimum circumscribed association in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.reference_maximum_inscribed_feature.__note"
The symbol for minimum circumscribed feature is N.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.reference_minimax_feature_with_external_material_constraint"
indicates that the toleranced feature specification element is the minimax (Chebyshev) association with the constraint external to the material in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.reference_minimax_feature_with_external_material_constraint.__note"
The symbol for minimax (Chebyshev) feature with external material constraint is CE.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.reference_minimax_feature_with_internal_material_constraint"
indicates that the toleranced feature specification element is the minimax (Chebyshev) association with the constraint internal to the material in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.reference_minimax_feature_with_internal_material_constraint.__note"
The symbol for minimax (Chebyshev) feature with external material constraint is CI.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.reference_minimax_feature_without_constraint"
indicates that the toleranced feature specification element is the minimax (Chebyshev) association without additional constraints in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.reference_minimax_feature_without_constraint.__note"
The symbol for minimax (Chebyshev) feature without constraint is C.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.reference_minimum_circumscribed_feature"
indicates that the toleranced feature specification element is the maximum inscribed association in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.reference_minimum_circumscribed_feature.__note"
The symbol for maximum inscribed feature is X.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.separate_requirement"
indicates that the tolerance is a separate requirement as defined in ASME Y14.5-2009, or later editions of that standard.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.separate_requirement.__note"
This is indicated by SEP REQT.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.separate_zones"
indicates that the tolerance is applied in a separate zone in accordance with ISO 1101.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.separate_zones.__note"
The symbol for separate zones is SZ.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.standard_deviation"
indicates that the parameter specification elements is the square root of the sum of the squares of the residuals or standard deviation of the toleranced feature relative to the reference feature in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.standard_deviation.__note"
The symbol for standard deviation is Q.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.statistical_tolerance"
indicates that the tolerance is based on statistical tolerances as defined in ASME Y14.5-2009, or later editions of that standard.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.statistical_tolerance.__note"
The symbol for statistical tolerance is \<ST\>.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.stock"
indicates that the tolerance is as furnished as defined in ASME Y14.5-2009 and ASME Y14.38, or later editions of those standards.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.stock.__note"
The symbol for stock is STK.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.tangent_plane"
indicates that the datum is the tangent plane established by contacting points as defined in ASME Y14.5-2009, or later editions of that standard.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.tangent_plane.__note"
The symbol for tangent plane is Ⓣ.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.tangent_plane.__note"
The associated_maximum_inscribed_feature is used for ISO 1101.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.total_range_deviations"
indicates that the parameter specification elements is the total range of deviations in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.total_range_deviations.__note"
The symbol for total range deviations is T.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.united_feature"
indicates that united feature applies in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.united_feature.__note"
The symbol for united feature is UF.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.unspecified_angular_tolerance_zone_offset"
indicates that the parameter specification elements are the angular tolerance zones defined in ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.unspecified_angular_tolerance_zone_offset.__note"
The symbol for unspecified angular tolerance zone offset is VA; a common synonym used is variable angle.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.unspecified_linear_tolerance_zone_offset"
indicates that the parameter specification elements are the tolerance zones defined in ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier.unspecified_linear_tolerance_zone_offset.__note"
