*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.shape_tolerance_select"
A **shape_tolerance_select** type indicates that a tolerance can either be a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance,geometric_tolerance>> or a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.plus_minus_tolerance,plus_minus_tolerance>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_method_definition"
The **tolerance_method_definition** type is the identification of the method used to generate a tolerance value.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.dimension_related_tolerance_zone_element"
A **dimension_related_tolerance_zone_element** is an association of a tolerance zone definition with a locating dimension.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.dimension_related_tolerance_zone_element.__note"
This entity is deprecated. It should not be used for new implementations.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.dimension_related_tolerance_zone_element.related_dimension"
a dimension that positions the <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_zone_definition,tolerance_zone_definition>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.dimension_related_tolerance_zone_element.related_element"
a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_zone_definition,tolerance_zone_definition>> that is defined with a specific location.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance"
A **geometric_tolerance** is the specification of the allowable range within which a geometrical property of a product may deviate. A **geometric_tolerance** is a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference,geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference>> and/or a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_defined_unit,geometric_tolerance_with_defined_unit>> and/or may be either a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_modifiers,geometric_tolerance_with_modifiers>> or a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.modified_geometric_tolerance,modified_geometric_tolerance>> and/or an <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.unequally_disposed_geometric_tolerance,unequally_disposed_geometric_tolerance>> and/or one of a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.cylindricity_tolerance,cylindricity_tolerance>>, a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.flatness_tolerance,flatness_tolerance>>, a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.line_profile_tolerance,line_profile_tolerance>>, a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.position_tolerance,position_tolerance>>, a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.roundness_tolerance,roundness_tolerance>>, a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.straightness_tolerance,straightness_tolerance>>, a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.surface_profile_tolerance,surface_profile_tolerance>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance.name"
the identification of the geometrical tolerance type.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance.name.__example"
Position, straightness, concentricity, parallelism, circular runout, etc., are names for geometrical tolerance types.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance.name.__note"
This identification may be one of the geometrical tolerance types specified in ISO 1101 when used to represent International Standard geometrical tolerances.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance.description"
a supplementary note that shall be used to convey additional requirements associated with geometric tolerance.

The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance.description.__note"
This description may state requirements that may have an affect on the *geometric_tolerance* for specific applications.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance.magnitude"
the size of a tolerance. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance.toleranced_shape_aspect"
the <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect,shape_aspect>> to which the tolerance applies.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance.controlling_shape"
specifies the <<express:product_property_definition_schema.product_definition_shape,product_definition_shape>> to which this **geometric_tolerance** applies through its **toleranced_shape_aspect** attribute.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance.id"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> that distinguishes the **geometric_tolerance**.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance.auxiliary_classification"
specifies a set of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_auxiliary_classification,geometric_tolerance_auxiliary_classification>> associated to the **geometric_tolerance**. A <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_auxiliary_classification,geometric_tolerance_auxiliary_classification>> need not be provided for a **geometric_tolerance**.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance.tolerance_relationship"
specifies a set of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_relationship,geometric_tolerance_relationship>> associated to the **geometric_tolerance**. A <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_relationship,geometric_tolerance_relationship>> need not be provided for a **geometric_tolerance**.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance.ur:UR1"
The combination of **name** and **controlling_shape** shall be unique within a population of **geometric_tolerance**.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance.wr:WR1"
The value of **magnitude** shall be equal to or greater than zero.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance.wr:WR2"
The attribute **controlling_shape** shall have a value.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance.wr:WR3"
In the case that **toleranced_shape_aspect** is a <<express:shape_dimension_schema.dimensional_location,dimensional_location>> the inherited attributes <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect_relationship.relating_shape_aspect,relating_shape_aspect>> and <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect_relationship.related_shape_aspect,related_shape_aspect>> shall reference to <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect,shape_aspect>> for the same <<express:product_property_definition_schema.product_definition_shape,product_definition_shape>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance.wr:WR4"
Each **geometric_tolerance** shall be the <<express:basic_attribute_schema.id_attribute.identified_item,identified_item>> in at most one <<express:basic_attribute_schema.id_attribute,id_attribute>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance.wr:WR5"
Each **geometric_tolerance** shall be reference by no more than one <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_relationship,geometric_tolerance_relationship>> with name = 'composite tolerance' with the attribute <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_relationship.relating_geometric_tolerance,relating_geometric_tolerance>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_relationship"
A **geometric_tolerance_relationship** is an association between two <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance,geometric_tolerance>>s.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_relationship.name"
the word or group of words by which the geometric tolerance relationship is referred.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_relationship.description"
text that describes the relationship.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_relationship.relating_geometric_tolerance"
one of the <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance,geometric_tolerance>>s that takes part in the relationship.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_relationship.related_geometric_tolerance"
the other <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance,geometric_tolerance>> that takes part in the relationship. If one of the <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance,geometric_tolerance>>s is dependent on the other, this attribute shall be the dependent one.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_relationship.wr:WR1"
For a **geometric_tolerance_relationship** with the name 'composite tolerance', the related and the relating subtype should be both either a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.position_tolerance,position_tolerance>>, a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.line_profile_tolerance,line_profile_tolerance>> or a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.surface_profile_tolerance,surface_profile_tolerance>>
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_relationship.wr:WR2"
For a **geometric_tolerance_relationship** with the name 'composite tolerance', the related and relating geometric_tolerances shall refer to the same <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect,shape_aspect>> with the attribute <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance.toleranced_shape_aspect,toleranced_shape_aspect>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_relationship.wr:WR3"
The graph of all **geometric_tolerance_relationship** shall be acyclic.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference"
A **geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference** is a type of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance,geometric_tolerance>> that references one or more <<express:shape_aspect_definition_schema.datum,datum>> for specifying the tolerance condition of a <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect,shape_aspect>>. Each **geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference** may be either an <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.angularity_tolerance,angularity_tolerance>>, a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.circular_runout_tolerance,circular_runout_tolerance>>, a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.coaxiality_tolerance,coaxiality_tolerance>>, a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.concentricity_tolerance,concentricity_tolerance>>, a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.parallelism_tolerance,parallelism_tolerance>>, a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.perpendicularity_tolerance,perpendicularity_tolerance>>, a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.symmetry_tolerance,symmetry_tolerance>>, or a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.total_runout_tolerance,total_runout_tolerance>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference.datum_system"
specifies the datum system or single datum reference the <<express:shape_aspect_definition_schema.datum,datum>> or combination of <<express:shape_aspect_definition_schema.datum,datum>> that define a reference for a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance,geometric_tolerance>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference.datum_system.__note"
This attribute is not equivalent to datum system as defined in ISO 5459.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference.wr:WR1"
If the attribute **datum_system** contains a <<express:shape_aspect_definition_schema.datum_system,datum_system>> there shall be only one and there shall be no <<express:shape_aspect_definition_schema.datum_reference,datum_reference>>s.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_defined_area_unit"
A **geometric_tolerance_with_defined_area_unit** is a type of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_defined_unit,geometric_tolerance_with_defined_unit>> specified on a per area unit basis of the <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect,shape_aspect>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_defined_area_unit.area_type"
specifies whether the area is circular, square, or rectangular.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_defined_area_unit.second_unit_size"
the second unit measure over which a tolerance applies. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_defined_area_unit.wr:WR1"
A value for **second_unit_size** shall be provided if and only if the **area_type** is rectangular, cylindrical, or spherical.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_defined_area_unit.wr:WR2"
If the **area_type** is cylindrical, the **unit_size** shall be a <<express:measure_schema.length_measure_with_unit,length_measure_with_unit>> and the **second_unit_size** shall be a <<express:measure_schema.plane_angle_measure_with_unit,plane_angle_measure_with_unit>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_defined_area_unit.wr:WR3"
If the **area_type** is rectangular, the **unit_size** shall be a <<express:measure_schema.length_measure_with_unit,length_measure_with_unit>> and the **second_unit_size** shall be a <<express:measure_schema.length_measure_with_unit,length_measure_with_unit>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_defined_area_unit.wr:WR4"
If the **area_type** is spherical, the **unit_size** shall be a <<express:measure_schema.plane_angle_measure_with_unit,plane_angle_measure_with_unit>> and the **second_unit_size** shall be a <<express:measure_schema.plane_angle_measure_with_unit,plane_angle_measure_with_unit>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_defined_area_unit.wr:WR5"
If the **area_type** is spherical, an <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.oriented_tolerance_zone,oriented_tolerance_zone>> shall be specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_defined_unit"
A **geometric_tolerance_with_defined_unit** is a type of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance,geometric_tolerance>> specified on a per length unit basis of the <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect,shape_aspect>>.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_defined_unit.__example"
A straightness tolerance defines the allowable amount of bending of a product feature on a unit length basis. A flatness tolerance defines the allowable amount of warping of a surface on a per square unit area basis.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_defined_unit.__note"
The use and application of the per unit basis are described in ISO 1101.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_defined_unit.unit_size"
the unit measure over which a tolerance applies.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_defined_unit.wr:WR1"
The unit length or area over which the tolerance is applied shall be defined by a positive value.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_maximum_tolerance"
A **geometric_tolerance_with_maximum_tolerance** is a type of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_modifiers,geometric_tolerance_with_modifiers>> that limits the allowable maximum geometric tolerance in combination with a maximum material requirement or least material requirement modifier.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_maximum_tolerance.__note"
The maximum geometric tolerance value is described in ASME Y14.5-2009 or later editions of that standard.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_maximum_tolerance.maximum_upper_tolerance"
specifies the limit.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_maximum_tolerance.wr:WR1"
A **geometric_tolerance_with_maximum_tolerance** shall only be used in combination with a maximum material requirement or least material requirement modifier
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_maximum_tolerance.wr:WR2"
The unit of **maximum_upper_tolerance** shall be identical to the unit of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance.magnitude,magnitude>>. The value of **maximum_upper_tolerance** shall be greater than the value of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance.magnitude,magnitude>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_modifiers"
A **geometric_tolerance_with_modifiers** is a type of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance,geometric_tolerance>> that indicates additional properties of the tolerance.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_modifiers.modifiers"
specifies the set of properties that affect the geometric tolerance. There shall exist one or more <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_modifier,geometric_tolerance_modifier>> for the **geometric_tolerance_with_modifiers**.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_modifiers.wr:WR1"
If the modifier circle-A is provided, then the <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance.toleranced_shape_aspect,toleranced_shape_aspect>> shall be a <<express:shape_aspect_definition_schema.centre_of_symmetry,centre_of_symmetry>> and shall not be on the surface of the product. on the surface.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_modifiers.wr:WR2"
If the modifier circle-A is provided, then the <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance.toleranced_shape_aspect,toleranced_shape_aspect>> shall specify one member.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_modifiers.wr:IP1"
If the modifier circle-A is provided, then there there shall be a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_item_specific_usage,geometric_item_specific_usage>> that associates the <<express:shape_aspect_definition_schema.centre_of_symmetry,centre_of_symmetry>> with an <<express:geometry_schema.axis2_placement_3d,axis2_placement_3d>> where the z-axis is the geometric representation of the derived feature.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_modifiers.wr:IP2"
If the modifier circle-A is provided, then the <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect,shape_aspect>> referenced by the following EXPRESS path **SELF\derived_shape_aspect.deriving_relationships[1]\shape_aspect_deriving_relationship.related_shape_aspect.shape_aspect** shall be a <<express:shape_aspect_definition_schema.symmetric_shape_aspect,symmetric_shape_aspect>> that is on the surface of the product and shall be referenced as definition by an <<express:product_property_representation_schema.item_identified_representation_usage,item_identified_representation_usage>> that specifies a set of <<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_item,geometric_representation_item>> instances that form a revolute geometric shape.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_modifiers.wr:WR3"
If any of individually, each element, or each radial element, are provided then the tolerance target shall be a <<express:shape_aspect_definition_schema.composite_shape_aspect,composite_shape_aspect>> .
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_modifiers.wr:WR4"
No more than one of individually, each element, or each radial element, shall be provided for a **geometric_tolerance_with_modifiers**.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.limits_and_fits"
A **limits_and_fits** is a pre-defined fit system for specifying the tolerances associated with the assembly of mating product features. Unless otherwise specified, the rules governing limits and fits defined in ISO 286-1 and ISO 286-2 shall apply.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.limits_and_fits.form_variance"
the fundamental deviation code.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.limits_and_fits.form_variance.__note"
The characters "A" to "ZC" for holes or "a" to "zc" for shafts are used for fundamental deviation.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.limits_and_fits.zone_variance"
specifies whether the tolerance declaration applies to a "cylinder" or "opposed parallel planes".
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.limits_and_fits.zone_variance.__note"
An empty string may be provided.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.limits_and_fits.grade"
the designation of the standard tolerance grade.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.limits_and_fits.grade.__example"
IT7 is a standard tolerance grade.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.limits_and_fits.source"
the description of the place for additional information and requirements on this tolerance.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.limits_and_fits.source.__note"
An empty string may be provided.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.modified_geometric_tolerance"
A **modified_geometric_tolerance** is a type of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance,geometric_tolerance>> with a material limit condition that applies to the <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect,shape_aspect>> being toleranced.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.modified_geometric_tolerance.__note"
The entity *modified_geometric_tolerance* is deprecated. For new implementations it is recommended that <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_modifiers,geometric_tolerance_with_modifiers>> be used.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.modified_geometric_tolerance.modifier"
the <<express:shape_aspect_definition_schema.limit_condition,limit_condition>> that is assigned to a geometrical tolerance.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.modified_geometric_tolerance.wr:IP1"
The SELF\<<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance.toleranced_shape_aspect,toleranced_shape_aspect>> shall be a <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect,shape_aspect>> defining a product feature that has size characteristics.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.non_uniform_zone_definition"
A **non_uniform_zone_definition** is a type of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_zone_definition,tolerance_zone_definition>> The boundaries of a **non_uniform_zone_definition** may have any shape.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.non_uniform_zone_definition.__note"
Non-uniform zone is described in ASME Y14.5-2009 or later editions of that standard.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.plus_minus_tolerance"
A **plus_minus_tolerance** is the specification of the limits within which the value of a dimension may vary. A **plus_minus_tolerance** may have a range specified by either a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_value,tolerance_value>> or a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.limits_and_fits,limits_and_fits>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.plus_minus_tolerance.range"
the limits that, when applied to the dimension value, define the allowable variation for the dimension.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.plus_minus_tolerance.toleranced_dimension"
the dimension to which the **plus_minus_tolerance** applies
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.plus_minus_tolerance.ur:UR1"
There shall be only one **plus_minus_tolerance** for a dimension.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.projected_zone_definition"
A **projected_zone_definition** is a type of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_zone_definition,tolerance_zone_definition>>. Unless otherwise specified, the rules governing projected tolerance zone defined in ISO 1101 shall apply.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.projected_zone_definition.projection_end"
the <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect,shape_aspect>> from which the projected tolerance zone originates.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.projected_zone_definition.projected_length"
the distance from the feature being toleranced.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.projected_zone_definition.wr:WR1"
The value of the **projected_length** shall be greater than 0.0.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.projected_zone_definition.wr:WR2"
The dimensional exponents of **projected_length** shall characterize a length unit.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.projected_zone_definition_with_offset"
A **projected_zone_definition_with_offset** is a type of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.projected_zone_definition,projected_zone_definition>>. A **projected_zone_definition_with_offset** is used when the origin of the projected tolerance zone is offset from the reference surface.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.projected_zone_definition_with_offset.offset"
specifies the value of the offset.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.runout_zone_definition"
A **runout_zone_definition** is a type of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_zone_definition,tolerance_zone_definition>> that is defined by the orientation of the measurement of the toleranced <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect,shape_aspect>> to the <<express:shape_aspect_definition_schema.centre_of_symmetry,centre_of_symmetry>> of a <<express:shape_aspect_definition_schema.datum_feature,datum_feature>>.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.runout_zone_definition.__figure"
[[figure-shape_tolerance_schema-fig_runout_zone_definition]]
.Runout zone definition
====
image::runout_zone_definition.gif[]
====
*)
(*"shape_tolerance_schema.runout_zone_definition.__example"
Figure 20 illustrates a *runout_zone_definition*.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.runout_zone_definition.orientation"
the orientation of a toleranced <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect,shape_aspect>> to the centre of symmetry of a <<express:shape_aspect_definition_schema.datum_feature,datum_feature>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.runout_zone_orientation"
A **runout_zone_orientation** is the specification of the orientation of the runout tolerance element to the centre of symmetry of a <<express:shape_aspect_definition_schema.datum_feature,datum_feature>>.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.runout_zone_orientation.__example"
Figure 13 illustrates an angle for a *runout_zone_orientation*. Rules specifying how the angle is measured shall be defined in an application protocol.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.runout_zone_orientation.angle"
an angle value that orients the tolerance zone from the centre of symmetry of a datum feature to which the runout zone is applied, or a specific value that is the normal to the surface of the <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect,shape_aspect>> that is applied to the runout tolerance.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.runout_zone_orientation.angle.__example"
An example of an *angle* defined by a descriptive value may be "normal".
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.runout_zone_orientation.angle.__note"
If a value other than a numeric value is desired then *angle* may be a <<express:measure_schema.descriptive_measure,descriptive_measure>>.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.runout_zone_orientation.wr:IP1"
The angle value shall range from 0 to 90 degrees if the angle is a planar angle.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.runout_zone_orientation_reference_direction"
A **runout_zone_orientation_reference_direction** is a type of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.runout_zone_orientation,runout_zone_orientation>> that specifies the reference direction for the orientation of the angle.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.runout_zone_orientation_reference_direction.orientation_defining_relationship"
the <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect_relationship,shape_aspect_relationship>> which specifies a directed relationship from the <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect_relationship.relating_shape_aspect,relating_shape_aspect>> to the <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect_relationship.related_shape_aspect,related_shape_aspect>> to define the reference direction in which the angle is to be oriented.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.statistical_distribution_for_tolerance"
A **statistical_distribution_for_tolerance** is a type of <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> that is defined by a set of <<express:qualified_measure_schema.measure_representation_item,measure_representation_item>> that provide the set of distribution parameters. Each distribution parameter is defined by a name and a <<express:measure_schema.measure_with_unit,measure_with_unit>>.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.statistical_distribution_for_tolerance.__example"
Normal Gaussian, Logarithmic or Rayleigh are names for statistical distributions.
*)
(*"shape_tolerance_schema.statistical_distribution_for_tolerance.__example"
Mean and standard deviation are characteristic parameters that define a Normal Gaussian distribution.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.statistical_distribution_for_tolerance.wr:WR1"
The <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> in the set **statistical_distribution_for_tolerance** shall be of type <<express:qualified_measure_schema.measure_representation_item,measure_representation_item>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.statistical_distribution_for_tolerance.wr:IP1"
The name of each parameter that is related to the **statistical_distribution_for_tolerance** shall be specified in the name attribute of each respective <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> in the items attribute of the representation
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_value"
A **tolerance_value** is the representation of plus-minus tolerances for a dimension. A **tolerance_value** specifies the numeric values added to the nominal dimension of a <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect,shape_aspect>>.

The **lower_bound** and **upper_bound** are applied to the value of the dimension to determine the acceptable range of measured values. A **tolerance_value** may be either assigned by the user or specified according to ISO 286-l and ISO 286-2.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_value.__example"
Since the only constraint on the attribute values is that the upper bound be greater than the lower bound, the specification of a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.plus_minus_tolerance,plus_minus_tolerance>> (e.g., 10.0+0.10+0.05) is permitted. In this case, the nominal dimension, 10.0, is not bounded by its associated tolerance zone.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_value.lower_bound"
the value of the tolerance that is added to the dimension value to establish the minimum deviation from the boundary toleranced from the nominal dimension.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_value.upper_bound"
the value of the tolerance that is added to the dimension value to establish the maximum deviation from the boundary toleranced from the nominal dimension.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_value.ubvc"
the numeric value of the **upper_bound** without unit component.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_value.lbvc"
the numeric value of the **lower_bound** without unit component.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_value.wr:WR1"
The value of the **upper_bound** shall be greater than the value of the **lower_bound**.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_value.wr:WR2"
The **upper_bound** and the **lower_bound** shall have the same unit.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_with_statistical_distribution"
A **tolerance_with_statistical_distribution** is the allocation of a tolerance in terms of a probability distribution. The <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.statistical_distribution_for_tolerance,statistical_distribution_for_tolerance>> may be associated with a tolerance value for a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance,geometric_tolerance>> or a range of tolerances for a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.plus_minus_tolerance,plus_minus_tolerance>>.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_with_statistical_distribution.__example"
The diameter of a shaft is toleranced by a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.plus_minus_tolerance,plus_minus_tolerance>>. The <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.plus_minus_tolerance,plus_minus_tolerance>> specifies the range in which the diameter may vary. The <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.statistical_distribution_for_tolerance,statistical_distribution_for_tolerance>> associated to this <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.plus_minus_tolerance,plus_minus_tolerance>> specifies that the actual diameter values shall conform to a statistical distribution within the tolerance range.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_with_statistical_distribution.associated_tolerance"
the tolerance that is specified with a statistical distribution.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_with_statistical_distribution.tolerance_allocation"
the statistical distribution that shall apply to the tolerance
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_zone"
A **tolerance_zone** is a type of <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect,shape_aspect>>. A **tolerance_zone** is the region within which the toleranced feature shall be defined. The characteristics of the region are specified by the manner in which the toleranced feature is dimensioned.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_zone.__example"
A geometric location tolerance applied to a hole defines a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_zone_form,tolerance_zone_form>> that may be described as cylindrical.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_zone.defining_tolerance"
all geometric tolerances which define a **tolerance_zone** for a <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect,shape_aspect>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_zone.form"
the representation of the applied shape that limits the specified tolerance for the **tolerance_zone**.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_zone_definition"
A **tolerance_zone_definition** is a specification of the defining boundaries of a tolerance zone. A **tolerance_zone_definition** may be either a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.projected_zone_definition,projected_zone_definition>> or a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.non_uniform_zone_definition,non_uniform_zone_definition>>, or a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.runout_zone_definition,runout_zone_definition>>.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_zone_definition.__example"
A flatness tolerance zone of a planar surface is bounded by two parallel, infinite planes separated by a distance of the tolerance magnitude.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_zone_definition.__note"
A pair of boundaries specified as a single *tolerance_zone_definition* may form either a partial or complete tolerance zone. When the tolerance zone is not fully bounded, it is appropriate to assume that the tolerance zone extends to infinity at the unbounded areas
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_zone_definition.zone"
the <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_zone,tolerance_zone>> being defined.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_zone_definition.boundaries"
a set of <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect,shape_aspect>> that define boundaries of the <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_zone,tolerance_zone>>.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_zone_definition.boundaries.__example"
A geometric location tolerance applied to a hole is defined to be a cylindrical zone in which the axis of the hole may vary. The cylindrical zone is symmetric about its axis. The two defining boundaries of this tolerance zone are the cylindrical surface and its axis. For a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_zone,tolerance_zone>> defined by two parallel planes (or lines), each plane (or line) defines a boundary of the *tolerance_zone_definition*.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_zone_form"
A **tolerance_zone_form** is a description of the shape of the <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_zone,tolerance_zone>>.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_zone_form.__example"
"within a circle", "between two concentric circles", "between two equidistant curves", "within a cylinder", "between two coaxial cylinders", "between two equidistant surfaces", "non-uniform", "cylindrical or circular", and "spherical" are examples of descriptions of tolerance zone shapes.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_zone_form.name"
the description of a tolerance zone shape
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.unequally_disposed_geometric_tolerance"
An **unequally_disposed_geometric_tolerance** is a type of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance,geometric_tolerance>> whose tolerance zone is offset from the default value. An **unequally_disposed_geometric_tolerance** shall be used in accordance with unequally disposed tolerance zone as defined in ISO 1101, or ASME Y14.5-2009 or later editions of that standard.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.unequally_disposed_geometric_tolerance.displacement"
specifies the offset of the tolerance zone from the true profile.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.unequally_disposed_geometric_tolerance.wr:WR1"
The **displacement** shall be a number.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.sts_get_product_definition_shape"
The **sts_get_product_definition_shape** function returns the <<express:product_property_definition_schema.product_definition_shape,product_definition_shape>> associated with the <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_target,geometric_tolerance_target>> as an **input**.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.sts_get_product_definition_shape.input"
the specified <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_target,geometric_tolerance_target>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.angularity_tolerance"
An **angularity_tolerance** is a type of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference,geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference>>. The rules governing angularity tolerance defined in ISO 1101, or ASME Y14.5-2009 or later editions of that standard shall apply.

The specified angle shall not be a multiple of 90 degrees. In the case of 0 or 180 degrees, a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.parallelism_tolerance,parallelism_tolerance>> shall be used. In the case of 90 or 270 degrees, a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.perpendicularity_tolerance,perpendicularity_tolerance>> shall be used. The specified angle shall be defined using an instance of <<express:shape_dimension_schema.angular_location,angular_location>>. The <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance.toleranced_shape_aspect,toleranced_shape_aspect>> is either a plane or a straight line.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.angularity_tolerance.wr:WR1"
The **angularity_tolerance** shall contain at least one element and at most two elements in its <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference.datum_system,datum_system>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.angularity_tolerance.wr:IP1"
The datums referenced shall be sufficient to identify a plane or a straight line.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.angularity_tolerance.wr:IP2"
The datums referred to in <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference.datum_system,datum_system>> shall be sufficient to enable orientation of the tolerance zone.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.circular_runout_tolerance"
A **circular_runout_tolerance** is a type of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference,geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference>>. The rules governing circular run-out tolerance defined in ISO 1101, or ASME Y14.5-2009 or later editions of that standard shall apply.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.circular_runout_tolerance.wr:WR1"
The **circular_runout_tolerance** shall contain one or two elements in its <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference.datum_system,datum_system>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.coaxiality_tolerance"
A **coaxiality_tolerance** is a type of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference,geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference>>. The rules governing coaxiality tolerance defined in ISO 1101, or ASME Y14.5-2018 or later editions of that standard shall apply.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.coaxiality_tolerance.wr:WR1"
The **coaxiality_tolerance** shall contain one or two elements in its <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference.datum_system,datum_system>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.coaxiality_tolerance.wr:IP1"
The <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect,shape_aspect>>, the **coaxiality_tolerance** is applied to, is a revolute surface feature.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.concentricity_tolerance"
A **concentricity_tolerance** is a type of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference,geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference>>. The rules governing concentricity tolerance defined in ISO 1101, or ASME Y14.5-2009 shall apply.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.concentricity_tolerance.wr:WR1"
The **concentricity_tolerance** shall contain exactly one element in its <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference.datum_system,datum_system>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.concentricity_tolerance.wr:IP1"
The <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect,shape_aspect>>, the **concentricity_tolerance** is applied to, is symmetrical with respect to rotation.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.cylindricity_tolerance"
A **cylindricity_tolerance** is a type of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance,geometric_tolerance>>. The rules governing cylindricity tolerance defined in ISO 1101, or ASME Y14.5-2009 or later editions of that standard shall apply.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.cylindricity_tolerance.wr:WR1"
The **cylindricity_tolerance** shall not be of type <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference,geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.cylindricity_tolerance.wr:IP1"
The <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect,shape_aspect>>, the **cylindricity_tolerance** is applied to, is a cylindrical face.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.directed_tolerance_zone"
A **directed_tolerance_zone** is a type of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_zone_with_datum,tolerance_zone_with_datum>> that represents an "intersection plane" for a geometric tolerance as defined in ISO 1101.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.directed_tolerance_zone.direction"
specifies the direction of the tolerance zone in respect to the referenced datum. It is either <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.directed_tolerance_zone_type.angular,angular>><<express:shape_tolerance_schema.directed_tolerance_zone_type.perpendicular,perpendicular>>, <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.directed_tolerance_zone_type.parallel,parallel>>, <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.directed_tolerance_zone_type.including,including>>. or <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.directed_tolerance_zone_type.symmetrical_to,symmetrical_to>>
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.directed_tolerance_zone_with_angle"
A **directed_tolerance_zone_with_angle** is a type of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.directed_tolerance_zone,directed_tolerance_zone>> that represents an "intersection plane" with a specified angle for a geometric tolerance as defined in ISO 1101.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.directed_tolerance_zone_with_angle.angle"
specifies the angle of the plane.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.directed_tolerance_zone_with_angle.wr:WR1"
The inherited attribute <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.directed_tolerance_zone.direction,direction>> shall specify <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.directed_tolerance_zone_type.angular,angular>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.direction_feature_tolerance_zone"
A **direction_feature_tolerance_zone** is a type of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_zone_with_datum,tolerance_zone_with_datum>> that represents a "direction feature" for a geometric tolerance as defined in ISO 1101.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.direction_feature_tolerance_zone.width_direction"
specifies the width of the tolerance zone according to the direction.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.direction_feature_tolerance_zone.angle"
specifies the angle of the direction. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.direction_feature_tolerance_zone.indicated_datum"
specifies the datum used in the direction feature indicator.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.direction_feature_tolerance_zone.wr:WR1"
The inherited attribute <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_zone_with_datum.datum_reference,datum_reference>> shall specify a <<express:shape_aspect_definition_schema.datum_system,datum_system>> that has exactly one member of <<express:shape_aspect_definition_schema.datum_system.constituents,constituents>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.direction_feature_tolerance_zone.wr:WR2"
The <<express:shape_aspect_definition_schema.datum_system,datum_system>> shall reference a datum.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.direction_feature_tolerance_zone.wr:WR3"
An angle value shall be specified if and only if the **width_direction** is of type inclined.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.direction_feature_tolerance_zone.wr:WR4"
The value of the associated attribute <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_zone_form.name,name>> shall be one of: 'between two coaxial cylinders', 'between two equidistant complex surfaces or two parallel planes', 'between two non-equidistant complex surfaces or two non-parallel planes', or 'between two equidistant surfaces'.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.direction_feature_tolerance_zone.wr:IP1"
If the geometric representation of the **indicated_datum** is a plane then the <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.direction_feature_application_type,direction_feature_application_type>> value shall not be runout.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.direction_feature_tolerance_zone.wr:IP2"
A **direction_feature_tolerance_zone** shall be represented by a plane, cylinder, or a cone.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.direction_feature_tolerance_zone.wr:IP3"
The geometric representation for the **indicated_datum** shall be a plane or an axis.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.oriented_tolerance_zone"
A **oriented_tolerance_zone** is a type of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_zone_with_datum,tolerance_zone_with_datum>> that represents an "orientation plane" for a geometric tolerance as defined in ISO 1101.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.oriented_tolerance_zone.orientation"
specifies the orientation of the tolerance zone in respect to the referenced datum. It is either <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.oriented_tolerance_zone_type.perpendicular,perpendicular>>, <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.oriented_tolerance_zone_type.parallel,parallel>> or <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.oriented_tolerance_zone_type.angular,angular>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.oriented_tolerance_zone.angle"
specifies an additional angle of the tolerance zone orientation in respect to the referenced datum.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.oriented_tolerance_zone.wr:WR1"
An <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.oriented_tolerance_zone.angle,angle>> value shall be specified if and only if the <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.oriented_tolerance_zone.orientation,orientation>> is of type <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.oriented_tolerance_zone_type.angular,angular>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.flatness_tolerance"
A **flatness_tolerance** is a type of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance,geometric_tolerance>>. The rules governing flatness tolerance defined in ISO 1101, or ASME Y14.5-2009 or later editions of that standard shall apply.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.flatness_tolerance.wr:WR1"
The **flatness_tolerance** shall not be of type <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference,geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.flatness_tolerance.wr:IP1"
The <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect,shape_aspect>>, the **flatness_tolerance** is applied to, shall be a nominally planar surface.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.line_profile_tolerance"
A **line_profile_tolerance** is a type of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance,geometric_tolerance>>. The rules governing profile tolerance defined in ISO 1101, or ASME Y14.5-2009 or later editions of that standard shall apply.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.line_profile_tolerance.wr:WR1"
The **line_profile_tolerance** shall contain at most three elements in its <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference.datum_system,datum_system>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.parallelism_tolerance"
A **parallelism_tolerance** is a type of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference,geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference>>. The rules governing parallelism tolerance defined in ISO 1101, or ASME Y14.5-2009 or later editions of that standard shall apply.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.parallelism_tolerance.wr:WR1"
The **parallelism_tolerance** shall contain at least one element and at most two elements in its <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference.datum_system,datum_system>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.parallelism_tolerance.wr:IP1"
The <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect,shape_aspect>>, the **parallelism_tolerance** is applied to, is an axis or a planar surface.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.parallelism_tolerance.wr:IP2"
The datums referenced shall be sufficient to define a plane or a straight line.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.perpendicularity_tolerance"
A **perpendicularity_tolerance** is a type of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference,geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference>>. The rules governing perpendicularity tolerance defined in ISO 1101, or ASME Y14.5-2009 or later editions of that standard shall apply.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.perpendicularity_tolerance.wr:WR1"
The **perpendicularity_tolerance** shall contain at least one element and at most three elements in its <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference.datum_system,datum_system>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.perpendicularity_tolerance.wr:IP1"
The <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance.toleranced_shape_aspect,toleranced_shape_aspect>> shall be either a plane or a straight line.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.perpendicularity_tolerance.wr:IP2"
The datums referenced shall be suffcient to define a plane or a straight line.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.position_tolerance"
A **position_tolerance** is a type of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance,geometric_tolerance>>. The rules governing position tolerance defined in ISO 1101 and ISO 5458, or ASME Y14.5-2009 or later editions of that standard shall apply.

The location of the tolerance zone shall be specified with instances of <<express:shape_dimension_schema.dimensional_location,dimensional_location>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.position_tolerance.__note"
When the <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance.toleranced_shape_aspect,toleranced_shape_aspect>> is a <<express:shape_aspect_definition_schema.composite_shape_aspect,composite_shape_aspect>>, e.g. eight holes, the tolerance zone may but need not be defined by referenced datums (see ISO 1101).
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.position_tolerance.__note"
The type <<express:shape_dimension_schema.dimensional_location,dimensional_location>> is defined in ISO 10303-47.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.position_tolerance.wr:WR1"
The **position_tolerance** shall contain at most three elements in its <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference.datum_system,datum_system>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.roundness_tolerance"
A **roundness_tolerance** is a type of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance,geometric_tolerance>>. The rules governing roundness tolerance defined in ISO 1101, or ASME Y14.5-2009 or later editions of that standard shall apply.

The <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance.toleranced_shape_aspect,toleranced_shape_aspect>> shall be of invariance class surface revolute feature but not a helical shape.

The actual surface shall lie in a tolerance zone limited by two co-planar and concentric circles with a difference in radii of the tolerance value.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.roundness_tolerance.__note"
In the case of a sphere, any axis through the centre point of the sphere may be considered.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.roundness_tolerance.wr:WR1"
The **roundness_tolerance** shall not be of type <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference,geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.straightness_tolerance"
A **straightness_tolerance** is a type of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance,geometric_tolerance>> that applies either to the intersection curves between the surface and the planes parallel to the reference plane, or to the extracted median curve. The rules governing straightness tolerance defined in ISO 1101, or ASME Y14.5-2009 or later editions of that standard shall apply.

The <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance.toleranced_shape_aspect,toleranced_shape_aspect>> is a surface or a straight line. Refer to the definition of straightness tolerance in ISO 1101 for a description of the different tolerance zones. In the case of intersection curves, the ideal features corresponding to the intersection curves shall be linear and there shall be another <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect,shape_aspect>>, which is related to the <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance.toleranced_shape_aspect,toleranced_shape_aspect>> by a <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect_relationship,shape_aspect_relationship>>. The <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect_relationship.name,name>> of the <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect_relationship,shape_aspect_relationship>> shall be 'affected plane association'.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.straightness_tolerance.wr:WR1"
The **straightness_tolerance** shall not be of type <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference,geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.surface_profile_tolerance"
A **surface_profile_tolerance** is a type of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance,geometric_tolerance>> that applies to a surface. The rules governing profile any surface tolerance defined in ISO 1101, or ASME Y14.5-2009 or later editions of that standard shall apply.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.surface_profile_tolerance.wr:WR1"
The **surface_profile_tolerance** shall contain at most three elements in its <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference.datum_system,datum_system>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.surface_profile_tolerance.wr:IP1"
The <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance.toleranced_shape_aspect,toleranced_shape_aspect>> shall refer to a surface that is neither planar nor cylindrical. In the case where the nominal feature is planar a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.flatness_tolerance,flatness_tolerance>> shall be used. In the case where the nominal feature is cylindrical a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.cylindricity_tolerance,cylindricity_tolerance>> shall be used.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.symmetry_tolerance"
A **symmetry_tolerance** is a type of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference,geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference>>. The rules governing symmetry tolerance defined in ISO 1101, or ASME Y14.5-2009 or later editions of that standard shall apply.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.symmetry_tolerance.wr:WR1"
The **symmetry_tolerance** shall contain at most three elements in its <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference.datum_system,datum_system>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_zone_with_datum"
A **tolerance_zone_with_datum** is a type of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_zone,tolerance_zone>> that includes direction or orientation classification with respect to referenced features.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_zone_with_datum.__note"
Typically only a primary datum is used.
*)

(*"shape_tolerance_schema.tolerance_zone_with_datum.datum_reference"
the <<express:shape_aspect_definition_schema.datum_system,datum_system>> which serves as the geometric reference for the **tolerance_zone_with_datum** orientation.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.total_runout_tolerance"
A **total_runout_tolerance** is a type of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference,geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference>>. The rules governing total run-out tolerance defined in ISO 1101, or ASME Y14.5-2009 or later editions of that standard shall apply. The set of referenced datums shall contain one revolute surface feature. The tolerance zone is limited by:

* two coaxial cylinders, with a difference in radii equal to the tolerance value. In this case, the axis of the cylinders shall be the axis of the revolute surface feature, and the ideal feature corresponding to the toleranced surface is a cylinder;
* two parallel planes, separated by the distance specified by the tolerance value. In this case, the planes are perpendicular to the axis of the revolute surface feature, and the ideal feature corresponding to the toleranced surface is a plane.
* two offset revolute surfaces of any shape, with an offset distance equal to the tolerance value. In this case, the surfaces may be conic, spherical, or any other revolute shape.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.total_runout_tolerance.wr:WR1"
The **total_runout_tolerance** shall contain one or two elements in its <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_datum_reference.datum_system,datum_system>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_auxiliary_classification_enum"
The **geometric_tolerance_auxiliary_classification_enum** is an extensible list of types of auxiliary classification that is used by <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_auxiliary_classification,geometric_tolerance_auxiliary_classification>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_auxiliary_classification_enum.all_over"
the rules governing all over defined in ISO 1101, or ASME Y14.5-2009 or later editions of that standard shall apply.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_auxiliary_classification_enum.unless_otherwise_specified"
the specification applies to all surfaces for which no other tolerance of the same type is defined.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.datum_system_for_composite_group_element"
A **datum_system_for_composite_group_element** is a type of <<express:shape_aspect_definition_schema.datum_system,datum_system>> that provides a capability to assign an <<express:geometry_schema.axis2_placement_3d,axis2_placement_3d>> to a specific element in a <<express:shape_aspect_definition_schema.composite_group_shape_aspect,composite_group_shape_aspect>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.datum_system_for_composite_group_element.associated_coordinate_system"
specifies the associated <<express:geometry_schema.axis2_placement_3d,axis2_placement_3d>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.datum_system_for_composite_group_element.coordinate_system_relation"
specifies the associated <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_item_specific_usage,geometric_item_specific_usage>> that specifies the coordinate system. A **datum_system_for_composite_group_element** is existence dependent on the associated <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_item_specific_usage,geometric_item_specific_usage>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.datum_system_for_composite_group_element.element"
specifies the <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect_relationship,shape_aspect_relationship>> that identifies a specific member of the group specified by <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.group_geometric_tolerance_with_datum_system_reference.toleranced_shape_aspect,toleranced_shape_aspect>>
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.datum_system_for_composite_group_element.wr:WR1"
A <<express:shape_aspect_definition_schema.composite_group_shape_aspect,composite_group_shape_aspect>> shall be referenced by the <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect_relationship.relating_shape_aspect,relating_shape_aspect>> of the <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect_relationship,shape_aspect_relationship>> referenced by the **element**.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.datum_system_for_composite_group_element.wr:WR2"
A <<express:shape_aspect_definition_schema.composite_group_shape_aspect,composite_group_shape_aspect>> shall not be referenced by the <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect_relationship.related_shape_aspect,related_shape_aspect>> of the <<express:product_property_definition_schema.shape_aspect_relationship,shape_aspect_relationship>> referenced by the **element**.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_auxiliary_classification"
A **geometric_tolerance_auxiliary_classification** is an additional classification applied to a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance,geometric_tolerance>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_auxiliary_classification.attribute_value"
specifies the <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_auxiliary_classification_enum,geometric_tolerance_auxiliary_classification_enum>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_auxiliary_classification.described_item"
a <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance,geometric_tolerance>> to which the **geometric_tolerance_auxiliary_classification** applies.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.gps_filtration_enumeration"
The **gps_filtration_enumeration** is the list of filter types that is used by <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance,geometric_tolerance>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.gps_filtration_enumeration.alternating_ball"
indicates that the filter symbol is AB in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.gps_filtration_enumeration.alternating_disc"
indicates that the filter symbol is AD in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.gps_filtration_enumeration.alternating_horizontal_segment"
indicates that the filter symbol is AH in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.gps_filtration_enumeration.ball_radius"
indicates that the ball radius nesting index applies in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.gps_filtration_enumeration.closing_ball"
indicates that the filter symbol is CB in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.gps_filtration_enumeration.closing_disc"
indicates that the filter symbol is CD in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.gps_filtration_enumeration.closing_horizontal_segment"
indicates that the filter symbol is CH in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.gps_filtration_enumeration.complex_wavelet"
indicates that the filter symbol is CW in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.gps_filtration_enumeration.cutoff_length"
indicates that the cutoff length nesting index applies in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.gps_filtration_enumeration.cutoff_upr"
indicates that the cutoff UPR nesting index applies in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.gps_filtration_enumeration.disc_radius"
indicates that the disc radius nesting index applies in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.gps_filtration_enumeration.fourier"
indicates that the filter symbol is F in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.gps_filtration_enumeration.gaussian"
indicates that the filter symbol is G in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.gps_filtration_enumeration.hull"
indicates that the filter symbol is H in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.gps_filtration_enumeration.long_wave_pass_filter"
indicates that long wave pass filter applies in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.gps_filtration_enumeration.opening_ball"
indicates that the filter symbol is OB in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.gps_filtration_enumeration.opening_disc"
indicates that the filter symbol is OD in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.gps_filtration_enumeration.opening_horizontal_segment"
indicates that the filter symbol is OH in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.gps_filtration_enumeration.robust_gaussian"
indicates that the filter symbol is RG in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.gps_filtration_enumeration.robust_spline"
indicates that the filter symbol is RS in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.gps_filtration_enumeration.segment_length"
indicates that the segment length nesting index applies in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.gps_filtration_enumeration.short_wave_pass_filter"
indicates that short wave pass filter applies in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.gps_filtration_enumeration.spline"
indicates that the filter symbol is S in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.gps_filtration_enumeration.spline_wavelet"
indicates that the filter symbol is SW in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.gps_filtration_enumeration.urp_number"
indicates that the UPR number nesting index applies in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.gps_filtration_enumeration.wavelength"
indicates that the wavelenght nesting index applies in accordance with ISO 1101 unless otherwise specified.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.gps_filtration_specification"
A **gps_filtration_specification** is a specification of the filtering of the toleranced feature. Unless otherwise specified the rules governing filtering specification defined in ISO 1101 shall apply.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.gps_filtration_specification.base_target"
specifies the toleranced feature on which the filter applies.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.gps_filtration_specification.filter_data"
specifies the list of filters.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.gps_filtration_specification.wr:IP1"
The content of the data set is governed by ISO 1101 or other GPS standards.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.gps_filter"
A **gps_filter** is a specification of a filtering element of the toleranced feature. Unless otherwise specified the rules governing filter specification element defined in ISO 1101 shall apply.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.gps_filter.filter_type"
specifies the filtering element type.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.gps_filter.filter_data"
specifies the list of value of the filter element.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.gps_filter.owner"
specifies the filtering list of value of the filter element.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.gps_filter.wr:WR1"
if a **gps_filter** is be used with <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_modifiers,geometric_tolerance_with_modifiers>> then the <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_with_modifiers.modifiers,modifiers>> shall not contains one or more of the following modifiers:

* C reference_minimax_feature_without_constraint,
* CE reference_minimax_feature_with_external_material_constraint,
* CI reference_minimax_feature_with_internal_material_constraint,
* G reference_least_square_feature_without_constraint,
* GE reference_least_square_feature_with_external_material_constraint,
* GI reference_least_square_feature_with_internal_material_constraint,
* X reference_minimum_circumscribed_feature,
* N reference_maximum_inscribed_feature,
* T total_range_deviations,
* P peak_height,
* V valley_depth,
* Q standard_deviation.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.gps_filter.wr:IP1"
The content of the data set is governed by ISO 1101 or other GPS standards.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.group_geometric_tolerance_with_datum_system_reference"
A **group_geometric_tolerance_with_datum_system_reference** is a type of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance,geometric_tolerance>> that provides an <<express:geometry_schema.axis2_placement_3d,axis2_placement_3d>> for specification of a coordinate system specific to each member of the group specified by the **toleranced_shape_aspect**.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.group_geometric_tolerance_with_datum_system_reference.datum_system"
specifies the role of the set of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.datum_system_for_composite_group_element,datum_system_for_composite_group_element>>. Each member of the set provides an <<express:geometry_schema.axis2_placement_3d,axis2_placement_3d>> for a specific member of the group specified by **toleranced_shape_aspect**.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.group_geometric_tolerance_with_datum_system_reference.toleranced_shape_aspect"
specifies the <<express:shape_aspect_definition_schema.composite_shape_aspect,composite_shape_aspect>> that provides the product data context for the **group_geometric_tolerance_with_datum_system_reference**.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.acyclic_geometric_tolerance_relationship"
The **acyclic_geometric_tolerance_relationship** function determines whether the graph of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_relationship,geometric_tolerance_relationship>> contains a cycle.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.acyclic_geometric_tolerance_relationship.relation"
the specified <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance_relationship,geometric_tolerance_relationship>>
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.acyclic_geometric_tolerance_relationship.relatives"
the specified set of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance,geometric_tolerance>>
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.acyclic_geometric_tolerance_relationship.specific_relation"
the specified STRING.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.subtype_exclusiveness_geometric_tolerance"
The **subtype_exclusiveness_geometric_tolerance** rule specifies that subtypes of <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.geometric_tolerance,geometric_tolerance>> for specific geometrical characteristics are mutually exclusive and that exactly one characteristic is used.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.subtype_exclusiveness_geometric_tolerance.wr:WR1"
Each instance of the subtypes of shall be only one of:

* <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.angularity_tolerance,angularity_tolerance>>;
* <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.circular_runout_tolerance,circular_runout_tolerance>>;
* <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.coaxiality_tolerance,coaxiality_tolerance>>;
* <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.concentricity_tolerance,concentricity_tolerance>>;
* <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.cylindricity_tolerance,cylindricity_tolerance>>;
* <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.flatness_tolerance,flatness_tolerance>>;
* <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.line_profile_tolerance,line_profile_tolerance>>;
* <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.parallelism_tolerance,parallelism_tolerance>>;
* <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.perpendicularity_tolerance,perpendicularity_tolerance>>;
* <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.position_tolerance,position_tolerance>>;
* <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.roundness_tolerance,roundness_tolerance>>;
* <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.straightness_tolerance,straightness_tolerance>>;
* <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.surface_profile_tolerance,surface_profile_tolerance>>;
* <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.symmetry_tolerance,symmetry_tolerance>>;
* <<express:shape_tolerance_schema.total_runout_tolerance,total_runout_tolerance>>.
*)


(*"shape_tolerance_schema.__schema_file"
data/resource_docs/shape_variation_tolerances/resource.xml
*)


