(*"structural_response_representation_schema.plane_surface_2d_element_representation.model_ref"

an application defined identifier of the <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_model,fea_model>> which possesses the plane surface 2D element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.plane_surface_2d_element_representation.element_descriptor"

a collection of information that specifies a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.plane_surface_2d_element_representation,plane_surface_2d_element_representation>>.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.plane_surface_2d_element_representation.property"

the section properties of the surface.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.plane_surface_2d_element_representation.depth_property"

the properties for a plane section. Analysis applications often assume that the value of the depth attribute of this property is 1.0.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.plane_surface_2d_element_representation.material"

the material properties associated with a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.plane_surface_2d_element_representation,plane_surface_2d_element_representation>>.

NOTE: The element id, a unique application defined identifier of an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.element_representation,element_representation>>, is specified by the *name* attribute of the <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> supertype.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.plane_surface_2d_element_representation.UR1"

the combination of an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_model,fea_model>> and element id shall be unique within a finite element analysis model.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.plane_surface_2d_element_representation.wr:WR1"

the <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_model,fea_model>> shall be planar.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.plane_surface_2d_element_representation.wr:WR2"

there shall be either a parametric property coordinate system (PARAMETRIC_SURFACE_2D_ELEMENT_COORDINATE_SYSTEM) or an aligned property coordinate system (ALIGNED_SURFACE_2D_ELEMENT_COORDINATE_SYSTEM) associated with a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.plane_surface_2d_element_representation,plane_surface_2d_element_representation>>.

The property coordinate system (parametric or aligned) is the orientation of the coordinate system for the element material and section properties. For a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.plane_surface_2d_element_representation,plane_surface_2d_element_representation>> the property coordinate system is defined such that: the stem:[x] axis is normal to the 2D analysis plane in the direction of the stem:[k] axis of the analysis 2D definition coordinate system, and the stem:[z] axis is normal to the element surface.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.plane_surface_2d_element_representation.wr:WR3"

there shall be at least one of the following <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_material_property_representation_item,fea_material_property_representation_item>> subtypes referenced by a *material*: <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_linear_elasticity,fea_linear_elasticity>>, <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_mass_density,fea_mass_density>>, <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_area_density,fea_area_density>>, <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_tangential_coefficient_of_linear_thermal_expansion,fea_tangential_coefficient_of_linear_thermal_expansion>>, <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_secant_coefficient_of_linear_thermal_expansion,fea_secant_coefficient_of_linear_thermal_expansion>>, <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_moisture_absorption,fea_moisture_absorption>>, <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_shell_membrane_stiffness,fea_shell_membrane_stiffness>>, <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_shell_bending_stiffness,fea_shell_bending_stiffness>>, <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_shell_membrane_bending_coupling_stiffness,fea_shell_membrane_bending_coupling_stiffness>>, and <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_shell_shear_stiffness,fea_shell_shear_stiffness>>.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.plane_surface_2d_element_representation.wr:WR4"

there shall be a parametric representation context associated with the element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.plane_surface_2d_element_representation.FU1"

the number of nodes in the node list of a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.plane_surface_2d_element_representation,plane_surface_2d_element_representation>> shall be the proper number based on the order of the <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.plane_surface_2d_element_representation,plane_surface_2d_element_representation>>.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_representation"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_representation,curve_3d_element_representation>> is an element that is a 1D shape (a curve) with a specified cross section.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_representation.model_ref"

an application defined identifier of the <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_model,fea_model>> which possesses the curve 3D element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_representation.element_descriptor"

a collection of information that specifies a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_representation,curve_3d_element_representation>>.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_representation.property"

the cross section properties of a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_representation,curve_3d_element_representation>>.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_representation.material"

the material properties associated with a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_representation,curve_3d_element_representation>>.

NOTE: The element id, a unique application defined identifier of an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.element_representation,element_representation>>, is specified by the *name* attribute of the <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> supertype.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_representation.UR1"

the combination of an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_model,fea_model>> and element id shall be unique within a finite element analysis model.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_representation.wr:WR1"

there shall be either a parametric property coordinate system (PARAMETRIC_CURVE_3D_ELEMENT_COORDINATE_SYSTEM) or an aligned property coordinate system (ALIGNED_CURVE_3D_ELEMENT_COORDINATE_SYSTEM) associated with a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_representation,curve_3d_element_representation>>.

The property coordinate system (parametric or aligned) is the orientation of the coordinate system for the element material and section properties.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_representation.wr:WR2"

there shall be at least one of the following <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_material_property_representation_item,fea_material_property_representation_item>> subtypes referenced by a *material*: <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_linear_elasticity,fea_linear_elasticity>>, <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_mass_density,fea_mass_density>>, <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_area_density,fea_area_density>>, <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_tangential_coefficient_of_linear_thermal_expansion,fea_tangential_coefficient_of_linear_thermal_expansion>>, <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_secant_coefficient_of_linear_thermal_expansion,fea_secant_coefficient_of_linear_thermal_expansion>>, and <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_moisture_absorption,fea_moisture_absorption>>.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_representation.wr:WR3"

there shall be a parametric representation context associated with the element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_representation.FU1"

the number of nodes in the node list of a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_representation,curve_3d_element_representation>> shall be the proper number based on the order of the <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_representation,curve_3d_element_representation>>.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.axisymmetric_curve_2d_element_representation"

An <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.axisymmetric_curve_2d_element_representation,axisymmetric_curve_2d_element_representation>> is an element with a specified cross section that is a 0D shape (a point) that is swept about the stem:[j] axis of the (stem:[i, j]) plane of the founding coordinate system (see <<subsec-geometric-founding-and-analysis-space>>). An <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.axisymmetric_curve_2d_element_representation,axisymmetric_curve_2d_element_representation>> shall lie in the (stem:[i, j]) plane of the founding coordinate system.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.axisymmetric_curve_2d_element_representation.model_ref"

an application defined identifier of the <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_model,fea_model>> which possesses the axisymmetric curve 2D element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.axisymmetric_curve_2d_element_representation.element_descriptor"

a collection of information that specifies an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.axisymmetric_curve_2d_element_representation,axisymmetric_curve_2d_element_representation>>.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.axisymmetric_curve_2d_element_representation.property"

the cross section properties of an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.axisymmetric_curve_2d_element_representation,axisymmetric_curve_2d_element_representation>>.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.axisymmetric_curve_2d_element_representation.angle_property"

the properties for an axisymmetric section. Analysis applications often assume that the value of the angle attribute of this property is stem:[2 pi].

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.axisymmetric_curve_2d_element_representation.material"

the material properties associated with an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.axisymmetric_curve_2d_element_representation,axisymmetric_curve_2d_element_representation>>.

NOTE: The element id, a unique application defined identifier of an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.element_representation,element_representation>>, is specified by the *name* attribute of the <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> supertype.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.axisymmetric_curve_2d_element_representation.UR1"

the combination of an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_model,fea_model>> and element id shall be unique within a finite element analysis model.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.axisymmetric_curve_2d_element_representation.wr:WR1"

the <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_model,fea_model>> shall be axisymmetric.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.axisymmetric_curve_2d_element_representation.wr:WR2"

there shall be a property coordinate system (CURVE_2D_ELEMENT_COORDINATE_SYSTEM) associated with an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.axisymmetric_curve_2d_element_representation,axisymmetric_curve_2d_element_representation>>.

The property coordinate system is the orientation of the coordinate system for the element material and section properties.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.axisymmetric_curve_2d_element_representation.wr:WR3"
there shall be at least one of the following <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_material_property_representation_item,fea_material_property_representation_item>> subtypes referenced by a *material*: <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_linear_elasticity,fea_linear_elasticity>>, <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_mass_density,fea_mass_density>>, <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_area_density,fea_area_density>>, <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_tangential_coefficient_of_linear_thermal_expansion,fea_tangential_coefficient_of_linear_thermal_expansion>>, <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_secant_coefficient_of_linear_thermal_expansion,fea_secant_coefficient_of_linear_thermal_expansion>>, and <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_moisture_absorption,fea_moisture_absorption>>.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.axisymmetric_curve_2d_element_representation.wr:WR4"

there shall be a parametric representation context associated with the element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.axisymmetric_curve_2d_element_representation.FU1"

the number of nodes in the node list of an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.axisymmetric_curve_2d_element_representation,axisymmetric_curve_2d_element_representation>> shall be the proper number for a point element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.plane_curve_2d_element_representation"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.plane_curve_2d_element_representation,plane_curve_2d_element_representation>> is an element with a specified cross section that is a 0D shape (a point) in the (stem:[i, j]) plane of the founding coordinate system (see <<subsec-geometric-founding-and-analysis-space>>) with a depth perpendicular to the (stem:[i, j]) plane. A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.plane_curve_2d_element_representation,plane_curve_2d_element_representation>> shall lie in the (stem:[i, j]) plane of the founding coordinate system.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.plane_curve_2d_element_representation.model_ref"

an application defined identifier of the <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_model,fea_model>> which possesses the plane curve 2D element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.plane_curve_2d_element_representation.element_descriptor"

a collection of information that specifies <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.plane_curve_2d_element_representation,plane_curve_2d_element_representation>>.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.plane_curve_2d_element_representation.property"

the cross section properties of a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.plane_curve_2d_element_representation,plane_curve_2d_element_representation>>.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.plane_curve_2d_element_representation.depth_property"

the properties for a planar section. Analysis applications often assume that the value of the depth attribute of this property is 1.0.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.plane_curve_2d_element_representation.material"

the material properties associated with a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.plane_curve_2d_element_representation,plane_curve_2d_element_representation>>.

NOTE: The element id, a unique application defined identifier of an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.element_representation,element_representation>>, is specified by the *name* attribute of the <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> supertype.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.plane_curve_2d_element_representation.UR1"

the combination of an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_model,fea_model>> and element id shall be unique within a finite element analysis model.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.plane_curve_2d_element_representation.wr:WR1"

the <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_model,fea_model>> shall be planar.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.plane_curve_2d_element_representation.wr:WR2"

there shall be a property coordinate system (CURVE_2D_ELEMENT_COORDINATE_SYSTEM) associated with a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.plane_curve_2d_element_representation,plane_curve_2d_element_representation>>.

The property coordinate system is the orientation of the coordinate system for the element material and section properties.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.plane_curve_2d_element_representation.wr:WR3"

there shall be at least one of the following <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_material_property_representation_item,fea_material_property_representation_item>> subtypes referenced by a *material*: <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_linear_elasticity,fea_linear_elasticity>>,
<<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_mass_density,fea_mass_density>>, <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_area_density,fea_area_density>>,
<<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_tangential_coefficient_of_linear_thermal_expansion,fea_tangential_coefficient_of_linear_thermal_expansion>>,
<<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_secant_coefficient_of_linear_thermal_expansion,fea_secant_coefficient_of_linear_thermal_expansion>>, and <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_moisture_absorption,fea_moisture_absorption>>.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.plane_curve_2d_element_representation.wr:WR4"

there shall be a parametric representation context associated with the element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.plane_curve_2d_element_representation.FU1"

the number of nodes in the node list of a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.plane_curve_2d_element_representation,plane_curve_2d_element_representation>> shall be the proper number for a point element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.element_descriptor"

An <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.element_descriptor,element_descriptor>> is a collection of information that specifies an element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.element_descriptor.topology_order"

the highest degree polynomial interpolation function used to describe the geometric shape of any edge of an element, which in turn is used to relate the node list of the element to the appropriate topology diagram in  <<sub-eltopo>>.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.element_descriptor.description"

additional information about the formulation or purpose of an element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.volume_3d_element_descriptor"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.volume_3d_element_descriptor,volume_3d_element_descriptor>> is a collection of information that specifies a volume 3D element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.volume_3d_element_descriptor.purpose"

the enumerated value specifying the response of a volume 3D element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.volume_3d_element_descriptor.shape"

the geometric shape of a volume 3D element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.axisymmetric_volume_2d_element_descriptor"

An <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.axisymmetric_volume_2d_element_descriptor,axisymmetric_volume_2d_element_descriptor>> is a collection of information that specifies an axisymmetric volume 2D element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.axisymmetric_volume_2d_element_descriptor.purpose"

the enumerated value specifying the response of an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.axisymmetric_volume_2d_element_representation,axisymmetric_volume_2d_element_representation>>. The purpose is a SET of SETs in order to allow the appropriate combinations of coupled and uncoupled responses.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.axisymmetric_volume_2d_element_descriptor.shape"

the geometric shape of an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.axisymmetric_volume_2d_element_representation,axisymmetric_volume_2d_element_representation>>.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.plane_volume_2d_element_descriptor"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.plane_volume_2d_element_descriptor,plane_volume_2d_element_descriptor>> is a collection of information that specifies a plane volume 2D element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.plane_volume_2d_element_descriptor.purpose"

the enumerated value specifying the response of <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.plane_volume_2d_element_representation,plane_volume_2d_element_representation>>. The purpose is a SET of SETs in order to allow the appropriate combinations of coupled and uncoupled responses.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.plane_volume_2d_element_descriptor.shape"

the geometric shape of a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.plane_volume_2d_element_representation,plane_volume_2d_element_representation>>.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.plane_volume_2d_element_descriptor.assumption"

the use of a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.plane_volume_2d_element_representation,plane_volume_2d_element_representation>> with 2D shape to model a volume.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.volume_3d_element_basis"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.volume_3d_element_basis,volume_3d_element_basis>> is the information that forms the basis of a volume 3D element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.volume_3d_element_basis.descriptor"

the association to the information describing a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.volume_3d_element_representation,volume_3d_element_representation>>.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.volume_3d_element_basis.variable"

the variable to be associated with an order and shape function for a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.volume_3d_element_representation,volume_3d_element_representation>>.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.volume_3d_element_basis.variable_order"

the mathematical order of polynomials used to define the shape function.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.volume_3d_element_basis.variable_shape_function"

the type of polynomial shape function used to interpolate the variable within a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.volume_3d_element_representation,volume_3d_element_representation>>.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.volume_3d_element_basis.evaluation_points"

the locations within a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.volume_3d_element_representation,volume_3d_element_representation>> where the *variable* is evaluated using the *variable_shape_function*.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.volume_2d_element_basis"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.volume_2d_element_basis,volume_2d_element_basis>> is the information that forms the basis of a volume 2D element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.volume_2d_element_basis.descriptor"

the association to the information describing a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.volume_2d_element_representation,volume_2d_element_representation>>.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.volume_2d_element_basis.variable"

the variable to be associated with an order and shape function for a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.volume_2d_element_representation,volume_2d_element_representation>>.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.volume_2d_element_basis.variable_order"

the mathematical order of polynomials used to define the shape function.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.volume_2d_element_basis.variable_shape_function"

the type of polynomial shape function used to interpolate the variable within a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.volume_2d_element_representation,volume_2d_element_representation>>.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.volume_2d_element_basis.evaluation_points"

the locations within a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.volume_2d_element_representation,volume_2d_element_representation>> where the *variable* is evaluated using the *variable_shape_function*.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.surface_3d_element_descriptor"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.surface_3d_element_descriptor,surface_3d_element_descriptor>> is a collection of information that specifies a surface 3D element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.surface_3d_element_descriptor.purpose"

the enumerated value specifying the response of a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.surface_3d_element_representation,surface_3d_element_representation>>. The purpose is a SET of SETs in order to allow the appropriate combinations of coupled and uncoupled responses.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.surface_3d_element_descriptor.shape"

the geometric shape of a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.surface_3d_element_representation,surface_3d_element_representation>>.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.axisymmetric_surface_2d_element_descriptor"

An <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.axisymmetric_surface_2d_element_descriptor,axisymmetric_surface_2d_element_descriptor>> is a collection of information that specifies an axisymmetric surface 2D element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.axisymmetric_surface_2d_element_descriptor.purpose"

the enumerated value specifying the response of an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.axisymmetric_surface_2d_element_representation,axisymmetric_surface_2d_element_representation>>. The purpose is a SET of SETs in order to allow the appropriate combinations of coupled and uncoupled responses.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.plane_surface_2d_element_descriptor"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.plane_surface_2d_element_descriptor,plane_surface_2d_element_descriptor>> is a collection of information that specifies a plane surface 2D element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.plane_surface_2d_element_descriptor.purpose"

the enumerated value specifying the response of a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.plane_surface_2d_element_representation,plane_surface_2d_element_representation>>. The purpose is a SET of SETs in order to allow the appropriate combinations of coupled and uncoupled responses.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.plane_surface_2d_element_descriptor.assumption"

the use of a curve element to model a surface.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.surface_3d_element_basis"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.surface_3d_element_basis,surface_3d_element_basis>> is the information that forms the basis of a surface 3D element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.surface_3d_element_basis.descriptor"

the association to the information describing a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.surface_3d_element_representation,surface_3d_element_representation>>.

