the mathematical order of polynomials used to define the shape function.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.surface_2d_element_basis.variable_shape_function"

the type of polynomial shape function used to interpolate the variable within a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.surface_2d_element_representation,surface_2d_element_representation>>.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.surface_2d_element_basis.evaluation_points"

the locations within a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.surface_2d_element_representation,surface_2d_element_representation>> where the *variable* is evaluated using the *variable_shape_function*.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_descriptor"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_descriptor,curve_3d_element_descriptor>> is a collection of information that specifies a curve 3D element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_descriptor.purpose"

the enumerated value specifying the response of a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_representation,curve_3d_element_representation>>. The purpose is a SET of SETs in order to allow the appropriate combinations of coupled and uncoupled responses.

