*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_basis.evaluation_points"

the locations within a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_representation,curve_3d_element_representation>> where the *variable* is evaluated using the *variable_shape_function*.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_2d_element_basis"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_2d_element_basis,curve_2d_element_basis>> is the information that forms the basis of a curve 2D element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_2d_element_basis.descriptor"

the association to the information describing a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_2d_element_representation,curve_2d_element_representation>>.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_2d_element_basis.variable"

the variable to be associated with an order and shape function for a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_2d_element_representation,curve_2d_element_representation>>.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.point_element_representation"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.point_element_representation,point_element_representation>> is a single noded explicit element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.point_element_representation.model_ref"

an application defined identifier of the <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_model,fea_model>> which possesses the point element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.point_element_representation.description"

information about the *point_element* purpose.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.point_element_representation.matrix_set"

the explicit element matrices.

NOTE: The element id, a unique application defined identifier of an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.element_representation,element_representation>>, is specified by the *name* attribute of the <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> supertype.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.point_element_representation.UR1"

the combination of an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_model,fea_model>> and element id shall be unique within a finite element analysis model.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.point_element_representation.wr:WR1"

there shall be exactly one coordinate system associated with a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.point_element_representation,point_element_representation>>.

A matrix coordinate system (FEA_AXIS2_PLACEMENT_3D) is the coordinate system with respect to which all of the matrices of the point element are defined. The degrees of freedom at a node are defined with respect to the local orthogonal triad of the specified coordinate system at that node.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.point_element_representation.FU1"

the number of nodes in the node list of a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.point_element_representation,point_element_representation>> shall be the proper number for a point element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.point_element_matrix"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.point_element_matrix,point_element_matrix>> is a matrix that represents a stationary mass, grounded spring, or grounded damper.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.stationary_mass"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.stationary_mass,stationary_mass>> is a point element nodal response matrix of type stationary mass. The <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.stationary_mass,stationary_mass>> matrix is populated as follows:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
\left(
   \begin{array}{cccccc}
      m_{x}  & & & & &               \\
      &  m_{y} & & & &               \\
      & &  m_{z} & & &               \\
      & & &    i_{xx} & i_{xy} & i_{xz}    \\
      & & &    i_{xy} & i_{yy} & i_{yz}    \\
      & & &    i_{xz} & i_{yz} & i_{zz}
   \end{array}
\right)
++++

NOTE: In all physical cases mass acts equally in all directions.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.stationary_mass.mass"

the point masses in the different directions is populated as follows:

Array item 1 is the mass acting in the stem:[x] direction, and is denoted stem:[m_x] in the matrix shown above; +
Array item 2 is the mass acting in the stem:[y] direction, and is denoted stem:[m_y] in the matrix shown above; +
Array item 3 is the mass acting in the stem:[z] direction, and is denoted stem:[m_z] in the matrix shown above;

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.stationary_mass.moments_of_inertia"

the moments of inertia of a point (denoted by stem:[i_{xx} ... i_{zz}] in the matrix shown above) in the different directions. The values of the inertias should be set to 0.0 if unwanted. The inertias are evaluated about the centre of mass.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.stationary_mass.coordinate_system"

the coordinate system which is used to specify the offset.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.stationary_mass.offset_vector"

the distance from the node to the position of the centre of mass with respect to the local orthogonal triad of the specified coordinate system at the node.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.grounded_spring"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.grounded_spring,grounded_spring>> is a point element nodal response matrix of type grounded spring. The <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.grounded_spring,grounded_spring>> matrix is populated as follows:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
\left(
   \begin{array}{cccccc}
      kt_{x}  & & & & &  \\
      &  kt_{y} & & & &  \\
      & &  kt_{z} & & &  \\
      & & &  kr_{x} & &  \\
      & & & &  kr_{y} &  \\
      & & & & &  kr_{z}
   \end{array}
\right)
++++

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.grounded_spring.stiffness_coefficients"

the stiffnesses in the different directions is populated as follows:

Array item 1 is the translational stiffness in the stem:[x] direction, denoted stem:[k t_x] in the matrix shown above. +
Array item 2 is the translational stiffness in the stem:[y] direction, denoted stem:[k t_y] in the matrix shown above. +
Array item 3 is the translational stiffness in the stem:[z] direction, denoted stem:[k t_z] in the matrix shown above. +
Array item 4 is the rotational stiffness about the stem:[x] direction, denoted stem:[k r_x] in the matrix shown above. +
Array item 5 is the rotational stiffness about the stem:[y] direction, denoted stem:[k r_y] in the matrix shown above. +
Array item 6 is the rotational stiffness about the stem:[z] direction, denoted stem:[k r_z] in the matrix shown above.
*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.grounded_damper"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.grounded_damper,grounded_damper>> is a point element nodal response matrix of type grounded damper. The <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.grounded_damper,grounded_damper>> matrix is populated as follows:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
\left(
   \begin{array}{cccccc}
      dt_{x}  & & & & &  \\
      &  dt_{y} & & & &  \\
      & &  dt_{z} & & &  \\
      & & &  dr_{x} & &  \\
      & & & &  dr_{y} &  \\
      & & & & &  dr_{z}
   \end{array}
\right)
++++

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.grounded_spring.damping_coefficients"

the damping in the different directions is populated as follows:

Array item 1 is the translational damping in the stem:[x] direction, denoted stem:[d t_x] in the matrix shown above. +
Array item 2 is the translational damping in the stem:[y] direction, denoted stem:[d t_y] in the matrix shown above. +
Array item 3 is the translational damping in the stem:[z] direction, denoted stem:[d t_z] in the matrix shown above. +
Array item 4 is the rotational damping about the stem:[x] direction, denoted stem:[d r_x] in the matrix shown above. +
Array item 5 is the rotational damping about the stem:[y] direction, denoted stem:[d r_y] in the matrix shown above. +
Array item 6 is the rotational damping about the stem:[z] direction, denoted stem:[d r_z] in the matrix shown above.
*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.directionally_explicit_element_representation"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.directionally_explicit_element_representation,directionally_explicit_element_representation>> is a two noded element for which the matrices (stiffness, damping and mass) are characterized by a single coefficient stem:[k]. The stem:[x] direction of the matrix is defined with respect to a coordinate system.

All elements of the matrix are populated from the single coefficient stem:[k]. The matrix is of the form:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
\begin{array}{cc}
\left(    \begin{array}{ccccccc}
        & & & & & & \\
        & +k & & & & -k  \\
        & & & & & & \\
        & & & & & & \\
        & & & & & & \\
        & -k & & & & +k
    \end{array}  \right)   &
         \begin{array}{cc}
                  & \\
                  \cdots & \mbox{degree of freedom 1, node 1} \\
                  & \\
                  & \\
                  & \\
                  \cdots & \mbox{degree of freedom 2, node 2}
         \end{array}      \\
                     & \\
        \begin{array}{cccccc}
           \vdots & & & & & \vdots
     \end{array}  & \\
     \begin{array}{cccc}
& \mbox{degree of}  & \mbox{degree of}  & \\
& \mbox{freedom 1,} & \mbox{freedom 2,} & \\
& \mbox{node 1} & \mbox{node 2}  &
    \end{array}    &
\end{array}
++++

Different degrees of freedom can be specified for the two nodes. For a simple axial spring or damper the stem:[x] translation degree of freedom in the aligned system is specified for both nodes. A two node explicit element can be used instead of a directionally explicit element, but an explicit element is less convenient because it is necessary to define each of the four matrix terms separately. Also, an aligned coordinate system cannot be defined for an explicit element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.directionally_explicit_element_representation.model_ref"

an application defined identifier of the <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_model,fea_model>> which possesses the directionally explicit element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.directionally_explicit_element_representation.systems_and_freedoms"

the coordinate systems and degrees of freedom with respect to which all of the matrices of the <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.directionally_explicit_element_representation,directionally_explicit_element_representation>> are defined. List item 1 specifies the coordinate system and degree of freedom at node 1 and list item 2 specifies the coordinate system and degree of freedom at node 2.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.directionally_explicit_element_representation.description"

information about the purpose of a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.directionally_explicit_element_representation,directionally_explicit_element_representation>>.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.directionally_explicit_element_representation.coefficient"

the single coefficient that characterizes the matrices of a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.directionally_explicit_element_representation,directionally_explicit_element_representation>>.

NOTE: The element id, a unique application defined identifier of an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.element_representation,element_representation>>, is specified by the *name* attribute of the <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> supertype.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.directionally_explicit_element_representation.UR1"

the combination of an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_model,fea_model>> and element id shall be unique within a finite element analysis model.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.directionally_explicit_element_representation.FU1"

the number of nodes in the node list of a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.directionally_explicit_element_representation,directionally_explicit_element_representation>> shall be the proper number based on the linear order of the <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.directionally_explicit_element_representation,directionally_explicit_element_representation>>.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.system_and_freedom"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.system_and_freedom,system_and_freedom>> is the coordinate system and degree of freedom for a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.directionally_explicit_element_representation,directionally_explicit_element_representation>> node.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.system_and_freedom.matrix_coordinate_system"

the coordinate system with respect to which all of the matrices of the <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.directionally_explicit_element_representation,directionally_explicit_element_representation>> are defined for a node. This system can be an aligned system derived form the positions of the element nodes, or it can be an arbitrary system. An aligned system shall not be specified if the two nodes of the element are coincident.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.system_and_freedom.freedom"

the degree of freedom at a node of a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.directionally_explicit_element_representation,directionally_explicit_element_representation>>.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.directionally_explicit_element_coefficient"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.directionally_explicit_element_coefficient,directionally_explicit_element_coefficient>> is the coefficient that characterizes the matrices of the directionally explicit element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.directionally_explicit_element_coefficient.property_type"

the enumerated value specifying the type of matrix (stiffness, mass, or damping).

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.directionally_explicit_element_coefficient.coefficient"

the coefficient that defines the matrix.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.explicit_element_representation"

An <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.explicit_element_representation,explicit_element_representation>> is an element in which the associated matrices (stiffness, mass, and damping) are specified directly.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.explicit_element_representation.model_ref"

an application defined identifier of the <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_model,fea_model>> which possesses the explicit element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.explicit_element_representation.description"

information about an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.explicit_element_representation,explicit_element_representation>> purpose.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.explicit_element_representation.matrix"

the explicit element matrix.

NOTE: The element id, a unique application defined identifier of an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.element_representation,element_representation>>, is specified by the *name* attribute of the <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> supertype.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.explicit_element_representation.UR1"

the combination of an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_model,fea_model>> and element id shall be unique within a finite element analysis model.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.explicit_element_representation.wr:WR1"

there shall be exactly one matrix coordinate system associated with an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.explicit_element_representation,explicit_element_representation>>.

A matrix coordinate system (FEA_AXIS2_PLACEMENT_3D) is the coordinate system with respect to which all of the matrices of an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.explicit_element_representation,explicit_element_representation>> are defined. The degrees of freedom at a node are defined with respect to the local orthogonal triad of the specified coordinate system at that node.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.explicit_element_representation.wr:WR2"

the lengths of the degree of freedom list and the required node list shall be the same.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.explicit_element_matrix"

An <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.explicit_element_matrix,explicit_element_matrix>> is stiffness, mass, or damping matrix associated with an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.explicit_element_representation,explicit_element_representation>>.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.explicit_element_matrix.property_type"

the type of matrix (stiffness, mass, or damping).

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.explicit_element_matrix.symmetry"

the symmetry of the matrix (symmetric or diagonal).

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.explicit_element_matrix.node_dof_list"

the degree of freedom at the nodes. The first list shall have the dimension of the number of <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.explicit_element_representation,explicit_element_representation>> nodes, the second list shall have the dimension of the number of freedoms for that node.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.explicit_element_matrix.matrix_values"

the coefficients that define the matrices of the <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.explicit_element_representation,explicit_element_representation>>.

NOTE: The matrix is square with freedoms in the sequence specified by the node_dof_list. The number of independent terms in the matrix and their position in the list depends on the attribute <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.matrix_symmetry,matrix_symmetry>>. Refer to the <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.matrix_symmetry,matrix_symmetry>> TYPE for the definitions of how these matrices are populated.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.explicit_element_matrix.wr:WR1"

the length of the *matrix_values* list shall be appropriate for the size and symmetry of the matrix.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.substructure_element_representation"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.substructure_element_representation,substructure_element_representation>> is a model that may have reduced degrees of freedom and is assembled into another model.

NOTE: The connectivity between the substructure nodes and the model is established with the <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.substructure_node_relationship,substructure_node_relationship>> entity.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.substructure_element_representation.model_ref"

the <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_model,fea_model>> in which the substructure element is to be assembled.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.substructure_element_representation.substructure_model_ref"

the <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_model,fea_model>> that possesses the substructure element.

NOTE: The element id, a unique application defined identifier of an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.substructure_element_representation,substructure_element_representation>>, is specified by the *name* attribute of the <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> supertype.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.substructure_element_representation.UR1"

the combination of an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_model,fea_model>> and element id shall be unique within a finite element analysis model.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.aligned_axis_tolerance"

An <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.aligned_axis_tolerance,aligned_axis_tolerance>> is a value for the tolerance of the alignment of coordinate systems

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.aligned_axis_tolerance.model_ref"

the model to which the tolerance applies.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.aligned_axis_tolerance.tolerance"

the value of the alignment tolerance.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.arbitrary_volume_3d_element_coordinate_system"

An <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.arbitrary_volume_3d_element_coordinate_system,arbitrary_volume_3d_element_coordinate_system>> is an arbitrary orthogonal coordinate system for a volume 3D element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.arbitrary_volume_3d_element_coordinate_system.coordinate_system"

the coordinate system for the volume 3D element. At a point within the element, information is defined with respect to the local orthogonal coordinate system triad of the specified coordinate system at that point.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.parametric_volume_3d_element_coordinate_system"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.parametric_volume_3d_element_coordinate_system,parametric_volume_3d_element_coordinate_system>> is the orthogonal coordinate system for a volume 3D element. At each point in the element an intermediate orthogonal coordinate system is derived from the parametric coordinate system of an element. Let the triad (stem:[xi, eta, zeta]) denote the axes of the parametric coordinate system, and (stem:[x', y', z']) denote the axis of an intermediate orthogonal coordinate system. The orthogonal coordinate system used to define information for the element, denoted (stem:[x, y, z]), is related to this intermediate orthogonal coordinate system (stem:[x', y', z']) by Euler angles.

For the purpose of reference by attributes *axis_1* and *axis_2*, let stem:[xi = 1], stem:[eta = 2] and, stem:[zeta = 3]. The intermediate orthogonal coordinate system shall be derived from the parametric coordinate system by the various combinations of *axis_1* and *axis_2* as follows:

* *axis_1* = 1 and *axis_2* = 2: +
+
--
[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
\bf{x^\prime} = \bf{\xi}
++++

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
\bf{z^\prime} = \langle \bf{\xi} \times \bf{\eta} \rangle
++++
--

* *axis_1* = 2 and *axis_2* = 3: +
+
--
[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
\bf{y^\prime} = \bf{\eta}
++++

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
\bf{x^\prime} = \langle \bf{\eta} \times \bf{\zeta} \rangle
++++
--

* *axis_1* = 3 and *axis_2* = 1: +
+
--
[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
\bf{z^\prime} = \bf{\zeta}
++++

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
\bf{y^\prime} = \langle \bf{\zeta} \times \bf{\xi} \rangle
++++
--

* *axis_1* = 1 and *axis_2* = 3: +
+
--
[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
\bf{x^\prime} = \bf{\xi}
++++

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
\bf{y^\prime} = \langle \bf{\zeta} \times \bf{\xi} \rangle
++++
--

* *axis_1* = 2 and *axis_2* = 1: +
+
--
[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
\bf{y^\prime} = \bf{\eta}
++++

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
\bf{z^\prime} = \langle \bf{\xi} \times \bf{\eta} \rangle
++++
--

* *axis_1* = 3 and *axis_2* = 2: +
+
--
[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
\bf{z^\prime} = \bf{\zeta}
++++

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
\bf{x^\prime} = \langle \bf{\eta} \times \bf{\zeta} \rangle
++++
--

The derivation of an orthogonal coordinate system for *axis_1* = 1 and *axis_2* = 2 is shown in <<fig-orthogonal-volume-3d-element-axis-1-axis-2>> for a linear hexahedron element. Here, the (stem:[x, y, z]) system is not rotated from the (stem:[x', y', z']) system and is therefore coincident. The stem:[z] and stem:[z'] axes are perpendicular to the stem:[xi eta] plane. The stem:[y] and stem:[y'] axes are perpendicular to the stem:[x']stem:[z'] and stem:[x]stem:[z] planes, positive right-hand rule.

[[fig-orthogonal-volume-3d-element-axis-1-axis-2]]
.Orthogonal volume 3D element coordinate system derivation for axis_1 = 1 and axis_2 = 2
image::images/fig-40.svg[]

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.parametric_volume_3d_element_coordinate_system.axis_1"

the first parametric axis used to derive the orthogonal coordinate system.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.parametric_volume_3d_element_coordinate_system.axis_2"

the second parametric axis used to derive the orthogonal coordinate system.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.parametric_volume_3d_element_coordinate_system.eu_angles"

three Euler angles that define the orthogonal element coordinate system (stem:[x, y, z]) with respect to (stem:[x', y', z']).

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.parametric_volume_3d_element_coordinate_system.wr:WR1"

the two defining axes of the coordinate system shall be 1, 2, or 3, and they shall not be the same.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.arbitrary_volume_2d_element_coordinate_system"

An <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.arbitrary_volume_2d_element_coordinate_system,arbitrary_volume_2d_element_coordinate_system>> specifies an arbitrary orthogonal coordinate system for a volume 2D element, for which the stem:[x] axis shall be normal to the 2D analysis plane and in the direction of the stem:[k] axis of the 2D analysis plane definition coordinate system.

The orientation of the coordinate systems is shown in <<fig-arbitrary-volume-2d-element-coordinate-system-orientation>>. The stem:[j] axis is the axis of symmetry, and the stem:[ij] plane is the 2D analysis plane. The stem:[yz] plane is coincident with the stem:[ij] plane. The stem:[y] axis is oriented by thevector <<express:geometry_schema.direction,direction>>.

[[fig-arbitrary-volume-2d-element-coordinate-system-orientation]]
.Arbitrary volume 2D element coordinate system orientation
image::images/fig-41.svg[]

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.arbitrary_volume_2d_element_coordinate_system.orientation"

the direction used to orient the orthogonal coordinate system at each point within the element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.arbitrary_volume_2d_element_coordinate_system.wr:WR1"

the space dimensionality of the direction shall be 2.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.parametric_volume_2d_element_coordinate_system"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.parametric_volume_2d_element_coordinate_system,parametric_volume_2d_element_coordinate_system>> is an orthogonal coordinate system for a volume 2D element. An intermediate orthogonal coordinate system (stem:[x', y', z']) is derived from the parametric coordinate system (stem:[xi, eta]) of an element. The stem:[z'] axis of the intermediate orthogonal coordinate system is normal to the 2D analysis plane and in the direction of the stem:[k] axis of the 2D analysis plane definition coordinate system. An axis of the intermediate orthogonal coordinate system in the 2D analysis plane shall be derived according to the *axis* attribute as follows:

* for *axis* = 1 the stem:[y'] axis of the intermediate orthogonal system is on the same directionas the axis stem:[xi] of the parametric coordinate system;

* for *axis* = 2 the stem:[z'] axis of the intermediate orthogonal system is in the same directionas the axis stem:[eta] of the parametric system.

The orthogonal coordinate system defined for the element, denoted(stem:[x, y, z]) is related to the intermediate orthogonal system (stem:[x', y', z']) by an angle.

The derivation of an orthogonal coordinate system for axis = 1 is shown in <<fig-parametric-volume-2d-element-coord-system-axis-1>>. Here, the (stem:[x, y, z]) system is not rotated from the (stem:[x', y', z']) system and is therefore coincident. The stem:[x] and stem:[x'] axes are perpendicular to the stem:[xi eta] plane. The stem:[z] and stem:[z'] axes are perpendicular to the stem:[x']stem:[y'] and stem:[x]stem:[y] planes, positive right-hand rule.

[[fig-parametric-volume-2d-element-coord-system-axis-1]]
.Parametric volume 2D element coordinate system derivation for axis = 1
image::images/fig-42.svg[]

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.parametric_volume_2d_element_coordinate_system.axis"

the axis of the parametric and intermediate coordinate systems that are aligned.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.parametric_volume_2d_element_coordinate_system.angle"

the angle from the stem:[x'] to the stem:[x] axis measured in a positive sense about the stem:[z'] axis.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.parametric_volume_2d_element_coordinate_system.wr:WR1"

the defining axis of the coordinate system shall be either 1 or 2.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.aligned_surface_3d_element_coordinate_system"

An <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.aligned_surface_3d_element_coordinate_system,aligned_surface_3d_element_coordinate_system>> is an aligned orthogonalcoordinate system for a surface 3D element that is derived from the local orthogonal triad of the specified arbitrary coordinate systemand the normal to the surface of an element. Let the triad (stem:[x, y, z]) denote theaxes of the aligned orthogonal system, and let (stem:[X, Y, Z]) denote the local orthogonal triad of the specified arbitrary system. At each point in the element the stem:[z] axis of thealigned orthogonal system shall be normal to the surface of an elementsuch that:

[stem%unnumbered]
++++
z * Z > 0
++++

The stem:[y] axis of the aligned orthogonal system is such that:

[stem%unnumbered]
++++
y = << z xx X >>
++++

Hence the stem:[X] axis is projected on the surface of the element to form the stem:[x] axis of the aligned orthogonal system. It is important that the aligned orthogonal coordinate system be well conditioned. To ensure this stem:[Z] shall be specified such that:

[stem%unnumbered]
++++
z * Z > "tolerance" |z| |Z|
++++

where the tolerance is specified by an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.aligned_axis_tolerance,aligned_axis_tolerance>> entity for the model.

The derivation of a surface 3D element aligned orthogonal coordinate system from an arbitrary coordinate system is shown in <<fig-aligned-surface-3d-element-coord-system-derivation>>.

[[fig-aligned-surface-3d-element-coord-system-derivation]]
.Aligned surface 3D element coordinate system derivation
image::images/fig-43.svg[]

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.aligned_surface_3d_element_coordinate_system.coordinate_system"

the coordinate system for the element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.parametric_surface_3d_element_coordinate_system"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.parametric_surface_3d_element_coordinate_system,parametric_surface_3d_element_coordinate_system>> is an orthogonal coordinate system for a surface 3D element. An intermediate orthogonal coordinate system (stem:[xi, eta, zeta]) at any point on the element is derived from the parametric coordinate system. This intermediate orthogonal system shall be derived from the parametric system according to the value of *axis* attribute as follows:

* for *axis* = 1 the stem:[x'] axis of the intermediate orthogonal system is in the same direction as the axis stem:[xi] of the parametric coordinate system;

* for *axis* = 2 the stem:[y'] axis of the intermediate orthogonal system is in the same direction as the axis stem:[eta] of the parametric coordinate system.

The stem:[z'] intermediate orthogonal axis shall be normal to the surface in the direction of the stem:[zeta] parametric coordinate system axis.   The orthogonal coordinate system defined for the element, denoted (stem:[x, y, z]) is related to the intermediate orthogonal coordinate system (stem:[x', y', z']) by the *angle* attribute.

The derivation of an orthogonal coordinate system for axis = 1 is shown in <<fig-parametric-surface-3d-axis-1>>. Here, the (stem:[x, y, z]) system is not rotated from the (stem:[x', y', z']) system and is therefore coincident. The stem:[z] and stem:[z'] axes are perpendicular to the stem:[xi eta] plane. The stem:[y] and stem:[y'] axes are perpendicular to the stem:[x']stem:[z'] and stem:[x]stem:[z] planes, positive right-hand rule.

[[fig-parametric-surface-3d-axis-1]]
.Parametric surface 3D element coordinate system derivation for axis = 1
image::images/fig-44.svg[]

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.parametric_surface_3d_element_coordinate_system.axis"

the axis of the parametric and intermediate orthogonal coordinate systems that are aligned.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.parametric_surface_3d_element_coordinate_system.angle"

the angle from the stem:[x'] to the stem:[x] axis measured in a positive sense about the stem:[z'] axis.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.parametric_surface_3d_element_coordinate_system.wr:WR1"

the defining axis of the coordinate system shall be either 1 or 2.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.constant_surface_3d_element_coordinate_system"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.constant_surface_3d_element_coordinate_system,constant_surface_3d_element_coordinate_system>> is an aligned orthogonal coordinate system for a surface 3D element, and is defined for each point on the surface as follows:

* an intermediate orthogonal coordinate system is derived from the parametric coordinate system at the centroid of the element in the way specified for the <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.parametric_surface_3d_element_coordinate_system,parametric_surface_3d_element_coordinate_system>>;

* an aligned orthogonal coordinate system is derived from this intermediate orthogonal system in the way specified for entity <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.aligned_surface_3d_element_coordinate_system,aligned_surface_3d_element_coordinate_system>>.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.constant_surface_3d_element_coordinate_system.axis"

the axis of the parametric and intermediate orthogonal coordinate systems that are aligned.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.constant_surface_3d_element_coordinate_system.angle"

the angle from the stem:[x'] to the stem:[x] axis measured in a positive sense about the stem:[z'] axis.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.constant_surface_3d_element_coordinate_system.wr:WR1"

the defining axis of the coordinate system shall be either 1 or 2.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.aligned_surface_2d_element_coordinate_system"

An <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.aligned_surface_2d_element_coordinate_system,aligned_surface_2d_element_coordinate_system>> is an aligned orthogonal coordinate system for a surface 2D element.

For the <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.aligned_surface_2d_element_coordinate_system,aligned_surface_2d_element_coordinate_system>> the stem:[x] axis shall be normal to the 2D analysis plane and in the direction of the stem:[k] axis of the 2D analysis plane. At each point in the element the stem:[z] axis of the aligned orthogonal coordinate system shall be normal to the surface of an element in the stem:[z > 0] direction, and stem:[y = z xx x] such that:

[stem%unnumbered]
++++
z * d > 0
++++

where stem:[d] is the specified direction.

It is important that the aligned orthogonal coordinate system be well conditioned. To ensure this, stem:[d] shall be specified such that:

[stem%unnumbered]
++++
d * x > "tolerance" |d| |x|
++++

where the tolerance is specified by an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.aligned_axis_tolerance,aligned_axis_tolerance>> entity for the model.

The derivation of a surface 2D element aligned coordinate system is shown in <<fig-aligned-surface-2d-element-coord-system-derivation>>.

[[fig-aligned-surface-2d-element-coord-system-derivation]]
.Aligned surface 2D element coordinate system derivation
image::images/fig-45.svg[]

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.aligned_surface_2d_element_coordinate_system.orientation"

the direction used to orient the orthogonal coordinate system at each point within the element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.aligned_surface_2d_element_coordinate_system.wr:WR1"

the space dimensionality of the direction shall be 2.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.parametric_surface_2d_element_coordinate_system"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.parametric_surface_2d_element_coordinate_system,parametric_surface_2d_element_coordinate_system>> is an orthogonal coordinate system for a surface 2D element. The stem:[y] orthogonal axis shall be in the direction of the parametric axis stem:[xi]. The stem:[x] orthogonal axis is normal to the 2D analysis plane and in the direction of the stem:[k] axis of the 2D analysis plane definition system. The derivation of an orthogonal coordinate system is shown in <<fig-parametric-surface-2d-coord-system-derivation>>.

[[fig-parametric-surface-2d-coord-system-derivation]]
.Parametric surface 2D element coordinate system derivation
image::images/fig-46.svg[]

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.aligned_curve_3d_element_coordinate_system"

An <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.aligned_curve_3d_element_coordinate_system,aligned_curve_3d_element_coordinate_system>> is an aligned orthogonal coordinate system for a curve 3D element. Let the triad (stem:[x, y, z]) denote the axes of the aligned orthogonal system and let (stem:[X, Y, Z]) denote the local orthogonal triad of the specified arbitrary system. At each point in the element the stem:[x] axis is tangential to the curve such that:

[stem%unnumbered]
++++
x * X > 0
++++

The stem:[z] axis of the aligned orthogonal system is such that:

[stem%unnumbered]
++++
z = << x xx Y >>
++++

The derivation of the aligned orthogonal system needs to be well conditioned. To ensure this stem:[X] shall be specified such that:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
\bf{x} \cdot \bf{X} > \bf{tolerance} \, |\bf{x}| \, |\bf{X}|
++++

where the tolerance is specified by an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.aligned_axis_tolerance,aligned_axis_tolerance>> entity for the model.

The derivation of a curve 3D element aligned orthogonal coordinate system is shown in <<fig-aligned-curve-3d-element-coord-system-derivation>>.

[[fig-aligned-curve-3d-element-coord-system-derivation]]
.Aligned curve 3D element coordinate system derivation
image::images/fig-47.svg[]

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.aligned_curve_3d_element_coordinate_system.coordinate_system"

the coordinate system for the element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.parametric_curve_3d_element_coordinate_system"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.parametric_curve_3d_element_coordinate_system,parametric_curve_3d_element_coordinate_system>> is an orthogonal coordinate system that is derived from the parametric coordinate system for a curve 3D element. Let the triad (stem:[x, y, z]) denote axes of the orthogonal system and let stem:[d] denote the specified direction. The stem:[x] orthogonal axis is tangential to the curve in the direction of the parametric axis stem:[xi]. The stem:[z] orthogonal axis is defined such that:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
\bf{z} = \langle \bf{x} \times \bf{d} \rangle
++++

The derivation of the orthogonal system needs to be well conditioned.   To ensure this stem:[d] shall be specified such that:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
\bf{y} \cdot \bf{d} > \bf{tolerance} \, |\bf{y}| \, |\bf{d}|
++++

where the tolerance is specified by an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.aligned_axis_tolerance,aligned_axis_tolerance>> entity for the model.

The derivation of an orthogonal coordinate system is shown in <<fig-parametric-curve-3d-element-coord-system-derivation>>.

[[fig-parametric-curve-3d-element-coord-system-derivation]]
.Parametric curve 3D element coordinate system derivation
image::images/fig-48.svg[]

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.parametric_curve_3d_element_coordinate_system.direction"

a direction used to orient the orthogonal coordinate system at each point in the element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.parametric_curve_3d_element_coordinate_direction"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.parametric_curve_3d_element_coordinate_direction,parametric_curve_3d_element_coordinate_direction>> is the parametric direction used to orient the orthogonal 3D coordinate system for a curve 3D element by the use of a direction.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.parametric_curve_3d_element_coordinate_direction.orientation"

a direction used to orient the orthogonal coordinate system at each point in the element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.parametric_curve_3d_element_coordinate_direction.wr:WR1"

the space dimensionality of the direction shall be 3.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_2d_element_coordinate_system"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_2d_element_coordinate_system,curve_2d_element_coordinate_system>> is an orthogonal coordinate system for a curve 2D element. The stem:[x] axis is tangential to the curve in the direction of the stem:[k] axis of the 2D analysis plane. The stem:[y] axis of the aligned orthogonal system shall be in the specified direction. The derivation of an orthogonal coordinate system is shown in <<fig-curve-2d-element-coord-system-derivation>>.

[[fig-curve-2d-element-coord-system-derivation]]
.Curve 2D element coordinate system derivation
image::images/fig-49.svg[]

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_2d_element_coordinate_system.orientation"

the direction of the stem:[y] axis, which is defined in the 2D analysis plane, used to orient the orthogonal coordinate system at each point in the element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_2d_element_coordinate_system.wr:WR1"

the space dimensionality of the direction shall be 2.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.directionally_explicit_element_coordinate_system_arbitrary"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.directionally_explicit_element_coordinate_system_arbitrary,directionally_explicit_element_coordinate_system_arbitrary>> is an arbitrary orthogonal coordinate system for a directionally explicit element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.directionally_explicit_element_coordinate_system_arbitrary.arbitrary_system"

an arbitrary coordinate system. Information is defined with respect to the local orthogonal triad of the specified system. The information is evaluated at the nodes of an element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.directionally_explicit_element_coordinate_system_aligned"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.directionally_explicit_element_coordinate_system_aligned,directionally_explicit_element_coordinate_system_aligned>> is an aligned orthogonal coordinate system for orienting a directionally explicit element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.directionally_explicit_element_coordinate_system_aligned.aligned_system"

a curve 3D element coordinate system. The information is evaluated at the nodes of an element. A coordinate system is defined for the directionally explicit element as if it were a linear curve element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.euler_angles"

An <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.euler_angles,euler_angles>> is used to define a coordinate system relative to a defining coordinate system. Typically the defining coordinate system will be an element coordinate system, and the relative coordinate system used to define anisotropic material directions.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.euler_angles.angles"

the relative orientation of a new (rotated) coordinate system with respect to a defining coordinate system using a series of three consecutive rotations. This method is known as Euler angles. The original coordinate system stem:[x1], stem:[y1], stem:[z1] is rotated about the stem:[z1] axis over angle angles[1], with the angle positive right hand rule. This yields coordinate system stem:[x2], stem:[y2], stem:[z2].   Coordinate system stem:[x2], stem:[y2], stem:[z2] is rotated about the stem:[y2] axis over angle angles[2], with the angle positive right hand rule. This yields coordinate system stem:[x3], stem:[y3], stem:[z3].   Coordinate system stem:[x3], stem:[y3], stem:[z3] is rotated about the stem:[x3] axis over angle angles[3], positive right hand rule. This yields the final coordinate system.

*)

