A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_integrated_matrix,curve_3d_element_integrated_matrix>> is the matrix to be integrated for a curve 3D element, and the method of integration.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_integrated_matrix.descriptor"

the association to the information describing a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_representation,curve_3d_element_representation>>.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_integrated_matrix.property_type"

the type of matrix being evaluated.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_integrated_matrix.integration_description"

the interpolation rule and integration method.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_integrated_matrix_with_definition"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_integrated_matrix_with_definition,curve_3d_element_integrated_matrix_with_definition>> is the method of integration.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_integrated_matrix_with_definition.integration_definition"

a definition of the integration within the curve.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_integration"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_integration,curve_3d_element_integration>> the method of integration for the length and section of a curve 3D element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_integration.element_length"

the integration of the quantity being integrated along the length of the element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_integration.section"

the integration of the quantity being integrated over the section of the element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_length_integration"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_length_integration,curve_3d_element_length_integration>> is a curve 3D length integration that shall be either algebraic, by rule, or explicit.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_length_integration_rule"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_length_integration_rule,curve_3d_element_length_integration_rule>> is the integration rule and order for a curve 3D element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_length_integration_rule.integration_method"

the integration rule for the quantity being integrated.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_length_integration_rule.integration_order"

the order of the specified rule for the quantity being integrated.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_length_integration_explicit"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_length_integration_explicit,curve_3d_element_length_integration_explicit>> is the explicit numerical integration for a curve 3D element length.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_length_integration_explicit.integration_positions_and_weights"

the integration positions for the quantity being integrated, and the corresponding weights for each integration position.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_position_weight"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_position_weight,curve_3d_element_position_weight>> is an integration position within a 3D curve element, and its weighting factor.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_position_weight.integration_position"

the integration positions for the quantity being integrated.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_position_weight.integration_weight"

the weight for each integration position.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_section_integration_explicit"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_section_integration_explicit,curve_section_integration_explicit>> is the explicit numerical integration for a curve element cross section.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_section_integration_explicit.integration_positions"

the integration positions across the section for the quantity being integrated.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_2d_element_integrated_matrix"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_2d_element_integrated_matrix,curve_2d_element_integrated_matrix>> is the matrix to be integrated for a curve 2D element, and the method of integration.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_2d_element_integrated_matrix.descriptor"

the association to the information describing a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_2d_element_representation,curve_2d_element_representation>>.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_2d_element_integrated_matrix.property_type"

the type of matrix being evaluated.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_2d_element_integrated_matrix.integration_description"

the interpolation rule and integration method.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_2d_element_integrated_matrix_with_definition"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_2d_element_integrated_matrix_with_definition,curve_2d_element_integrated_matrix_with_definition>> is the method of integration.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_2d_element_integrated_matrix_with_definition.integration_definition"

a definition of the integration within the curve.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_2d_element_integration"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_2d_element_integration,curve_2d_element_integration>> is the method of integration for the section of a curve 2D element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_2d_element_integration.section"

a definition of the integration of the quantity being integrated over the section of the element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_parametric_point"

An <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_parametric_point,fea_parametric_point>> is a position within a finite element, and specifies its parametric coordinates stem:[xi], stem:[eta], and stem:[zeta].

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_parametric_point.coordinates"

the coordinates of the position. The first value of the coordinate is the stem:[xi] coordinate, the second the stem:[eta] coordinate, and the third the stem:[zeta] coordinate (if applicable).

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_parametric_point.wr:WR1"

each coordinate shall lie in the range from -1.0 to +1.0.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_parametric_point.wr:WR2"

only the SUBTYPE of <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_parametric_point,fea_parametric_point>> shall exist in this instance.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.volume_element_location"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.volume_element_location,volume_element_location>> is a location within a volume element, and specifies its parametric coordinates stem:[xi], stem:[eta] and stem:[zeta].

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.volume_element_location.coordinates"

the coordinates of the location. The first value of the coordinate is the stem:[xi] coordinate, the second the stem:[eta] coordinate, and the third the stem:[zeta] coordinate (if applicable).

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.surface_volume_element_location"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.surface_volume_element_location,surface_volume_element_location>> is a location within the volume of a surface element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.surface_volume_element_location.field_location"

the location over the surface of the element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.surface_volume_element_location.section_location"

the location on the section (through the thickness) of the element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.surface_element_location"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.surface_element_location,surface_element_location>> is a location on the surface of a surface element, that specifies its parametric coordinates stem:[xi] and, if appropriate, stem:[eta].

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.surface_element_location.coordinates"

the coordinates of the location. The first value of the pair is the stem:[xi] coordinate, and the second the stem:[eta] coordinate (if applicable).

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.surface_section_element_location"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.surface_section_element_location,surface_section_element_location>> is a location on the section (through the thickness) of a surface element. A section location can be specified as an offset from the nominal plane of the surface, or as a dimensionless section coordinate.

Within a surface of a composite material, a field variable may be discontinuous at a material boundary. If a section location is specified at a material boundary, a flag can be set to indicate whether the value of the variable is to be evaluated above or below the discontinuity.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.surface_section_element_location.above_material_discontinuity"

the side of a material discontinuity on which the field variable is to be evaluated.

If the value is TRUE, then the variable is evaluated on the side of the discontinuity in the direction of the positive stem:[z] axis of the property coordinate system for the element. If the value is FALSE, then the variable is evaluated on the other side of the discontinuity. If the value is UNKNOWN, then there is no discontinuity.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.surface_section_element_location_absolute"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.surface_section_element_location_absolute,surface_section_element_location_absolute>> is a location on the section (through the thickness)of a surface element that is specified by giving a distance from the nominal plane of the surface.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.surface_section_element_location_absolute.offset"

the distance of the location from the nominal plane of the element.

A positive value indicates an offset in the direction of the positive stem:[z] axis of the property coordinate system for the element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.surface_section_element_location_dimensionless"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.surface_section_element_location_dimensionless,surface_section_element_location_dimensionless>> is a location on the section (through the thickness) of a surface element that is specified by giving a dimensionless section coordinate.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.surface_section_element_location_dimensionless.coordinate"

the section coordinate of the location. A section coordinate of 1.0 indicates the surface of the element in the direction of the positive stem:[z] axis of the property coordinate system for the element. A section coordinate of -1.0 indicates the other surface.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.surface_section_element_location_dimensionless.wr:WR1"

the section coordinate shall be within the range from -1.0 to +1.0.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_volume_element_location"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_volume_element_location,curve_volume_element_location>> is a location within the volume of a curve element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_volume_element_location.field_location"

the location along the length of the element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_volume_element_location.section_location"

the location on the section (through the thickness) of the element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_location"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_location,curve_element_location>> is a location along the length of a curve element, that is specified by its parametric coordinate stem:[xi].

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_location.coordinate"

the coordinate of the location. The value is the stem:[xi] coordinate.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_section_element_location"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_section_element_location,curve_section_element_location>> is a location on the section (through the thickness) of a curve element. A section location is specified by giving distances from the nominal axis of the curve.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_section_element_location.offsets"

the distances of the location from the nominal axis of the element.

A positive value for the first coordinate indicates an offset in the direction of the positive stem:[y] axis of the property coordinate system for the element.

A positive value for the second coordinate item indicates an offset in the direction of the positive stem:[z] axis of the property coordinate system for the element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.element_material"

An <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.element_material,element_material>> is the aggregation of the material properties of the continuum that a finite element represents.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.element_material.material_id"

a unique application defined identifier for the material to be used during the finite element analysis.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.element_material.description"

a text narrative about the substance.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.element_material.properties"

the material properties that characterize a finite element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.element_material.wr:IP1"

the combination of <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_model,fea_model>> referenced by an element using an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.element_material,element_material>> and *material_id* shall be unique within a finite element analysis model.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_material_property_geometric_relationship"

An <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_material_property_geometric_relationship,fea_material_property_geometric_relationship>> associates finite element material properties to a <<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_item,geometric_representation_item>> within the context of a particular representation.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_material_property_geometric_relationship.material_ref"

the material properties to be associated.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_material_property_geometric_relationship.item"

the <<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_item,geometric_representation_item>> to which material properties are to be related.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_material_property_geometric_relationship.wr:WR1"

there shall be a geometric shape representation item associated with the finite element material properties.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_material_property_representation"

An <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_material_property_representation,fea_material_property_representation>> is a property of the substance of the continuum that a finite element represents. The property is defined with respect to the data environment specified in the <<express:material_property_representation_schema.material_property_representation,material_property_representation>> supertype.

NOTE: For layered composite material properties for surface elements the total thickness for the element is defined by adding up all the ply thicknesses in the material. The plies are defined by a defining Application Protocol.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_material_property_representation.wr:WR1"

there shall be exactly one of the following <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_material_property_representation_item,fea_material_property_representation_item>> subtypes associated with an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_material_property_representation,fea_material_property_representation>>:

* <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_linear_elasticity,fea_linear_elasticity>>;
* <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_mass_density,fea_mass_density>>;
* <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_area_density,fea_area_density>>;
* <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_tangential_coefficient_of_linear_thermal_expansion,fea_tangential_coefficient_of_linear_thermal_expansion>>;
* <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_secant_coefficient_of_linear_thermal_expansion,fea_secant_coefficient_of_linear_thermal_expansion>>;
* <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_moisture_absorption,fea_moisture_absorption>>;
* <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_shell_membrane_stiffness,fea_shell_membrane_stiffness>>;
* <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_shell_bending_stiffness,fea_shell_bending_stiffness>>;
* <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_shell_membrane_bending_coupling_stiffness,fea_shell_membrane_bending_coupling_stiffness>>;
* <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_shell_shear_stiffness,fea_shell_shear_stiffness>>.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_material_property_representation.wr:WR2"

the *definition* attribute that is inherited from the <<express:product_property_representation_schema.property_definition_representation,property_definition_representation>> supertype of an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_material_property_representation,fea_material_property_representation>> shall be a <<express:material_property_definition_schema.material_property,material_property>>.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_material_property_representation_item"

An <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_material_property_representation_item,fea_material_property_representation_item>> is the representation of mechanical material properties suitably idealized for finite element analysis.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_linear_elasticity"

An <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_linear_elasticity,fea_linear_elasticity>> is the collection of mechanical material properties representing a linear response of an *fea_material* to a small change in strain at a constant temperature. The response is a change in stress caused by a small change in strain as follows:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
\Delta\sigma_{ij} = \sum_{k=1}^3 \sum_{l=1}^3  d_{ijkl} \: \Delta\varepsilon_{kl}
++++

where:

stem:[d]:: is the fourth order elasticity tensor;

stem:[Delta sigma]:: is a change in the stress tensor;

stem:[Delta varepsilon]:: is a change in the strain tensor.

NOTE: This property is usually a function of temperature and other independent variables.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_linear_elasticity.fea_constants"

the values of the elasticity properties.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_mass_density"

An <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_mass_density,fea_mass_density>> is the mass of *fea_material* per unit volume of an element in a strain free state.

NOTE: This property is usually a function of temperature and other independent variables.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_mass_density.fea_constant"

the value of the FEA mass density property.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_area_density"

An <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_area_density,fea_area_density>> is the mass of *fea_material* per unit area of a surface element in a strain free state.

NOTE: This property is usually defined in a strain free state that has a reference temperature and other independent variables.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_area_density.fea_constant"

the value of the FEA area density property.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_tangential_coefficient_of_linear_thermal_expansion"

An <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_tangential_coefficient_of_linear_thermal_expansion,fea_tangential_coefficient_of_linear_thermal_expansion>> is the relationship of a change in thermal strain in an element to a small change in temperature as follows:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
 \Delta\varepsilon_{ij} =  \alpha_{ij}(T) \: \Delta T
++++

where:

stem:[alpha]:: is the tangential coefficient of linear thermal expansion for the material at temperature stem:[T];

stem:[Delta varepsilon]:: is the change in the strain tensor caused by the small change in temperature at temperature stem:[T];

stem:[Delta T]:: is a change in temperature in the neighborhood of stem:[T] in which the incremental thermal expansion is linear;

stem:[T]:: is the temperature.

NOTE: This property is usually a function of temperature and other independent variables.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_tangential_coefficient_of_linear_thermal_expansion.fea_constants"

the value of the FEA tangential coefficient of linear thermal expansion tensor.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_secant_coefficient_of_linear_thermal_expansion"

An <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_secant_coefficient_of_linear_thermal_expansion,fea_secant_coefficient_of_linear_thermal_expansion>> is the relationship of the thermal strain of an element caused by a change from a reference temperature to a specified temperature as follows:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
 \varepsilon_{ij} =  \alpha_{ij} \: ( T \:  -  \: T_o )
++++

where:

stem:[alpha (T)]:: is the secant coefficient of linear thermal expansion for the material at temperature stem:[T];

stem:[varepsilon]:: is the thermal strain caused by a change in temperature from its reference value stem:[T_o] to stem:[T];

stem:[T_o]:: is the reference temperature;

stem:[T]:: is the temperature.

The secant and the tangential coefficients of linear thermal expansion are different if the coefficients are temperature dependent.

NOTE: This property is usually a function of temperature and other independent variables.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_secant_coefficient_of_linear_thermal_expansion.fea_constants"

the value of the FEA secant coefficient of linear thermal expansion tensor.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_secant_coefficient_of_linear_thermal_expansion.reference_temperature"

the value of the reference temperature.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_moisture_absorption"

An <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_moisture_absorption,fea_moisture_absorption>> is the relationship of a change in moisture strain in an element to a small change in moisture as follows:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
 \Delta\varepsilon_{ij} =  \beta_{ij}(M) \: \Delta M
++++

where:

stem:[beta]:: is the coefficient of linear moisture expansion for the material at moisture content stem:[M];

stem:[Delta varepsilon]:: is the change in the strain tensor caused by the small change in moisture at moisture content stem:[M];

stem:[Delta M]:: is the change in moisture;

stem:[m]:: is the moisture content.

NOTE: This property is usually a function of temperature and other independent variables.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_moisture_absorption.fea_constants"

the value of the FEA linear moisture expansion tensor.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_shell_membrane_stiffness"

An <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_shell_membrane_stiffness,fea_shell_membrane_stiffness>> is the collection of mechanical properties representing a linear response of a *fea_material* to a small change in membrane strain. The response is a change in surface membrane force caused by a small change in membrane strain as follows:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
 \Delta N_{ij} =  \sum_{k=1}^2 \sum_{l=1}^2 d_{ijkl} \: \Delta\varepsilon_{kl}
++++

where:

stem:[d]:: is the shell membrane elasticity tensor;

stem:[n]:: is the 2D second order surface membrane force tensor;

stem:[varepsilon]:: is the 2D second order membrane strain tensor:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
\varepsilon = \frac{1}{2} ( J + J^t )
++++

where:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
J = \left( \begin{array}{cc}
  {\displaystyle \frac{\partial u}{\partial x}}   &
        {\displaystyle \frac{\partial v}{\partial x}}   \\
    {\displaystyle \frac{\partial u}{\partial y}}    &
        {\displaystyle \frac{\partial v}{\partial y}}
       \end{array}  \right)
++++

and where:

stem:[J]:: is the Jacobian;

stem:[J^t]:: is the transpose of the Jacobian;

stem:[u]:: is displacement in the stem:[x] direction;

stem:[v]:: is displacement in the stem:[y] direction.

NOTE: This property is usually a function of temperature and other independent variables.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_shell_membrane_stiffness.fea_constants"

the value of the FEA surface membrane elasticity tensor.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_shell_bending_stiffness"

An <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_shell_bending_stiffness,fea_shell_bending_stiffness>> is the collection of mechanical properties representing a linear response of an *fea_material* to a small change in curvature. The response is a change in surface aggregate bending moment caused by a small change in curvature as follows:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
 \Delta D_{ij} =  \sum_{k=1}^2 \sum_{l=1}^2  d_{ijkl} \: \Delta c_{kl}
++++

where:

stem:[d]:: is the shell bending elasticity tensor;

stem:[d]:: is the 2D second order aggregate surface bending moment tensor;

stem:[c]:: is the symmetric 2D second order surface curvature tensor:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
\left( \begin{array}{cc}
  {\displaystyle - \frac{\partial^2 w}{\partial x^2}}   &
        {\displaystyle - \frac{\partial^2 w}{\partial x \partial y}}   \\
    {\displaystyle - \frac{\partial^2 w}{\partial x \partial y}}    &
        {\displaystyle - \frac{\partial^2 w}{\partial y^2}}
       \end{array}  \right)
++++

where:

stem:[w]:: is displacement in the stem:[z] direction.

NOTE: This property is usually a function of temperature and other independent variables.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_shell_bending_stiffness.fea_constants"

the value of the FEA shell bending elasticity tensor.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_shell_membrane_bending_coupling_stiffness"

An <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_shell_membrane_bending_coupling_stiffness,fea_shell_membrane_bending_coupling_stiffness>> is the collection of mechanical properties representing a linear response of an *fea_material* to a small change in curvature. The response is a change in surface membrane force caused by a small change in curvature as follows:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
 \Delta N_{ij} =  \sum_{k=1}^2 \sum_{l=1}^2  d_{ijkl} \: \Delta c_{kl}
++++

where:

stem:[d]:: is the shell membrane bending coupling elasticity tensor;

stem:[n]:: is the 2D second order surface membrane force tensor;

stem:[c]:: is the symmetric 2D second order surface curvature tensor.

NOTE: This property is usually a function of temperature and other independent variables.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_shell_membrane_bending_coupling_stiffness.fea_constants"

the value of the FEA shell membrane bending coupling elasticity tensor.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_shell_shear_stiffness"

An <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_shell_shear_stiffness,fea_shell_shear_stiffness>> is the collection of mechanical properties representing a linear response of an *fea_material* to a small change in surface out of plane shear strain. The response is a change in surface aggregate out of plane shear forces caused by a small change in surface out of plane shear strain as follows:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
\Delta F_{i} = \sum_{j = 1}^2  s_{ij} \: \Delta\varepsilon_{j}
++++

where:

stem:[s]:: is the shell shear elasticity tensor;

stem:[F]:: is the 2D surface aggregate out of plane shear force vector;

stem:[varepsilon]:: is the 2D surface out of plane shear strain vector:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
\left( \begin{array}{c}
  {\displaystyle \frac{\partial w}{\partial x} +
                 \frac{\partial u}{\partial z}}  \\
  {\displaystyle \frac{\partial w}{\partial y} +
                  \frac{\partial v}{\partial z}}
       \end{array}  \right)
++++

where:

stem:[u]:: is displacement in the stem:[x] direction.

stem:[v]:: is displacement in the stem:[y] direction.

stem:[w]:: is displacement in the stem:[z] direction.

NOTE: This property is usually a function of temperature and other independent variables.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_shell_shear_stiffness.fea_constants"

the value of the FEA shell shear elasticity tensor.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.surface_element_property"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.surface_element_property,surface_element_property>> is the section properties for a surface element.

NOTE: The material of the surface is specified by subtypes of <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_material_property_representation_item,fea_material_property_representation_item>>. Material property subtypes that apply to surface elements have a rule associating the property to an element. If several material property matrices are needed then each would be an instance of a separate environment in an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_material_property_representation_item,fea_material_property_representation_item>>.

[example]
Membrane, bending, membrane-bending coupling, or shear are types of material property matrices.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.surface_element_property.property_id"

an application defined identifier of the surface element properties.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.surface_element_property.description"

the surface element properties.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.surface_element_property.section"

the properties over the field of the surface element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.surface_element_property.wr:IP1"

the combination of an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_model,fea_model>> referenced by an element using a <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.surface_element_property,surface_element_property>> and *property_id* shall be unique within a finite element analysis model.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.surface_section_field"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.surface_section_field,surface_section_field>> is a surface section field that shall be either constant or varying.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.surface_section_field_constant"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.surface_section_field_constant,surface_section_field_constant>> is a surface section field that has a constant value over the field of a surface element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.surface_section_field_constant.definition"

the surface section definition for the surface element. There is only one value that is constant over the entire surface.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.surface_section_field_varying"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.surface_section_field_varying,surface_section_field_varying>> is a surface section field that varies over the field of a surface element. The values in the surface section definition list (which correspond in order to the node list) are interpolated using the element shape functions.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.surface_section_field_varying.definitions"

the surface section definition for the surface element. The values in the surface section definition list (which correspond in order to the node list) are interpolated using the element shape functions.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.surface_section_field_varying.additional_node_values"

indicates whether values are given for all nodes of the element (TRUE), or just the vertex nodes (FALSE).

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.surface_section"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.surface_section,surface_section>> is a surface section definition that shall be uniform, with or without layers.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.surface_section.offset"

the distance between the neutral plane for bending and the reference surface which is defined by the positions of the nodes and the element shape functions. Surface element properties are defined with respect to the property coordinate system of the element. If the offset is positive, the neutral plane for bending is on the same side of the reference plane as the positive 3 direction of the property coordinate system.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.surface_section.non_structural_mass"

the non-structural mass per unit area of the reference plane of the surface element. This mass is in addition to the structural mass which is calculated from the volume of the element and the density of the material of the element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.surface_section.non_structural_mass_offset"

the offset direction which is defined with respect to the reference plane of the surface which in turn is defined by the positions of the nodes and the element shape functions.   Surface element properties are defined with respect to the property coordinate system of the element. If the offset is positive, the offset direction is on the same side of the reference plane as the positive 3 direction of the property coordinate system.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.uniform_surface_section"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.uniform_surface_section,uniform_surface_section>> is a surface section field that is uniform through the thickness of a surface element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.uniform_surface_section.thickness"

the membrane thickness of the surface element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.uniform_surface_section.bending_thickness"

this attribute specifies the effective thickness for bending of the surface. If it is not supplied, it is assumed to be of the same value as *thickness*.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.uniform_surface_section.shear_thickness"

the effective thickness for transverse shear (shear normal to the reference plane). This attribute shall be supplied if the surface element permits shear deformation. If it is not supplied for an element that supports shear deformation, then the analysis program shall use the appropriate value for a uniform shell.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.uniform_surface_section_layered"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.uniform_surface_section_layered,uniform_surface_section_layered>> is a surface section field that is layered through the thickness of a surface element. All layer information shall be specified in a using application protocol. The thickness, and if necessary the bending and shear thickness of the element shall be specified by the sum of the layer thicknesses and the layer properties and orientations.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_surface_section_geometric_relationship"

An <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_surface_section_geometric_relationship,fea_surface_section_geometric_relationship>> is the association of a surface section definition to a geometric shape representation item.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_surface_section_geometric_relationship.section_ref"

the surface section definition being related to geometry.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_surface_section_geometric_relationship.item"

the geometric representation item to which the surface section definition is being related.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_surface_section_geometric_relationship.wr:WR1"

the representation item associated with the surface section definition shall be a geometric representation item.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_property"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_property,curve_3d_element_property>> is a cross-section for a curve 3D element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_property.property_id"

an application defined identifier for the property, and is unique within the finite element analysis model.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_property.description"

the curve element properties.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_property.interval_definitions"

the material and section properties for each of the element intervals. The intervals shall be defined in sequence beginning with the interval closest to node 1 and ending with the interval closest to node 2.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_property.end_offsets"

the end offsets for the curve element. The item 1 of the array references the definition of the end offset at node 1 of the element. Item 2 references the definition of the end offset at node 2 of the element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_property.end_releases"

the end releases for the curve element. The item 1 of the array references the definition of the end release at node 1 of the element. Item 2 references the definition of the end release at node 2 of the element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_property.wr:IP1"

the combination of an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_model,fea_model>> and *property_id* shall be unique within a finite element analysis model.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_interval"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_interval,curve_element_interval>> is a curve element interval that shall be either constant or linearly varying.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_interval.finish_position"

the position of the end of the interval closest to node 2 of the curve element. The position is defined by the coordinate with respect to the parametric axis established graphically in  <<sub-eltopo>>. The intervals of a curve element are listed in the attribute *interval_definitions* of the curve_3d_element_property. The start position for each interval in the list (except the first) is the finish position of the previous interval. The start position for the first interval in the list has a parametric coordinate -1.0. This is the end at node 1. The finish position for the last interval has a parametric coordinate of 1.0. A finish position of 1.0 shall be supplied for the last interval in the list.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_interval.eu_angles"

three Euler angles that define a relative coordinate system with respect to the element parametric coordinate system that is used to define the material directions. The stem:[x] material direction shall be aligned with the relative coordinate system stem:[x] axis, similarly the material stem:[y] direction shall be aligned with the relative coordinate system stem:[y] axis, and the material stem:[z] direction shall be aligned with the relative coordinate systems stem:[z] axis.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_interval_constant"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_interval_constant,curve_element_interval_constant>> is a curve section that is constant over an interval of a curve element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_interval_constant.section"

the section definition for the interval.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_interval_linearly_varying"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_interval_linearly_varying,curve_element_interval_linearly_varying>> is a curve section that varies linearly over an interval of a curve element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_interval_linearly_varying.sections"

the section definitions at each end of the interval. Item 1 of the array references the section at the end of the interval nearest to node 1 of the element. Item 2 of the array references the section at the end of the interval nearest to node 2 of the element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_2d_element_property"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_2d_element_property,curve_2d_element_property>> is the section properties of a curve 2D element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_2d_element_property.property_id"

an application defined identifier for the property, which is unique within the finite element analysis model.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_2d_element_property.description"

the curve element properties.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_2d_element_property.section"

the section definition for the element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_2d_element_property.wr:IP1"

the combination of an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_model,fea_model>> and *property_id* shall be unique within a finite element analysis model.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_section_definition"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_section_definition,curve_element_section_definition>> is the section at a point on the curve element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_section_definition.description"

the curve element definition.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_section_definition.section_angle"

the orientation angle of the curve element section about the curve element stem:[x] axis. The angle is positive with respect to the right hand rule.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_section_derived_definitions"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_section_derived_definitions,curve_element_section_derived_definitions>> is cross-sectional information for a curve element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_section_derived_definitions.cross_sectional_area"

the cross sectional area of the section.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_section_derived_definitions.shear_area"

the shear area of the section. Array item 1 specifies the shear area effective for deformation in the stem:[xy] plane of the property coordinate system. Array item 2 specifies the shear area effective for deformation in the stem:[xz] plane of the property coordinate system. An Eulerian beam formulation assumes that there is no shear deformation, that is, the shear area is infinite. For such elements no shear area need be specified.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_section_derived_definitions.second_moment_of_area"

the second moments of area about the section centroid. The components of the inertia tensor with respect to the stem:[y] and stem:[z] axes of the property coordinate system are stored as follows: array item 1 contains stem:[I_{yy}], array item 2 contains stem:[I_{zz}], array item 3 contains stem:[I_{yz}].

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_section_derived_definitions.torsional_constant"

the torsional stiffness of the section. A precise definition of this attribute without any warping contributions is as follows:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
\frac{\Delta \theta}{\Delta L} = \frac{T }{J \: G}
++++

where:

stem:[theta]:: is the angle of twist;

stem:[T]:: is the applied torsional moment;

stem:[L]:: is the length of the curve;

stem:[J]:: is the torsional constant whose units are stem:[("length")^{4}];

stem:[G]:: is the shear modulus of the material.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_section_derived_definitions.warping_constant"

the warping coefficient of the section. The torsional behaviour of a curve element is described by the torsional constant and the warping coefficient using the following equation:

[latexmath%unnumbered]
++++
T = G \: J \: \frac{\partial \theta}{\partial x}
             - E \: \frac{\partial^2}{\partial x^2} ( C_w \:
                                  \frac{\partial \theta}{\partial x} )
++++

where:

stem:[T]:: is the applied torsional moment;

stem:[J]:: is the torsional constant;

stem:[G]:: is the shear modulus of the material;

stem:[C_w]:: is the warping constant whose units are stem:[("length")^{6}];

stem:[E]:: is the elastic modulus of the material;

stem:[theta]:: is the angle of twist;

stem:[x]:: is distance along the stem:[x] axis of the curve element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_section_derived_definitions.location_of_centroid"

The distance of the section centroid from the parametric axis. Array item 1 specifies the distance in the direction of the property coordinate system stem:[x] axis. Array item 2 specifies the distance in the direction of the property coordinate system stem:[y] axis.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_section_derived_definitions.location_of_shear_centre"

The distance of the section shear centre from the parametric axis. Array item 1 specifies the distance in the direction of the property coordinate system stem:[x] axis. Array item 2 specifies the distance in the direction of the property coordinate system stem:[y] axis.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_section_derived_definitions.location_of_non_structural_mass"

The distance of the non-structural mass from the parametric axis. Array item 1 specifies the distance in the direction of the property coordinate system stem:[x] axis. Array item 2 specifies the distance in the direction of the property coordinate system stem:[y] axis.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_section_derived_definitions.non_structural_mass"

the non-structural mass per unit length of the curve element parametric axis.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_section_derived_definitions.polar_moment"

the polar moment of area of the curve element. This attribute is used to calculate the dynamic inertia of the curve element. It is NOT used to calculate the torsional stiffness. The polar moment is the sum of the perpendicular moments unless there are contributions from non-structural mass.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_curve_section_geometric_relationship"

An <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_curve_section_geometric_relationship,fea_curve_section_geometric_relationship>> is the association of a curve section definition to a geometric shape representation item.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_curve_section_geometric_relationship.section_ref"

the curve section definition being related to geometry.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_curve_section_geometric_relationship.item"

the geometric representation item to which the curve section definition is being related.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_curve_section_geometric_relationship.wr:WR1"

the representation item associated with the curve section definition shall be a geometric representation item.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_end_offset"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_end_offset,curve_element_end_offset>> is the offset of the end attachment of a curve element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_end_offset.coordinate_system"

the coordinate system that is used to specify the end offset.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_end_offset.offset_vector"

the distance from the node to the end position of the element with respect to the local orthogonal triad of the specified coordinate system at the node.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_end_release"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_end_release,curve_element_end_release>> are the releases of a curve element end.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_end_release.coordinate_system"

the coordinate system that is used to specify the end release.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_end_release.releases"

pairs of the degrees of freedom released between the node and the element with respect to the orthogonal triad of the specified coordinate system evaluated at the node, and the associated release stiffness.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_end_release_packet"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_end_release_packet,curve_element_end_release_packet>> is the release degree of freedom and stiffness of a curve element end. If a degree of freedom is not released then the joint stiffness is infinite.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_end_release_packet.release_freedom"

the degrees of freedom released between the node and the element with respect to the orthogonal triad of the specified coordinate system evaluated at the node. If there are no releases then the enumeration of *none* shall be used.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_element_end_release_packet.release_stiffness"

the stiffness associated with the degree of freedom. If no stiffnesses are desired, the value is set to 0.0.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.axisymmetric_2d_element_property"

An <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.axisymmetric_2d_element_property,axisymmetric_2d_element_property>> defines the properties for all types of axisymmetric 2D elements.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.axisymmetric_2d_element_property.angle"

the segment considered in an axisymmetric analysis.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.plane_2d_element_property"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.plane_2d_element_property,plane_2d_element_property>> defines the properties for all types of plane 2D elements.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.plane_2d_element_property.depth"

a depth of a plane stress or plane strain section.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.simple_plane_2d_element_property"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.simple_plane_2d_element_property,simple_plane_2d_element_property>> has no further properties.

NOTE: This entity is supplied for extensibility of the information model.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_group"

An <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_group,fea_group>> is a group that shall be either be a group of elements or nodes.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_group.model_ref"

an application definied identifier of the <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_model,fea_model>> which possesses the group.

[NOTE]
====
The group id, a unique application defined identifier of an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_group,fea_group>> is specified by the *name* attribute of the <<express:group_schema.group,group>> supertype. Similarly a description is specified by the *description* attribute of the <<express:group_schema.group,group>> supertype.

[example]
The description may be whatever label the analyst chooses for group identification, such as 'Bu 1', 'AY_0328', or 'eseridir'.
====

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_group.wr:IP1"

the combination of an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_model,fea_model>> and group id shall be unique within a finite element analysis model.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.element_group"

An <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.element_group,element_group>> is a group containing only elements.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.element_group.elements"

the elements being grouped.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.node_group"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.node_group,node_group>> is a group containing only nodes.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.node_group.nodes"

the nodes being grouped.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_group_relation"

An <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_group_relation,fea_group_relation>> is an aggregation of FEA groups.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_group_relation.wr:WR1"

the relating_group attribute shall be associated with an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_group,fea_group>>.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.fea_group_relation.wr:WR2"

the related_group attribute shall be associated with an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.fea_group,fea_group>>.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.volume_3d_element_group"

An <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.volume_3d_element_group,volume_3d_element_group>> is a group containing only volume 3D elements.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.volume_3d_element_group.wr:WR1"

there shall be only <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.volume_3d_element_representation,volume_3d_element_representation>> entities in the group.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.volume_2d_element_group"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.volume_2d_element_group,volume_2d_element_group>> is a group containing only volume 2D elements.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.volume_2d_element_group.wr:WR1"

there shall be only volume 2d element representation entities in the group.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.surface_3d_element_group"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.surface_3d_element_group,surface_3d_element_group>> is a group containing only surface 3D elements.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.surface_3d_element_group.wr:WR1"

there shall be only <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.surface_3d_element_representation,surface_3d_element_representation>> entities in the group.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.surface_2d_element_group"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.surface_2d_element_group,surface_2d_element_group>> is a group containing only surface 2D elements.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.surface_2d_element_group.wr:WR1"

there shall be only surface 2D element representation entities in the group.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_group"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_group,curve_3d_element_group>> is a group containing only curve 3D elements.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_group.wr:WR1"

there shall be only <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_3d_element_representation,curve_3d_element_representation>> entities in the group.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_2d_element_group"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_2d_element_group,curve_2d_element_group>> is a group containing only curve 2D elements.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.curve_2d_element_group.wr:WR1"

there shall be only curve 2D element representation entities in the group.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.required_0d_nodes"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.required_0d_nodes,required_0d_nodes>> verifies that the node list for a 0D (point) element contains a single node.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.required_0d_nodes.node_list"

input argument consisting of a list of one to many of the nodes in a 0D element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.required_1d_nodes"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.required_1d_nodes,required_1d_nodes>> verifies that the node list for a 1D (curve) element contains the proper number of nodes based on the order of the element. The number of nodes shall be equal to the number of end nodes, plus any additional nodes for the element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.required_1d_nodes.node_list"

input argument consisting of a list of one to many of the nodes in a 1D element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.required_1d_nodes.order"

input argument defining the geometric order of interpolation of the element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.required_2d_nodes"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.required_2d_nodes,required_2d_nodes>> verifies that the node list for a 2D element (triangle or quadrilateral) contains the proper number of nodes based on the shape and order of the element. The number of nodes shall be equal to either the sum of the vertex and edge nodes, or the sum of the vertex, edge, face, and body nodes for the element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.required_2d_nodes.node_list"

input argument consisting of a list of one to many of the nodes in a 2D element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.required_2d_nodes.element_shape"

input argument defining the geometric shape of the element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.required_2d_nodes.order"

input argument defining the geometric order of interpolation of the element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.required_3d_nodes"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.required_3d_nodes,required_3d_nodes>> verifies that the node list for a 3D (hexahedron, wedge, tetrahedron, or pyramid) element contains the proper number of nodes based on the shape and order of the element. The number of nodes shall be equal to either the sum of the vertex and edge nodes, or the sum of the vertex, edge, face, and body nodes for the element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.required_3d_nodes.node_list"

input argument consisting of a list of one to many of the nodes in a 3D element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.required_3d_nodes.element_shape"

input argument defining the geometric shape of the element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.required_3d_nodes.order"

input argument defining the geometric order of interpolation of the element.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.number_of_terms"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.number_of_terms,number_of_terms>> is used to derive the number of terms in a matrix.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.number_of_terms.node_dof_list"

input argument consisting of a list of one to many of a list of one to many of the degrees of freedom in a matrix.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.number_of_terms.matrix_symmetry"

input argument defining the type of symmetry for the matrix.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.number_of_terms.number_of_terms"

integer output argument that is set to the total number of terms in the matrix.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.valid_parametric_coordinate"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.valid_parametric_coordinate,valid_parametric_coordinate>> ensures each of the parametric coordinates lies in the range from -1.0 to +1.0.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.valid_parametric_coordinate.coordinates"

input argument consisting of the element parametric coordinates that are being checked.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.build_direction_node"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.build_direction_node,build_direction_node>> calculates the components of a direction that is defined by a vector from *node_1* to *node_2*. The components are expressed in a cartesian coordinate space whose axes are coincident with those of the cartesian, cylindrical, or spherical coordinate space defining the location of the first node in the argument list.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.build_direction_node.node_1"

identifies the first node defining the direction. This node is the origin point of the direction.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.build_direction_node.node_2"

identifies the second node defining the direction. This node is the point defining the positive sense of the direction.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.build_direction_node.nodal_direction_ratios"

output argument that contains the calculated direction.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.consistent_geometric_reference"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.consistent_geometric_reference,consistent_geometric_reference>> ensures that a given element aspect (volume, face, edge) is related to the appropriate type of geometric representation item. The element aspect <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.element_volume,element_volume>> shall be related to a solid model;
element aspects <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_3d_face,volume_3d_face>>, <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_2d_face,volume_2d_face>>,
<<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_3d_face,surface_3d_face>>, and <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_2d_face,surface_2d_face>> shall be related to either a geometric surface or a topological face surface;
and element aspects <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_3d_edge,volume_3d_edge>>, <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_2d_edge,volume_2d_edge>>,
<<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_3d_edge,surface_3d_edge>>, and <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_2d_edge,surface_2d_edge>> shall be related to either a geometric curve or a topological edge curve. The function shall return TRUE if the element aspect is paired with an appropriate geometric representation item, and return FALSE otherwise.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.consistent_geometric_reference.aspect"

identifies the element aspect.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.consistent_geometric_reference.item"

identifies the geometric representation item.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.consistent_element_or_group_reference"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.consistent_element_or_group_reference,consistent_element_or_group_reference>> ensures that a given element aspect (face, edge, volume) is consistent with the element type for a given element or set of elements. The function shall return TRUE if the element aspect is associated with the element type for a given element representation, or for all the elements in a given element group.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.consistent_element_or_group_reference.element"

identifies the element or group of elements.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.consistent_element_or_group_reference.aspect"

identifies the element aspect.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.consistent_element_reference"

A <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.consistent_element_reference,consistent_element_reference>> ensures that a given element aspect (face, edge, volume) is consistent with the element type for an <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.element_representation,element_representation>>. The element aspect <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.element_volume,element_volume>> may be associated with any element type;
element aspects <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_3d_face,volume_3d_face>> and <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_3d_edge,volume_3d_edge>> shall be associated with a volume 3D element;
element aspects <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_2d_face,volume_2d_face>> and <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.volume_2d_edge,volume_2d_edge>> shall be associated with a volume 2D element;
element aspects <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_3d_face,surface_3d_face>> and <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_3d_edge,surface_3d_edge>> shall be associated with a surface 3D element;
element aspects <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_2d_face,surface_2d_face>> and <<express:finite_element_analysis_control_and_result_schema.surface_2d_edge,surface_2d_edge>> shall be associated with a surface 2D element;
and the element aspect <<express:structural_response_representation_schema.curve_edge,curve_edge>> shall be associated with a curve 2D or 3D element. The function shall return TRUE if the element aspect is paired with an appropriate element representation, and return FALSE otherwise.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.consistent_element_reference.element"

identifies the element representation.

*)

(*"structural_response_representation_schema.consistent_element_reference.aspect"

identifies the element aspect.

*)

