(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.analysis_model"
An **analysis_model** is a type of <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> used to represent an analysis.
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.analysis_model.context_of_items"
the representation context for the analysis model.
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.analysis_model_relationship"
An **analysis_model_relationship** is a relationship that specifies that an <<express:systems_engineering_representation_schema.analysis_model,analysis_model>> is idealized by a particular <<express:systems_engineering_representation_schema.analysis_model_idealisation_item,analysis_model_idealisation_item>>.
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.analysis_model_relationship.id"
the identifier for the relationship
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.analysis_model_relationship.name"
the words by which the relationship is known
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.analysis_model_relationship.description"
the text that provides further information about the relationship
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.analysis_model_relationship.idealised"
the model that is idealised
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.analysis_model_relationship.idealisation"
the item that idealises the model
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.analysis_representation_context"
An **analysis_representation_context** is a type of <<express:representation_schema.representation_context,representation_context>> used in the definition of analysis models.
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.description_text"
A **description_text** is a set of words that describe something.
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.description_text_assignment.description"
the <<express:systems_engineering_representation_schema.description_text,description_text>> that is the description
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.description_text_assignment"
A **description_text_assignment** is the assignment of a description to something.
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.description_text.description"
the text that constitutes the description
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.description_text_assignment_relationship"
A **description_text_assignment_relationship** is a relationship between two <<express:systems_engineering_representation_schema.description_text_assignment,description_text_assignment>> objects.
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.description_text_assignment_relationship.description"
the text or the set of texts that provide further information about the **description_text_assignment_relationship**. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.description_text_assignment_relationship.id"
the identifier or set of identifiers for the **description_text_assignment_relationship**.
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.description_text_assignment_relationship.related"
the other object of <<express:systems_engineering_representation_schema.description_text_assignment,description_text_assignment>> that is part of the relationship.
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.description_text_assignment_relationship.relating"
one object of <<express:systems_engineering_representation_schema.description_text_assignment,description_text_assignment>> that is part of the relationship.
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.description_text_assignment_relationship.relation_type"
the meaning of the relationship.
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.description_text_assignment_relationship.wr:WR1"
An **description_text_assignment_relationship** shall not participate in its own definition.
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.action_method_assignment_relationship"
A **action_method_assignment_relationship** is a relationship between two <<express:management_resources_schema.action_method_assignment,action_method_assignment>>s.
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.action_method_assignment_relationship.relating_assignment"
the relating assignment
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.action_method_assignment_relationship.related_assignment"
the related assignment
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.expression_assignment"
An **expression_assignment** is an assignment of an expression to product data.
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.expression_assignment.assigned_expression"
the expression that is assigned
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.expression_assignment.role"
the role played by the assigned expression
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.expression_representation"
An **expression_representation** is a type of <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> that is an expression.
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.expression_representation.context_of_items"
the representation context for the expression representation
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.expression_representation.items"
the items that constitute the representation
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.expression_representation_context"
An **expression_representation_context** is a type of <<express:representation_schema.representation_context,representation_context>> that is the context for an expression representation.
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.expression_item_representation_item"
An **expression_item_representation_item** is a type of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> used in the definition of an expression representation.
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.expression_role"
An **expression_role** is the role an expression plays.
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.expression_role.name"
the words by which the role is known.
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.expression_role.description"
a description of the role.
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.expression_item_representation_item.item"
the item used to represent the expression representation.
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.functional_model"
A **functional_model** is a type of <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> used to represent behaviour in the form of a functional model.
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.functional_model.context_of_items"
the representation context for the functional model.
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.functional_model.items"
the items used to represent the functional model.
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.functional_representation_context"
A **functional_representation_context** is a type of <<express:representation_schema.representation_context,representation_context>> used in the definition of functional models, this will include information regarding the functional modelling paradigm.
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.functional_representation_item"
A **functional_representation_item** is a type of <<express:systems_engineering_representation_schema.representation_proxy_item,representation_proxy_item>> used in the definition of a functional model.
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.functional_representation_item.item"
the actual <<express:action_schema.action_method,action_method>> used to represent an aspect of a functional model.
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.state_based_behaviour_model"
A **state_based_behaviour_model** is a type of <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> used in the definition of state-based behaviour model.
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.state_based_behaviour_model.context_of_items"
the representation context for the state-based behaviour
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.state_based_behaviour_model.items"
the representation item for the state-based behaviour
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.state_based_behaviour_representation_context"
A **state_based_behaviour_representation_context** is a type of <<express:representation_schema.representation_context,representation_context>> used in the definition of state-based behaviour model.
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.state_based_behaviour_representation_item"
A **state_based_behaviour_representation_item** is a type of <<express:systems_engineering_representation_schema.representation_proxy_item,representation_proxy_item>> used in the definition of state-based behaviour model.
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.state_based_behaviour_representation_item.item"
the representation of the state-based behaviour
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.representation_proxy_item"
A **representation_proxy_item** is a type of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> used in the definition of representation when the actual items required are not subtypes of representation item.
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.representation_proxy_item.item"
the item used as a representation item.
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.acyclic_description_text_assignment_relationship"
The **acyclic_description_text_assignment_relationship** function determines whether the graph of instances of the entity data type <<express:systems_engineering_representation_schema.description_text_assignment,description_text_assignment>> that contains relation as one of its links contains a cycle. This function may be used to evaluate either a <<express:systems_engineering_representation_schema.description_text_assignment_relationship,description_text_assignment_relationship>> or any of its subtypes.

The function returns TRUE if no cycle has been detected. Otherwise it returns FALSE.
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.acyclic_description_text_assignment_relationship.__note"
The algorithm of the function is explained in annex E.2.
*)

(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.acyclic_description_text_assignment_relationship.relation"
(input) the candidate <<express:systems_engineering_representation_schema.description_text_assignment_relationship,description_text_assignment_relationship>> to be checked.
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.acyclic_description_text_assignment_relationship.relatives"
(input) the set of instances of the entity data type <<express:systems_engineering_representation_schema.description_text_assignment,description_text_assignment>> for which the function is searching in the <<express:systems_engineering_representation_schema.description_text_assignment_relationship.relating,relating>> parameter of the relation argument.
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.acyclic_description_text_assignment_relationship.specific_relation"
(input) the fully qualified name of a subtype of the <<express:systems_engineering_representation_schema.description_text_assignment_relationship,description_text_assignment_relationship>> entity.
*)


(*"systems_engineering_representation_schema.__schema_file"
data/resource_docs/systems_engineering_representation/resource.xml
*)


