(*"topology_schema.dummy_tri"
A **dummy_tri** is a constant that is a partial entity definition to be used when types of <<express:topology_schema.topological_representation_item,topological_representation_item>> are constructed. It provides the correct supertypes and the <<express:representation_schema.representation_item.name,name>> attribute as an empty string.
*)


(*"topology_schema.shell"
The **shell** type collects together, for reference when constructing more complex models, the subtypes which have the characteristics of a shell.

A **shell** is a connected object of fixed dimensionality stem:[d = 0], 1, or 2, typically used to bound a region. The domain of a shell, if present, includes its bounds and stem:[0 le Xi < infty]

A shell of dimensionality 0 is represented by a graph consisting of a single vertex. The vertex shall not have any associated edges.

A shell of dimensionality 1 is represented by a connected graph of dimensionality 1.

A shell of dimensionality 2 is a topological entity constructed by joining faces along edges. Its domain, if present, is a connected, orientable 2-manifold with boundary, that is, a connected, oriented, finite, non-self-intersecting surface, which may be closed or open.
*)


(*"topology_schema.reversible_topology_item"
The **reversible_topology_item** select type specifies all the topological representation items which can participate in the operation of reversing their orientation. This type is used by the function <<express:topology_schema.conditional_reverse,conditional_reverse>>.
*)


(*"topology_schema.list_of_reversible_topology_item"
The **list_of_reversible_topology_item** type defines a list of reversible topology items; it is used by the function <<express:topology_schema.list_of_topology_reversed,list_of_topology_reversed>>
*)


(*"topology_schema.set_of_reversible_topology_item"
The **set_of_reversible_topology_item** type defines a set of reversible topology items; it is used by the function <<express:topology_schema.set_of_topology_reversed,set_of_topology_reversed>>.
*)


(*"topology_schema.reversible_topology"
The **reversible_topology** identifies all types of reversible topology items; it is used by the function <<express:topology_schema.topology_reversed,topology_reversed>>.
*)


(*"topology_schema.topological_representation_item"
A **topological_representation_item** is a type of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> that represents the topology, or connectivity, of entities which make up the representation of an object. The **topological_representation_item** is the supertype for all the representation items in the topology schema.
*)


(*"topology_schema.topological_representation_item.__note"
As subtypes of <<express:representation_schema.representation_item,representation_item>> there is an implicit and/or relationship between <<express:geometry_schema.geometric_representation_item,geometric_representation_item>> and *topological_representation_item*. The only complex instances intended to be created are <<express:topology_schema.edge_curve,edge_curve>>, <<express:topology_schema.face_surface,face_surface>>, and <<express:topology_schema.vertex_point,vertex_point>>.
*)

(*"topology_schema.topological_representation_item.__note"
The definition of *topological_representation_item* defines an and/or relationship between <<express:topology_schema.loop,loop>> and <<express:topology_schema.path,path>>. The only valid complex instance is the <<express:topology_schema.edge_loop,edge_loop>> entity.
*)

(*"topology_schema.topological_representation_item.permanent_id"
an identifier that distinguishes the **topological_representation_item**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.topological_representation_item.permanent_id.__note"
This attribute is an enhancement to the definition of *topological_representation_item* using a method that is upwardly compatible with ISO 10303-42.
*)

(*"topology_schema.topological_representation_item.permanent_id.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"topology_schema.topological_representation_item.permanent_id.__note"
The context in which <<express:topology_schema.topological_representation_item.permanent_id,permanent_id>> is used as a discriminating characteristic can be identified in an annotated Express schema that uses or specializes this entity, or by default, in an agreement of common understanding between partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"topology_schema.topological_representation_item.permanent_aggregate_id"
an identifier that distinguishes the **topological_representation_item**. A **permanent_aggregate_id** supports the assignment of more than one instance of **topological_representation_item** to the same identifier.
*)


(*"topology_schema.topological_representation_item.permanent_aggregate_id.__note"
This attribute is an enhancement to the definition of *topological_representation_item* using a method that is upwardly compatible with ISO 10303-42.
*)

(*"topology_schema.topological_representation_item.permanent_aggregate_id.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"topology_schema.topological_representation_item.permanent_aggregate_id.__note"
The context in which <<express:topology_schema.topological_representation_item.permanent_aggregate_id,permanent_aggregate_id>> is used as a discriminating characteristic can be identified in an annotated Express schema that uses or specializes this entity, or by default, in an agreement of common understanding between partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"topology_schema.topological_representation_item.wr:WR1"
Each **topological_representation_item** shall be the identified_item in at most one id_attribute.
*)


(*"topology_schema.topological_representation_item.wr:WR1.__note"
The <<express:basic_attribute_schema.id_attribute,id_attribute>> data type is defined in <<express:basic_attribute_schema,basic_attribute_schema>> of ISO 10303-42.
*)

(*"topology_schema.topological_representation_item.wr:WR1.__note"
A template for constraining the population of the entity data types defined in the <<express:basic_attribute_schema,basic_attribute_schema>> is described in annex E of ISO 10303-41.
*)

(*"topology_schema.topological_representation_item.wr:WR2"
Each **topological_representation_item** shall be the identified_item in at most one aggregate_id_attribute.
*)


(*"topology_schema.topological_representation_item.wr:WR2.__note"
The <<express:basic_attribute_schema.aggregate_id_attribute,aggregate_id_attribute>> data type is defined in <<express:basic_attribute_schema,basic_attribute_schema>> of ISO 10303-42.
*)

(*"topology_schema.topological_representation_item.wr:IP1"
For each **topological_representation_item**, consider the set of <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> instances, <<express:topology_schema.edge_curve,edge_curve>>, and <<express:topology_schema.face_surface,face_surface>> instances that are referenced, either directly or recursively, from that **topological_representation_item**. (Do not include in this set oriented edges or faces, but do include the non-oriented edges and faces on which they are based.) Then no two distinct elements in this set shall have domains that intersect.
*)


(*"topology_schema.vertex"
A **vertex** is a type of <<express:topology_schema.topological_representation_item,topological_representation_item>>, and is the topological construct corresponding to a point. It has dimensionality 0 and extent 0. The domain of a vertex, if present, is a point in stem:[m] dimensional real space stem:[RR^m]; this is represented by the <<express:topology_schema.vertex_point,vertex_point>> subtype.
*)


(*"topology_schema.vertex.wr:IP1"
The **vertex** has dimensionality 0. This is a fundamental property of the vertex.
*)


(*"topology_schema.vertex.wr:IP2"
The extent of a **vertex** is defined to be zero.
*)


(*"topology_schema.vertex_point"
A **vertex_point** is a type of <<express:topology_schema.vertex,vertex>>, which has its geometry defined as a point.
*)


(*"topology_schema.vertex_point.vertex_geometry"
the geometric point which defines the position in geometric space of the vertex;
*)


(*"topology_schema.vertex_point.wr:IP1"
The domain of the vertex is formally defined to be the domain of its **vertex_geometry**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.edge"
An **edge** is a type of <<express:topology_schema.topological_representation_item,topological_representation_item>>, corresponding to the connection between two vertices. More abstractly, it may stand for a logical relationship between the two vertices. The domain of an edge, if present, is a finite, non-self-intersecting open curve in stem:[RR^m], that is, a connected 1-dimensional manifold. The bounds of an **edge** are two vertices, which need not be distinct. The edge is oriented by choosing its traversal direction to run from the first to the second vertex. If the two vertices are the same, the edge is a self-loop. The domain of the edge does not include its bounds, and stem:[0 < Xi < infty].

Associated with an edge may be a geometric <<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> to locate the edge in a coordinate space; this is represented by the **edge_curve** subtype. The curve shall be finite and non-self-intersecting within the domain of the edge. An **edge** is a graph, so its multiplicity M and graph genus stem:[G^e] may be determined by the graph traversal algorithm. Since stem:[M = bb E = 1], the Euler equation reduces in this case to

[[eqn2]]

[stem]
++++
V - (2 - G^{e}) = 0
++++

where stem:[V = 1] or 2, and stem:[G^e = 1] or 0.

Specifically, the topological edge defining data shall satisfy:

* An edge has two vertices, stem:[|E[V]| = 2 ]
* The vertices need not be distinct, stem:[1 le |E{V}| le 2]
* Equation <<eqn2>> shall hold stem:[|E{V}| - 2 + G^e = 0]
*)


(*"topology_schema.edge.edge_start"
start point (<<express:topology_schema.vertex,vertex>>) of the **edge**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.edge.edge_end"
end point (<<express:topology_schema.vertex,vertex>>) of the **edge**. The same <<express:topology_schema.vertex,vertex>> can be used for both **edge_start** and **edge_end**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.edge.wr:IP1"
The **edge** has dimensionality 1.
*)


(*"topology_schema.edge.wr:IP2"
The extent of an **edge** shall be finite and nonzero.
*)


(*"topology_schema.edge_curve"
An **edge_curve** is a type of <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>>, which has its geometry fully defined. The geometry is defined by associating the edge with a <<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> which may be unbounded. As the topological and geometric directions may be opposed, an indicator ({blank} **same_sense** {blank}) is used to identify whether the edge and curve directions agree or are opposed. The Boolean value indicates whether the <<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> direction agrees with (TRUE) or is in the opposite direction (FALSE) to the <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> direction. Any geometry associated with the vertices of the edge shall be consistent with the edge geometry. Multiple edges can reference the same curve.
*)

(*"topology_schema.edge_curve.__figure"
[[figure-topology_schema-Topfig23]]
.Edge_curve
====
image::Topfig23.gif[]
====
*)

(*"topology_schema.edge_curve.edge_geometry"
the <<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> which defines the shape and spatial location of the edge. This curve may be unbounded and is implicitly trimmed by the vertices of the edge; this defines the edge domain.
*)


(*"topology_schema.edge_curve.same_sense"
a logical flag which indicates whether (TRUE), or not (FALSE) the senses of the <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> and the <<express:geometry_schema.curve,curve>> defining the edge geometry are the same. The sense of an edge is from the edge start vertex to the edge end vertex; the sense of a curve is in the direction of increasing parameter.
*)


(*"topology_schema.edge_curve.same_sense.__note"
See <<figure-topology_schema-Topfig23>> for illustration of attributes.
*)

(*"topology_schema.edge_curve.wr:IP1"
The domain of the **edge_curve** is formally defined to be the domain of its **edge_geometry** as trimmed by the vertices. This domain does not include the vertices.
*)


(*"topology_schema.edge_curve.wr:IP2"
The extent of an **edge_curve** shall be finite and nonzero.
*)


(*"topology_schema.edge_curve.wr:IP3"
An **edge_curve** is a manifold.
*)


(*"topology_schema.edge_curve.wr:IP4"
An **edge_curve** is arcwise connected.
*)


(*"topology_schema.edge_curve.wr:IP5"
The edge start is not part of the edge domain.
*)


(*"topology_schema.edge_curve.wr:IP6"
The edge end is not part of the edge domain.
*)


(*"topology_schema.edge_curve.wr:IP7"
Vertex geometry shall be consistent with edge geometry.
*)


(*"topology_schema.oriented_edge"
An **oriented_edge** is a type of <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>>, constructed from another <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> and contains a BOOLEAN orientation flag to indicate whether or not the orientation of the constructed <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> agrees with the orientation of the original <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>>. Except for possible re-orientation, the **oriented_edge** is equivalent to the original <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>>.
*)


(*"topology_schema.oriented_edge.__note"
A common practice in solid modelling systems is to have an entity that represents the " use" or " traversal " of an <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>>. This "use" entity explicitly represents the requirement in a manifold solid that each edge must be traversed exactly twice, once in each direction. The "use" functionality is provided by the <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> subtype *oriented_edge*.
*)

(*"topology_schema.oriented_edge.edge_element"
an <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> entity used to construct this **oriented_edge** ;
*)


(*"topology_schema.oriented_edge.orientation"
a BOOLEAN, if TRUE, the topological orientation as used coincides with the orientation, from start vertex to end vertex, of the **edge_element**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.oriented_edge.edge_start"
the start vertex of the oriented edge, this is derived from the vertices of the **edge_element** after taking account of the **orientation**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.oriented_edge.edge_end"
the end vertex of the oriented edge, this is derived from the vertices of the **edge_element** after taking account of the **orientation**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.oriented_edge.wr:WR1"
The **edge_element** shall not be an **oriented_edge**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.seam_edge"
A **seam_edge** is a type of <<express:topology_schema.oriented_edge,oriented_edge>>, which, additionally, identifies a corresponding <<express:geometry_schema.pcurve,pcurve>>. A **seam_edge** is always related to an <<express:topology_schema.edge_curve,edge_curve>> having a <<express:geometry_schema.seam_curve,seam_curve>> as <<express:topology_schema.edge_curve.edge_geometry,edge_geometry>>. The <<express:topology_schema.seam_edge,seam_edge>> identifies which, of the two <<express:geometry_schema.pcurve,pcurve>> instances defining the <<express:geometry_schema.seam_curve,seam_curve>>, is appropriate for this <<express:topology_schema.oriented_edge,oriented_edge>>.
*)


(*"topology_schema.seam_edge.__note"
The inherited <<express:topology_schema.oriented_edge.orientation,orientation>> attribute refers to the relationship to the <<express:topology_schema.oriented_edge.edge_element,edge_element>> and not to the sense of the <<express:geometry_schema.pcurve,pcurve>>.
*)

(*"topology_schema.seam_edge.pcurve_reference"
the <<express:geometry_schema.pcurve,pcurve>> associated with the current orientation of the <<express:topology_schema.oriented_edge.edge_element,edge_element>>;
*)


(*"topology_schema.seam_edge.wr:WR1"
the <<express:topology_schema.oriented_edge.edge_element,edge_element>> attribute of this type of oriented edge shall be a <<express:geometry_schema.seam_curve,seam_curve>>.
*)


(*"topology_schema.seam_edge.wr:WR2"
The **pcurve_reference** shall be one of the <<express:geometry_schema.pcurve,pcurve>> instances in the <<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve.associated_geometry,associated_geometry>> list of the <<express:topology_schema.oriented_edge.edge_element,edge_element>>.
*)


(*"topology_schema.subedge"
A **subedge** is a type of <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>>, whose domain is a connected portion of the domain of an existing <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>>. The topological constraints on a **subedge** are the same as those on an <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>>.
*)


(*"topology_schema.subedge.parent_edge"
the <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>>, or **subedge**, which contains the **subedge**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.subedge.wr:IP1"
The domain of the **subedge** is formally defined to be the domain of the **parent_edge**, as trimmed by the **subedge.edge_start** and **subedge.edge_end**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.subedge.wr:IP2"
The <<express:topology_schema.edge.edge_start,edge_start>> and <<express:topology_schema.edge.edge_end,edge_end>> shall be within the union of the domains of the vertices of the **parent_edge** and the domain of the **parent_edge**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.subedge.wr:WR1"
An instance of **subedge** shall not also be the instance of <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> in the role of **parent_edge**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.path"
A **path** is a type of <<express:topology_schema.topological_representation_item,topological_representation_item>>, consisting of an ordered collection of <<express:topology_schema.oriented_edge,oriented_edge>> instances, such that the <<express:topology_schema.edge.edge_start,edge_start>> vertex of each edge coincides with the <<express:topology_schema.edge.edge_end,edge_end>> of its predecessor. The path is ordered from the <<express:topology_schema.edge.edge_start,edge_start>> of its first <<express:topology_schema.oriented_edge,oriented_edge>> to the <<express:topology_schema.edge.edge_end,edge_end>> of its last <<express:topology_schema.oriented_edge,oriented_edge>>.

The BOOLEAN value <<express:topology_schema.oriented_edge.orientation,orientation>> in the <<express:topology_schema.oriented_edge,oriented_edge>> indicates whether the edge direction agrees with the direction of the path (TRUE) or is in the opposite direction (FALSE).

An individual <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> can only be referenced once by an individual **path**.

An <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> can be referenced by multiple **path** instances. An <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> can exist independently of a **path**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.path.edge_list"
the list of <<express:topology_schema.oriented_edge,oriented_edge>> entities which are concatenated together to form this **path**.;
*)


(*"topology_schema.path.wr:WR1"
The end vertex of each <<express:topology_schema.oriented_edge,oriented_edge>> shall be the same as the start vertex of its successor.
*)


(*"topology_schema.path.wr:IP1"
A **path** has dimensionality 1.
*)


(*"topology_schema.path.wr:IP2"
A **path** is arcwise connected.
*)


(*"topology_schema.path.wr:IP3"
The edges of the path do not intersect except at common vertices.
*)


(*"topology_schema.path.wr:IP4"
A path has a finite, non-zero extent.
*)


(*"topology_schema.path.wr:IP5"
No **path** shall include two oriented edges with the same edge element and the same orientation.
*)


(*"topology_schema.subpath"
A **subpath** is a type of <<express:topology_schema.path,path>>, whose domain is a connected portion of the domain of an existing <<express:topology_schema.path,path>>. An instance of **subpath** may contain a combination of <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> and <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> such that the resulting domain of <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> and <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>>, together with their bounding vertices, is an arcwise connected, non-intersecting (except at common vertices), and 1-dimensional subdomain of the domain defined by the **parent_path**. The topological constraints on a **subpath** are the same as on a <<express:topology_schema.path,path>>.
*)


(*"topology_schema.subpath.parent_path"
the <<express:topology_schema.path,path>>, which contains the **subpath**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.subpath.wr:WR1"
An instance of **subpath** shall not also be the instance of <<express:topology_schema.path,path>> in the role of **parent_path**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.subpath.wr:WR2"
An instance of **subpath** that is an <<express:topology_schema.edge_loop,edge_loop>> shall not reference an instance of <<express:topology_schema.open_path,open_path>> in the role of **parent_path**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.subpath.wr:IP1"
The domain of the **subpath** shall be within the domain of the **parent_path**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.subpath.wr:IP2"
If the **subpath** is an <<express:topology_schema.edge_loop,edge_loop>>, the domain of the **subpath** shall be the same as the **parent_path**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.subpath.wr:IP2.__note"
The domain of the *subpath* that is an <<express:topology_schema.edge_loop,edge_loop>> is not a proper subset of the domain of the *parent_path* when that *parent_path* is also an edge_loop.
*)

(*"topology_schema.subpath.wr:IP3"
If the **subpath** is an <<express:topology_schema.edge_loop,edge_loop>> and the **parent_path** is an <<express:topology_schema.oriented_path,oriented_path>>, the <<express:topology_schema.oriented_path,oriented_path>> shall be closed to form a loop.
*)


(*"topology_schema.subpath.wr:IP3.__note"
The orientation of the *subpath* and *parent_path* loops can be different if the *subpath* is an <<express:topology_schema.edge_loop,edge_loop>> and the *parent_path* is an <<express:topology_schema.oriented_path,oriented_path>>.
*)

(*"topology_schema.oriented_path"
An **oriented_path** is a type of <<express:topology_schema.path,path>>, constructed from another <<express:topology_schema.path,path>> and contains a BOOLEAN orientation flag to indicate whether or not the orientation of the constructed <<express:topology_schema.path,path>> agrees with the orientation of the original <<express:topology_schema.path,path>>. Except for perhaps orientation, the **oriented_path** is equivalent to the other <<express:topology_schema.path,path>>.
*)


(*"topology_schema.oriented_path.path_element"
the <<express:topology_schema.path,path>> entity used to construct this **oriented_path** ;
*)


(*"topology_schema.oriented_path.orientation"
a BOOLEAN, if TRUE, the topological orientation as used coincides with the orientation of the **path_element** ;
*)


(*"topology_schema.oriented_path.edge_list"
the list of <<express:topology_schema.oriented_edge,oriented_edge>>s which form the **oriented_path** ; this list is derived from the **path_element** after taking account of the **orientation** attribute;
*)


(*"topology_schema.oriented_path.wr:WR1"
The **path_element** shall not be an **oriented_path**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.open_path"
An **open_path** is a type of <<express:topology_schema.path,path>>, such that a traversal of the path visits each of its vertices exactly once. In particular, the start vertex and end vertex are different. An **open_path** is a graph for which stem:[M = 1] and stem:[bb G^p = 0], so the Euler equation link:6_schema.xml#eqnGM1 reduces in this case to

[[eqn3]]

[stem]
++++
(V - E) - 1 = 0
++++

where stem:[bb V] and stem:[bb E] are the number of unique vertices and edges in the path. Specifically, the topological attributes of a <<express:topology_schema.path,path>> shall meet the following constraints:

* The edges in the Path are unique,
[stem]
++++
(P)[E] = (P){E}
++++

* In the list ((P)[E])[V], two vertices appear once only and every other vertex appears exactly twice.
* The graph genus of the path is zero.
* Equation <<eqn3>> is interpreted as
[stem]
++++
|((P)[E]){V}| - |(P){E}| - 1 = 0
++++
*)


(*"topology_schema.open_path.ne"
the number of elements in the edge list of the path supertype;
*)


(*"topology_schema.open_path.wr:WR1"
The start vertex of the first edge shall not coincide with the end vertex of the last edge.
*)


(*"topology_schema.open_path.wr:IP1"
An **open_path** visits its <<express:topology_schema.vertex,vertex>>s exactly once. This implies that if a list of vertices is constructed from the edge data the first and last vertex will occur once in this list and all other vertices will occur twice.
*)


(*"topology_schema.loop"
A **loop** is a type of <<express:topology_schema.topological_representation_item,topological_representation_item>>, constructed from a single vertex, or by stringing together connected (oriented) edges, or linear segments beginning and ending at the same vertex. A loop has dimensionality 0 or 1. The domain of a 0-dimensional loop is a single point. The domain of a 1-dimensional loop is a connected, oriented curve, but need not be a manifold. As the loop is a cycle, the location of its beginning/ending point is arbitrary. The domain of the loop includes its bounds, and stem:[0 le Xi < infty]

A loop is represented by a single vertex, or by an ordered collection of <<express:topology_schema.oriented_edge,oriented_edge>> instances, or by an ordered collection of points.

A loop is a graph, so M and the graph genus stem:[G^l] may be determined by the graph traversal algorithm. Since M = 1, the Euler equation reduces in this case to

[[eqn4]]

[stem]
++++
(V - E_{l}) - (1 - G^{l}) = 0
++++

where stem:[bb V] and stem:[bb E] are the number of unique vertices and oriented edges in the loop and stem:[G^l] is the genus of the loop.
*)


(*"topology_schema.loop.wr:IP1"
A **loop** has a finite, or, in the case of the <<express:topology_schema.vertex_loop,vertex_loop>>, zero extent.
*)


(*"topology_schema.loop.wr:IP2"
A **loop** describes a closed (topological) curve with coincident start and end vertices.
*)


(*"topology_schema.vertex_loop"
A **vertex_loop** is a type of <<express:topology_schema.loop,loop>>, of zero genus consisting of a single <<express:topology_schema.vertex,vertex>>. A <<express:topology_schema.vertex,vertex>> can exist independently of a **vertex_loop**. The topological data shall satisfy the following constraint:

Euler equation <<eqn4>> shall be satisfied:

[stem]
++++
|(L){V}| - 1 = 0
++++
*)


(*"topology_schema.vertex_loop.loop_vertex"
the <<express:topology_schema.vertex,vertex>> which defines the entire <<express:topology_schema.loop,loop>>;
*)


(*"topology_schema.vertex_loop.wr:IP1"
A **vertex_loop** has zero extent and dimensionality.
*)


(*"topology_schema.vertex_loop.wr:IP2"
The **vertex_loop** has genus 0.
*)


(*"topology_schema.edge_loop"
An **edge_loop** is a type of <<express:topology_schema.loop,loop>>, with nonzero extent. It is a <<express:topology_schema.path,path>> in which the start and end vertices are the same. Its domain, if present, is a closed curve. An **edge_loop** may overlap itself.
*)


(*"topology_schema.edge_loop.ne"
the number of elements in the edge list of the <<express:topology_schema.loop,loop>> supertype.
*)


(*"topology_schema.edge_loop.wr:WR1"
The start vertex of the first edge shall be the same as the end vertex of the last edge; this ensures that the path is closed to form a loop.
*)


(*"topology_schema.edge_loop.wr:IP1"
The Euler formula shall be satisfied: (number of vertices) + genus - (number of edges) = 1.
*)


(*"topology_schema.edge_loop.wr:IP2"
No <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> may be referenced more than once by the same **edge_loop** with the same <<express:topology_schema.oriented_edge.orientation,orientation>>.
*)


(*"topology_schema.poly_loop"
A **poly_loop** is a type of <<express:topology_schema.loop,loop>>, with straight edges bounding a planar region in space. A **poly_loop** is a <<express:topology_schema.loop,loop>> of genus 1 where the <<express:topology_schema.loop,loop>> is represented by an ordered coplanar collection of <<express:geometry_schema.point,point>>s forming the vertices of the loop. The loop is composed of straight-line segments joining a point in the collection to the succeeding point in the collection. The closing segment is from the last to the first point in the collection. The direction of the loop is in the direction of the line segments. Unlike the <<express:topology_schema.loop,loop>> entity, the edges of the **poly_loop** are implicitly defined by the **polygon** points.

A **poly_loop** shall conform to the following topological constraints:

* The loop has a genus of one.
* Euler equation <<eqn4>> shall be satisfied:
[stem]
++++
|(L){V}| - |(L){E_{l}}| = 0
++++
*)


(*"topology_schema.poly_loop.__note"
This entity exists primarily to facilitate the efficient communication of faceted boundary representation models.
*)

(*"topology_schema.poly_loop.__note"
The *poly_loop* has vertices and <<express:topology_schema.oriented_edge,oriented_edge>>s which are implicitly created. If, for example, A and B are consecutive points in the *polygon* list, there is an implicit <<express:topology_schema.oriented_edge,oriented_edge>> from vertex point A to vertex point B with orientation value TRUE. It is assumed that when the higher-level entities such as shell and B-rep require checks on edge usage that this check will recognise, for example, a straight oriented edge from point B to point A with orientation TRUE as equal to an oriented edge from A to B with orientation FALSE.
*)

(*"topology_schema.poly_loop.polygon"
a list of <<express:geometry_schema.point,point>>s defining the loop; there are no repeated <<express:geometry_schema.point,point>>s in the list;
*)


(*"topology_schema.poly_loop.wr:IP1"
All the points in the **polygon** defining the **poly_loop** shall be coplanar.
*)


(*"topology_schema.poly_loop.wr:IP2"
The implicit edges of the **poly_loop** shall not intersect each other. The implicit edges are the straight lines joining consecutive <<express:geometry_schema.point,point>>s in the **polygon**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.face_bound"
A **face_bound** is a type of <<express:topology_schema.topological_representation_item,topological_representation_item>>, and is a loop which is intended to be used for bounding a face.
*)


(*"topology_schema.face_bound.bound"
the <<express:topology_schema.loop,loop>> which will be used as a face boundary;
*)


(*"topology_schema.face_bound.orientation"
indicates whether (TRUE), or not (FALSE) the loop has the same sense when used to bound the face as when first defined; if **orientation** is FALSE, the senses of all its component oriented edges are implicitly reversed when used in the face;
*)


(*"topology_schema.face_outer_bound"
A **face_outer_bound** is a type of <<express:topology_schema.face_bound,face_bound>>, which carries the additional semantics of defining an outer boundary on the face. A **face_outer_bound** shall separate the interior of the <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> from the exterior and shall enclose the interior domain of the <<express:topology_schema.face,face>>.

No more than one boundary of a <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> shall be of this type.
*)

(*"topology_schema.face_outer_bound.__example"
Any <<express:topology_schema.edge_loop,edge_loop>> on a plane surface may be used to define a *face_outer_bound* provided it is not enclosed in any other loop in the <<express:topology_schema.face,face>>.
*)
(*"topology_schema.face_outer_bound.__example"
A circular loop on a cylindrical surface cannot define a *face_outer_bound* since it does not enclose a closed domain in the surface.
*)

(*"topology_schema.face"
A **face** is a type of <<express:topology_schema.topological_representation_item,topological_representation_item>>, of dimensionality 2 corresponding to the intuitive notion of a piece of surface bounded by loops. Its domain, if present, is an oriented, connected, finite 2-manifold in stem:[RR^m]. A face domain shall not have handles, but it may have holes, each hole bounded by a loop. The domain of the underlying geometry of the face, if present, does not contain its bounds, and stem:[0 < Xi < infty]. A face is represented by its bounding loops, which are defined as <<express:topology_schema.face_bound,face_bound>> instances. A face shall have at least one bound, and the bounds shall be distinct and shall not intersect. One <<express:topology_schema.loop,loop>> is optionally distinguished, using the <<express:topology_schema.face_outer_bound,face_outer_bound>> subtype, as the "outer" loop of the face. If so, it establishes a preferred way of embedding the face domain in the plane, in which the other bounding loops of the face are "inside" the outer loop. Because the face domain is arcwise connected, no inner loop shall contain any other loop. This is true regardless of which embedding in the plane is chosen.

A geometric <<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> may be associated with the face. This may be done explicitly through the <<express:topology_schema.face_surface,face_surface>> subtype, or implicitly if the faces are defined by <<express:topology_schema.poly_loop,poly_loop>> instances. In the latter case, the surface is the plane containing the points of the <<express:topology_schema.poly_loop,poly_loop>> instances. In either case, a topological normal **n** is associated with the face, such that the cross product stem:[n xx t] points toward the interior of the face, where **t** is the tangent to a bounding loop. That is, each loop runs counter-clockwise around the face when viewed from above, if we consider the normal **n** to point up. Each loop is associated through a **face_bound** entity with a BOOLEAN flag to signify whether the loop direction is oriented correctly with respect to the face normal (TRUE) or should be reversed (FALSE). For a face of the subtype <<express:topology_schema.face_surface,face_surface>>, the topological normal **n** is defined from the normal of the underlying surface, together with the BOOLEAN attribute <<express:topology_schema.face_surface.same_sense,same_sense>>, and this in turn, determines on which side of the loop the face interior lies, using the cross-product rule described above.

When a <<express:topology_schema.vertex_loop,vertex_loop>> is used as a <<express:topology_schema.face_bound,face_bound>> the sense of the topological normal is derived from any other bounding loops, or, in the case of a <<express:topology_schema.face_surface,face_surface>>, from the <<express:topology_schema.face_surface.face_geometry,face_geometry>> and the <<express:topology_schema.face_surface.same_sense,same_sense>> flag. If the **face** has only one bound and this is of type <<express:topology_schema.vertex_loop,vertex_loop>>, then the interior of the **face** is the domain of the <<express:topology_schema.face_surface.face_geometry,face_geometry>>. In such a case the underlying surface shall be closed (such as a spherical surface.)

The situation is different for a face on an implicit planar surface, such as one defined by <<express:topology_schema.poly_loop,poly_loop>> instances, which has no unique surface normal. Since the face and its bounding loops lie in a plane, the outer loop can always be found without ambiguity. Since the face is required to be finite, the face interior must lie inside the outer loop, and outside each of the remaining loops. These conditions, together with the specified loop orientations, define the topological normal **n** using the cross-product rule described above. All <<express:topology_schema.poly_loop,poly_loop>> orientations for a given face shall produce the same value for **n**.

The edges and vertices referenced by the loops of a face form a graph, of which the individual loops are the connected components. The Euler equation for this graph becomes:

[[eqn5]]

[stem]
++++
(V - E) - (L - Sigma^{L}_{i=1} (G_{i}^{l})) = 0
++++

where stem:[G_i^l] is the graph genus of the stem:[i"th"] loop.

More specifically, the following topological constraints shall be met:

* The loops are unique (F){L} = (F)[L]
* In the list ((F)[L])[E] an individual edge occurs no more than twice.
* Each <<express:topology_schema.oriented_edge,oriented_edge>> shall be unique
[stem]
++++
((F)[L])\{E_{l}} = ((F)[L])[E_{l}]
++++

* Equation <<eqn5>> shall be satisfied
[stem]
++++
|(((F)[L^{e}]){E}){V}| + |((F)[L^{v}]){V}| - |((F)[L]){E}| - |(F)[L]| + Sigma G^{l} = 0
++++
*)


(*"topology_schema.face.bounds"
boundaries of the **face** ; no more than one of these shall be a <<express:topology_schema.face_outer_bound,face_outer_bound>>;
*)


(*"topology_schema.face.bounds.__note"
For some types of closed or partially closed surfaces, it may not be possible to identify a unique outer bound.
*)

(*"topology_schema.face.wr:WR1"
If any loop of the face is a poly loop, all loops of the face shall be poly loops.
*)


(*"topology_schema.face.wr:WR2"
At most, one of the **bounds** shall be of type <<express:topology_schema.face_outer_bound,face_outer_bound>>.
*)


(*"topology_schema.face.wr:IP1"
No edge shall be referenced by the face more than twice, or, more than once in the same direction.
*)


(*"topology_schema.face.wr:IP2"
Distinct **face_bound** s of the **face** shall have no common vertices.
*)


(*"topology_schema.face.wr:IP3"
If geometry is present, distinct loops of the same face shall not intersect.
*)


(*"topology_schema.face.wr:IP4"
The face shall satisfy the Euler equation (see equation <<eqn5>>):

(number of vertices) - (number of edges) - (number of loops) + (sum of genus for loops) = 0.
*)


(*"topology_schema.face.wr:IP5"
Each <<express:topology_schema.loop,loop>> referred to in **bounds** shall be unique.
*)


(*"topology_schema.face_surface"
A **face_surface** is a type of <<express:topology_schema.face,face>>, in which the geometry is defined by an associated <<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>>. The portion of the surface used by the face shall be embeddable in the plane as an open disk, possibly with holes. However, the union of the face with the edges and vertices of its bounding loops need not be embeddable in the plane. It may, for example, cover an entire sphere or torus. As both a face and a geometric surface have defined normal directions, a BOOLEAN flag (the orientation attribute) is used to indicate whether the surface normal agrees with (TRUE) or is opposed to (FALSE) the face normal direction. The geometry associated with any component of the loops of the face shall be consistent with the surface geometry, in the sense that the domains of all the vertex points and edge curves are contained in the face geometry surface. A <<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> may be referenced by more than one **face_surface**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.face_surface.face_geometry"
the surface which defines the internal shape of the face; this surface may be unbounded; the domain of the face is defined by this surface and the bounding loops in the inherited attribute <<express:topology_schema.face.bounds,bounds>>;
*)


(*"topology_schema.face_surface.same_sense"
flag indicates whether the sense of the surface normal agrees with (TRUE), or opposes (FALSE), the sense of the topological normal to the <<express:topology_schema.face,face>>;
*)


(*"topology_schema.face_surface.wr:WR1"
An <<express:geometry_schema.oriented_surface,oriented_surface>> shall not be used to define the **face_geometry**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.face_surface.wr:IP1"
The domain of the **face_surface** is formally defined to be the domain of its **face_geometry** as trimmed by the loops, this domain does not include the bounding loops.
*)


(*"topology_schema.face_surface.wr:IP2"
A **face_surface** has nonzero finite extent.
*)


(*"topology_schema.face_surface.wr:IP3"
A **face_surface** is a manifold.
*)


(*"topology_schema.face_surface.wr:IP4"
A **face_surface** is arcwise connected.
*)


(*"topology_schema.face_surface.wr:IP5"
A **face_surface** has surface genus 0.
*)


(*"topology_schema.face_surface.wr:IP6"
The loops are not part of the face domain.
*)


(*"topology_schema.face_surface.wr:IP7"
Loop geometry shall be consistent with face geometry. This implies that any <<express:topology_schema.edge_curve,edge_curve>> instances or <<express:topology_schema.vertex_point,vertex_point>> instances used in defining the loops bounding the **face_surface** shall lie on the **face_geometry**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.face_surface.wr:IP8"
The loops of the face shall not intersect.
*)


(*"topology_schema.oriented_face"
An **oriented_face** is a type of <<express:topology_schema.face,face>>, which contains an additional orientation BOOLEAN flag to indicate whether, or not, the sense of the oriented face agrees with its sense as originally defined in the face element.
*)


(*"topology_schema.oriented_face.face_element"
a <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> entity used to construct this **oriented_face**.;
*)


(*"topology_schema.oriented_face.orientation"
the relationship of the topological orientation of this entity to that of the **face_element** ; if TRUE, the topological orientation as used coincides with the orientation of the **face_element** ;
*)


(*"topology_schema.oriented_face.bounds"
the bounds of the **oriented_face** are derived from those of the **face_element** after taking account of the orientation which may reverse the direction of these bounds;
*)


(*"topology_schema.oriented_face.wr:WR1"
The **face_element** shall not be an **oriented_face**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.subface"
A **subface** is a type of <<express:topology_schema.face,face>>, which is a portion of the domain of a <<express:topology_schema.face,face>>, or another **subface**. The topological constraints on a **subface** are the same as on a <<express:topology_schema.face,face>>.
*)


(*"topology_schema.subface.parent_face"
the <<express:topology_schema.face,face>>, (or **subface** {blank}) which contains the **subface** being defined by <<express:topology_schema.face.bounds,bounds>>.
*)


(*"topology_schema.subface.wr:WR1"
The type of <<express:topology_schema.loop,loop>>s in the **subface** shall match the type of <<express:topology_schema.loop,loop>> instances in the **parent_face** entity.
*)


(*"topology_schema.subface.wr:WR2"
An instance of **subface** shall not also be the instance of <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> in the role of **parent_face**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.subface.wr:IP1"
The domain of the **subface** is formally defined to be the domain of the parent face, as trimmed by the loops of the subface.
*)


(*"topology_schema.subface.wr:IP2"
All loops of the subface shall be contained in the union of the domain of the parent face and the domains of the parent face's bounding loops.
*)


(*"topology_schema.connected_face_set"
A **connected_face_set** is a type of <<express:topology_schema.topological_representation_item,topological_representation_item>>, which is a set of <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> instances such that the domain of the faces together with their bounding edges and vertices is connected.
*)


(*"topology_schema.connected_face_set.cfs_faces"
a set of <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> instances arcwise connected along common <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> instances or <<express:topology_schema.vertex,vertex>> instances.;
*)


(*"topology_schema.connected_face_set.wr:IP1"
The union of the domains of the <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> instances and their bounding <<express:topology_schema.loop,loop>> instances shall be arcwise connected.
*)


(*"topology_schema.vertex_shell"
A **vertex_shell** is a type of <<express:topology_schema.topological_representation_item,topological_representation_item>>, which is a <<express:topology_schema.shell,shell>> consisting of a single <<express:topology_schema.vertex_loop,vertex_loop>>.

A **vertex_shell_extent** shall be unique.

A <<express:topology_schema.vertex_loop,vertex_loop>> can only be used by a single **vertex_shell**.

A <<express:topology_schema.vertex_loop,vertex_loop>> can exist independently of a **vertex_shell**
*)


(*"topology_schema.vertex_shell.vertex_shell_extent"
a single <<express:topology_schema.vertex_loop,vertex_loop>> which constitutes the extent of this type of <<express:topology_schema.shell,shell>>;
*)


(*"topology_schema.vertex_shell.wr:IP1"
The extent and dimensionality of a **vertex_shell** are both zero.
*)


(*"topology_schema.vertex_shell.wr:IP2"
The genus of a **vertex_shell** is 0.
*)


(*"topology_schema.wire_shell"
A **wire_shell** is a type of <<express:topology_schema.topological_representation_item,topological_representation_item>>, which is a <<express:topology_schema.shell,shell>> of dimensionality 1. A **wire_shell** can be regarded as a graph constructed of vertices and edges. However, it is not represented directly as a graph, but indirectly, as a set of loops. It is the union of the vertices and edges of these loops that form the graph. The domain of a wire shell, if present, is typically not a manifold.

Two restrictions are placed on the structure of a wire shell.

(a) The graph as a whole shall be connected.

(b) Each edge in the graph shall be referenced exactly twice by the set of loops.

Writing stem:[G^w] for the graph genus, and setting the number of connected components M =1, the Euler graph equation becomes:

[[eqn6]]

[stem]
++++
(V - E) - (1 -G^{w}) = 0
++++

More specifically, the following topological constraints shall be met:

* The loops shall be unique.
[stem]
++++
(S^{w}){L} = (S^{w})[L]
++++

* Each edge shall either be referenced by two loops, or twice by a single loop. That is, in the list stem:[((S^w)[L\])[E\]], each edge appears exactly twice.
[stem]
++++
|((S^{w})[L])[E]| = 2|((S^{w})[L]){E}|
++++

* Each oriented edge shall be unique.
[stem]
++++
((S^{w})[L]){E_{l}} = ((S^{w})[L])[E_{l}]
++++

* Equation <<eqn6>> shall be satisfied.
[stem]
++++
|(((S^{w})[L]){E}){V}| - |((S^{w})[L]){E}| - 1 +G^{w} = 0
++++
*)


(*"topology_schema.wire_shell.__note"
Two main applications of wire shells are contemplated.
*)

(*"topology_schema.wire_shell.__note"
Any connected graph can be written as a single loop obeying condition (b) by using the graph traversal algorithm. Such a graph may serve as a bound for a region.
*)

(*"topology_schema.wire_shell.__note"
The set of loops referenced by the faces of a closed shell automatically obey condition (b), but need not be connected. However, the faces of a closed shell can always be subdivided in such a way that their loops form a connected graph, and hence a wire shell. Thus, wire shells can represent the ``one-dimensional skeleta'' of closed shells.
*)

(*"topology_schema.wire_shell.wire_shell_extent"
a list of <<express:topology_schema.loop,loop>> instances defining the **wire_shell** ;
*)


(*"topology_schema.wire_shell.wr:WR1"
The loops making up the wire shell shall not be a mixture of <<express:topology_schema.poly_loop,poly_loop>> instances and other loop types.
*)


(*"topology_schema.wire_shell.wr:IP1"
The **wire_shell** has dimensionality 1.
*)


(*"topology_schema.wire_shell.wr:IP2"
The extent of the **wire_shell** is finite and greater than 0.
*)


(*"topology_schema.wire_shell.wr:IP3"
Each edge appears precisely twice in the wire shell with opposite orientations.
*)


(*"topology_schema.wire_shell.wr:IP4"
The Euler equation shall be satisfied.
*)


(*"topology_schema.wire_shell.wr:IP5"
The <<express:topology_schema.loop,loop>> instances defining the **wire_shell_extent** do not intersect except at common <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> instances or <<express:topology_schema.vertex,vertex>> instances.
*)


(*"topology_schema.open_shell"
An **open_shell** is a type of <<express:topology_schema.connected_face_set,connected_face_set>>, which is a <<express:topology_schema.shell,shell>> of dimensionality 2. Its domain, if present, is a finite, connected, oriented, 2-manifold with boundary, but is not a closed surface. It can be thought of as a <<express:topology_schema.closed_shell,closed_shell>> with one or more holes punched in it. The domain of an open shell satisfies stem:[0 < Xi < infty]. An open shell is functionally more general than a <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> because its domain can have handles. The shell is defined by a collection of <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> instances, which may be **oriented_face** instances. The sense of each face, after taking account of the orientation, shall agree with the shell normal as defined below. The **orientation** can be supplied directly as a BOOLEAN attribute of an <<express:topology_schema.oriented_face,oriented_face>>, or be defaulted to TRUE if the shell member is a <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> without the orientation attribute.

The following combinatorial restrictions on open shells and geometrical restrictions on their domains are designed, together with the informal propositions, to ensure that any domain associated with an open shell is an orientable manifold.

* Each face reference shall be unique.
* An **open_shell** shall have at least one <<express:topology_schema.face,face>>.
* A given <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> may exist in more than one **open_shell**.

The boundary of an open shell consists of the edges that are referenced only once by the <<express:topology_schema.face_bound,face_bound>> instances (loops) of its faces, together with all of their vertices. The domain of an open shell, if present, contains all edges and vertices of its faces.

The surface genus and topological normal of an open shell are those that would be obtained by filling in the holes in its domain to produce a closed shell. The topological normal can also be derived from the face normals after taking account of their orientation. The following Euler equation is satisfied by open shells. It is the most general form of Euler equation for connected, orientable surfaces.

[[eqn7]]

[stem]
++++
(V - E - L_{l} + 2F) - (2 - 2H - B) = 0
++++

where stem:[V], stem:[E],  stem:[bb(L)_l], stem:[F] are, respectively, the numbers of distinct vertices, edges, face bounds, and faces, H is the surface genus, and stem:[B] is the number of holes. stem:[B] can be determined directly from the graph of edges and vertices defining the bounds of the face, in the following manner:

Delete all edges from the graph that are referenced twice by the face bounds of the face.

Delete all vertices that have no associated edges.

Compute stem:[B] = the genus of the resulting graph.

If known a priori, the surface genus H may be used to check equation <<eqn7>> as an exact equality. Typically, this will not be the case, so equation <<eqn7>> or some equivalent formulation shall be used to compute the genus. Since H shall be a non-negative integer, this leads to the following inequality, a necessary condition for well-formed open shells.

[[eqn8]]
[stem]
++++
V - E - L_{l} + B "shall be even and" le 2-2F
++++

Specifically, the following topological constraints shall be met:

* Each face in the shell is unique. stem:[(S^o){F} = (S^o)[F\]]
* Each face bound in the shell is unique.
+
[stem]
++++
((S^{o})[F]){ L_{l}} = ((S^{o})[F])[L_{l}]
++++

* Each <<express:topology_schema.oriented_edge,oriented_edge>> in the shell is unique.
+
[stem]
++++
((S^{o})[F])[L_{l}]){E_{l}} = ((S^{o})[F])[L_{l}])[E_{l}]
++++

* In the list stem:[(((S^o)[F\])[L_l\])[E\]] there is at least one edge that only appears once and no edges appear more than twice; the singleton edges are on the boundary of the shell.
* The Euler condition <<eqn8>>, and equation <<eqn7>> shall be satisfied.
+
[stem]
++++
|((((S^{o})[F]){ L_{l}^{e}}){E\}){V\}| + |(((S^{o})[F]){ L_{l}^{v}}){V}| - |(((S^{o})[F]){L_{l}})\{E\}|
++++
+
[stem]
++++
- |((S^{o})[F])[L_{l}]| + B "is even and" le 2 - 2|(S^{o})[F]|
++++
+
[stem]
++++
2 - 2H - B = |((((S^{o})[F]){ L_{l}^{e0}){E}){V}| + |(((S^{o})[F]){ L_{l}^{v}}){V}|
++++
+
[stem]
++++
- |(((S^{o})[F]){ L_{l}}){E}| - |((S^{o})[F])[L_{l}]| + 2|(S^{o})[F]|
++++
*)


(*"topology_schema.open_shell.__note"
This is slightly different from the definition of a face domain, which includes none of its bounds. For example, a face domain may exclude an isolated point or line segment. An open shell domain may not. (See the algorithm for computing _*B*_ below.)
*)

(*"topology_schema.open_shell.wr:IP1"
Every <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> shall be referenced at least once, but no more than twice by the <<express:topology_schema.face_bound,face_bound>> instances of the <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> instances.
*)


(*"topology_schema.open_shell.wr:IP2"
Each <<express:topology_schema.oriented_edge,oriented_edge>> reference shall be unique.
*)


(*"topology_schema.open_shell.wr:IP3"
No <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> may be referenced by more than two <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> instances.
*)


(*"topology_schema.open_shell.wr:IP4"
Distinct <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> instances of the shell do not intersect, but may share edges, or vertices.
*)


(*"topology_schema.open_shell.wr:IP5"
Distinct <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> instances do not intersect, but may share vertices.
*)


(*"topology_schema.open_shell.wr:IP6"
The Euler equation shall be satisfied.
*)


(*"topology_schema.open_shell.wr:IP7"
The **open_shell** shall be an oriented arcwise connected 2-manifold.
*)


(*"topology_schema.open_shell.wr:IP8"
The **open_shell** shall contain at least one hole.
*)


(*"topology_schema.open_shell.wr:IP9"
The topological normal to each <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> of the **open_shell** shall be consistent with the topological normal to the **open_shell**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.oriented_open_shell"
An **oriented_open_shell** is a type of <<express:topology_schema.open_shell,open_shell>>, constructed from another <<express:topology_schema.open_shell,open_shell>> and contains a BOOLEAN direction flag to indicate whether or not the orientation of the constructed <<express:topology_schema.open_shell,open_shell>> agrees with the orientation of the original <<express:topology_schema.open_shell,open_shell>>. Except for perhaps orientation, the **oriented_open_shell** is equivalent to the original <<express:topology_schema.open_shell,open_shell>>.
*)


(*"topology_schema.oriented_open_shell.open_shell_element"
the <<express:topology_schema.open_shell,open_shell>>, which defines the faces of the **oriented_open_shell** ;
*)


(*"topology_schema.oriented_open_shell.orientation"
the relationship between the orientation of the **oriented_open_shell** being defined and the **open_shell_element** referenced;
*)


(*"topology_schema.oriented_open_shell.cfs_faces"
the set of faces for the **oriented_open_shell**, obtained from those of the **open_shell_element** after possibly reversing their orientation.
*)


(*"topology_schema.oriented_open_shell.wr:WR1"
The type of **open_shell_element** shall not be an **oriented_open_shell**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.closed_shell"
A **closed_shell** is a type of <<express:topology_schema.connected_face_set,connected_face_set>>, which is a <<express:topology_schema.shell,shell>> of dimensionality 2 which typically serves as a bound for a region in stem:[RR^3]. A closed shell has no boundary, and has non-zero finite extent. If the shell has a domain with coordinate space stem:[RR^3], it divides that space into two connected regions, one finite and the other infinite. In this case, the topological normal of the shell is defined as being directed from the finite to the infinite region.

The shell is defined by a collection of <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> instances, which may be <<express:topology_schema.oriented_face,oriented_face>> instances. The sense of each face, after taking account of the orientation, shall agree with the shell normal as defined above. The <<express:topology_schema.oriented_face.orientation,orientation>> can be supplied directly as a BOOLEAN attribute of an <<express:topology_schema.oriented_face,oriented_face>>, or be defaulted to TRUE if the shell member is a <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> without the orientation attribute.

The combinatorial restrictions on closed shells and geometrical restrictions on their domains ensure that any domain associated with a closed shell is a closed, orientable manifold. The domain of a closed shell, if present, is a connected, closed, oriented 2-manifold. It is always topologically equivalent to an H-fold torus for some stem:[H ge 0]. The number H is referred to as the {_surface genus_ of the shell. If a shell of genus H has a domain with coordinate space stem:[R^3], the finite region of space inside it is topologically equivalent to a solid ball with H tunnels drilled through it.

The surface Euler equation <<eqn7>> applies with stem:[bb B = 0], because in this case there are no holes. As in the case of <<express:topology_schema.open_shell,open_shell>> instances, the surface genus H may not be known a priori, but shall be an integer stem:[ge 0].

Thus, a necessary, but not sufficient, condition for a well-formed closed shell is the following:

[[eqn9]]

[stem]
++++
V - E - L_{l} " shall be even and" le 2 - 2F
++++

Specifically, the following topological constraints shall be met:

* Each face in the shell is unique. stem:[(S^c){F} = (S^c)[F\]]
* Each face bound in the shell is unique. stem:[((S^c)[F\]){L_l} = ((S^c)[F\])[L_l\]]
* Each <<express:topology_schema.oriented_edge,oriented_edge>> in the shell is unique.
[stem]
++++
((S^{c})[F])[L_{l}]){E_{l}} = ((S^{c})[F])[L_{l}])[E_{l}]
++++

* Each edge in the shell is either used by exactly two face bounds or is used twice by one face bound.
[stem]
++++
|(((S^{c})[F])[L_{l}])\{E_{l}}| = 2|(((S^{c})[F])[L_{l}]){E}|
++++

That is, in the list stem:[(((S^c)[F\])[L_l\])[E\]] each edge appears exactly twice.
* The Euler conditions <<eqn9>>, or optionally <<eqn7>> shall be satisfied.
[stem]
++++
2 - 2H = |((((S^{c})[F]){ L_{l}^{e0}){E}){V}| + |(((S^{c})[F]){ L_{l}^{v}}){V}|
++++

[stem]
++++
- |(((S^{c})[F]){ L_{l}}){E}| - |((S^{c})[F])[L_{l}]| + 2|(S^{c})[F]|
++++

[stem]
++++
|((((S^{c})[F]){ L_{l}^{e}}){E\}){V\}| + |(((S^{c})[F]){ L_{l}^{v}}){V}| - |(((S^{c})[F]){L_{l}}){E}|
++++

[stem]
++++
- |((S^{c})[F])[L_{l}]| + B "is even and" le 2 - 2|(S^{c})[F]|
++++
*)


(*"topology_schema.closed_shell.wr:IP1"
Every <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> shall be referenced exactly twice by the <<express:topology_schema.face_bound,face_bound>> instances of the faces.
*)


(*"topology_schema.closed_shell.wr:IP2"
Each <<express:topology_schema.oriented_edge,oriented_edge>> reference shall be unique.
*)


(*"topology_schema.closed_shell.wr:IP3"
No <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> shall be referenced by more than two <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> instances.
*)


(*"topology_schema.closed_shell.wr:IP4"
Distinct <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> instances of the shell do not intersect, but may share edges, or vertices.
*)


(*"topology_schema.closed_shell.wr:IP5"
Distinct <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> instances do not intersect, but may share vertices.
*)


(*"topology_schema.closed_shell.wr:IP6"
Each <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> reference shall be unique.
*)


(*"topology_schema.closed_shell.wr:IP7"
The <<express:topology_schema.loop,loop>> instances of the shell\> shall not be a mixture of <<express:topology_schema.poly_loop,poly_loop>> instances and other <<express:topology_schema.loop,loop>> types.
*)


(*"topology_schema.closed_shell.wr:IP8"
The **closed_shell** shall be an oriented arcwise connected-manifold.
*)


(*"topology_schema.closed_shell.wr:IP9"
The Euler equation shall be satisfied.
*)


(*"topology_schema.closed_shell.wr:IP10"
The topological normal to each <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> of the **closed_shell** shall be consistent with the topological normal to the **closed_shell**. This implies that the topological normal to each <<express:topology_schema.face,face>>, after taking account of orientation, if present, shall point from the finite region bounded by the **closed_shell** into the infinite region outside.
*)


(*"topology_schema.oriented_closed_shell"
An **oriented_closed_shell** is a type of <<express:topology_schema.closed_shell,closed_shell>>, constructed from another <<express:topology_schema.closed_shell,closed_shell>> and contains a BOOLEAN direction flag to indicate whether or not the orientation of the constructed <<express:topology_schema.closed_shell,closed_shell>> agrees with the orientation of the original <<express:topology_schema.closed_shell,closed_shell>>. Except for perhaps orientation, the **oriented_closed_shell** is equivalent to the original <<express:topology_schema.closed_shell,closed_shell>>.
*)


(*"topology_schema.oriented_closed_shell.closed_shell_element"
the <<express:topology_schema.closed_shell,closed_shell>>, which defines the faces of the **oriented_closed_shell** ;
*)


(*"topology_schema.oriented_closed_shell.orientation"
the relationship between the orientation of the **oriented_closed_shell** being defined and the **closed_shell_element** referenced;
*)


(*"topology_schema.oriented_closed_shell.cfs_faces"
the set of faces for the **oriented_closed_shell**, obtained from those of the **closed_shell_element** after possibly reversing their orientation.;
*)


(*"topology_schema.oriented_closed_shell.wr:WR1"
The type of **closed_shell_element** shall not be an **oriented_closed_shell**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.connected_face_sub_set"
A **connected_face_sub_set** is a type of <<express:topology_schema.connected_face_set,connected_face_set>>, whose domain is a connected portion of the domain of an existing <<express:topology_schema.connected_face_set,connected_face_set>>. As a complex subtype, an instance of **connected_face_sub_set** may also be of type <<express:topology_schema.open_shell,open_shell>>, or, if appropriate, <<express:topology_schema.closed_shell,closed_shell>>. The bounding loops of the faces of the **connected_face_sub_set** may reference <<express:topology_schema.subedge,subedge>> instances. The topological constraints on a **connected_face_sub_set** are the same as on a <<express:topology_schema.connected_face_set,connected_face_set>>.
*)


(*"topology_schema.connected_face_sub_set.wr:WR1"
An instance of **connected_face_sub_set** shall not also be the instance of <<express:topology_schema.connected_face_set,connected_face_set>> in the role of **parent_face_set**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.get_tri_in_representations"
The FUNCTION **get_tri_in_representations** returns the SET of <<express:topology_schema.topological_representation_item,topological_representation_item>> that are referenced by the SET of representations provided as input to the function.
*)


(*"topology_schema.get_tri_in_representations.members"
the SET of representations that are the input to the function.
*)


(*"topology_schema.connected_face_sub_set.parent_face_set"
the <<express:topology_schema.connected_face_set,connected_face_set>>, which contains the **connected_face_sub_set** ; the **parent_face_set** may be of type <<express:topology_schema.open_shell,open_shell>> or of type <<express:topology_schema.closed_shell,closed_shell>>.
*)


(*"topology_schema.connected_face_sub_set.orientation"
the relationship between the orientation of the **connected_face_sub_set** being defined and the **closed_shell_element** referenced;
*)


(*"topology_schema.connected_face_sub_set.cfs_faces"
the set of faces for the **connected_face_sub_set**, obtained from those of the **closed_shell_element** after possibly reversing their orientation.;
*)


(*"topology_schema.connected_face_sub_set.wr:IP1"
The domain of the **connected_face_sub_set** shall be within the domain of the **parent_face_set**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.connected_edge_set"
A **connected_edge_set** is a type of <<express:topology_schema.topological_representation_item,topological_representation_item>>, and is a set of <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> instances such that the domain of the edges together with their bounding vertices is arcwise connected.
*)


(*"topology_schema.connected_edge_set.ces_edges"
a set of <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> instances arcwise connected at common <<express:topology_schema.vertex,vertex>> instances;
*)


(*"topology_schema.connected_edge_set.wr:IP1"
The dimensionality of the **connected_edge_set** is 1.
*)


(*"topology_schema.connected_edge_set.wr:IP2"
The domains of the edges of the **connected_edge_set** shall not intersect.
*)


(*"topology_schema.connected_edge_sub_set"
A **connected_edge_sub_set** is a type of <<express:topology_schema.connected_edge_set,connected_edge_set>>, whose domain is a connected portion of the domain of an existing <<express:topology_schema.connected_edge_set,connected_edge_set>>. An instance of **connected_edge_sub_set** may contain a combination of <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> and <<express:topology_schema.subedge,subedge>> such that the resulting domain of <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> and <<express:topology_schema.subedge,subedge>>, together with their bounding vertices, is an arcwise connected, non-intersecting, and 1-dimensional subdomain of the domain defined by the **parent_edge_set**. The topological constraints on a **connected_edge_sub_set** are the same as on a <<express:topology_schema.connected_edge_set,connected_edge_set>>.
*)


(*"topology_schema.connected_edge_sub_set.parent_edge_set"
the <<express:topology_schema.connected_edge_set,connected_edge_set>>, which contains the **connected_edge_sub_set**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.connected_edge_sub_set.wr:WR1"
An instance of **connected_edge_sub_set** shall not also be the instance of <<express:topology_schema.connected_edge_set,connected_edge_set>> in the role of **parent_edge_set**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.connected_edge_sub_set.wr:IP1"
The domain of the **connected_edge_sub_set** shall be within the domain of the **parent_edge_set**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.volume_with_faces"
A **volume_with_faces** is a type of <<express:topology_schema.topological_representation_item,topological_representation_item>> and an explicitly defined solid, in contrast to a boundary representation solid, which is implicitly defined by its boundaries. The volume is limited by faces, which provide means for representation of adjacency information and which allow the subtypes of this entity to take part in a <<express:topology_schema.connected_volume_set,connected_volume_set>>. The geometry of a **volume_with_faces** is defined by an associated <<express:geometry_schema.volume,volume>>. The portion of the volume used by **the volume_with_faces** shall be embeddable in the **volume_with_faces**. The geometry associated with any component of the faces of the **volume_with_faces** shall be consistent with the volume geometry, in the sense that the domains of all the <<express:topology_schema.vertex_point,vertex_point>> instances, <<express:topology_schema.edge_curve,edge_curve>> instances and <<express:topology_schema.face_surface,face_surface>> instances are contained in the **volume_with_faces** geometry volume. A <<express:geometry_schema.volume,volume>> may be referenced by more than one **volume_with_faces**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.valid_tri_ids"
The FUNCTION **valid_tri_ids** returns TRUE if each <<express:topology_schema.topological_representation_item,topological_representation_item>> has an id and if each id is used only once in the SET of <<express:topology_schema.topological_representation_item,topological_representation_item>>.
*)


(*"topology_schema.valid_tri_ids.__note"
The value of <<express:topology_schema.topological_representation_item.permanent_aggregate_id,permanent_aggregate_id>> and of <<express:topology_schema.topological_representation_item.permanent_id,permanent_id>> shall be disjoint in order to support possible use cases where there shall be no more than one id of any kind assigned to a <<express:topology_schema.topological_representation_item,topological_representation_item>>.
*)

(*"topology_schema.valid_tri_ids.objs"
the SET OF <<express:topology_schema.topological_representation_item,topological_representation_item>> that are the input to the function.
*)


(*"topology_schema.volume_with_faces.volume_geometry"
the trivariate volume that defines the internal shape of the **volume_with_faces**. The domain of the **volume_with_faces** is defined by this volume and its bounding faces. The bounding faces are specified in the subtypes of the **volume_with_faces**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.volume_with_parametric_boundary"
A **volume_with_parametric_boundary** is a type of <<express:topology_schema.volume_with_faces,volume_with_faces>> where the boundary is specified by six faces. The associated surfaces of these faces shall correspond to the bounding surfaces of the inherited attributed <<express:topology_schema.volume_with_faces.volume_geometry,volume_geometry>>.
*)

(*"topology_schema.volume_with_parametric_boundary.__example"
This entity is suitable for use in a block structured model where the blocks meet in a corner-to-corner configuration, in the context of isogeometric analysis. A *volume_with_parametric_boundary* may represent one block in a block structured computational mesh.
*)

(*"topology_schema.volume_with_parametric_boundary.outer_bound"
the external boundaries of the **volume_with_parametric_boundary**. The <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> instances in the array are related to the parameters and their lower and upper values as follows:

* face 1: lower boundary in the first parameter direction;
* face 2: upper boundary in the first parameter direction;
* face 3: lower boundary in the second parameter direction;
* face 4: upper boundary in the second parameter direction;
* face 5: lower boundary in the third parameter direction;
* face 6: upper boundary in the third parameter direction.
*)


(*"topology_schema.volume_with_shell"
A **volume_with_shell** is a type of <<express:topology_schema.volume_with_faces,volume_with_faces>> where the boundary is specified by a <<express:topology_schema.closed_shell,closed_shell>>. The volume shall not have voids. This entity enables the representation of trimmed volumes. It can also be used to represent blocks in a block structured volume model with T-joints, that is, no corner-to-corner condition is applied. In the latter case, the faces of the <<express:topology_schema.closed_shell,closed_shell>> represent the boundary trimming of the volume.
*)


(*"topology_schema.volume_with_shell.outer_bound"
the <<express:topology_schema.closed_shell,closed_shell>> that defines the faces of the external boundary of the **volume_with_shell**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.connected_volume_set"
A **connected_volume_set** is a type of <<express:topology_schema.topological_representation_item,topological_representation_item>> and is a set of <<express:topology_schema.volume_with_faces,volume_with_faces>> such that the domain of the volumes together with their bounding faces, edges and vertices is connected.
*)


(*"topology_schema.connected_volume_set.__note"
This concept may be used in isogeometric analysis where the computational mesh is block structured and each block is defined by an explicitly defined volume.
*)

(*"topology_schema.connected_volume_set.cvs_volumes"
the SET of <<express:topology_schema.volume_with_faces,volume_with_faces>> from which the **connected_volume_set** is constructed.
*)


(*"topology_schema.connected_volume_set.wr:IP1"
The union of the domains of the volumes and their bounding faces shall be arcwise connected.
*)


(*"topology_schema.connected_volume_set.wr:IP2"
No <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> in the **connected_volume_set** shall be referenced more than twice as <<express:topology_schema.volume_with_parametric_boundary.outer_bound,outer_bound>>.
*)


(*"topology_schema.connected_volume_set.wr:IP3"
When 2 <<express:topology_schema.volume_with_faces,volume_with_faces>> in the **connected_volume_set** share a <<express:topology_schema.face,face>>, the faces shall be of type <<express:topology_schema.oriented_face,oriented_face>> and have opposite orientations.
*)


(*"topology_schema.connected_volume_sub_set"
A **connected_volume_sub_set** is a type of <<express:topology_schema.connected_volume_set,connected_volume_set>> whose domain is a connected portion of the domain of an existing <<express:topology_schema.connected_volume_set,connected_volume_set>>. The bounding faces of the volumes of the **connected_volume_sub_set** may reference <<express:topology_schema.subface,subface>> instances. The topological constraints on a **connected_volume_sub_set** are the same as on a <<express:topology_schema.connected_volume_set,connected_volume_set>>.
*)


(*"topology_schema.connected_volume_sub_set.parent_volume_set"
the <<express:topology_schema.connected_volume_set,connected_volume_set>> that contains the **connected_volume_sub_set**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.connected_volume_sub_set.wr:IP1"
The domain of the **connected_volume_sub_set** shall be within the domain of the <<express:topology_schema.connected_volume_sub_set.parent_volume_set,parent_volume_set>>.
*)


(*"topology_schema.connected_volume_sub_set.wr:WR1"
An instance of **connected_volume_sub_set** shall not also be the instance of <<express:topology_schema.connected_volume_sub_set.parent_volume_set,parent_volume_set>> in the role of **parent_volume_set**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.conditional_reverse"
Depending on its first argument the **conditional_reverse** function returns either the input topology unchanged or a copy of the input topology with its orientation reversed.
*)


(*"topology_schema.conditional_reverse.p"
(input) a BOOLEAN value indicating whether or not orientation reversal is required;
*)


(*"topology_schema.conditional_reverse.an_item"
(input) an item of topology which can be reversed if required.
*)


(*"topology_schema.topology_reversed"
The **topology_reversed** function returns topology equivalent to the input topology except that the orientation is reversed.
*)


(*"topology_schema.topology_reversed.an_item"
(input) an item of reversible topology which is to have its orientation reversed;
*)


(*"topology_schema.topology_reversed.item_reversed"
(output) a <<express:topology_schema.topological_representation_item,topological_representation_item>> which is the result of reversing the orientation of **an_item**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.edge_reversed"
The **edge_reversed** function returns an <<express:topology_schema.oriented_edge,oriented_edge>> equivalent to the input <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> except that the orientation is reversed.
*)


(*"topology_schema.edge_reversed.an_edge"
(input) the <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> which is to have its orientation reversed.
*)


(*"topology_schema.edge_reversed.the_reverse"
(output) A <<express:topology_schema.oriented_edge,oriented_edge>> that is the result of the orientation reversal.
*)


(*"topology_schema.path_reversed"
The **path_reversed** function returns an <<express:topology_schema.oriented_path,oriented_path>> equivalent to the input <<express:topology_schema.path,path>> except that the orientation is reversed.
*)


(*"topology_schema.path_reversed.a_path"
(input) the <<express:topology_schema.path,path>> which is to have its orientation reversed.
*)


(*"topology_schema.path_reversed.the_reverse"
(output) A <<express:topology_schema.oriented_path,oriented_path>> that is the result of the orientation reversal.
*)


(*"topology_schema.face_bound_reversed"
The **face_bound_reversed** function returns a <<express:topology_schema.face_bound,face_bound>> equivalent to the input <<express:topology_schema.face_bound,face_bound>> except that the orientation is reversed.
*)


(*"topology_schema.face_bound_reversed.a_face_bound"
(input) the <<express:topology_schema.face_bound,face_bound>> which is to have its orientation reversed.
*)


(*"topology_schema.face_bound_reversed.the_reverse"
(output) A <<express:topology_schema.face_bound,face_bound>> that is the result of the orientation reversal.
*)


(*"topology_schema.face_reversed"
The **face_reversed** function returns an <<express:topology_schema.oriented_face,oriented_face>> equivalent to the input <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> except that the orientation is reversed.
*)


(*"topology_schema.face_reversed.a_face"
(input) the <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> which is to have its orientation reversed.
*)


(*"topology_schema.face_reversed.the_reverse"
(output) a <<express:topology_schema.oriented_face,oriented_face>> that is the result of the orientation reversal.
*)


(*"topology_schema.shell_reversed"
The **shell_reversed** function returns an <<express:topology_schema.oriented_open_shell,oriented_open_shell>> or <<express:topology_schema.oriented_closed_shell,oriented_closed_shell>> equivalent to the input <<express:topology_schema.shell,shell>> except that the orientation is reversed.
*)


(*"topology_schema.shell_reversed.a_shell"
(input) the <<express:topology_schema.shell,shell>> which is to have its orientation reversed.
*)


(*"topology_schema.shell_reversed.the_reverse"
(output) The result of the orientation reversal.
*)


(*"topology_schema.closed_shell_reversed"
The **closed_shell_reversed** function returns an <<express:topology_schema.oriented_closed_shell,oriented_closed_shell>> equivalent to the input <<express:topology_schema.closed_shell,closed_shell>> except that the orientation is reversed.
*)


(*"topology_schema.closed_shell_reversed.a_shell"
(input) the <<express:topology_schema.closed_shell,closed_shell>> which is to have its orientation reversed.
*)


(*"topology_schema.closed_shell_reversed.the_reverse"
(output) A <<express:topology_schema.oriented_closed_shell,oriented_closed_shell>> that is the result of the orientation reversal.
*)


(*"topology_schema.open_shell_reversed"
The **open_shell_reversed** function returns an <<express:topology_schema.oriented_open_shell,oriented_open_shell>> equivalent to the input <<express:topology_schema.open_shell,open_shell>> except that the orientation is reversed.
*)


(*"topology_schema.open_shell_reversed.a_shell"
(input) the <<express:topology_schema.open_shell,open_shell>> which is to have its orientation reversed.
*)


(*"topology_schema.open_shell_reversed.the_reverse"
(output) A <<express:topology_schema.oriented_open_shell,oriented_open_shell>> that is the result of the orientation reversal.
*)


(*"topology_schema.set_of_topology_reversed"
The **set_of_topology_reversed** function returns a set of topology equivalent to the input set of topology except that the orientation of each element of the set is reversed.
*)


(*"topology_schema.set_of_topology_reversed.a_set"
(input) the set of topology items which are to have their orientation reversed.
*)


(*"topology_schema.set_of_topology_reversed.the_reverse"
(output) The result of the orientation reversal.
*)


(*"topology_schema.list_of_topology_reversed"
The **list_of_topology_reversed** function returns a list of topologies equivalent to the input list of topologies except that the orientation of each element of the list is reversed and the order of the elements in the list is reversed.
*)


(*"topology_schema.list_of_topology_reversed.a_list"
(input) the list of topology items which are to have their orientation and list order reversed.
*)


(*"topology_schema.list_of_topology_reversed.the_reverse"
(output) The result of the orientation and order reversal.
*)


(*"topology_schema.boolean_choose"
The **boolean_choose** function returns one of two choices depending the value of a Boolean input argument. The two choices are given as input arguments.
*)


(*"topology_schema.boolean_choose.b"
the Boolean value used to select the element choice1 (TRUE) or choice2 (FALSE);
*)


(*"topology_schema.boolean_choose.choice1"
(input) the first item which may be selected;
*)


(*"topology_schema.boolean_choose.choice2"
(input) the second item which may be selected.
*)


(*"topology_schema.path_head_to_tail"
The **path_head_to_tail** function returns TRUE if for the <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> instances of the input <<express:topology_schema.path,path>>, the end vertex of each <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> is the same as the start vertex of its successor.
*)


(*"topology_schema.path_head_to_tail.a_path"
(input) the path for which it is required to verify that its component edges are arranged consecutively head-to-tail.
*)


(*"topology_schema.path_head_to_tail.p"
(output) A LOGICAL variable which is TRUE if all <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> instances in the <<express:topology_schema.path,path>> join head-to-tail.
*)


(*"topology_schema.list_face_loops"
Given a <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> (or a <<express:topology_schema.subface,subface>>), the **list_face_loops** function returns the list of <<express:topology_schema.loop,loop>> s in the <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> or <<express:topology_schema.subface,subface>>.
*)


(*"topology_schema.list_face_loops.f"
(input) the <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> for which it is required to generate the list of bounding <<express:topology_schema.loop,loop>> instances.
*)


(*"topology_schema.list_face_loops.loops"
(output) The list of <<express:topology_schema.loop,loop>> instances for **f**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.list_loop_edges"
Given a <<express:topology_schema.loop,loop>>, the **list_loop_edges** function returns the list of <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> s in the <<express:topology_schema.loop,loop>>.
*)


(*"topology_schema.list_loop_edges.l"
(input) the <<express:topology_schema.loop,loop>> for which it is required to generate the list of <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> instances.
*)


(*"topology_schema.list_loop_edges.edges"
(output) The list of <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> instances for **l**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.list_shell_edges"
Given a <<express:topology_schema.shell,shell>>, the **list_shell_edges** function returns the list of <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> s in the <<express:topology_schema.shell,shell>>.
*)


(*"topology_schema.list_shell_edges.s"
(input) the <<express:topology_schema.shell,shell>> for which it is required to generate the list of <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> instances.
*)


(*"topology_schema.list_shell_edges.edges"
(output) The list of <<express:topology_schema.edge,edge>> instances for **s**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.list_shell_faces"
Given a <<express:topology_schema.shell,shell>>, the **list_shell_faces** function returns the list of <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> s in the <<express:topology_schema.shell,shell>>.
*)


(*"topology_schema.list_shell_faces.s"
(input) the <<express:topology_schema.shell,shell>> for which it is required to generate the list of <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> instances.
*)


(*"topology_schema.list_shell_faces.faces"
(output) The list of <<express:topology_schema.face,face>> instances for **s**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.list_shell_loops"
Given a <<express:topology_schema.shell,shell>>, the **list_shell_loops** function returns the list of <<express:topology_schema.loop,loop>> s in the <<express:topology_schema.shell,shell>>.
*)


(*"topology_schema.list_shell_loops.s"
(input) the <<express:topology_schema.shell,shell>> for which it is required to generate the list of <<express:topology_schema.loop,loop>> instances.
*)


(*"topology_schema.list_shell_loops.loops"
(output) The list of <<express:topology_schema.loop,loop>> instances for **s**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.mixed_loop_type_set"
Given a set of <<express:topology_schema.loop,loop>> instances, the **mixed_loop_type_set** function returns TRUE if the set includes both <<express:topology_schema.poly_loop,poly_loop>> instances and other types (edge and vertex) of loops.
*)


(*"topology_schema.mixed_loop_type_set.l"
(input) the set of <<express:topology_schema.loop,loop>> instances for which it is required to determine whether, or not, it is a mixture of <<express:topology_schema.poly_loop,poly_loop>> instances and others.
*)


(*"topology_schema.list_to_set"
The **list_to_set** function creates a SET from a LIST, the type of element for the SET will be the same as that in the original LIST.
*)


(*"topology_schema.list_to_set.l"
(input) The list of elements to be converted to a set.
*)


(*"topology_schema.list_to_set.s"
(output) The set corresponding to **l**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.edge_curve_pcurves"
The **edge_curve_pcurves** function returns the set of pcurves that are associated with (i.e., represent the geometry of) an <<express:topology_schema.edge_curve,edge_curve>>.
*)


(*"topology_schema.edge_curve_pcurves.an_edge"
(input) the <<express:topology_schema.edge_curve,edge_curve>> whose associated pcurves are to be found;
*)


(*"topology_schema.edge_curve_pcurves.the_surface_curves"
(input) the set of all <<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve,surface_curve>> instances within the scope of the search for <<express:geometry_schema.pcurve,pcurve>> instances.
*)


(*"topology_schema.edge_curve_pcurves.result"
(output) the set of all <<express:geometry_schema.pcurve,pcurve>> instances associated with **an_edge**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.vertex_point_pcurves"
The **vertex_point_pcurves** function returns the set of pcurves that are associated with (i.e., represent the geometry of) a <<express:topology_schema.vertex_point,vertex_point>>.
*)


(*"topology_schema.vertex_point_pcurves.a_vertex"
(input) the <<express:topology_schema.vertex_point,vertex_point>> whose associated pcurves are to be found;
*)


(*"topology_schema.vertex_point_pcurves.the_degenerates"
(input) the set of all <<express:geometry_schema.evaluated_degenerate_pcurve,evaluated_degenerate_pcurve>> instances within the scope of the search for <<express:geometry_schema.pcurve,pcurve>> instances.
*)


(*"topology_schema.vertex_point_pcurves.result"
(output) The set of all <<express:geometry_schema.evaluated_degenerate_pcurve,evaluated_degenerate_pcurve>> instances having the same geometry as **a_vertex**.
*)


(*"topology_schema.advanced_face"
An **advanced_face** is a type of
// face_surface
<<express:topology_schema.face_surface,face_surface>> that has additional constraints to ensure that the geometry is directly and completely defined. The **advanced_face** is the top level entity that is used to formulate the precise definition of a face with explicit topological bounds and fully defined geometry.

An **advanced_face** is required to be fully bounded by
// edge_loop
<<express:topology_schema.edge_loop,edge_loop>> instances or by
// vertex_loop
<<express:topology_schema.vertex_loop,vertex_loop>> instances.

At most one of the <<express:topology_schema.face.bounds,bounds>> instances of the face may be of type
// face_outer_bound
<<express:topology_schema.face_outer_bound,face_outer_bound>>.
*)

(*"topology_schema.advanced_face.__example"
Any
// edge_loop
<<express:topology_schema.edge_loop,edge_loop>> on a plane surface may be used to define a
// face_outer_bound
<<express:topology_schema.face_outer_bound,face_outer_bound>> provided it is not enclosed in any other loop in the
// face
<<express:topology_schema.face,face>>.
*)
(*"topology_schema.advanced_face.__example"
A circular loop on a
// cylindrical_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.cylindrical_surface,cylindrical_surface>> cannot define a
// face_outer_bounds
<<express:topology_schema.face_outer_bound,face_outer_bound>> since it does not enclose a closed domain in the surface.
*)

(*"topology_schema.advanced_face.__note"
For some types of closed or partially closed surfaces, it may not be possible to identify a unique outer bound.
*)

(*"topology_schema.advanced_face.face_geometry"
one of:
// elementary_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.elementary_surface,elementary_surface>>,
// swept_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.swept_surface,swept_surface>>, or
// b_spline_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_surface,b_spline_surface>>.
*)


(*"topology_schema.advanced_face.wr:WR1"
The geometry of all bounding edges of the face shall be fully defined as
// edge_curve
<<express:topology_schema.edge_curve,edge_curve>> instances.
*)


(*"topology_schema.advanced_face.wr:WR2"
The types of curve used to define the geometry of edges shall be restricted to
// line
<<express:geometry_schema.line,line>> instances,
// conic
<<express:geometry_schema.conic,conic>> instances,
// polyline
<<express:geometry_schema.polyline,polyline>> instances,
// surface_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve,surface_curve>> instances, or
// b_spline_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_curve,b_spline_curve>> instances.
*)


(*"topology_schema.advanced_face.wr:WR3"
All vertices used in the face definition shall be of type
// vertex_point
<<express:topology_schema.vertex_point,vertex_point>> with geometry defined by a
// cartesian_point
<<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_point,cartesian_point>>.
*)


(*"topology_schema.advanced_face.wr:WR4"
The use of oriented paths in the definition of the
// edge_loop
<<express:topology_schema.edge_loop,edge_loop>> instances of the
// advanced_face
<<express:topology_schema.advanced_face,advanced_face>> is prohibited.
*)


(*"topology_schema.advanced_face.wr:WR5"
If the face geometry is of type
// swept_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.swept_surface,swept_surface>> then the
// swept_surface.swept_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.swept_surface.swept_curve,swept_curve>> used in the definition shall be of type
// line
<<express:geometry_schema.line,line>>,
// conic
<<express:geometry_schema.conic,conic>>,
// polyline
<<express:geometry_schema.polyline,polyline>>, or
// b_spline_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_curve,b_spline_curve>>.
*)


(*"topology_schema.advanced_face.wr:WR6"
For any
// vertex_loop
<<express:topology_schema.vertex_loop,vertex_loop>> used to bound the face the
// loop_vertex
<<express:topology_schema.vertex_loop.loop_vertex,loop_vertex>> shall be of type
// vertex_point
<<express:topology_schema.vertex_point,vertex_point>> and the geometry shall be defined by a
// cartesian_point
<<express:geometry_schema.cartesian_point,cartesian_point>>.
*)


(*"topology_schema.advanced_face.wr:WR7"
The face bounds shall be defined by either
// edge_loop
<<express:topology_schema.edge_loop,edge_loop>> instances or
// vertex_loop
<<express:topology_schema.vertex_loop,vertex_loop>> instances.
*)


(*"topology_schema.advanced_face.wr:WR8"
If a
// surface_curve
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve,surface_curve>> is used as part of a face bound then the
// surface_curve.associated_geometry
<<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve.associated_geometry,associated_geometry>> attribute shall reference
// pcurve
<<express:geometry_schema.pcurve,pcurve>> instances not
// surface
<<express:geometry_schema.surface,surface>> instances.
*)


(*"topology_schema.advanced_face.wr:WR9"
If a
// polyline
<<express:geometry_schema.polyline,polyline>> is used either to define a
// swept_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.swept_surface,swept_surface>> or as part of a face bound, it shall contain at least three points.
*)


(*"topology_schema.advanced_face.wr:IP1"
Any instance of **advanced_face** which has the geometry of a complete
// spherical_surface
<<express:geometry_schema.spherical_surface,spherical_surface>> shall be bounded by a
// vertex_loop
<<express:topology_schema.vertex_loop,vertex_loop>> located at the point where the z axis of the placement coordinate system leaves the surface of the sphere, (i.e at the 'North Pole' of the sphere).
*)


(*"topology_schema.__schema_file"
data/resource_docs/geometric_and_topological_representation/resource.xml
*)


